{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789616589.400231, "id": "9b403df766cf", "tool_call_id": "call_1ca7c6a11fb741cbbb77830c", "content": "1: \"\"\"Windows local-shell adaptation: ONE shell decision, every consumer agrees.\n2: \n3: localshell decides which shell local run_command text executes under (the\n4: host's POSIX sh / a detected Git Bash / cmd.exe). These tests PIN that decision\n5: (reset_cache) and verify every consumer follows it:\n6: \n7:   - split_command                    tokenizer flavor (backslash + quoting rules)\n8:   - LocalTransport.run               spawn shape (argv vs shell=True, utf-8 decode)\n9:   - shell.run_command/_blocked_reason  unparseable-command guard + REPL lexer\n10:   - PermissionEvaluator.escaped_paths  flavor comes from the WORKSPACE, so a\n11:                                      remote (SSH) workspace tokenizes POSIX even\n12:                                      on a host pinned to cmd\n13:   - context.derive_messages          the local-environment hint (and its absence\n14:                                      on posix-sh / remote workspaces)\n15:   - supervisor._SafeStdStream        the no-fcntl (Windows) stdio degradation\n16: \n17: Run: uv run python3 -m tests.local_shell_test\n18: \"\"\"\n19: \n20: from __future__ import annotations\n21: \n22: import io\n23: import subprocess\n24: import tempfile\n25: import threading\n26: import time\n27: \n28: from tests.testsupport import check\n29: \n30: from agent.config import Config\n31: from agent.core.context import derive_messages\n32: from agent.core.lazy import LazyEventLog\n33: from agent.core.permission import PermissionEvaluator\n34: from agent.supervisor import _SafeStdStream\n35: from agent.tools import shell as shell_mod\n36: from agent.tools.localshell import LocalShell, local_shell, reset_cache, split_command\n37: from agent.tools.transport import LocalTransport\n38: from agent.tools.workspace import LocalWorkspace, RemoteWorkspace\n39: \n40: # pinned decisions (argv