ears early (within first ~600 chars), description right after (~within 1200), stargazers_count somewhere mid (~3-4KB), pushed_at later. head -c 4500 should capture through stargazers_count. That's 3 queries × 4.5KB = 13.5KB of noise. Acceptable but heavy. Alternatively use the search API with more items per page but they're even bigger.\n\nBetter: try python one-liner first — if allowed it's cleanest."}
