{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789616857.1503499, "id": "c957da84723f", "content": "结构信息齐了。开始实现。设计决策（结合调研）：\n\n**调研结论**：现成方案有 `deedy5/ddgs`（免 key 聚合搜索，但靠爬引擎 HTML，易碎）、`searxng`（要自建实例）、`tavily`（质量最好但要 key）、MCP 参考实现（可借鉴 fetch/搜索的模式）。本项目信奉「关键逻辑自己实现 + 最小依赖」，所以**自己设计**：一个 stdlib 实现的多后端搜索链（Tavily→SearXNG→Bing RSS→DDG，无 key 开箱即用）+ 一个网页正文提取工具，正好复用本会话验证过的 Bing RSS 通路。\n\n先加配置项：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_0211b813771a41c69bd334bf", "name": "edit_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"agent/config.py\",\"old_string\":\"    # Tool execution\\n    command_timeout: float = 30.0\\n    output_limit: int = 6000\\n    output_head: int = 2500\\n    output_tail: int = 2500\\n    read_max_chars: int = 20000\",\"new_string\":\"    # Tool execution\\n    command_timeout: float = 30.0\\n    output_limit: int = 6000\\n    output_head: int = 2500\\n    output_tail: int = 2500\\n    read_max_chars: int = 20000\\n\\n    # Web access (tools/websearch.py): keyless out of the box (Bing RSS -> DDG\\n    # HTML); better backends activate automatically once their env is present\\n    web_search_timeout: float = 15.0\\n    web_search_max_results: int = 8\\n    # Tavily (https://tavily.com, LLM-first search API, free tier)\\n    tavily_api_key: str | None = field(\\n        default_factory=lambda: os.environ.get(\\\"CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY\\\") or os.environ.get(\\\"TAVILY_API_KEY\\\")\\n    )\\n    # Self-hosted SearXNG instance exposing format=json (searxng/searxng)\\n    searxng_url: str = field(\\n        default_factory=lambda: (\\n            os.environ.get(\\\"CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL\\\") or os.environ.get(\\\"SEARXNG_URL\\\") or \\\"\\\"\\n        ).rstrip(\\\"/\\\")\\n    )\"}"}], "reasoning": "UI references tool names only for display; adding new tools won't break the UI (unknown tools presumably render generically).\n\nNow I have the full picture. Design decisions:\n\n**Research conclusion (to report to user):**\n- Existing open-source options for search APIs:\n  - `deedy5/ddgs` (2.9k★): Python metasearch lib, no key, scrapes multiple engines — convenient but a scraping dep that breaks with engine markup changes.\n  - `searxng/searxng`: self-host metasearch with clean JSON API — great if user runs an instance; needs an instance.\n  - `tavily-ai/tavily-python` (1.4k★): LLM-first search API — best result quality, needs key (free tier).\n  - `modelcontextprotocol/servers` (90k★): reference `fetch` + brave-search MCP servers — patterns to copy (fetch with readable-text extraction, key-based search), not a drop-in for a Python tool registry.\n  - Bing RSS endpoint: undocumented but stable, keyless, works from CN — verified live in this session.\n- Decision: self-built (self-designed), consistent with project ethos (self-built loop, minimal deps): one stdlib module implementing a backend chain (Tavily → SearXNG → Bing RSS → DDG HTML) + a readability fetch tool, honoring CLUTCH_* env config. No new dependencies, keyless out of the box, and it works in chat mode too (fixing today's clunky curl|head dance).\n\n**Implementation plan:**\n1. `agent/tools/websearch.py` — module with `_http_get`, backends, `web_search`, `web_fetch`.\n2. `agent/config.py` — add `web_search_timeout`, `web_search_max_results`, `tavily_api_key`, `searxng_url` (env-driven defaults).\n3. `agent/tools/registry.py` — register both tools in BOTH modes.\n4. `agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md`, `web_fetch.md` — descriptions.\n5. `tests/websearch_test.py` — offline parser/fallback/SSRF tests + `--live` end-to-end flag.\n6. README — add web_search/web_fetch to the tools list line + env keys mention.\n\nAlso `agent/tools/__init__.py` — check what it exports (probably nothing needed). Quick check before writing.\n\nNow write the module. Key details:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Web access tools: web_search (multi-backend search) and web_fetch (page -> text).\n\n...poka-yoke list...\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n-http_get(url, *, timeout, cancel, max_bytes) -> tuple[str final_url, str content_type, bytes body]\n  - scheme check http/https\n  - _safe_host(url): resolve via socket.getaddrinfo → all IPs must be global (ipaddress.ip_address(ip).is_global, also reject is_loopback/is_private/is_link_local/is_reserved/is_multicast). IPv6 handled by getaddrinfo AF_UNSPEC? getaddrinfo returns tuples (family, ...). Use ipaddress.ip_address(ip) on the sockaddr.\n  - RedirectHandler: subclass HTTPRedirectHandler.redirect_request → validate target host before following; raise on private.\n  - Request headers: UA, Accept, Accept-Language, Accept-Encoding: gzip (and handle); urllib adds Host/Connection.\n  - read loop chunks with cancel check; enforce max_bytes.\n  - Content-Encoding gzip → gzip.decompress; deflate → zlib.\n  \n- decode_body(body, content_type) -> str: charset from Content-Type `charset=`, else scan first 2048 bytes for <meta charset=\"...\">/<meta http-equiv content charset, else try utf-8 then gbk? fallback: utf-8 errors=\"replace\" (plus attempt locale-independent detection utf-16 BOMs).\n\n- _strip_tags(s) via HTMLParser-based _TextExtractor reused for RSS snippets? RSS snippet: use re.sub(r\"<[^>]+>\", \" \", s) + html.unescape + collapse whitespace. Fine (small trusted-ish input).\n\n- class _TextExtractor(HTMLParser): \n  - SKIP = {\"script\",\"style\",\"noscript\",\"template\",\"svg\",\"head\",\"iframe\",\"object\"}\n  - on starttag: if tag in BLOCKS: emit \"\\n\" (but not inside skip); if tag==\"title\": capturing=True (handle in handle_data? title is inside head which we skip — capture title separately: treat \"title\" specially: set self._in_title, collect data into self.title)\n  - handle_data: if in_title → title += data; elif skip_depth>0 → ignore; else buffer.append(data)\n  - endtag: close skip tracking; block tags → \"\\n\"\n  - compact(): split lines, rstrip each, drop empties, collapse internal runs of spaces (data may include \"\\n\" from source: treat all whitespace runs as space within a line? Simpler: treat emitted data as-is, then post-process: replace \\xa0 with space, collapse 3+ newlines, collapse multiple spaces.)\n  - Blocks: p, div, li, tr, h1..h6, br, section, article, header, footer, table, ul, ol, pre, blockquote, form, hr.\n  - Entity handling: HTMLParser with convert_charrefs=True (default) handles it.\n\n- Backends:\n  - _tavily(query, limit, cfg, http): POST json {\"query\":..., \"max_results\":...} headers Authorization: Bearer key, Content-Type json → resp[\"results\"] → title/url/content.\n  - _searxng: GET {base}/search?q=&format=json&language=auto → resp[\"results\"] title/url/content.\n  - _bing: GET bing/search?q=&format=rss&count=&mkt=zh-CN... careful: earlier redirect mangled UTF-8 → the request must go with url-encoded UTF-8 quote(query) which urllib does correctly (ASCII command line isn't involved — this is in-process Python). Note the RSS response had <item><title/><link/><description/>. Namespace none. Parse with ET.fromstring, iter \"item\".\n  - _ddg: GET html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q= ; parse with HTMLParser-based link extractor: anchors class result__a → href (uddg= param urldecode), text; snippet in <a class=\"result__snippet\"> data. Implement _DdgParser(HTMLParser) collecting (href,title) pairs and snippets; then zip.\n  \n- BACKENDS = {\"tavily\": _tavily, \"searxng\": _searxng, \"bing\": _bing, \"ddg\": _ddg}; DEFAULT_CHAIN = (\"tavily\", \"searxng\", \"bing\", \"ddg\"); availability check: tavily needs cfg.tavily_api_key; searxng needs cfg.searxng_url. Chain computed at runtime: [b for b in DEFAULT_CHAIN if available] or raise. If backend param given: just that one (error if unavailable).\n\n- web_search(ws, cfg, query, max_results=None, backend=\"\") -> dict:\n  - query strip; empty → error\n  - limit = min(max(cfg.web_search_max_results, 1), 20) unless param 1..20\n  - errors: list per backend \"name: reason\" (truncate each reason to ~120 chars)\n  - success format:\n    header: f\"{n} results for {query!r} (via {used})\"\n    entries: f\"{i}. {title}\\n   {url}\\n   {snippet}\"\n  - all failed → {\"content\": \"ERROR: all search backends failed\\n- bing: ...\", \"error\": True}\n\n- web_fetch(ws, cfg, url, max_chars=None, start=0):\n  - url strip; scheme check; private-IP guard (inside _http_get)\n  - html → extractor: output f\"{title}\\n\\n{text}\" windowed: start char offset, max_chars default cfg.read_max_chars cap; note \"(N more chars; pass start=...)\" tail hint when truncated? read_file uses offset/limit lines; here: \"start\" param name (0-based char offset; description clarifies). Add tail note: f\"... [{remaining} chars truncated; fetch again with start={next_start}]\".\n  - non-text content types (image/binary) → error \"unsupported content-type\".\n  - text/plain or json etc → raw body windowed similarly.\n  - cancel respected via _http_get chunks.\n\n- http_get signature includes `http` injection? Tests inject at module level by monkeypatching `websearch._http_get`? For backend tests, simpler: each backend takes `get` callable param. web_search passes _http_get-bound partial. Let me design backends as functions f(query, limit, cfg, ctx) where ctx is a small dataclass with `get(url, **kw) -> HttpResponse` and cancel/timeout baked. Hmm — simpler: backends take (query, limit, cfg, get) where get = functools.partial(_http_get, timeout=..., cancel=...). Tests pass a fake `get(url) -> FakeResponse(final_url, content_type, body_bytes)`. web_search builds real get once. Clean.\n\nRegistry func signature: lambda sb, cfg, **kw: websearch.web_search(sb, cfg, **kw). Registry adds cancel only if declared; add cancel param to both web tools (they poll between chunks): func=lambda sb, cfg, cancel=None, **kw: websearch.web_search(sb, cfg, cancel=cancel, **kw) — declares cancel → cancelable. Good (long fetches stoppable).\n\nConfig additions with env defaults:\n```python\n# Web access (tools/websearch.py): keyless out of the box (Bing RSS -> DDG),\n# optional better backends via env\nweb_search_timeout: float = 15.0\nweb_search_max_results: int = 8\ntavily_api_key: str | None = field(default_factory=lambda: os.environ.get(\"CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY\") or os.environ.get(\"TAVILY_API_KEY\"))\nsearxng_url: str = field(default_factory=lambda: (os.environ.get(\"CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL\") or os.environ.get(\"SEARXNG_URL\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\"))\n```\n\nPrompts (English, matching existing style):\nweb_search.md:\n\"Search the web and return ranked results (title, URL, snippet). Use it for facts the workspace cannot answer: current events, library versions, release notes, error messages, docs lookup. Then use web_fetch on a promising URL for the full page. query is the search string (engine syntax like quoted phrases and site: filters work); max_results caps entries (default $max). Backends try in order: tavily (needs CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY), searxng (needs CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL), bing RSS, duckduckgo — the first that returns results wins; when all fail the error lists each backend's reason. Short factual queries beat long sentences.\"\n\nweb_fetch.md:\n\"Fetch a web page by URL and return its readable text (title + body; navigation/scripts stripped). Works for HTML pages and raw text/JSON responses; binary types are rejected. max_chars caps the returned text (default $max) and start skips ahead in characters — a tail note gives the next start value when content was truncated. Non-public hosts (localhost, LAN IPs) are refused. Pair with web_search: search first, then fetch the 1-2 most relevant URLs rather than many.\"\n\nNow the module itself — write carefully, stdlib only. Let me also check agent/tools/__init__.py content quickly (probably empty) — skip, imports in registry are `from . import filesystem, shell` so I add `websearch` there similarly.\n\nPotential pitfall: `http.client` / urllib on Windows with cancel between chunks — fine.\n\ngetaddrinfo blocking + timeout: resolution itself can hang; socket.setdefaulttimeout not needed since urlopen(timeout=) covers connect (it applies to socket including DNS? DNS via getaddrinfo is not covered by socket timeout — acceptable; typical resolvers return fast; note in docstring).\n\nIP guard details:\n```python\ndef _assert_public_host(url: str) -> None:\n    host = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).hostname\n    if not host: raise WebError(f\"URL has no host: {url!r}\")\n    if host in (\"localhost\",) or host.endswith(\".localhost\") or host.endswith(\".local\") or host.endswith(\".internal\"):\n        raise ...\n    infos = socket.getaddrinfo(host, None)\n    for info in infos:\n        ip = ipaddress.ip_address(info[4][0])\n        if not ip.is_global: raise WebError(f\"non-public host refused: {host} ({ip})\")\n```\nis_global excludes private/loopback/link-local/reserved? `is_global` is True only for public addresses (it checks against the not-global networks incl. 100.64/10 CGNAT, 192.0.0/24, etc.). Also reject IPv4-mapped IPv6 (::ffff:127.0.0.1) — ipaddress normalizes IPv6 mapped → .ipv4_mapped; is_global on ::ffff:127.0.0.1 is False (it's considered via mapped?). In Python, ip_address('::ffff:127.0.0.1').is_global → False (since it has .ipv4_mapped set and properties consider it). Good. Also 0.0.0.0 is_global False. And redirect guard: HTTPRedirectHandler override:\n\n```python\nclass _SafeRedirects(HTTPRedirectHandler):\n    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):\n        _assert_public_host(newurl)\n        return super().redirect_request(req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl)\n```\n\nDocker Hub-style DNS pinning (TOCTOU: resolve-check then connect resolves again) — true mitigation needs pinning the IP in the connection; overkill here (work mode has full shell anyway; chat mode promise is about workspace). Docstring note it's a guard, not a sandbox.\n\nBing RSS parse:\n```python\ndef _bing(query, limit, cfg, get):\n    q = urllib.parse.urlencode({\"q\": query, \"format\": \"rss\", \"count\": str(min(limit*2, 30))})\n    resp = get(f\"https://www.bing.com/search?{q}\", accept=\"application/rss+xml, application/xml\")\n    root = ET.fromstring(resp.body)\n    out = []\n    for item in root.iter(\"item\"):\n        title = (item.findtext(\"title\") or \"\").strip()\n        link = (item.findtext(\"link\") or \"\").strip()\n        desc = _clean_snippet(item.findtext(\"description\") or \"\")\n        if title and link: out.append({\"title\": title, \"url\": link, \"snippet\": desc})\n        if len(out) >= limit: break\n    if not out: raise BackendError(\"no items in RSS (blocked or no results)\")\n    return out\n```\nNote: earlier live response: items had title/link/description — confirmed shape.\n\nDDG parse: html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q=... Form POST also exists; GET works normally. Parser:\n```python\nclass _DdgParser(HTMLParser):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)\n        self.results = []\n        self._mode = None  # \"title\" | \"snippet\"\n        self._buf = []\n        self._pending = None\n    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\n        a = dict(attrs)\n        cls = a.get(\"class\", \"\")\n        if tag == \"a\":\n            href = a.get(\"href\", \"\")\n            if \"result__a\" in cls:\n                uddg = urllib.parse.parse_qs(urllib.parse.urlsplit(href).query).get(\"uddg\")\n                url = urllib.parse.unquote(uddg[0]) if uddg else href\n                self._pending = {\"url\": url, \"title\": \"\", \"snippet\": \"\"}\n                self._mode, self._buf = \"title\", []\n        elif tag == \"a\" and \"result__snippet\" in cls:  # unreachable (tag==a checked above) \n```\nCareful: result__snippet is also an <a>. Restructure:\n```python\nif tag == \"a\":\n    cls = a.get(\"class\", \"\")\n    href = a.get(\"href\", \"\")\n    if \"result__a\" in cls:\n        flush pending? (snippet may come after title; title then snippet) -> append pending when new title starts if it has title\n        ...\n        self._mode = \"title\"; self._buf = []\n    elif \"result__snippet\" in cls and self._pending is not None... \n```\nActually snippets appear before the title in DDG markup? In html.duckduckgo.com, each result: <h2><a class=\"result__a\">title</a></h2> then <a class=\"result__snippet\">snippet</a>. Title first, then snippet. So pending starts at result__a; mode=title; on its endtag → save title, mode=None; at result__snippet start → mode=snippet; endtag → snippet=buf, append pending to results, pending=None.\nhandle_endtag: if tag==\"a\" and mode in (\"title\",\"snippet\"): commit.\nSimplify with a generic approach; tests use canned fixture.\n\nTavily:\n```python\ndef _tavily(query, limit, cfg, get):\n    body = json.dumps({\"query\": query, \"max_results\": limit, \"search_depth\": \"basic\"}).encode()\n    resp = get(\"https://api.tavily.com/search\", method=\"POST\", content_type=\"application/json\", body=body, authorization=f\"Bearer {cfg.tavily_api_key}\")\n    data = json.loads(resp.body)\n    out = [{\"title\": r.get(\"title\",\"\"), \"url\": r.get(\"url\",\"\"), \"snippet\": (r.get(\"content\") or \"\").strip()} for r in data.get(\"results\", [])]\n```\nget() signature grows: _http_get(url, *, method=\"GET\", body=None, headers=None, timeout, cancel, max_bytes). Keep headers dict.\n\nSearXNG:\n```python\nbase = cfg.searxng_url.rstrip(\"/\")\nresp = get(f\"{base}/search?{urlencode({'q': query, 'format': 'json'})}\", headers={\"Accept\": \"application/json\"})\ndata = json.loads(resp.body); results → title/url/content\n```\n\nResponse container: small dataclass HttpResp(url, status, content_type, body: bytes).\n\n_http_get returns HttpResp; raises WebError(reason) with short messages; timeout → WebError(\"timeout after Xs\"); HTTPError → WebError(f\"HTTP {code}\"); URLError → WebError(str(reason)).\n\nCancel: check before request, between chunks; if set → WebError(\"aborted\")? loop.py treats ToolResult error normally; Stop kills run — run_command returns command_aborted error. For web: raise WebError(\"aborted by user\") and catch → error content. Fine.\n\nNow truncation helper for fetch:\n```python\ndef _window(text, start, limit) -> tuple[str, int|None]:  # returns (chunk, next_start)\n```\n\nLet me now write all files. Order:\n1. agent/config.py edit\n2. agent/tools/websearch.py new\n3. agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md + web_fetch.md new\n4. agent/tools/registry.py edit (import + two Tool adds)\n5. tests/websearch_test.py new\n6. run tests (+ live run)\n7. README edit\n\nCheck agent/tools/__init__.py quickly? registry does `from . import filesystem, shell` — I'll extend to `..., websearch`. __init__ contents irrelevant.\n\nWrite config edit first."}
