{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789619631.2972033, "id": "bd669d9fbb37", "tool_call_id": "call_18a740aad6704728be2a744a", "content": "81:         return self._streams.pop(0)()\n82: \n83: \n84: def _client(max_retries: int, streams):\n85:     c = OpenaiLlmClient(\n86:         api_key=\"sk-test\",\n87:         base_url=\"http://localhost/v1\",\n88:         model=\"test-model\",\n89:         max_retries=max_retries,\n90:     )\n91:     comps = _FakeCompletions(streams)\n92:     c.client = SimpleNamespace(chat=SimpleNamespace(completions=comps))\n93:     return c, comps\n94: \n95: \n96: def _collect(gen):\n97:     \"\"\"Drain a stream generator: (events, error-or-None).\"\"\"\n98:     out = []\n99:     error = None\n100:     try:\n101:         for ev in gen:\n102:             out.append(ev)\n103:     except LlmError as e:\n104:         error = e\n105:     return out, error\n106: \n107: \n108: def main() -> int:\n109:     oc_mod.time = SimpleNamespace(sleep=lambda _s: None)\n110:     retryable_status = frozenset({429, 500, 502, 503, 504})\n111: \n112:     # 1. classify: raw httpx2 transport errors -> retryable structured codes\n113:     err = LlmError.classify(httpx2.ReadTimeout(\"timed out\"), retryable_status)\n114:     check(err.code == \"timeout\" and err.retryable, \"read timeout -> retryable timeout\")\n115:     check(err.message == \"Request timed out.\", \"read timeout -> clean message\")\n116:     err = LlmError.classify(httpx2.ConnectError(\"refused\"), retryable_status)\n117:     check(err.code == \"connection\" and err.retryable, \"connect error -> retryable connection\")\n118:     err = LlmError.classify(httpx2.ReadError(\"reset\"), retryable_status)\n119:     check(err.code == \"connection\" and err.retryable, \"read error -> retryable connection\")\n120:     err = LlmError.classify(RuntimeError(\"boom\"), retryable_status)\n121:     check(err.code == \"unknown\" and not err.retryable, \"unexpected error stays non-retryable\")\n122:     check(err.message == \"boom\", \"unexpected error keeps its message (LlmError.__str__ is empty)\")\n123: \n124:     # 2. pre-token failure retries transparently, announcing the attempt\n125:     client, comps = _client(3, [_fail_stream, _ok_stream])\n126:     evs, err = _collect(client.stream([{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]))\n127:     check(err is None, \"transient pre-token failure recovers after one retry\")\n128:     types = [e[\"type\"] for e in evs]\n129:     check(types == [\"retry\", \"text\", \"finish\"], \"retry notice precedes the recovered stream\")\n130:     check(evs[0][\"attempt\"] == 1 and evs[0][\"max\"] == 3, \"retry notice carries attempt/max\")\n131:     check(\"retrying (1/3)\" in evs[0][\"message\"], \"retry notice message names the attempt\")\n132:     check(comps.calls == 2, \"exactly two requests were issued\")\n133:     check([e[\"delta\"] for e in evs if e[\"type\"] == \"text\"] == [\"hi\"], \"no duplicated partial text\")\n134: \n135:     # 3. every attempt failing surfaces a clear, attempt-aware timeout\n136:     client, comps = _client(2, [_fail_stream, _fail_stream])\n137:     evs, err = _collect(client.stream([{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]))\n138:     check([e[\"type\"] for e in evs] == [\"retry\"], \"one retry notice before exhaustion\")\n139:     check(evs[0][\"attempt\"] == 1 and evs[0][\"max\"] == 2, \"retry notice counts down the budget\")\n140:     check(err is not None and err.code == \"timeout\" and err.retryable, \"exhaustion raises retryable timeout\")\n141:     check(\"after 2 attempts\" in err.message, \"exhaustion message states the attempt count\")\n142:     check(comps.calls == 2, \"no extra request after exhaustion\")\n143: \n144:     # 4. a failure AFTER content was delivered raises immediately: restarting\n145:     #    from scratch would re-emit \"partial\" and duplicate it in the transcript\n146:     client, comps = _client(3, [_partial_then_fail])\n147:     evs, err = _collect(client.stream([{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]))\n148:     check([e[\"type\"] for e in evs] == [\"text\"], \"partial token streamed before the failure\")\n149:     check(evs[0][\"delta\"] == \"partial\", \"partial content was delivered once\")\n150:     check(err is not None and err.code == \"timeout\", \"mid-stream failure raises instead of duplicating\")\n151:     check(comps.calls == 1, \"no retry request after partial delivery\")\n152: \n153:     print(\"\\nall passed\")\n154:     return 0\n155: \n156: \n157: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n158:     sys.exit(main())", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789619663.0289419, "id": "45080a7a19b7", "content": "测试断言了超时消息文案，改动时要同步更新。先确认 httpx2 顶层的超时异常类型名，然后动手：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_3f00aa7a5644442daa6fa47f", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"Timeout\\\" .venv/Lib/site-packages/httpx2/__init__.py | head\"}"}], "reasoning": "Now I have the full picture. Note test line 115: `check(err.message == \"Request timed out.\", ...)` — my classify change will alter messages, so update that assertion.\n\nDiagnosis is complete. Root cause:\n\n**问题根源**: `openai_client.py:31` — `httpx2.Client(..., timeout=60)` 一个浮点数把 connect/read/write/pool 全部设为 60s。对流式 SSE 响应，read 超时指的是「两个数据块之间的最大间隔」。只要模型/API 60 秒没有吐出任何字节——供应商过载停顿、中转站缓存整段响应最后才 flush（长回复必超时）、或 GFW 对长连接限流——就抛 ReadTimeout → \"Request timed out.\"。网络\"好\"（短请求秒回）完全不影响这个场景。重试 3 次每次又等 60s，观感就是频繁超时。\n\n**修复**:\n1. 拆分超时预算: connect=min(15, request_timeout)（死路由快速失败），read=新的 llm_read_timeout(240s 默认)（容忍长间隔），write/pool=request_timeout。\n2. classify 给出阶段化消息，让 UI 上的错误自己解释自己。\n\nEdits:\n\n1. config.py — add after llm_request_timeout line:\n```python\n    llm_request_timeout: float = 60.0\n    # Streaming read budget: httpx read timeout is per CHUNK GAP, not total, so\n    # one float (request_timeout) used to cap gaps at 60s — a provider stall or\n    # a buffering relay that flushes long replies only at the end then reads as\n    # \"request timed out\" despite a healthy network. Connect stays tight\n    # (fail fast on dead routes); reads get their own, generous budget.\n    llm_read_timeout: float = 240.0\n```\n\n2. openai_client.py __init__:\n```python\n        self.request_timeout = request_timeout\n        self.read_timeout = read_timeout\n        ...\n        # split budgets: connect fails fast (dead route), read tolerates long\n        # chunk gaps (streaming stall / buffering relay) — see Config.llm_read_timeout\n        timeout = httpx2.Timeout(\n            self.request_timeout, connect=min(15.0, self.request_timeout), read=self.read_timeout\n        )\n        proxy = get_proxy_for_url(base_url)\n        http_client = httpx2.Client(proxy=proxy, trust_env=False, timeout=timeout)\n        self.client = OpenAI(api_key=self.api_key, base_url=base_url, http_client=http_client)\n```\nSignature add read_timeout: float = 240.0.\n\n3. client.py classify:\n```python\n        if isinstance(e, httpx2.TimeoutException):\n            if isinstance(e, httpx2.ConnectTimeout):\n                return LlmError(code=\"timeout\", retryable=True, message=\"Connect timed out: no route to the API endpoint (network to the provider, a proxy, or the base_url).\")\n            if isinstance(e, httpx2.PoolTimeout):\n                return LlmError(code=\"timeout\", retryable=True, message=\"Timed out waiting for a connection slot.\")\n            return LlmError(code=\"timeout\", retryable=True, message=\"Read timed out: the API sent no data for a long stretch (provider stall or a buffering relay).\")\n```\nDoes httpx2 expose ConnectTimeout/PoolTimeout at top level? httpx does (httpx.ConnectTimeout...). httpx2 — check: .venv/Lib/site-packages/httpx2/__init__.py exports. Verify via grep quickly.\n\nAlso keep openai.APITimeoutError branch before (SDK-wrapped, message \"Request timed out.\" verbatim from SDK — fine).\n\n4. factory.py: `read_timeout=kwargs.pop(\"read_timeout\", 240.0),`\n\n5. base.py _build_llm: add `read_timeout=cfg.llm_read_timeout,`\n\n6. tests/llm_client_test.py: update message assertions + add new checks:\n- line 113-115: ReadTimeout message now \"Read timed out: ...\" → update.\n- add: ConnectTimeout → connect message; PoolTimeout → pool message.\n- add: client construction uses split budgets? Constructing OpenaiLlmClient builds a REAL httpx2.Client (needs no network) — can inspect c.client._client.timeout? In _client() they replace c.client with fake AFTER construction; construction itself does httpx2.Client(...) + OpenAI(...) — OpenAI() with custom client validates httpx2 client — fine offline (no network at construction). Check timeout: `c._raw_timeout`? I'll expose `self.timeout = timeout` on the client instance for testability: check(oc.timeout.connect == 15.0 and oc.timeout.read == 240.0). httpx2.Timeout attributes: .connect .read .write .pool exist. Test in section 1.5:\n```python\n    c = OpenaiLlmClient(api_key=\"k\", base_url=\"http://localhost/v1\", model=\"m\")\n    check(c.timeout.connect == 15.0 and c.timeout.read == 240.0 and c.timeout.write == 60.0, \"timeout budgets split: tight connect, generous read\")\n```\n\nCheck httpx2 exports first. Then run tests/llm_client_test.py.\n\nAfter that: websearch module etc. (the still-pending feature), then README, memory. Given turn size, prioritize: timeout fix + tests green → websearch implementation → tests → README → summary. Let me move fast."}
