{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789621090.534358, "id": "1fd5aa993ab7", "tool_call_id": "call_b310ca499f7349938885eb21", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\nagent/prompts/system.md:57: - A bare unquoted subgraph title is a lexical error: `subgraph 中文标题` fails.\r\nagent/prompts/system.md:58: Always use an id plus a quoted title: `subgraph inner[\"中文标题\"]`.\r\n---\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789621203.2445846, "id": "4134d940c757", "content": "库里的 agent 面向文案全部是英文（唯一中文是 system.md 里 mermaid 的 CJK 示例标签，属有意为之）；测试 diff 里的「孵化」只是 UTF-8 解码夹具字节，不是提示。如果界面某处还看到中文提示，指给我，我马上改。\n\n现在继续写 websearch.py——按承诺**分四段小步写入**，每段一次 stream 短，避开长流被 RST 的问题。第 1 段（模块骨架 + HTTP 核心）：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_e9dfc85d603749038a4b735a", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Web access tools: web_search (multi-backend search) + web_fetch (page -> text).\\n\\nBuilt on the stdlib only (urllib + html.parser + ElementTree) — the LLM loop is\\nhand-rolled here, and so is web access: no scraping SDK that rots when an\\nengine tweaks its markup. Backends, tried in order, first success wins:\\n\\n  tavily   LLM-first search API, best quality   (CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY)\\n  searxng  self-hosted metasearch, JSON API     (CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL)\\n  bing     the undocumented RSS endpoint of cn.bing.com — keyless, CN-friendly\\n  ddg      duckduckgo html endpoint — keyless\\n\\nPoka-yoke (make it hard for the model to misuse):\\n- timeout: every request is bounded (Config.web_search_timeout); Stop is\\n  honored between chunks so a hung fetch never outlives the user's patience\\n- size cap: responses larger than max_bytes are rejected, not swallowed\\n- private-network guard: web_fetch refuses loopback/LAN hosts (and follows\\n  redirects only to public hosts) — a GET into the agent's own API or the\\n  LAN stays impossible even when the model is talked into trying\\n- error-as-data: backend failures list each reason; a truncating fetch says\\n  how to fetch the next slice, mirroring read_file's offset hints\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport functools\\nimport gzip\\nimport ipaddress\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nimport socket\\nimport urllib.error\\nimport urllib.parse\\nimport urllib.request\\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\\nimport zlib\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\\nfrom typing import Any, Callable\\n\\nfrom ..config import Config\\nfrom .workspace import Workspace\\n\\n# browser-shaped but honest about the product; several CDNs 403 blank UAs\\nUSER_AGENT = (\\n    \\\"Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) \\\"\\n    \\\"Chrome/124.0 Safari/537.36 ClutchAgent/0.1\\\"\\n)\\n\\n_MAX_BYTES = 2_000_000  # hard cap per response: pages are for reading, not hoarding\\n\\n\\nclass WebError(Exception):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A request-level failure (DNS, timeout, size cap, private host).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass BackendError(Exception):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A backend responded but yielded nothing usable (blocked, layout changed).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass HttpResp:\\n    url: str  # final URL after redirects\\n    content_type: str\\n    body: bytes\\n\\n\\n# ---- HTTP core -------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n\\ndef _assert_public_host(url: str) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Refuse non-public destinations: loopback, LAN, link-local, reserved.\\n\\n    Guards web_fetch against being pointed at the agent's own HTTP API or the\\n    surrounding network. Resolve-then-connect leaves a (narrow) DNS-rebinding\\n    race; this is a guard against honest mistakes, not a sandbox — work mode\\n    already has full shell access.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    host = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).hostname\\n    if not host:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"URL has no host: {url!r}\\\")\\n    if host == \\\"localhost\\\" or host.endswith((\\\".localhost\\\", \\\".local\\\", \\\".internal\\\")):\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"non-public host refused: {host}\\\")\\n    try:\\n        infos = socket.getaddrinfo(host, None)\\n    except OSError as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"cannot resolve host {host!r}: {e}\\\") from e\\n    for info in infos:\\n        ip = ipaddress.ip_address(info[4][0])\\n        if not ip.is_global:\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"non-public host refused: {host} ({ip})\\\")\\n\\n\\nclass _SafeRedirects(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Redirects pass through the same public-host check as the first hop.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):\\n        _assert_public_host(newurl)\\n        return super().redirect_request(req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl)\\n\\n\\ndef _drain(resp: Any, cancel: Any, max_bytes: int) -> bytes:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read the body in chunks, honoring Stop between chunks.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    chunks: list[bytes] = []\\n    total = 0\\n    while True:\\n        if cancel is not None and cancel.is_set():\\n            raise WebError(\\\"aborted by user\\\")\\n        block = resp.read(65_536)\\n        if not block:\\n            break\\n        total += len(block)\\n        if total > max_bytes:\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"response exceeds {max_bytes} bytes\\\")\\n        chunks.append(block)\\n    return b\\\"\\\".join(chunks)\\n\\n\\ndef _http_get(\\n    url: str,\\n    timeout: float = 15.0,\\n    cancel: Any = None,\\n    method: str = \\\"GET\\\",\\n    body: bytes | None = None,\\n    headers: dict[str, str] | None = None,\\n    max_bytes: int = _MAX_BYTES,\\n) -> HttpResp:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One bounded HTTP request. Raises WebError with a short, model-readable\\n    reason; every caller turns that into error-as-data.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if cancel is not None and cancel.is_set():\\n        raise WebError(\\\"aborted by user\\\")\\n    scheme = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).scheme.lower()\\n    if scheme not in (\\\"http\\\", \\\"https\\\"):\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"unsupported URL scheme {scheme!r} (http/https only)\\\")\\n    _assert_public_host(url)\\n    req_headers = {\\n        \\\"User-Agent\\\": USER_AGENT,\\n        \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"*/*\\\",\\n        \\\"Accept-Language\\\": \\\"zh-CN,zh;q=0.9,en;q=0.8\\\",\\n        \\\"Accept-Encoding\\\": \\\"gzip\\\",\\n    }\\n    if headers:\\n        req_headers.update(headers)\\n    request = urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=req_headers, method=method)\\n    try:\\n        resp = urllib.request.build_opener(_SafeRedirects()).open(request, timeout=timeout)\\n    except WebError:\\n        raise\\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}\\\") from e\\n    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\\n        reason = getattr(e, \\\"reason\\\", e)\\n        if isinstance(reason, (socket.timeout, TimeoutError)):\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"timed out after {timeout:.0f}s\\\") from e\\n        raise WebError(str(reason) or \\\"request failed\\\") from e\\n    except (ValueError, OSError) as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"request failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n    with resp:\\n        raw = _drain(resp, cancel, max_bytes)\\n    if resp.headers.get(\\\"Content-Encoding\\\", \\\"\\\").lower() == \\\"gzip\\\":\\n        try:\\n            raw = gzip.decompress(raw)\\n        except OSError as e:\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"malformed gzip body from {url}\\\") from e\\n    elif resp.headers.get(\\\"Content-Encoding\\\", \\\"\\\").lower() == \\\"deflate\\\":\\n        try:\\n            raw = zlib.decompress(raw)\\n        except zlib.error:\\n            raw = zlib.decompress(raw, -zlib.MAX_WBITS)  # raw-deflate variant\\n    return HttpResp(url=resp.geturl(), content_type=resp.headers.get(\\\"Content-Type\\\", \\\"\\\"), body=raw)\\n\\n\\n_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\\\"charset=[\\\\\\\"']?([\\\\w\\\\-:+.]+)\\\", re.I)\\n_META_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\\\"<meta[^>]+charset=[\\\\\\\"']?([\\\\w\\\\-:+.]+)\\\", re.I)\\n\\n\\ndef _decode_body(raw: bytes, content_type: str) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Bytes -> text: header charset, then a meta sniff, then utf-8, then\\n    latin-1 (which never fails, so decoding cannot raise).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    m = _CHARSET_RE.search(content_type or \\\"\\\")\\n    charset = m.group(1) if m else None\\n    if not charset:\\n        m = _META_CHARSET_RE.search(raw[:4096].decode(\\\"ascii\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\"))\\n        charset = m.group(1) if m else None\\n    if charset:\\n        try:\\n            return raw.decode(charset, errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        except (LookupError, ValueError):\\n            pass  # unknown charset name: fall through to BOM/utf-8\\n    for bom, enc in ((b\\\"\\\\xff\\\\xfe\\\", \\\"utf-16-le\\\"), (b\\\"\\\\xfe\\\\xff\\\", \\\"utf-16-be\\\")):\\n        if raw.startswith(bom):\\n            return raw.decode(enc, errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n    try:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"latin-1\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n\"}"}], "reasoning": "Interesting — the ONLY Chinese in agent-facing text is in system.md, which is quoting CJK examples in the mermaid rules (legitimately needed as examples of CJK labels). And NO Python file under agent/ contains Chinese. So my committed/uncommitted changes contain no Chinese agent-facing messages.\n\nWait — then what \"提示\" was the user complaining about?? Let me re-read their message: \"另外你的修改也不合理，本项目的所有文字都是英文，这里的提示不应该使用中文。\" — \"这里的提示\" (the hint HERE). Combined with the first part about connection interrupts while writing \"this py file\"... Hmm, maybe the complaint targets MY CONVERSATION-LEVEL output — i.e., in the Clutch chat UI, my replies/summaries have been in Chinese, and the user is pointing out that the PROJECT's texts (tool descriptions, error hints that get rendered in the UI) are all English, so the hint I ADDED shouldn't be Chinese...\n\nOR — crucially — maybe they mean the system prompt/tool description text in THIS environment I'm running in (the system prompt at the top of this conversation): look at my run_command tool result earlier: \"CHAT MODE: this command was rejected because it is not provably read-only — it may modify the workspace or system state (write: segment 'sed' is a write operation).\" That's English. But the error the user saw: \"[WinError 10054] 远程主机强迫关闭了一个现有的连接\" is Windows' own localized (Chinese) error text — not something I wrote.\n\nHold on — maybe the \"提示\" refers to the chat-mode read-only rejection message or read_only_command.md error template. Let me check errors/read_only_command.md content — it's model-facing. It says per shell.py: render(\"errors/read_only_command.md\", verdict=..., detail=..., command=...). Let me read it. If IT contains Chinese (\"该命令可能修改工作区\"...), that would be \"这里的提示\". But my CJK scan of all agent/prompts/*.md found ONLY system.md lines 57-58. So read_only_command.md is English.\n\nSo... there is NO Chinese hint in the repo. Unless the complaint is about system.md's mermaid examples — \"subgraph 中文标题\" — that's an example label demonstrating CJK usage; legit.\n\nAlternative interpretation: the user is talking about THIS conversation's UI hints — when my write_file attempt got interrupted, the UI displayed something in Chinese? No...\n\nMost plausible: In an EARLIER compacted session, I probably added a Chinese hint somewhere and it was REVERTED/committed... Actually — wait. Check scratch files and the untracked tests/perm-args-test.js? Those are mine. Not hints.\n\nHmm, actually let me reconsider: maybe the user means the **config.py comment or the error messages I JUST added** in this session... all English though. Let me not over-index; the honest answer: I scanned everything; the only Chinese in agent-facing text is two mermaid example labels in system.md (intentional). If the user saw a Chinese hint somewhere specific, ask them to point at it, OR proactively check the UI (ui/ is full of Chinese strings — that's the project's UI language... wait is it? README is Chinese. ui/app.js — let me check if UI strings are Chinese).\n\nActually from the very first read of README: it's Chinese. And commit \"fix(ui): bundle Noto Sans SC — CJK prose no longer falls back to Microsoft YaHei\" — the UI deliberately supports CJK prose. So the project UI is bilingual-ish (Chinese product, English code text).\n\nGiven ambiguity, the right move: state plainly that I audited all my modifications + all agent-facing texts for Chinese: found none in my changes (only the UTF-8 test fixture bytes and two intentional mermaid examples in system.md), and ask them to point at the exact place if they saw one — while ALSO double-checking the two most likely spots (read_only_command.md and run_command_chat.md) by reading them right now to be thorough. Actually my scan already covered all .md. Enough.\n\nNow the second part: \"每次写这个py文件时都会这样\" — the WinError 10054 during big write_file. I committed to mitigating by chunked writes. Let me now actually write websearch.py — in SMALL pieces:\n\n1. write_file skeleton: module docstring + imports + WebError/HttpResp + small helpers (~120 lines) — moderate size.\n2. edit_file append: _http_get + drain + decode + SSRF guard.\n3. edit_file append: HTML text extractor + DDG parser.\n4. edit_file append: backends (tavily/searxng/bing/ddg).\n5. edit_file append: web_search + web_fetch entry points.\n\nEach edit adds ~60-90 lines — much smaller streams than one 400-line write. This also directly addresses their complaint pattern.\n\nThen prompts (2 small md files), registry wiring (one edit), tests (write in 2 chunks), run tests, README, memory, final summary.\n\nLet me also verify: config already has the web knobs (added earlier: web_search_timeout, web_search_max_results, tavily_api_key, searxng_url). Yes (+15 lines earlier).\n\nWrite piece 1 now. Design recap for the module:\n\n- docstring: purpose + poka-yoke bullets + backends + \"why stdlib\".\n- imports: functools, gzip, ipaddress, json, re, socket, threading?, urllib.parse, urllib.request, urllib.error, xml.etree.ElementTree, zlib, html.parser.HTMLParser, dataclasses.\n- WebError(Exception), _BackendError(Exception), HttpResp dataclass(url, content_type, body).\n- USER_AGENT.\n- _assert_public_host(url), _SafeRedirects.\n- _drain(resp, cancel, max_bytes), _http_get(...).\n- _decode_body(raw, content_type).\n- _clean_snippet(text).\n- _TextExtractor.\n- _window(text, start, limit).\n- _DdgParser.\n- backends _tavily, _searxng, _bing, _ddg.\n- _BACKENDS, _DEFAULT_CHAIN, _available(config).\n- _short(msg).\n- web_search(workspace, config, query, max_results=None, backend=\"\", cancel=None).\n- web_fetch(workspace, config, url, max_chars=None, start=0, cancel=None).\n\nPiece 1: through _decode_body. Piece 2: extractor+parser+window. Piece 3: backends+chain. Piece 4: entry points. ~4 chunks of 80-110 lines each.\n\nCareful about correctness details:\n\n- _http_get signature: (url, *, get timeout/cancel from caller via functools.partial) — I'll define full signature: _http_get(url, timeout, cancel=None, method=\"GET\", body=None, headers=None, max_bytes=2_000_000). Backends receive `get` = partial(_http_get, timeout=..., cancel=...).\n\n- gzip decompress errors → WebError(\"malformed gzip body\").\n\n- Deflate: some servers send raw deflate; handle zlib with wbits=-15 fallback: try zlib.decompress(raw) except: zlib.decompress(raw, -zlib.MAX_WBITS). Only when Content-Encoding deflate.\n\n- charset: content_type may be like \"text/html; charset=UTF-8\". meta sniff on first 4096 bytes ascii-ignore.\n\n- _decode_body utf-16 BOM: codecs.BOM_UTF16_LE/BE check before utf-8.\n\n- Bing RSS: ET.fromstring on bytes handles encoding declaration. findtext('title') etc. XML may have namespaces? Bing RSS items plain. Robust: iterate root.iter('item').\n\n- DDG html: anchors class result__a with href=/l/?uddg=<enc>; snippet anchor class result__snippet. Parser: track pending result; title from result__a; snippet from result__snippet; append on snippet end (or on next title if snippet missing).\n\nEdge: DDG now often returns a JS-check page for bots → 0 results → BackendError \"no results parsed (blocked or layout changed)\". Fine — chain continues to next... wait, ddg is LAST in chain. Fine.\n\n- _clean_snippet: strip tags → unescape → collapse whitespace to single spaces, strip. Cap 300 chars in web_search formatting.\n\n- web_search output format:\n```\n8 results for 'query' (via bing):\n\n1. Title\n   https://...\n   snippet text\n...\n```\n- dedupe by normalized url across the one backend's list.\n\n- failures list: f\"- {name}: {short}\" → error content \"ERROR: all search backends failed\\n\" + lines. Also when chain empty (can't happen — bing/ddg always available) — still handle.\n\n- backend param: unknown name → error \"unknown backend ... available: tavily (needs CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY), searxng (needs CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL), bing, ddg\". Available check: backend given but unavailable (tavily w/o key) → error naming the env var.\n\n- web_fetch:\n  - timeout: config.web_search_timeout (one knob).\n  - content-type binary check: startswith image/ video/ audio/ or in {application/pdf, application/zip, application/gzip, application/x-tar, application/octet-stream}.\n  - HTML detect: ctype contains \"html\" OR body starts with '<' after lstrip (and no ctype text/plain? if ctype is json/xml/text → raw). Order: if \"html\" in ctype → html; elif ctype startswith text/ or contains json/xml/javascript → text; else sniff '<'→html else text.\n  - window: start (0-based char), max_chars default config.read_max_chars; tail note: f\"\\n... [{remaining} chars truncated; fetch again with start={next}]\".\n  - title line: f\"# {title}\\n\\n\".\n  - empty text → \"(no extractable text on the page; it may be JS-rendered)\" as content (not error? make it error=False but note). I'll return as content with note.\n\n- registry: import websearch; append two Tools after run_command for BOTH modes (before skills/memories). Descriptions render from prompts with $max placeholders: render(\"tools/web_search.md\", max_results=config.web_search_max_results, timeout=config.web_search_timeout?) keep just max_results. cancel passthrough: func=lambda sb, cfg, cancel=None, **kw: websearch.web_search(sb, cfg, cancel=cancel, **kw).\n\n- prompts/tools/web_search.md & web_fetch.md — English, following grep.md style.\n\n- tests/websearch_test.py: no pytest; main() + check(); sections:\n  1. _clean_snippet.\n  2. _TextExtractor (script/style removal, title, block newlines).\n  3. _window truncation + next-start note? _window returns (chunk, next_start); test boundaries.\n  4. _DdgParser on canned fixture.\n  5. _bing on canned RSS fixture.\n  6. tavily/searxng parse with fake get.\n  7. chain fallback: fake get failing for first backend → second used; ordering of failures message when all fail.\n  8. _assert_public_host: localhost/private refused; public ok (use a non-resolving name? resolution in tests: getaddrinfo(\"localhost\") works offline; for private use \"127.0.0.1\"; for public use \"example.com\" — needs DNS... offline-safe: skip public positive test or use IP literal \"93.184.216.34\" (public IP literal → getaddrinfo on numeric IP needs no DNS). Use IP literals: \"127.0.0.1\" refused; \"8.8.8.8\" allowed (is_global True).\n  9. web_fetch binary rejection + SSRF refusal via fake get? web_fetch calls _http_get directly (real network) — for tests, monkeypatch websearch._http_get with stub (module attr swap like oc_mod.time pattern).\n 10. registry wiring: build_default_tools(Config(mode=\"chat\")).names() contains web_search & web_fetch; same for work mode; memory tools present.\n 11. --live flag: real Bing query + real fetch of a result — I'll run it here to verify end-to-end (bing works from this host).\n\nFor fake get signature: def fake_get(url, **kw) → HttpResp(...). _http_get called by web_search via functools.partial(_http_get, timeout=..., cancel=...) — for tests, patch websearch._http_get BEFORE calling web_search (partial binds whatever _http_get resolves at call time? functools.partial(websearch._http_get, ...) binds the FUNCTION OBJECT at partial creation — inside web_search I build `get = functools.partial(_http_get, ...)` referencing module global at call time — monkeypatching websearch._http_get replaces the global → web_search picks up the stub if I reference it as module-global `_http_get` inside web_search. Yes: within the module, `_http_get` name lookup happens at call time → patch works.\n\nNow write piece 1 (skeleton + errors + http core). Keep each write ≤ ~110 lines."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789621203.2445571, "id": "9369ad47ff5c", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Web access tools: web_search (multi-backend search) + web_fetch (page -> text).\\n\\nBuilt on the stdlib only (urllib + html.parser + ElementTree) — the LLM loop is\\nhand-rolled here, and so is web access: no scraping SDK that rots when an\\nengine tweaks its markup. Backends, tried in order, first success wins:\\n\\n  tavily   LLM-first search API, best quality   (CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY)\\n  searxng  self-hosted metasearch, JSON API     (CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL)\\n  bing     the undocumented RSS endpoint of cn.bing.com — keyless, CN-friendly\\n  ddg      duckduckgo html endpoint — keyless\\n\\nPoka-yoke (make it hard for the model to misuse):\\n- timeout: every request is bounded (Config.web_search_timeout); Stop is\\n  honored between chunks so a hung fetch never outlives the user's patience\\n- size cap: responses larger than max_bytes are rejected, not swallowed\\n- private-network guard: web_fetch refuses loopback/LAN hosts (and follows\\n  redirects only to public hosts) — a GET into the agent's own API or the\\n  LAN stays impossible even when the model is talked into trying\\n- error-as-data: backend failures list each reason; a truncating fetch says\\n  how to fetch the next slice, mirroring read_file's offset hints\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport functools\\nimport gzip\\nimport ipaddress\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nimport socket\\nimport urllib.error\\nimport urllib.parse\\nimport urllib.request\\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\\nimport zlib\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\\nfrom typing import Any, Callable\\n\\nfrom ..config import Config\\nfrom .workspace import Workspace\\n\\n# browser-shaped but honest about the product; several CDNs 403 blank UAs\\nUSER_AGENT = (\\n    \\\"Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) \\\"\\n    \\\"Chrome/124.0 Safari/537.36 ClutchAgent/0.1\\\"\\n)\\n\\n_MAX_BYTES = 2_000_000  # hard cap per response: pages are for reading, not hoarding\\n\\n\\nclass WebError(Exception):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A request-level failure (DNS, timeout, size cap, private host).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass BackendError(Exception):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A backend responded but yielded nothing usable (blocked, layout changed).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass HttpResp:\\n    url: str  # final URL after redirects\\n    content_type: str\\n    body: bytes\\n\\n\\n# ---- HTTP core -------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n\\ndef _assert_public_host(url: str) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Refuse non-public destinations: loopback, LAN, link-local, reserved.\\n\\n    Guards web_fetch against being pointed at the agent's own HTTP API or the\\n    surrounding network. Resolve-then-connect leaves a (narrow) DNS-rebinding\\n    race; this is a guard against honest mistakes, not a sandbox — work mode\\n    already has full shell access.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    host = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).hostname\\n    if not host:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"URL has no host: {url!r}\\\")\\n    if host == \\\"localhost\\\" or host.endswith((\\\".localhost\\\", \\\".local\\\", \\\".internal\\\")):\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"non-public host refused: {host}\\\")\\n    try:\\n        infos = socket.getaddrinfo(host, None)\\n    except OSError as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"cannot resolve host {host!r}: {e}\\\") from e\\n    for info in infos:\\n        ip = ipaddress.ip_address(info[4][0])\\n        if not ip.is_global:\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"non-public host refused: {host} ({ip})\\\")\\n\\n\\nclass _SafeRedirects(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Redirects pass through the same public-host check as the first hop.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):\\n        _assert_public_host(newurl)\\n        return super().redirect_request(req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl)\\n\\n\\ndef _drain(resp: Any, cancel: Any, max_bytes: int) -> bytes:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read the body in chunks, honoring Stop between chunks.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    chunks: list[bytes] = []\\n    total = 0\\n    while True:\\n        if cancel is not None and cancel.is_set():\\n            raise WebError(\\\"aborted by user\\\")\\n        block = resp.read(65_536)\\n        if not block:\\n            break\\n        total += len(block)\\n        if total > max_bytes:\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"response exceeds {max_bytes} bytes\\\")\\n        chunks.append(block)\\n    return b\\\"\\\".join(chunks)\\n\\n\\ndef _http_get(\\n    url: str,\\n    timeout: float = 15.0,\\n    cancel: Any = None,\\n    method: str = \\\"GET\\\",\\n    body: bytes | None = None,\\n    headers: dict[str, str] | None = None,\\n    max_bytes: int = _MAX_BYTES,\\n) -> HttpResp:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One bounded HTTP request. Raises WebError with a short, model-readable\\n    reason; every caller turns that into error-as-data.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if cancel is not None and cancel.is_set():\\n        raise WebError(\\\"aborted by user\\\")\\n    scheme = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).scheme.lower()\\n    if scheme not in (\\\"http\\\", \\\"https\\\"):\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"unsupported URL scheme {scheme!r} (http/https only)\\\")\\n    _assert_public_host(url)\\n    req_headers = {\\n        \\\"User-Agent\\\": USER_AGENT,\\n        \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"*/*\\\",\\n        \\\"Accept-Language\\\": \\\"zh-CN,zh;q=0.9,en;q=0.8\\\",\\n        \\\"Accept-Encoding\\\": \\\"gzip\\\",\\n    }\\n    if headers:\\n        req_headers.update(headers)\\n    request = urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=req_headers, method=method)\\n    try:\\n        resp = urllib.request.build_opener(_SafeRedirects()).open(request, timeout=timeout)\\n    except WebError:\\n        raise\\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}\\\") from e\\n    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\\n        reason = getattr(e, \\\"reason\\\", e)\\n        if isinstance(reason, (socket.timeout, TimeoutError)):\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"timed out after {timeout:.0f}s\\\") from e\\n        raise WebError(str(reason) or \\\"request failed\\\") from e\\n    except (ValueError, OSError) as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"request failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n    with resp:\\n        raw = _drain(resp, cancel, max_bytes)\\n    if resp.headers.get(\\\"Content-Encoding\\\", \\\"\\\").lower() == \\\"gzip\\\":\\n        try:\\n            raw = gzip.decompress(raw)\\n        except OSError as e:\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"malformed gzip body from {url}\\\") from e\\n    elif resp.headers.get(\\\"Content-Encoding\\\", \\\"\\\").lower() == \\\"deflate\\\":\\n        try:\\n            raw = zlib.decompress(raw)\\n        except zlib.error:\\n            raw = zlib.decompress(raw, -zlib.MAX_WBITS)  # raw-deflate variant\\n    return HttpResp(url=resp.geturl(), content_type=resp.headers.get(\\\"Content-Type\\\", \\\"\\\"), body=raw)\\n\\n\\n_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\\\"charset=[\\\\\\\"']?([\\\\w\\\\-:+.]+)\\\", re.I)\\n_META_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\\\"<meta[^>]+charset=[\\\\\\\"']?([\\\\w\\\\-:+.]+)\\\", re.I)\\n\\n\\ndef _decode_body(raw: bytes, content_type: str) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Bytes -> text: header charset, then a meta sniff, then utf-8, then\\n    latin-1 (which never fails, so decoding cannot raise).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    m = _CHARSET_RE.search(content_type or \\\"\\\")\\n    charset = m.group(1) if m else None\\n    if not charset:\\n        m = _META_CHARSET_RE.search(raw[:4096].decode(\\\"ascii\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\"))\\n        charset = m.group(1) if m else None\\n    if charset:\\n        try:\\n            return raw.decode(charset, errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        except (LookupError, ValueError):\\n            pass  # unknown charset name: fall through to BOM/utf-8\\n    for bom, enc in ((b\\\"\\\\xff\\\\xfe\\\", \\\"utf-16-le\\\"), (b\\\"\\\\xfe\\\\xff\\\", \\\"utf-16-be\\\")):\\n        if raw.startswith(bom):\\n            return raw.decode(enc, errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n    try:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"latin-1\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_e9dfc85d603749038a4b735a"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789621203.2606375, "id": "25fdb6924330", "tool_call_id": "call_e9dfc85d603749038a4b735a", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\agent\\tools\\websearch.py (7390 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/agent\\tools\\websearch.py\n+++ b/agent\\tools\\websearch.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,195 @@\n+\"\"\"Web access tools: web_search (multi-backend search) + web_fetch (page -> text).\n+\n+Built on the stdlib only (urllib + html.parser + ElementTree) — the LLM loop is\n+hand-rolled here, and so is web access: no scraping SDK that rots when an\n+engine tweaks its markup. Backends, tried in order, first success wins:\n+\n+  tavily   LLM-first search API, best quality   (CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY)\n+  searxng  self-hosted metasearch, JSON API     (CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL)\n+  bing     the undocumented RSS endpoint of cn.bing.com — keyless, CN-friendly\n+  ddg      duckduckgo html endpoint — keyless\n+\n+Poka-yoke (make it hard for the model to misuse):\n+- timeout: every request is bounded (Config.web_search_timeout); Stop is\n+  honored between chunks so a hung fetch never outlives the user's patience\n+- size cap: responses larger than max_bytes are rejected, not swallowed\n+- private-network guard: web_fetch refuses loopback/LAN hosts (and follows\n+  redirects only to public hosts) — a GET into the agent's own API or the\n+  LAN stays impossible even when the model is talked into trying\n+- error-as-data: backend failures list each reason; a truncating fetch says\n+  how to fetch the next slice, mirroring read_file's offset hints\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import functools\n+import gzip\n+import ipaddress\n+import json\n+import re\n+import socket\n+import urllib.error\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n+import zlib\n+from dataclasses import dataclass\n+from html.parser import HTMLParser\n+from typing import Any, Callable\n+\n+from ..config import Config\n+from .workspace import Workspace\n+\n+# browser-shaped but honest about the product; several CDNs 403 blank UAs\n+USER_AGENT = (\n+    \"Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) \"\n+    \"Chrome/124.0 Safari/537.36 ClutchAgent/0.1\"\n+)\n+\n+_MAX_BYTES = 2_000_000  # hard cap per response: pages are for reading, not hoarding\n+\n+\n+class WebError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"A request-level failure (DNS, timeout, size cap, private host).\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+class BackendError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"A backend responded but yielded nothing usable (blocked, layout changed).\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class HttpResp:\n+    url: str  # final URL after redirects\n+    content_type: str\n+    body: bytes\n+\n+\n+# ---- HTTP core -------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+def _assert_public_host(url: str) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Refuse non-public destinations: loopback, LAN, link-local, reserved.\n+\n+    Guards web_fetch against being pointed at the agent's own HTTP API or the\n+    surrounding network. Resolve-then-connect leaves a (narrow) DNS-rebinding\n+    race; this is a guard against honest mistakes, not a sandbox — work mode\n+    already has full shell access.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    host = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).hostname\n+    if not host:\n+        raise WebError(f\"URL has no host: {url!r}\")\n+    if host == \"localhost\" or host.endswith((\".localhost\", \".local\", \".internal\")):\n+        raise WebError(f\"non-public host refused: {host}\")\n+    try:\n+        infos = socket.getaddrinfo(host, None)\n+    except OSError as e:\n+        raise WebError(f\"cannot resolve host {host!r}: {e}\") from e\n+    for info in infos:\n+        ip = ipaddress.ip_address(info[4][0])\n+        if not ip.is_global:\n+            raise WebError(f\"non-public host refused: {host} ({ip})\")\n+\n+\n+class _SafeRedirects(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):\n+    \"\"\"Redirects pass through the same public-host check as the first hop.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):\n+        _assert_public_host(newurl)\n+        return super().redirect_request(req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl)\n+\n+\n+def _drain(resp: Any, cancel: Any, max_bytes: int) -> bytes:\n+    \"\"\"Read the body in chunks, honoring Stop between chunks.\"\"\"\n+    chunks: list[bytes] = []\n+    total = 0\n+    while True:\n+        if cancel is not None and cancel.is_set():\n+            raise WebError(\"aborted by user\")\n+        block = resp.read(65_536)\n+        if not block:\n+            break\n+        total += len(block)\n+        if total > max_bytes:\n+            raise WebError(f\"response exceeds {max_bytes} bytes\")\n+        chunks.append(block)\n+    return b\"\".join(chunks)\n+\n+\n+def _http_get(\n+    url: str,\n+    timeout: float = 15.0,\n+    cancel: Any = None,\n+    method: str = \"GET\",\n+    body: bytes | None = None,\n+    headers: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n+    max_bytes: int = _MAX_BYTES,\n+) -> HttpResp:\n+    \"\"\"One bounded HTTP request. Raises WebError with a short, model-readable\n+    reason; every caller turns that into error-as-data.\"\"\"\n+    if cancel is not None and cancel.is_set():\n+        raise WebError(\"aborted by user\")\n+    scheme = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).scheme.lower()\n+    if scheme not in (\"http\", \"https\"):\n+        raise WebError(f\"unsupported URL scheme {scheme!r} (http/https only)\")\n+    _assert_public_host(url)\n+    req_headers = {\n+        \"User-Agent\": USER_AGENT,\n+        \"Accept\": \"*/*\",\n+        \"Accept-Language\": \"zh-CN,zh;q=0.9,en;q=0.8\",\n+        \"Accept-Encoding\": \"gzip\",\n+    }\n+    if headers:\n+        req_headers.update(headers)\n+    request = urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=req_headers, method=method)\n+    try:\n+        resp = urllib.request.build_opener(_SafeRedirects()).open(request, timeout=timeout)\n+    except WebError:\n+        raise\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        raise WebError(f\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}\") from e\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        reason = getattr(e, \"reason\", e)\n+        if isinstance(reason, (socket.timeout, TimeoutError)):\n+            raise WebError(f\"timed out after {timeout:.0f}s\") from e\n+        raise WebError(str(reason) or \"request failed\") from e\n+    except (ValueError, OSError) as e:\n+        raise WebError(f\"request failed: {e}\") from e\n+    with resp:\n+        raw = _drain(resp, cancel, max_bytes)\n+    if resp.headers.get(\"Content-Encoding\", \"\").lower() == \"gzip\":\n+        try:\n+            raw = gzip.decompress(raw)\n+        except OSError as e:\n+            raise WebError(f\"malformed gzip body from {url}\") from e\n+    elif resp.headers.get(\"Content-Encoding\", \"\").lower() == \"deflate\":\n+        try:\n+            raw = zlib.decompress(raw)\n+        except zlib.error:\n+            raw = zlib.decompress(raw, -zlib.MAX_WBITS)  # raw-deflate variant\n+    return HttpResp(url=resp.geturl(), content_type=resp.headers.get(\"Content-Type\", \"\"), body=raw)\n+\n+\n+_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\"charset=[\\\"']?([\\w\\-:+.]+)\", re.I)\n+_META_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\"<meta[^>]+charset=[\\\"']?([\\w\\-:+.]+)\", re.I)\n+\n+\n+def _decode_body(raw: bytes, content_type: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Bytes -> text: header charset, then a meta sniff, then utf-8, then\n+    latin-1 (which never fails, so decoding cannot raise).\"\"\"\n+    m = _CHARSET_RE.search(content_type or \"\")\n+    charset = m.group(1) if m else None\n+    if not charset:\n+        m = _META_CHARSET_RE.search(raw[:4096].decode(\"ascii\", errors=\"ignore\"))\n+        charset = m.group(1) if m else None\n+    if charset:\n+        try:\n+            return raw.decode(charset, errors=\"replace\")\n+        except (LookupError, ValueError):\n+            pass  # unknown charset name: fall through to BOM/utf-8\n+    for bom, enc in ((b\"\\xff\\xfe\", \"utf-16-le\"), (b\"\\xfe\\xff\", \"utf-16-be\")):\n+        if raw.startswith(bom):\n+            return raw.decode(enc, errors=\"replace\")\n+    try:\n+        return raw.decode(\"utf-8\")\n+    except UnicodeDecodeError:\n+        return raw.decode(\"latin-1\", errors=\"replace\")\n"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789621227.5, "id": "828eb19bc89d", "content": "第 1 段写入成功，连接没断——分段策略有效。第 2 段（HTML 正文提取 + DDG 解析器 + 字符窗口）：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_b87329a4ea2344b08113af1e", "name": "edit_file", "arguments": "{\"new_string\":\"    try:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"latin-1\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ---- HTML -> readable text --------------------------------------------------\\n\\n_SNIPPET_TAG_RE = re.compile(r\\\"<[^>]+>\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _clean_snippet(text: str) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Feed/blurb HTML to one line of plain text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    text = _SNIPPET_TAG_RE.sub(\\\" \\\", text)\\n    text = text.replace(\\\"\\\\xa0\\\", \\\" \\\")\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", text).strip()[:300]\\n\\n\\nclass _TextExtractor(HTMLParser):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Page HTML to title + readable text: script/style/nav chrome dropped,\\n    block boundaries become newlines, runs of blank lines collapse.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    _SKIP = frozenset(\\n        {\\\"script\\\", \\\"style\\\", \\\"noscript\\\", \\\"template\\\", \\\"svg\\\", \\\"iframe\\\", \\\"object\\\",\\n         \\\"embed\\\", \\\"canvas\\\", \\\"nav\\\", \\\"aside\\\", \\\"footer\\\", \\\"form\\\", \\\"button\\\",\\n         \\\"select\\\", \\\"option\\\", \\\"input\\\", \\\"label\\\", \\\"head\\\"}\\n    )\\n    _BLOCK = frozenset(\\n        {\\\"p\\\", \\\"div\\\", \\\"li\\\", \\\"tr\\\", \\\"table\\\", \\\"ul\\\", \\\"ol\\\", \\\"dl\\\", \\\"dt\\\", \\\"dd\\\", \\\"pre\\\",\\n         \\\"blockquote\\\", \\\"section\\\", \\\"article\\\", \\\"main\\\", \\\"figure\\\", \\\"figcaption\\\",\\n         \\\"h1\\\", \\\"h2\\\", \\\"h3\\\", \\\"h4\\\", \\\"h5\\\", \\\"h6\\\", \\\"br\\\", \\\"hr\\\"}\\n    )\\n\\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\\n        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)\\n        self.title = \\\"\\\"\\n        self._chunks: list[str] = []\\n        self._skip_depth = 0\\n        self._in_title = False\\n\\n    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\\n        if tag == \\\"title\\\":\\n            self._in_title = True\\n            return\\n        if tag in self._SKIP:\\n            self._skip_depth += 1\\n        elif not self._skip_depth and tag in self._BLOCK:\\n            self._chunks.append(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n    def handle_endtag(self, tag):\\n        if tag == \\\"title\\\":\\n            self._in_title = False\\n        elif tag in self._SKIP and self._skip_depth:\\n            self._skip_depth -= 1\\n        elif not self._skip_depth and tag in self._BLOCK:\\n            self._chunks.append(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n    def handle_data(self, data):\\n        if self._in_title:\\n            self.title += data.strip()\\n        elif not self._skip_depth:\\n            self._chunks.append(data)\\n\\n    def text(self) -> str:\\n        raw = \\\"\\\".join(self._chunks).replace(\\\"\\\\xa0\\\", \\\" \\\")\\n        lines = (re.sub(r\\\"[ \\\\t\\\\r\\\\f]+\\\", \\\" \\\", ln).strip() for ln in raw.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\"))\\n        return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(ln for ln in lines if ln)\\n\\n\\ndef _window(text: str, start: int, limit: int) -> tuple[str, int | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One character slice plus the next offset (None when nothing remains).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    start = max(0, start)\\n    chunk = text[start : start + limit]\\n    rest = len(text) - (start + len(chunk))\\n    return chunk, (start + len(chunk) if rest > 0 else None)\\n\\n\\n# ---- result parsers ----------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n\\nclass _DdgParser(HTMLParser):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The duckduckgo html endpoint: <a class=\\\"result__a\\\">title</a> whose href\\n    is a /l/?uddg=<encoded> redirect, then <a class=\\\"result__snippet\\\">blurb</a>.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\\n        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)\\n        self.results: list[dict[str, str]] = []\\n        self._pending: dict[str, str] | None = None\\n        self._mode = \\\"\\\"  # \\\"\\\" | \\\"title\\\" | \\\"snippet\\\"\\n        self._buf: list[str] = []\\n\\n    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\\n        if tag != \\\"a\\\":\\n            return\\n        cls = dict(attrs).get(\\\"class\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n        if \\\"result__a\\\" in cls:\\n            self._flush()\\n            href = dict(attrs).get(\\\"href\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n            qs = urllib.parse.parse_qs(urllib.parse.urlsplit(href).query).get(\\\"uddg\\\")\\n            self._pending = {\\\"url\\\": urllib.parse.unquote(qs[0]) if qs else href, \\\"title\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"\\\"}\\n            self._mode, self._buf = \\\"title\\\", []\\n        elif \\\"result__snippet\\\" in cls and self._pending is not None:\\n            self._mode, self._buf = \\\"snippet\\\", []\\n\\n    def handle_data(self, data):\\n        if self._mode:\\n            self._buf.append(data)\\n\\n    def handle_endtag(self, tag):\\n        if tag != \\\"a\\\" or not self._pending:\\n            return\\n        if self._mode == \\\"title\\\":\\n            self._pending[\\\"title\\\"] = re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", \\\"\\\".join(self._buf)).strip()\\n            self._mode = \\\"\\\"\\n        elif self._mode == \\\"snippet\\\":\\n            self._pending[\\\"snippet\\\"] = _clean_snippet(\\\"\\\".join(self._buf))\\n            self.results.append(self._pending)\\n            self._pending, self._mode = None, \\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def _flush(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"A result__a without a trailing snippet still counts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self._pending and self._pending[\\\"title\\\"]:\\n            self.results.append(self._pending)\\n        self._pending, self._mode = None, \\\"\\\"\",\"old_string\":\"    try:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"latin-1\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\",\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "Piece 1 written without a connection drop (7.4KB stream — manageable). Piece 2: HTML text extraction + DDG parser + char windowing. Append via edit_file at the end of the file."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789621227.4999623, "id": "fc6b5296694e", "name": "edit_file", "arguments": "{\"new_string\":\"    try:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"latin-1\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ---- HTML -> readable text --------------------------------------------------\\n\\n_SNIPPET_TAG_RE = re.compile(r\\\"<[^>]+>\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _clean_snippet(text: str) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Feed/blurb HTML to one line of plain text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    text = _SNIPPET_TAG_RE.sub(\\\" \\\", text)\\n    text = text.replace(\\\"\\\\xa0\\\", \\\" \\\")\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", text).strip()[:300]\\n\\n\\nclass _TextExtractor(HTMLParser):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Page HTML to title + readable text: script/style/nav chrome dropped,\\n    block boundaries become newlines, runs of blank lines collapse.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    _SKIP = frozenset(\\n        {\\\"script\\\", \\\"style\\\", \\\"noscript\\\", \\\"template\\\", \\\"svg\\\", \\\"iframe\\\", \\\"object\\\",\\n         \\\"embed\\\", \\\"canvas\\\", \\\"nav\\\", \\\"aside\\\", \\\"footer\\\", \\\"form\\\", \\\"button\\\",\\n         \\\"select\\\", \\\"option\\\", \\\"input\\\", \\\"label\\\", \\\"head\\\"}\\n    )\\n    _BLOCK = frozenset(\\n        {\\\"p\\\", \\\"div\\\", \\\"li\\\", \\\"tr\\\", \\\"table\\\", \\\"ul\\\", \\\"ol\\\", \\\"dl\\\", \\\"dt\\\", \\\"dd\\\", \\\"pre\\\",\\n         \\\"blockquote\\\", \\\"section\\\", \\\"article\\\", \\\"main\\\", \\\"figure\\\", \\\"figcaption\\\",\\n         \\\"h1\\\", \\\"h2\\\", \\\"h3\\\", \\\"h4\\\", \\\"h5\\\", \\\"h6\\\", \\\"br\\\", \\\"hr\\\"}\\n    )\\n\\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\\n        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)\\n        self.title = \\\"\\\"\\n        self._chunks: list[str] = []\\n        self._skip_depth = 0\\n        self._in_title = False\\n\\n    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\\n        if tag == \\\"title\\\":\\n            self._in_title = True\\n            return\\n        if tag in self._SKIP:\\n            self._skip_depth += 1\\n        elif not self._skip_depth and tag in self._BLOCK:\\n            self._chunks.append(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n    def handle_endtag(self, tag):\\n        if tag == \\\"title\\\":\\n            self._in_title = False\\n        elif tag in self._SKIP and self._skip_depth:\\n            self._skip_depth -= 1\\n        elif not self._skip_depth and tag in self._BLOCK:\\n            self._chunks.append(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n    def handle_data(self, data):\\n        if self._in_title:\\n            self.title += data.strip()\\n        elif not self._skip_depth:\\n            self._chunks.append(data)\\n\\n    def text(self) -> str:\\n        raw = \\\"\\\".join(self._chunks).replace(\\\"\\\\xa0\\\", \\\" \\\")\\n        lines = (re.sub(r\\\"[ \\\\t\\\\r\\\\f]+\\\", \\\" \\\", ln).strip() for ln in raw.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\"))\\n        return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(ln for ln in lines if ln)\\n\\n\\ndef _window(text: str, start: int, limit: int) -> tuple[str, int | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One character slice plus the next offset (None when nothing remains).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    start = max(0, start)\\n    chunk = text[start : start + limit]\\n    rest = len(text) - (start + len(chunk))\\n    return chunk, (start + len(chunk) if rest > 0 else None)\\n\\n\\n# ---- result parsers ----------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n\\nclass _DdgParser(HTMLParser):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The duckduckgo html endpoint: <a class=\\\"result__a\\\">title</a> whose href\\n    is a /l/?uddg=<encoded> redirect, then <a class=\\\"result__snippet\\\">blurb</a>.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\\n        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)\\n        self.results: list[dict[str, str]] = []\\n        self._pending: dict[str, str] | None = None\\n        self._mode = \\\"\\\"  # \\\"\\\" | \\\"title\\\" | \\\"snippet\\\"\\n        self._buf: list[str] = []\\n\\n    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\\n        if tag != \\\"a\\\":\\n            return\\n        cls = dict(attrs).get(\\\"class\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n        if \\\"result__a\\\" in cls:\\n            self._flush()\\n            href = dict(attrs).get(\\\"href\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n            qs = urllib.parse.parse_qs(urllib.parse.urlsplit(href).query).get(\\\"uddg\\\")\\n            self._pending = {\\\"url\\\": urllib.parse.unquote(qs[0]) if qs else href, \\\"title\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"\\\"}\\n            self._mode, self._buf = \\\"title\\\", []\\n        elif \\\"result__snippet\\\" in cls and self._pending is not None:\\n            self._mode, self._buf = \\\"snippet\\\", []\\n\\n    def handle_data(self, data):\\n        if self._mode:\\n            self._buf.append(data)\\n\\n    def handle_endtag(self, tag):\\n        if tag != \\\"a\\\" or not self._pending:\\n            return\\n        if self._mode == \\\"title\\\":\\n            self._pending[\\\"title\\\"] = re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", \\\"\\\".join(self._buf)).strip()\\n            self._mode = \\\"\\\"\\n        elif self._mode == \\\"snippet\\\":\\n            self._pending[\\\"snippet\\\"] = _clean_snippet(\\\"\\\".join(self._buf))\\n            self.results.append(self._pending)\\n            self._pending, self._mode = None, \\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def _flush(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"A result__a without a trailing snippet still counts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self._pending and self._pending[\\\"title\\\"]:\\n            self.results.append(self._pending)\\n        self._pending, self._mode = None, \\\"\\\"\",\"old_string\":\"    try:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError:\\n        return raw.decode(\\\"latin-1\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\",\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_b87329a4ea2344b08113af1e"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789621227.5662746, "id": "7c8eb2bd5594", "tool_call_id": "call_b87329a4ea2344b08113af1e", "content": "OK: edited C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\agent\\tools\\websearch.py (+120 -0 lines)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/agent\\tools\\websearch.py\n+++ b/agent\\tools\\websearch.py\n@@ -193,3 +193,123 @@\n         return raw.decode(\"utf-8\")\n     except UnicodeDecodeError:\n         return raw.decode(\"latin-1\", errors=\"replace\")\n+\n+\n+# ---- HTML -> readable text --------------------------------------------------\n+\n+_SNIPPET_TAG_RE = re.compile(r\"<[^>]+>\")\n+\n+\n+def _clean_snippet(text: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Feed/blurb HTML to one line of plain text.\"\"\"\n+    text = _SNIPPET_TAG_RE.sub(\" \", text)\n+    text = text.replace(\"\\xa0\", \" \")\n+    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text).strip()[:300]\n+\n+\n+class _TextExtractor(HTMLParser):\n+    \"\"\"Page HTML to title + readable text: script/style/nav chrome dropped,\n+    block boundaries become newlines, runs of blank lines collapse.\"\"\"\n+\n+    _SKIP = frozenset(\n+        {\"script\", \"style\", \"noscript\", \"template\", \"svg\", \"iframe\", \"object\",\n+         \"embed\", \"canvas\", \"nav\", \"aside\", \"footer\", \"form\", \"button\",\n+         \"select\", \"option\", \"input\", \"label\", \"head\"}\n+    )\n+    _BLOCK = frozenset(\n+        {\"p\", \"div\", \"li\", \"tr\", \"table\", \"ul\", \"ol\", \"dl\", \"dt\", \"dd\", \"pre\",\n+         \"blockquote\", \"section\", \"article\", \"main\", \"figure\", \"figcaption\",\n+         \"h1\", \"h2\", \"h3\", \"h4\", \"h5\", \"h6\", \"br\", \"hr\"}\n+    )\n+\n+    def __init__(self) -> None:\n+        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)\n+        self.title = \"\"\n+        self._chunks: list[str] = []\n+        self._skip_depth = 0\n+        self._in_title = False\n+\n+    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\n+        if tag == \"title\":\n+            self._in_title = True\n+            return\n+        if tag in self._SKIP:\n+            self._skip_depth += 1\n+        elif not self._skip_depth and tag in self._BLOCK:\n+            self._chunks.append(\"\\n\")\n+\n+    def handle_endtag(self, tag):\n+        if tag == \"title\":\n+            self._in_title = False\n+        elif tag in self._SKIP and self._skip_depth:\n+            self._skip_depth -= 1\n+        elif not self._skip_depth and tag in self._BLOCK:\n+            self._chunks.append(\"\\n\")\n+\n+    def handle_data(self, data):\n+        if self._in_title:\n+            self.title += data.strip()\n+        elif not self._skip_depth:\n+            self._chunks.append(data)\n+\n+    def text(self) -> str:\n+        raw = \"\".join(self._chunks).replace(\"\\xa0\", \" \")\n+        lines = (re.sub(r\"[ \\t\\r\\f]+\", \" \", ln).strip() for ln in raw.split(\"\\n\"))\n+        return \"\\n\".join(ln for ln in lines if ln)\n+\n+\n+def _window(text: str, start: int, limit: int) -> tuple[str, int | None]:\n+    \"\"\"One character slice plus the next offset (None when nothing remains).\"\"\"\n+    start = max(0, start)\n+    chunk = text[start : start + limit]\n+    rest = len(text) - (start + len(chunk))\n+    return chunk, (start + len(chunk) if rest > 0 else None)\n+\n+\n+# ---- result parsers ----------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+class _DdgParser(HTMLParser):\n+    \"\"\"The duckduckgo html endpoint: <a class=\"result__a\">title</a> whose href\n+    is a /l/?uddg=<encoded> redirect, then <a class=\"result__snippet\">blurb</a>.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def __init__(self) -> None:\n+        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)\n+        self.results: list[dict[str, str]] = []\n+        self._pending: dict[str, str] | None = None\n+        self._mode = \"\"  # \"\" | \"title\" | \"snippet\"\n+        self._buf: list[str] = []\n+\n+    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\n+        if tag != \"a\":\n+            return\n+        cls = dict(attrs).get(\"class\", \"\")\n+        if \"result__a\" in cls:\n+            self._flush()\n+            href = dict(attrs).get(\"href\", \"\")\n+            qs = urllib.parse.parse_qs(urllib.parse.urlsplit(href).query).get(\"uddg\")\n+            self._pending = {\"url\": urllib.parse.unquote(qs[0]) if qs else href, \"title\": \"\", \"snippet\": \"\"}\n+            self._mode, self._buf = \"title\", []\n+        elif \"result__snippet\" in cls and self._pending is not None:\n+            self._mode, self._buf = \"snippet\", []\n+\n+    def handle_data(self, data):\n+        if self._mode:\n+            self._buf.append(data)\n+\n+    def handle_endtag(self, tag):\n+        if tag != \"a\" or not self._pending:\n+            return\n+        if self._mode == \"title\":\n+            self._pending[\"title\"] = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", \"\".join(self._buf)).strip()\n+            self._mode = \"\"\n+        elif self._mode == \"snippet\":\n+            self._pending[\"snippet\"] = _clean_snippet(\"\".join(self._buf))\n+            self.results.append(self._pending)\n+            self._pending, self._mode = None, \"\"\n+\n+    def _flush(self):\n+        \"\"\"A result__a without a trailing snippet still counts.\"\"\"\n+        if self._pending and self._pending[\"title\"]:\n+            self.results.append(self._pending)\n+        self._pending, self._mode = None, \"\"\n"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789621245.718822, "id": "c31dcacd8f3d", "content": "第 3 段（四个后端 + 回退链）：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_756540c08216408fba637392", "name": "edit_file", "arguments": "{\"new_string\":\"    def _flush(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"A result__a without a trailing snippet still counts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self._pending and self._pending[\\\"title\\\"]:\\n            self.results.append(self._pending)\\n        self._pending, self._mode = None, \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\n# ---- backends: (query, limit, config, get) -> list[{title,url,snippet}] ------\\n\\n\\ndef _tavily(query: str, limit: int, config: Config, get: Callable[..., HttpResp]) -> list[dict[str, str]]:\\n    payload = json.dumps({\\\"query\\\": query, \\\"max_results\\\": limit}).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    resp = get(\\n        \\\"https://api.tavily.com/search\\\",\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n        body=payload,\\n        headers={\\n            \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\",\\n            \\\"Authorization\\\": f\\\"Bearer {config.tavily_api_key}\\\",\\n            \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\",\\n        },\\n    )\\n    try:\\n        data = json.loads(resp.body)\\n        raw = data.get(\\\"results\\\") or []\\n    except ValueError as e:\\n        raise BackendError(f\\\"tavily returned non-JSON body: {e}\\\") from e\\n    out = [\\n        {\\n            \\\"title\\\": str(r.get(\\\"title\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip(),\\n            \\\"url\\\": str(r.get(\\\"url\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip(),\\n            \\\"snippet\\\": _clean_snippet(str(r.get(\\\"content\\\") or \\\"\\\")),\\n        }\\n        for r in raw\\n        if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get(\\\"url\\\")\\n    ]\\n    if not out:\\n        raise BackendError(\\\"response had no usable results\\\")\\n    return out[:limit]\\n\\n\\ndef _searxng(query: str, limit: int, config: Config, get: Callable[..., HttpResp]) -> list[dict[str, str]]:\\n    url = f\\\"{config.searxng_url}/search?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'q': query, 'format': 'json'})}\\\"\\n    resp = get(url, headers={\\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"})\\n    try:\\n        data = json.loads(resp.body)\\n        raw = data.get(\\\"results\\\") or []\\n    except ValueError as e:\\n        raise BackendError(f\\\"searxng returned non-JSON body (format=json enabled?): {e}\\\") from e\\n    out = [\\n        {\\n            \\\"title\\\": str(r.get(\\\"title\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip(),\\n            \\\"url\\\": str(r.get(\\\"url\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip(),\\n            \\\"snippet\\\": _clean_snippet(str(r.get(\\\"content\\\") or \\\"\\\")),\\n        }\\n        for r in raw\\n        if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get(\\\"url\\\")\\n    ]\\n    if not out:\\n        raise BackendError(\\\"response had no usable results\\\")\\n    return out[:limit]\\n\\n\\ndef _bing(query: str, limit: int, config: Config, get: Callable[..., HttpResp]) -> list[dict[str, str]]:\\n    url = \\\"https://www.bing.com/search?\\\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(\\n        {\\\"q\\\": query, \\\"format\\\": \\\"rss\\\", \\\"count\\\": str(min(limit, 30))}\\n    )\\n    resp = get(url, headers={\\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/rss+xml, application/xml;q=0.9, */*;q=0.8\\\"})\\n    try:\\n        root = ET.fromstring(resp.body)\\n    except ET.ParseError as e:\\n        raise BackendError(f\\\"bing RSS is not parseable XML: {e}\\\") from e\\n    out = []\\n    for item in root.iter(\\\"item\\\"):\\n        title = (item.findtext(\\\"title\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n        link = (item.findtext(\\\"link\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n        if not (title and link):\\n            continue\\n        out.append({\\\"title\\\": _clean_snippet(title), \\\"url\\\": link, \\\"snippet\\\": _clean_snippet(item.findtext(\\\"description\\\") or \\\"\\\")})\\n        if len(out) >= limit:\\n            break\\n    if not out:\\n        raise BackendError(\\\"no items in the RSS (blocked, or genuinely no results)\\\")\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef _ddg(query: str, limit: int, config: Config, get: Callable[..., HttpResp]) -> list[dict[str, str]]:\\n    url = \\\"https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/?\\\" + urllib.parse.urlencode({\\\"q\\\": query})\\n    resp = get(url)\\n    parser = _DdgParser()\\n    parser.feed(_decode_body(resp.body, resp.content_type))\\n    parser.close()\\n    out = [r for r in parser.results if r[\\\"url\\\"]][:limit]\\n    if not out:\\n        raise BackendError(\\\"no results parsed (bot-checked, blocked, or layout changed)\\\")\\n    return out\\n\\n\\n_BACKENDS: dict[str, Callable[[str, int, Config, Callable[..., HttpResp]], list[dict[str, str]]]] = {\\n    \\\"tavily\\\": _tavily,\\n    \\\"searxng\\\": _searxng,\\n    \\\"bing\\\": _bing,\\n    \\\"ddg\\\": _ddg,\\n}\\n_DEFAULT_CHAIN = (\\\"tavily\\\", \\\"searxng\\\", \\\"bing\\\", \\\"ddg\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _available_backends(config: Config) -> tuple[str, ...]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The usable subset of the chain: keyless backends are always in.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    out = []\\n    for name in _DEFAULT_CHAIN:\\n        if name == \\\"tavily\\\" and not config.tavily_api_key:\\n            continue\\n        if name == \\\"searxng\\\" and not config.searxng_url:\\n            continue\\n        out.append(name)\\n    return tuple(out)\",\"old_string\":\"    def _flush(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"A result__a without a trailing snippet still counts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self._pending and self._pending[\\\"title\\\"]:\\n            self.results.append(self._pending)\\n        self._pending, self._mode = None, \\\"\\\"\",\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "Piece 2 done (+120 lines, no drop). Piece 3: the four backends + chain."}
