{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789621590.3594508, "id": "9577d41ae2a0", "content": "200 字符的限制是刻意设计的（网页端抓取不应支持微小的 `max_chars`），因此测试工具（test fixture）需要填入更多内容。我将延长页面长度，并让测试验证该限制（`max_chars=60` → `next start=200`）：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_2491949f57b84c87ab426b1f", "name": "edit_file", "arguments": "{\"new_string\":\"    # 8. web_fetch: html extraction, truncation hint with next start, redirect note\\n    # max_chars below the 200-char floor is raised to 200, hence start=200 (not 60).\\n    def _fetch_get(url: str, **kw) -> ws.HttpResp:\\n        if \\\"final.example\\\" in url:\\n            long_page = PAGE_HTML.replace(\\\"</div>\\\", \\\"</div><p>\\\" + \\\"filler \\\" * 60 + \\\"</p>\\\")\\n            return _resp(long_page, url=\\\"https://final.example/page\\\")\\n        raise AssertionError(f\\\"unexpected fetch: {url}\\\")\\n\\n    ws._http_get = _fetch_get\\n    try:\\n        r = ws.web_fetch(ws.Workspace, Config(read_max_chars=60), \\\"https://final.example/page\\\")\\n        check(not r.get(\\\"error\\\") and \\\"Page Title\\\" in r[\\\"content\\\"], \\\"fetch: title + body extracted\\\")\\n        check(\\\"chars truncated\\\" in r[\\\"content\\\"] and \\\"start=200\\\" in r[\\\"content\\\"], \\\"fetch: truncation names the next start\\\")\\n        r2 = ws.web_fetch(ws.Workspace, Config(read_max_chars=200), \\\"https://final.example/page\\\", start=200)\\n        check(\\\"start=200\\\" in r2[\\\"content\\\"] or r2[\\\"content\\\"], \\\"fetch: continuation works\\\")\",\"old_string\":\"    # 8. web_fetch: html extraction, truncation hint with next start, redirect note\\n    def _fetch_get(url: str, **kw) -> ws.HttpResp:\\n        if \\\"final.example\\\" in url:\\n            return _resp(PAGE_HTML, url=\\\"https://final.example/page\\\")\\n        raise AssertionError(f\\\"unexpected fetch: {url}\\\")\\n\\n    ws._http_get = _fetch_get\\n    try:\\n        r = ws.web_fetch(ws.Workspace, Config(read_max_chars=60), \\\"https://final.example/page\\\")\\n        check(not r.get(\\\"error\\\") and \\\"Page Title\\\" in r[\\\"content\\\"], \\\"fetch: title + body extracted\\\")\\n        check(\\\"chars truncated\\\" in r[\\\"content\\\"] and \\\"start=60\\\" in r[\\\"content\\\"], \\\"fetch: truncation names the next start\\\")\\n        r2 = ws.web_fetch(ws.Workspace, Config(read_max_chars=60), \\\"https://final.example/page\\\", start=60)\\n        check(\\\"start=60\\\" in r2[\\\"content\\\"] or r2[\\\"content\\\"], \\\"fetch: continuation works\\\")\",\"path\":\"tests/websearch_test.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "The 200 floor is intentional (web_fetch shouldn't honor tiny max_chars). The test should exercise the truncation path with a page longer than the effective limit. The cleanest fix, keeping the test meaningful: make the fixture page long enough (>200 chars) and check `start=200` with default floor... but passing `read_max_chars=200` would be clearer. Actually simpler: keep `Config(read_max_chars=60)` to also verify the floor — no wait, then next_start would be 200 only if page > 200 chars.\n\nPlan: append a long filler to PAGE_HTML (e.g. a paragraph repeated), making extracted text > 200 chars. Then:\n- r = web_fetch(..., read_max_chars=60) → limit floored to 200 → truncation says start=200 (verifies the floor too).\n- r2 = web_fetch(..., start=200) → continuation.\n\nBut test at line 151 checks \"start=60\". I'll update the test to expect start=200 with a comment noting the floor. Also line 153's continuation `start=60` → would re-fetch from 60, fine either way, but should be start=200.\n\nWait — test 7 (window tests) uses ws._window directly, so floor doesn't matter there.\n\nBetter design alternative: the test intent \"truncation names the next start\" — I'll rewrite the fetch test to use a long page. Let me modify PAGE_HTML to add a long paragraph, or build the long page inside section 8 by repeating. Simpler and more local: inside section 8, use `LONG_PAGE = PAGE_HTML.replace(\"</div>\", \"</div><p>\" + \"filler \" * 60 + \"</p>\")`? That'd add ~420 chars of text (\"filler \" * 60 = 420 chars). Extracted text = 54 - 0 + 421ish. Title line included. Good: len ≈ 475 > 200.\n\nActually careful: \"One paragraph.\" etc. Fine.\n\nThen:\n```python\nLONG = PAGE_HTML.replace(\"</div>\", \"</div><p>\" + \"filler \" * 60 + \"</p>\")\nr = ws.web_fetch(ws.Workspace, Config(read_max_chars=60), \"https://final.example/page\")\ncheck(... \"start=200\" ...)\n```\nThis documents the 200 floor. And r2 with start=200.\n\nLet me read lines 141-156 again and edit."}
