{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789621845.7004151, "id": "d23731e24108", "content": "完成。全部测试通过，汇报如下：\n\n## 测试结果\n\n- **离线 31 项全过**：`python -m tests.websearch_test`\n- **实网验证通过**：`--live` 走真实 Bing RSS 搜索（哈工深查询返回 3 条结果）+ 真实 fetch `hitsz.edu.cn` 全文提取\n- **回归无破坏**：`selfcheck`、`loop_test`、`llm_client_test`、`server_test` 全部通过\n\n## 修的两处问题\n\n1. **`_clean_snippet` 不解码 HTML 实体**：`&nbsp;`/`&amp;` 原样残留（代码只处理了字面 `\\xa0`）。加了 `html.unescape()`。\n2. **`--live` 测试自身的两个 bug**：\n   - 取 URL 时按行号取到了**标题行**去当 URL（所以报 `unsupported URL scheme ''`），改为正则提取第一个 `https?://\\S+`，并补上漏掉的 `import re`；\n   - 中文在 Windows 控制台显示乱码——**数据本身解码是正确的**（写入 UTF-8 文件验证过，`哈尔滨工业大学（深圳）` 完好），只是 GBK 管道显示问题，live 分支加了 `sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")`。\n\n另外一处测试预期修正：`web_fetch` 的 `max_chars` 有 200 字符下限（防止模型传极小值），测试夹具页面只有 54 字符永远触发不了截断。我把夹具加长，并让测试**同时验证下限行为**（`max_chars=60` → 提示 `start=200`）。\n\n## README 更新\n\n- 项目结构工具清单补上 `web_search / web_fetch`\n- 新增一段：联网搜索开箱即用（内置 Bing 免 key 后端），`CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY` / `CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL` 可启用优先后端，fetch 带 SSRF 防护\n- 测试清单加 `tests.websearch_test`\n\n## 关于断连\n\n超时修复（`llm_read_timeout=240`、按阶段报错）已在库里，但**需要重启后端进程才生效**。这次会话没再出现 10054——大文件分段写入的策略（websearch.py 当时分 4 段写）继续沿用即可。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": ""}
{"type": "final", "timestamp": 1789621845.7036917, "id": "45c3b0226b69", "status": "completed", "summary": "完成。全部测试通过，汇报如下：\n\n## 测试结果\n\n- **离线 31 项全过**：`python -m tests.websearch_test`\n- **实网验证通过**：`--live` 走真实 Bing RSS 搜索（哈工深查询返回 3 条结果）+ 真实 fetch `hitsz.edu.cn` 全文提取\n- **回归无破坏**：`selfcheck`、`loop_test`、`llm_client_test`、`server_test` 全部通过\n\n## 修的两处问题\n\n1. **`_clean_snippet` 不解码 HTML 实体**：`&nbsp;`/`&amp;` 原样残留（代码只处理了字面 `\\xa0`）。加了 `html.unescape()`。\n2. **`--live` 测试自身的两个 bug**：\n   - 取 URL 时按行号取到了**标题行**去当 URL（所以报 `unsupported URL scheme ''`），改为正则提取第一个 `https?://\\S+`，并补上漏掉的 `import re`；\n   - 中文在 Windows 控制台显示乱码——**数据本身解码是正确的**（写入 UTF-8 文件验证过，`哈尔滨工业大学（深圳）` 完好），只是 GBK 管道显示问题，live 分支加了 `sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")`。\n\n另外一处测试预期修正：`web_fetch` 的 `max_chars` 有 200 字符下限（防止模型传极小值），测试夹具页面只有 54 字符永远触发不了截断。我把夹具加长，并让测试**同时验证下限行为**（`max_chars=60` → 提示 `start=200`）。\n\n## README 更新\n\n- 项目结构工具清单补上 `web_search / web_fetch`\n- 新增一段：联网搜索开箱即用（内置 Bing 免 key 后端），`CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY` / `CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL` 可启用优先后端，fetch 带 SSRF 防护\n- 测试清单加 `tests.websearch_test`\n\n## 关于断连\n\n超时修复（`llm_read_timeout=240`、按阶段报错）已在库里，但**需要重启后端进程才生效**。这次会话没再出现 10054——大文件分段写入的策略（websearch.py 当时分 4 段写）继续沿用即可。"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789625632.5432227, "id": "742e857ab9bf", "content": "所以为什么当时涉及到websearch.py的地方总会超时？"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789625668.275785, "id": "52539962a0f0", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_3633d809b8d545eab4f6ffb5", "name": "grep", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py\",\"pattern\":\"Timeout|timeout\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user asks: \"所以为什么当时涉及到websearch.py的地方总会超时？\" (So why did things involving websearch.py always time out back then?)\n\nThis refers to the earlier sessions where operations involving websearch.py kept timing out. From the conversation summary, there were several distinct timeout/disconnect phenomena:\n\n1. WinError 10054 disconnects \"每次写大 py 文件断连\" — large write_file calls with long streaming args got RST. websearch.py was a big new file (~524 lines), so writing it in one shot triggered this. Fixed by writing in 4 segments.\n\n2. LLM \"Request timed out\" — openai_client.py used a single float timeout=60 for connect/read/write/pool; read timeout is \"gap between chunks\" semantics, so any streaming pause >60s during long generations (like producing a whole big websearch.py at once) would abort. Long file generation = long uninterrupted streaming = pauses over the threshold → timeouts. Short requests didn't trigger it.\n\nSo the answer: it wasn't the websearch.py content itself being special — it was the correlation: websearch.py was the biggest file being written at that time. Generating a large file means one long LLM streaming turn (long tool-call arguments), which:\n\n- stresses the read timeout (a single long stream; any provider-side pause > 60s, or the proxy buffering the whole segment and flushing at the end, exceeded the read timeout) → \"Request timed out\"\n- the long tool arguments streaming through also meant the client's write side was pushing a large payload; middleboxes/proxies could RST the connection (WinError 10054) → connection reset\n\nBoth failures clustered on websearch.py because it was the largest single artifact being produced. The content of websearch.py had nothing to do with it — no code inside it caused timeouts. The `web_search_timeout` config (15s) inside websearch.py is a separate thing, and actually the module itself was never run against the network until the live test.\n\nAlso worth noting: at the time, the tool descriptions/registry work also touched websearch.py repeatedly, requiring re-reads and multiple edits, each edit being a long-turn generation again.\n\nLet me structure the answer:\n\n1. 表面现象:涉及 websearch.py 的操作总超时\n2. 真正原因:websearch.py 是当时最大的单次产出物\n   - 一次生成整个大文件 = 一条超长的流式响应\n   - read timeout 语义是\"块间隔\"不是\"总时长\"——供应商停顿/中转缓存整段最后 flush/长连接被限流,任何一次 >60s 的停顿就 \"Request timed out\"\n   - 短请求根本测不出来,所以显得\"只有 websearch.py 会超时\"\n   - 另一个独立现象:超长 write_file 参数在传输层被 RST(WinError 10054)——大参数长流被中间设备掐断\n3. 为什么修复有效:\n   - Timeout(60, connect=15, read=240) 把 read 放宽到 240s\n   - 分 4 段写 websearch.py,把单条流的长度压下来,绕开了传输层 RST\n4. 澄清:websearch.py 的代码本身没有任何导致超时的东西;`web_search_timeout: 15` 是模块运行时的 HTTP 超时,是另一码事,而且直到今天 --live 才第一次真正联网\n\nUse a diagram? Maybe a small mermaid timeline or just markdown. A table contrasting the two phenomena would be clear.\n\nKeep it in Chinese, concise, concrete. No tool calls needed — this is a pure explanation question. Maybe I could double-check the openai_client.py current state to quote the exact code... I have the summary but the exact contents aren't in context. Since this is an explanation of past behavior, I can cite from the summary confidently. But to \"show rather than tell\", quoting the actual current code would be nice. Let me do a quick grep to quote the exact timeout lines — that's cheap and makes the answer concrete.\n\nLet me grep openai_client.py for Timeout and read the relevant lines."}
