ection 跨设备使用\n\nLet me investigate. The truth matters: if the whole agent process runs remotely, then websearch runs remotely → network from remote server. If tools run locally... Actually wait — in remote SSH scenario, what does the remote do? The user earlier mentioned \"正常\" scenario meaning: the UI connects over SSH to a remote workspace; the LLM API calls — where do they go through? Earlier work: \"websearch对网络的访问\" — the user wants to know whether Bing requests go out from their local machine or the remote server.\n\nFrom the summary of earlier sessions: there's an SSH tunnel from the UI to the remote... \"ui/ Electron 前端(设置、SSH 隧道、LLM 反代)\" — LLM 反代 (LLM reverse proxy) is in the UI, meaning LLM requests may be proxied through the local UI. And the backend... Let me actually read the code.\n\nKey question decomposition:\n1. Where does the agent backend process run in SSH mode? (local or remote)\n2. Where does websearch code execute? (it's part of the backend)\n3. Therefore whose network does the Bing request use?\n\nLet me read supervisor.py and browsing.py, and check how SSH mode works. Also ui/app.js might have the tunnel logic. Let me grep for relevant things."}
