{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789626939.1599834, "id": "e3df30f90f0a", "tool_call_id": "call_472d8794ea6a4da7bf2406b8", "content": "157:         raise WebError(f\"request failed: {e}\") from e\n158:     with resp:\n159:         raw = _drain(resp, cancel, max_bytes)\n160:     if resp.headers.get(\"Content-Encoding\", \"\").lower() == \"gzip\":\n161:         try:\n162:             raw = gzip.decompress(raw)\n163:         except OSError as e:\n164:             raise WebError(f\"malformed gzip body from {url}\") from e\n165:     elif resp.headers.get(\"Content-Encoding\", \"\").lower() == \"deflate\":\n166:         try:\n167:             raw = zlib.decompress(raw)\n168:         except zlib.error:\n169:             raw = zlib.decompress(raw, -zlib.MAX_WBITS)  # raw-deflate variant\n170:     return HttpResp(url=resp.geturl(), content_type=resp.headers.get(\"Content-Type\", \"\"), body=raw)\n171: \n172: \n173: _CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\"charset=[\\\"']?([\\w\\-:+.]+)\", re.I)\n174: _META_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\"<meta[^>]+charset=[\\\"']?([\\w\\-:+.]+)\", re.I)\n175: \n176: \n177: def _decode_body(raw: bytes, content_type: str) -> str:\n178:     \"\"\"Bytes -> text: header charset, then a meta sniff, then utf-8, then\n179:     latin-1 (which never fails, so decoding cannot raise).\"\"\"\n180:     m = _CHARSET_RE.search(content_type or \"\")\n181:     charset = m.group(1) if m else None\n182:     if not charset:\n183:         m = _META_CHARSET_RE.search(raw[:4096].decode(\"ascii\", errors=\"ignore\"))\n184:         charset = m.group(1) if m else None\n185:     if charset:\n186:         try:\n187:             return raw.decode(charset, errors=\"replace\")\n188:         except (LookupError, ValueError):\n189:             pass  # unknown charset name: fall through to BOM/utf-8\n190:     for bom, enc in ((b\"\\xff\\xfe\", \"utf-16-le\"), (b\"\\xfe\\xff\", \"utf-16-be\")):\n191:         if raw.startswith(bom):\n192:             return raw.decode(enc, errors=\"replace\")\n193:     try:\n194:         return raw.decode(\"utf-8\")\n195:     except UnicodeDecodeError:\n196:         return raw.decode(\"latin-1\", errors=\"replace\")\n... (showing lines 157-196 of 525; use offset=197 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789626996.7163827, "id": "60c7fd9de390", "content": "可以访问**大部分公开的文本网页**，但它是一个「给 LLM 读的文本抽取器」，不是浏览器——有六条明确的硬边界：\n\n## 能做到的\n\n- **任意公网 http(s) 页面**：服务端渲染的 HTML、纯文本，甚至 JSON/XML API 端点(非 HTML 的响应直接按文本返回，所以它能当通用 GET 工具用，比如打 `api.github.com`);\n- **长页面**：默认返回前 2 万字符，截断时提示 `fetch again with start=N`,模型可以一窗窗读完整篇；\n- **中文编码**：HTTP header charset → `<meta>` 嗅探(前 4KB)→ BOM → UTF-8 → latin-1 兜底，GBK/GB2312 页面也能正确解码；\n- gzip/deflate 自动解压，重定向自动跟随(每一跳都过 SSRF 检查)。\n\n## 做不到的(六条边界)\n\n| 边界 | 机制 | 模型看到的 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **JS 渲染的页面**(SPA) | `HTMLParser` 只解析静态 HTML,无浏览器内核 | `(no extractable text; the page is probably JS-rendered)` |\n| **二进制内容** | Content-Type 黑名单：image/video/audio/pdf/zip/tar… | `unsupported content-type ... (text pages only)` |\n| **内网/本机** | DNS 解析后逐 IP 查 `is_global`,拒 loopback/LAN;重定向逐跳复查 | `non-public host refused` |\n| **非 http(s) 协议** | scheme 白名单 | `unsupported URL scheme` |\n| **登录墙/付费墙/反爬** | 无 cookie、无登录态、UA 自报 `ClutchAgent/0.1`;Cloudflare 挑战页过不去 | 拿到的是登录页/挑战页的 HTML 文本，而非正文 |\n| **慢站/超大页** | 15s 超时、单响应 2MB 硬上限 | `request timed out` / `response exceeds ...` |\n\n另外两条软限制：\n\n- **可达性 = 本地网络出口**。上一条说过 web 工具走本机网络，所以本机连不上的站(这个网络下 Google 系、DDG 大概率不通)它也够不着；\n- **web_search 只是入口**：返回标题/URL/摘要(摘要截 300 字符)，要正文必须跟一次 `web_fetch`;Bing 反爬时 RSS 会 403,链自动落往下家，全挂时把每个后端的失败原因列给模型。\n\n## 对实际使用意味着什么\n\n- **适合的**：技术文档、release notes、错误信息、Stack Overflow、GitHub——恰好是编码 agent 的高频需求，而且这些站点绝大多数有服务端渲染或 API 替代路径；\n- **会失手的**：重 SPA 的站点(部分新版文档站整个是前端渲染)、反爬激进的站点、PDF 论文原文。这时模型看到的错误是「错误即数据」式的——它会读原因自己绕(比如改抓 GitHub raw、找 API 端点、换来源)；\n- **work 模式的暗门**:`run_command` 在远端执行 `curl` 可以拿到远端视角的页面，但同样没有 JS 渲染。真要啃 SPA 得上 headless browser(Playwright 之类)，项目刻意没引——破坏零依赖取向，目前没有这个后端。\n\n一句话：**公网上静态可读的文本，基本都能读；需要浏览器行为(JS、登录、下载)的，读不了。**", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "Good — decoding is robust: header charset → meta sniff (first 4KB) → BOM → utf-8 → latin-1. So GBK pages with meta charset are handled. Unknown charset names fall through gracefully.\n\nNow I can write the complete answer. Structure:\n\n1. 一句话:大部分公开文本网页可以,但有明确的边界——它是一个「给 LLM 读的文本抽取器」,不是浏览器。\n\n2. 能做(什么网页拿得到):\n   - 任意公网 http(s) 文本页面:HTML 服务端渲染、纯文本、JSON/XML API 端点(非 HTML 直接当文本返回)\n   - 大页面:start=N 分窗续读,默认 2 万字符\n   - 编码:HTTP header charset → meta 嗅探 → BOM → utf-8,GBK 中文页也能解\n   - gzip/deflate 自动解压,重定向自动跟(逐跳 SSRF 检查)\n\n3. 不能做(六个硬边界)表格:\n\n| 边界 | 机制 | 模型看到的报错 |\n|---|---|---|\n| JS 渲染的页面(SPA) | HTMLParser 只解析静态 HTML,无浏览器内核 | \"(no extractable text; the page is probably JS-rendered)\" |\n| 二进制内容 | Content-Type 黑名单 image/video/audio + pdf/zip/tar/... | \"unsupported content-type ... (text pages only)\" |\n| 内网/本机(SSRF) | 解析 DNS 后逐 IP is_global 检查,重定向逐跳复查 | \"non-public host refused\" |\n| 非 http(s) | scheme 白名单 | \"unsupported URL scheme\" |\n| 登录墙/付费墙/反爬 | 无 cookie、无登录态、UA 是标记过的 ClutchAgent;Cloudflare 挑战页拿不到正文 | 拿到的是登录页/挑战页的 HTML 文本 |\n| 慢站/大站 | 15s 超时、2MB 上限 | \"request timed out\" / \"response exceeds ...\" |\n\n4. web_search 的边界:只是搜索入口(标题/URL/摘要),Bing RSS 反爬时会 403 → 链式回退;DDG 在本网络不可达;本地网络决定可达性(GFW:Google 系大概率不通——Bing 国内版可用)。\n\n5. 和 run_command 的关系:work 模式下模型还有 curl(远端!),但同样没有 JS 渲染。真正要浏览 JS 页面需要 headless browser(如 playwright),项目刻意没引——不符合零依赖取向。如果需要,后续可以加一个可选的 CLUTCH_BROWSER_COMMAND 后端?——不要过度设计,点到为止。\n\n6. 总结判断:对「给编码 agent 用」的场景(查文档、release notes、错误信息、Stack Overflow),覆盖率足够;对 SPA 重的现代站点(很多文档站是 SPA!比如一些新版文档站)会失手——但很多文档站有 SSR 或有 GitHub raw / API 替代路径,模型会自己绕。\n\nKeep it tight. Use one table + short lists. No mermaid needed this time (previous answers had diagrams; a table suffices). Maybe a small note on what the model experiences: error-as-data means it reads the reason and adapts.\n\nActually one more useful detail: JSON endpoints — web_fetch on a JSON API returns the raw text (not html ctype → page = text). So it doubles as a generic GET tool for APIs. That's a \"can do\" worth mentioning — models use it to hit public APIs (e.g. api.github.com works from this network, confirmed during调研).\n\nAlso truncation: \"fetch again with start=N to continue\" — long pages are navigable.\n\nLength: medium. Chinese."}
{"type": "final", "timestamp": 1789626996.719358, "id": "16353326f30f", "status": "completed", "summary": "可以访问**大部分公开的文本网页**，但它是一个「给 LLM 读的文本抽取器」，不是浏览器——有六条明确的硬边界：\n\n## 能做到的\n\n- **任意公网 http(s) 页面**：服务端渲染的 HTML、纯文本，甚至 JSON/XML API 端点(非 HTML 的响应直接按文本返回，所以它能当通用 GET 工具用，比如打 `api.github.com`);\n- **长页面**：默认返回前 2 万字符，截断时提示 `fetch again with start=N`,模型可以一窗窗读完整篇；\n- **中文编码**：HTTP header charset → `<meta>` 嗅探(前 4KB)→ BOM → UTF-8 → latin-1 兜底，GBK/GB2312 页面也能正确解码；\n- gzip/deflate 自动解压，重定向自动跟随(每一跳都过 SSRF 检查)。\n\n## 做不到的(六条边界)\n\n| 边界 | 机制 | 模型看到的 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **JS 渲染的页面**(SPA) | `HTMLParser` 只解析静态 HTML,无浏览器内核 | `(no extractable text; the page is probably JS-rendered)` |\n| **二进制内容** | Content-Type 黑名单：image/video/audio/pdf/zip/tar… | `unsupported content-type ... (text pages only)` |\n| **内网/本机** | DNS 解析后逐 IP 查 `is_global`,拒 loopback/LAN;重定向逐跳复查 | `non-public host refused` |\n| **非 http(s) 协议** | scheme 白名单 | `unsupported URL scheme` |\n| **登录墙/付费墙/反爬** | 无 cookie、无登录态、UA 自报 `ClutchAgent/0.1`;Cloudflare 挑战页过不去 | 拿到的是登录页/挑战页的 HTML 文本，而非正文 |\n| **慢站/超大页** | 15s 超时、单响应 2MB 硬上限 | `request timed out` / `response exceeds ...` |\n\n另外两条软限制：\n\n- **可达性 = 本地网络出口**。上一条说过 web 工具走本机网络，所以本机连不上的站(这个网络下 Google 系、DDG 大概率不通)它也够不着；\n- **web_search 只是入口**：返回标题/URL/摘要(摘要截 300 字符)，要正文必须跟一次 `web_fetch`;Bing 反爬时 RSS 会 403,链自动落往下家，全挂时把每个后端的失败原因列给模型。\n\n## 对实际使用意味着什么\n\n- **适合的**：技术文档、release notes、错误信息、Stack Overflow、GitHub——恰好是编码 agent 的高频需求，而且这些站点绝大多数有服务端渲染或 API 替代路径；\n- **会失手的**：重 SPA 的站点(部分新版文档站整个是前端渲染)、反爬激进的站点、PDF 论文原文。这时模型看到的错误是「错误即数据」式的——它会读原因自己绕(比如改抓 GitHub raw、找 API 端点、换来源)；\n- **work 模式的暗门**:`run_command` 在远端执行 `curl` 可以拿到远端视角的页面，但同样没有 JS 渲染。真要啃 SPA 得上 headless browser(Playwright 之类)，项目刻意没引——破坏零依赖取向，目前没有这个后端。\n\n一句话：**公网上静态可读的文本，基本都能读；需要浏览器行为(JS、登录、下载)的，读不了。**"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789628958.3537366, "id": "570bb0ead3ca", "content": "现在很多社区，例如知乎/小红书/CSDN都需要登录后才能查看完整内容，这一部分有解决办法吗"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789629069.1415336, "id": "8e0a820422ac", "content": "这个问题正好可以用刚上线的工具做实证——先别谈方案，先测「墙到底挡没挡住文本抽取器」。三站各搜一条、抓一条：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_9ab1ee2cbb9e4ff582dc8d2c", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\".venv/Scripts/python.exe -c \\\"\\nimport sys,re\\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8',errors='replace')\\nsys.path.insert(0,'.')\\nfrom agent.config import Config\\nfrom agent.tools import websearch as ws\\ncfg=Config()\\nfor name,q in [('CSDN','site:blog.csdn.net rag tutorial'),('ZHIHU','site:zhuanlan.zhihu.com agent'),('XHS','site:xiaohongshu.com')]:\\n    print('='*16,name)\\n    r=ws.web_search(None,cfg,q,max_results=2)\\n    print(r['content'][:400])\\n    m=re.search(r'https?://\\\\S+',r['content'])\\n    if m:\\n        f=ws.web_fetch(None,cfg,m.group(0))\\n        c=f['content']\\n        print('--- fetch:',m.group(0)[:90])\\n        print('len:',len(c),'error:',f.get('error'))\\n        print(c[:300].replace(chr(10),' | '))\\n\\\"\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user returns to their original task question: many communities like Zhihu/Xiaohongshu/CSDN require login to view full content — is there a solution for this part?\n\nThis is the original task from the beginning of the conversation (the task listed at the top). Now they're asking it again in the context of the completed websearch/web_fetch work. So the question: can our agent access login-walled content? What are the solutions?\n\nI should analyze this properly, considering:\n\n1. **What these sites actually do:**\n   - 知乎 (Zhihu): login wall for some content, anti-crawler heavily. Actually Zhihu shows partial content to anonymous users; some answers behind login. They also check UA + cookies; unauthenticated requests often get 403 or redirect to login. `zhuanlan.zhihu.com` articles are usually readable without login via web; answers too but with occasional login pops.\n   - 小红书 (Xiaohongshu): content is behind login for web viewing (web shows login-required), heavily signature-based anti-crawler (X-s, X-t headers signed via JS), data fetched via API with signatures. Web without login shows almost nothing. Very hard without browser automation or signature reverse engineering.\n   - CSDN: content is publicly viewable but has \"关注博主/登录\" popups and sometimes forces login after N articles (\"登录后查看全文\" for some). Actually CSDN full content is viewable; the login prompt is cosmetic overlay. Scraping CSDN HTML usually works without login (content is server-rendered), just need to strip the overlay. But some are now requiring login for full article (\"展开全文\").\n\n2. **Solution tiers for an agent like Clutch:**\n\n   **Tier 0 — often enough: alternative sources** (the pragmatic answer)\n   - Model behavior: when web_fetch hits a login wall, it should try mirrors/alternates: Google cache? Not available. Bing cache (cc.bingj)? Bing cache discontinued? r.jina.ai reader proxy! That's a big one: `https://r.jina.ai/<url>` — free tier reader that renders JS and bypasses some walls, returns markdown. Great fit for our zero-dependency design: just another URL the model can fetch.\n   - For CSDN specifically: content is in the server-rendered HTML; the wall is CSS overlay — our text extractor actually gets the full text already! Let me think: CSDN article pages are server-rendered with full content in `div#content_views`; login prompt is an overlay. So web_fetch on CSDN article URLs likely already works. Similarly 知乎 column articles (zhuanlan) are server-rendered. Zhihu answers too (initial state JSON in HTML). So the \"需要登录\" perception is partially wrong for CSDN (cosmetic wall) and partially true (Zhihu sometimes, Xiaohongshu strictly).\n   - 小红书: server returns little without login; needs signed API calls → realistically requires cookie injection.\n\n   **Tier 1 — cookie/session injection (the real \"login\" solution)**\n   - Let user paste cookies (e.g. `CLUTCH_WEB_COOKIES` env or per-domain cookie config, or a cookies.txt/Netscape file path). web_fetch adds `Cookie` header. This solves Zhihu (z_c0 cookie), CSDN, and partially Xiaohongshu (web session a1/web_session cookies) since browser cookies carry the login state.\n   - Design considerations: cookies are credentials — must not be sent to arbitrary domains! Need a scoping rule: only send a domain's cookies to that domain (and subdomains). Never log them. Storage: env var or local config file outside repo.\n   - This fits the existing architecture: `_http_get` already accepts headers dict; add cookie jar support.\n\n   **Tier 2 — headless browser (playwright) backend**\n   - For JS-rendered + signature-heavy sites, reuse the user's real browser profile (playwright with `--user-data-dir`, or connect over CDP to the user's running Chrome `--remote-debugging-port`). Then the \"login\" is whatever the user did in their own browser. Heavy: new dependency, contradicts zero-dep; but it's the robust general solution. Could be optional: `CLUTCH_BROWSER_CDP` env, off by default.\n\n   **Tier 3 — reader proxies**\n   - r.jina.ai (free, no key, renders and returns markdown), or self-hosted. Zero-dependency: model just fetches `r.jina.ai/https://...`. Caveat: rate limits, privacy (third party sees URLs), availability in this network (need testing; jina might be reachable?).\n\n3. **What's legitimate/appropriate:** Respect robots/ToS — logging in via shared cookies to scrape is a ToS gray zone; personal use with own account is common practice but should be rate-limited; don't build bulk scraping. As an agent assistant, mention this briefly and neutrally.\n\n4. **What can we implement in Clutch within the current architecture (concrete proposal):**\n   - Add `web_cookies` config: dict domain → cookie string, or simpler `CLUTCH_COOKIE_ZHIHU=...`? Cleaner: a `cookies.txt`-style local file `~/.clutch/cookies.txt` (Netscape format, exportable from browser extensions), parsed at request time, `SameSite`-style domain match before attaching.\n   - Modify `_http_get` to attach `Cookie` header when host matches.\n   - Prompt update for web_fetch: on login-wall detection (title like \"登录\", content mentions), suggest cookie or mirror strategies — better: add fallback hints in the tool doc.\n   - Optional reader-proxy fallback: if content looks like a login wall, try `r.jina.ai` — but careful: privacy & third-party. Make it opt-in via config.\n\n5. **Also worth noting the immediate zero-code answer:** test what actually happens today. CSDN articles: web_fetch likely returns full text already (server-rendered + overlay wall). Zhihu zhuanlan: likely works. Zhihu answers: often work via initial-state JSON. Xiaohongshu: fails. I can't verify now without... actually I COULD verify! Chat mode allows read-only commands, curl is available (bare curl allowed; curl without -o). I can curl a CSDN article and check whether full content is in the HTML, and a zhihu page. That would make the answer concrete and evidence-based!\n\nLet me try:\n- `curl -s -A \"Mozilla...\" https://blog.csdn.net/...` — need a real article URL. I don't have one handy; could search Bing for site:blog.csdn.net article and fetch one. That's two steps. Doable: use our own websearch module via python! `.venv/Scripts/python.exe -c \"...web_search('CSDN 某文章')...\"` then fetch the first result and check content length + whether login text appears. That's a great live experiment using the shipped tools. And for zhihu: search site:zhuanlan.zhihu.com, fetch, check.\n- Xiaohongshu: search site:xiaohongshu.com, fetch, see what comes back.\n\nThis is read-only (network GETs) — allowed in chat mode. Writing probe output to a file? That would be a write... `rm -f` earlier was allowed?? Wait, earlier I ran `rm -f websearch_live_probe.txt` in a command — that passed the whitelist?! Interesting, it did succeed earlier (\"rm -f websearch_live_probe.txt\" appended after the test command with `;`). Hmm, that was in work mode? No — this whole session is chat mode. It succeeded then. But to be safe, avoid writes; print to stdout with utf-8 reconfigure instead, or write to stdout only.\n\nLet me run the experiment:\n\n```python\nimport sys, io\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom agent.config import Config\nfrom agent.tools import websearch as ws\n# search CSDN article\nr = ws.web_search(None, Config(), 'site:blog.csdn.net transformer 教程', max_results=3)\nprint(r['content'][:800])\n```\n\nthen fetch the first URL and print first ~500 chars + length, check for \"登录\" wall markers.\n\nActually simpler: do it all in one script: search, take first URL, fetch, print stats. Do for csdn, zhihu (zhuanlan), xiaohongshu. Three fetches. Each 15s timeout max. Fine.\n\nNote: web_search(None, ...) — workspace param unused, passing None is fine (websearch never touches sb).\n\nXiaohongshu search on Bing might return xhslink.com short links which redirect to xiaohongshu.com — redirect handling works.\n\nLet me write the probe script carefully:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom agent.config import Config\nfrom agent.tools import websearch as ws\n\ncfg = Config()\nfor site, q in [(\"CSDN\", \"site:blog.csdn.net RAG 教程\"),\n                (\"知乎专栏\", \"site:zhuanlan.zhihu.com\"),\n                (\"小红书\", \"site:xiaohongshu.com 攻略\")]:\n    r = ws.web_search(None, cfg, q, max_results=2)\n    print(\"=\" * 20, site)\n    print(r[\"content\"][:500])\n    # extract first url\n    import re\n    m = re.search(r\"https?://\\S+\", r[\"content\"])\n    if m and \"error\" not in r:\n        f = ws.web_fetch(None, cfg, m.group(0))\n        c = f[\"content\"]\n        print(f\"--- fetch {m.group(0)[:80]} -> {len(c)} chars, error={f.get('error')}\")\n        print(c[:400].replace(\"\\n\", \" | \"))\n```\n\nWait — web_search signature: web_search(workspace, config, query, ...). Passing None for workspace fine. web_fetch(workspace, config, url...) likewise.\n\nCareful about the 30s command timeout: 3 searches + 3 fetches, each up to 15s → could exceed 30s! Bing RSS is fast (~1s), fetches ~1-3s each. Should be ~10s total. Risk acceptable; if timeout, split into separate runs per site.\n\nThen based on results, craft the answer:\n\nExpected outcomes (my prediction):\n- CSDN: fetch returns several-K-char article text including body (server-rendered). Wall is cosmetic → already solved by our extractor.\n- Zhihu zhuanlan: server-rendered article JSON → likely works, maybe some anti-bot 403.\n- Xiaohongshu: login wall / almost no text.\n\nThen the solution menu:\n\n**结论先行**: 部分已经解决(墙是摆设的 CSDN/知乎专栏),真正登录墙的(小红书)有三层方案,按成本排序:\n\n1. **零改动——绕路**(模型已会做): 错误即数据 + 模型自寻替代源\n2. **小改动——Cookie 注入**(推荐,~40 行): 浏览器导出 cookies.txt → `~/.clutch/cookies.txt`(或 env),`_http_get` 按域名附加 Cookie 头;关键安全设计:按域名作用域,绝不发给第三方,不写日志。这解决知乎(回答需登录时)、CSDN 全文展开、小红书 Web 端(浏览器会话 cookie + a1 签名头……注意小红书还需要 X-s 签名,纯 cookie 可能不够——诚实说明)\n3. **大改动——接真实浏览器**: CDP 连用户日常 Chrome(`--remote-debugging-port`),登录态天然继承,签名由真页面 JS 算;违反零依赖/复杂度高,做成可选后端\n4. **灰色地带——第三方 reader 代理**(r.jina.ai): 零依赖,模型直接 fetch 该前缀;隐私和可用性权衡\n\n还有合规提醒一句:用自己的账号、低频访问、尊重 ToS;别做批量爬取。\n\nImplementation sketch for Tier 2 (concrete but compact):\n\n```python\n# config.py\ncookie_file: str = field(default_factory=lambda: os.environ.get(\"CLUTCH_COOKIE_FILE\", \"\"))\n\n# websearch.py\ndef _cookie_header(url: str, jar: dict[str, str]) -> str:\n    host = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).hostname or \"\"\n    return \"; \".join(v for k, v in jar.items() if host == k or host.endswith(\".\" + k))\n\n# in _http_get: if cookies: req_headers[\"Cookie\"] = ...\n```\n\nNetscape cookies.txt parsing: ~15 lines. Domain match: suffix match per cookie's domain field.\n\nSecurity notes:\n- cookie file 在仓库外(用户目录),README 注明不入库\n- 永不 echo Cookie 头到错误消息/日志\n- 不跟随到不同域的重定向时带 cookie?严格做:重定向跨域要重算 _cookie_header(newurl) —— 我们的 _SafeRedirects 每跳都过 _assert_public_host,cookie 也要每跳重算——urllib 的 redirect handler 会保留原 headers,所以需要清除/重设。这是实现时的真坑,值得提。\n\nAlso mention: for our tool specifically the pages that need login to *render* (小红书) vs *paywall overlay* (CSDN) behave differently. And note that many \"walls\" are CSS overlays over server-rendered text — text extraction already bypasses those, which is legal-ish reading of publicly served HTML (still ToS gray, keep to personal use).\n\nLet me run the live probe now to ground the answer. I'll do one command for all three but keep result printing small. If the command times out at 30s, I'll split.\n\nActually, careful: printing Chinese to stdout — reconfigure to utf-8 as established. And the command itself must not contain Chinese (GBK arg mangling) — keep query strings ASCII! \"site:blog.csdn.net RAG tutorial\" etc. Search quality might differ but fine. Or percent-encode Chinese. Use ASCII queries to be safe: \"site:blog.csdn.net rag tutorial\", \"site:zhuanlan.zhihu.com llm\", \"site:xiaohongshu.com travel\". Hmm xiaohongshu search on Bing — fine whatever comes.\n\nLet me write the script to a heredoc? Heredoc via run_command — python -c with a long -c string: quoting pain. Better: `python - <<'EOF'` — is stdin heredoc allowed? \"Interactive commands blocked\", but `python - <<EOF` is non-interactive... The whitelist rejected `sed` in pipes before (false positive on write ops). Heredoc might pass. Earlier `python -c` worked. I'll use python -c with double quotes carefully — the script contains single quotes only for Python strings, and I wrap -c in double quotes. Contains no $ or backticks — safe.\n\nScript (ASCII only):\n\nimport sys,re\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\",errors=\"replace\")\nsys.path.insert(0,'.')\nfrom agent.config import Config\nfrom agent.tools import websearch as ws\ncfg=Config()\nfor name,q in [(\"CSDN\",\"site:blog.csdn.net rag tutorial\"),(\"ZHIHU\",\"site:zhuanlan.zhihu.com agent\"),(\"XHS\",\"site:xiaohongshu.com\")]:\n    print(\"=\"*16,name)\n    r=ws.web_search(None,cfg,q,max_results=2)\n    print(r[\"content\"][:400])\n    m=re.search(r\"https?://\\S+\",r[\"content\"])\n    if m:\n        f=ws.web_fetch(None,cfg,m.group(0))\n        c=f[\"content\"]\n        print(\"--- fetch:\",m.group(0)[:90])\n        print(\"len:\",len(c),\"error:\",f.get(\"error\"))\n        print(c[:300].replace(chr(10),\" | \"))\n\nchr(10) avoids newline-in-string quoting issues. The `\"=\"*16` fine. Double-quote wrapping: my python uses only single quotes — good. No double quotes inside except none. OK.\n\nTiming: 3*(search ~2s + fetch ~2-5s) ≈ 15s. OK.\n\nThen write the final answer. Also save_memory? The finding \"CSDN/zhihu readable without login via extractor; xhs is real wall\" is session-specific but useful project knowledge. Maybe append to the web tools memory... The memory already covers web tools; add a short memory about login-wall findings + cookie-injection plan if user wants it built. I'll save one memory noting the probe results and the proposed Tier-2 design (user hasn't approved building yet — chat mode anyway)."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789629069.141497, "id": "4584c82ca687", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\".venv/Scripts/python.exe -c \\\"\\nimport sys,re\\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8',errors='replace')\\nsys.path.insert(0,'.')\\nfrom agent.config import Config\\nfrom agent.tools import websearch as ws\\ncfg=Config()\\nfor name,q in [('CSDN','site:blog.csdn.net rag tutorial'),('ZHIHU','site:zhuanlan.zhihu.com agent'),('XHS','site:xiaohongshu.com')]:\\n    print('='*16,name)\\n    r=ws.web_search(None,cfg,q,max_results=2)\\n    print(r['content'][:400])\\n    m=re.search(r'https?://\\\\S+',r['content'])\\n    if m:\\n        f=ws.web_fetch(None,cfg,m.group(0))\\n        c=f['content']\\n        print('--- fetch:',m.group(0)[:90])\\n        print('len:',len(c),'error:',f.get('error'))\\n        print(c[:300].replace(chr(10),' | '))\\n\\\"\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_9ab1ee2cbb9e4ff582dc8d2c"}
