{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789629421.5600438, "id": "79927638a2c0", "content": "这次专门做小红书方向的开源调研。先查 GitHub(本网络 `api.github.com` 可用):", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_973c6d091f65473d8338868c", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"curl -s \\\"https://api.github.com/search/repositories?q=xiaohongshu&sort=stars&order=desc&per_page=8\\\" | grep -E \\\"full_name|\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\"|stargazers_count|pushed_at|\\\\\\\"archived\\\\\\\"\\\" | head -60\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user asks again (this was the original task question at the very start of the conversation): \"找找看小红书目前有没有开源的解决方案\" — find whether there are open-source solutions for Xiaohongshu (the login wall / content access problem).\n\nEarlier in the project (per memory), a similar GitHub survey was done for general web search backends. Now specifically for Xiaohongshu. I should do actual research — network is available (api.github.com works, Bing works, DDG doesn't from this network). Chat mode restrictions: network GETs via curl were allowed earlier in this session? Earlier (per summary) \"bare curl | head, python -c, direct grep -rn were usable\" in chat mode. But the last attempts showed .venv/Scripts/python.exe being rejected as \"cannot be proven read-only\". Bare curl might still pass. Let me try the GitHub search API via curl — that's read-only.\n\nGitHub search API: https://api.github.com/search/repositories?q=xiaohongshu&sort=stars — no auth needed (rate limit 10/min for search without token, 60/hr for core). Let me query several keywords:\n- xiaohongshu\n- 小红书 (needs URL encoding — UTF-8 percent-encoded manually: %E5%B0%8F%E7%BA%A2%E4%B9%A6)\n- xhs\n- rednote (new official English name! Xiaohongshu's international name is now \"rednote\" since early 2025)\n- \"小红书 爬虫\" spider\n\nKnown projects from my training knowledge (should verify freshness via API):\n- ReaJason/xhs — Python 签名库 (X-s signature via JS execution), was very popular (~3k+ stars), had DMCA/takedown history? I recall ReaJason/xhs was archived or removed at some point (the author took it down in 2022? There was a \"xhs\" library and the author deleted it due to legal pressure... Actually I recall ReaJason archived it). Need to check current state.\n- cv-cat/Spider_XHS — 小红书爬虫 (~2-3k stars)\n- NanmiCoder/MediaCrawler — 小红书|抖音|快手|B站|微博 crawler, very popular (~10k+ stars), actively maintained. This is THE big one now.\n- xhspy/xhs (formerly ReaJason/xhs moved?) — Actually ReaJason/xhs was taken over/moved to xhspy/xhs? I believe the xhs python lib now lives at xhspy/xhs (\"xhs\" a signature library). Let me verify via API.\n- kajweb? Sign signature service: kajweb/xhs-sign? There was \"xhs-sign\" implementing X-s locally in JS.\n- stemosa/xhs_downloader? Not sure.\n- JoeanAmier/XHS-Downloader — 小红书图文/视频下载工具 (~5k+ stars?) Tauri-based. Name might be \"JoeanAmier/XHS-Downloader\". Verify.\n- for signed: WeChat? no.\n- MediaCrawler is the flagship: supports xhs via Playwright holding login state (QR scan), cookies reuse — exactly the \"Tier 2\" approach.\n- Also \"Xhs\" MCP servers emerging in 2025: e.g. \"xiaohongshu-mcp\" projects (xpzouying/xiaohongshu-mcp? there are several MCP servers for xhs browsing/searching posting). A2A? There's \"aki66938/xiaohongshu-mcp\"? I'm not certain of names; verify via search API.\n- 签名服务: \"Xhs-Tools\"? \"xhs_signature\"? There's \"Sakura?\"... verify.\n\nPlan: use curl against api.github.com search endpoints (search/repositories with queries), parse with python? python.exe is blocked in chat mode now. Parsing JSON via python -c blocked. Alternatives: curl + grep/sed pipes? Chat whitelist misjudges pipes with sed/grep sometimes (\"echo hi | grep x\" was classified read in their classify test, so pipes with grep are fine). Earlier note: \"chat 模式命令白名单会把管道中的 sed/grep 误判为写操作而拒绝;裸 curl | head、python -c、直接 grep -rn 可用\" — so curl | head is fine.\n\nBetter: query GitHub API and pipe through `head -c` or use `grep -o` to extract fields. Or use the API with per_page=5 and just print raw JSON (it's manageable size). Fields I want: full_name, stargazers_count, pushed_at, description, archived. Raw JSON is verbose but with q and per_page=5 it's OK. I can eyeball it from output.\n\nTo reduce noise: use `curl -s \"...&per_page=5\" | grep -E '\"full_name\"|\"stargazers_count\"|\"pushed_at\"|\"archived\"|\"description\"'` — grep -E with quotes inside command... The whitelist had trouble with complex quoting; keep it simple. Maybe `curl -s URL | grep -E \"full_name|stargazers_count|description\"`. Chinese in command-line args gets GBK-mangled — avoid Chinese in queries; use percent-encoded UTF-8 for 小红书 queries: xiaohongshu works fine ASCII. \"rednote\" ASCII.\n\nAlso Bing search for recent news/alternatives: bing.com/search returns HTML (our earlier finding: format=rss for API-free). Bing web RSS: https://www.bing.com/search?q=xiaohongshu+github+crawler&format=rss — works for news-ish queries. Could search for \"小红书 开源 MCP\" — Chinese in URL → percent-encode manually.\n\nAlso verify MediaCrawler's current stats and whether it still supports xhs, and MCP servers for xhs. Also check \"xhs\" python package on PyPI? api not needed; GitHub search suffices plus maybe pypi.org/pypi/xhs/json (read-only GET).\n\nSequence (each command independent, but I want results before deciding next):\n1. curl GitHub search: q=xiaohongshu&sort=stars&per_page=8\n2. curl GitHub search: q=xhs+OR+rednote&sort=stars (GitHub search syntax: q=xhs%20rednote doesn't OR like that; use q=xhs&sort=stars and q=rednote&sort=stars separately)\n3. Maybe q=MediaCrawler to get exact stats.\n4. pypi xhs package info.\n5. Bing RSS for \"小红书 开源 爬虫 2025\" percent-encoded.\n\nThen synthesize:\n- MediaCrawler (旗舰, Playwright + 登录态, 对应我们 Tier 2)\n- Spider_XHS (requests + 签名, 简单爬取)\n- xhspy/xhs (签名库, 供自己组合)\n- JoeanAmier/XHS-Downloader (下载单个笔记, 无需登录多数情况)\n- xiaohongshu MCP servers (2025 新物种, 给 agent 用 — 和 Clutch 最相关!)\n- 签名项目: xhs-sign / js 逆向仓库, 灰色法律地带注意\n\nAnd map to our Tier framework:\n- 对应 Tier 1 (cookie): Spider_XHS 的 cookie 复用模式\n- 对应 Tier 2 (真浏览器): MediaCrawler / MCP servers (playwright)\n- 纯 HTTP 无签名: 无解 (所有活跃项目都过签名关)\n\nLegal note: 这些项目多在灰色地带,有 DMCA/封号风险;MediaCrawler README 强调仅供学习。\n\nLet me start probing. First command: GitHub search for xiaohongshu sorted by stars.\n\ncurl -s \"https://api.github.com/search/repositories?q=xiaohongshu&sort=stars&order=desc&per_page=8\" — then to trim output pipe to grep for the wanted fields. JSON is one line (GitHub API returns compact JSON? Actually it returns pretty-printed multi-line JSON — yes, GitHub API responses are pretty-printed with newlines, so grep per line works nicely).\n\nCommand: curl -s \"https://api.github.com/search/repositories?q=xiaohongshu&sort=stars&order=desc&per_page=8\" | grep -E \"full_name|\\\"description\\\"|stargazers_count|pushed_at|\\\"archived\\\"\" | head -60\n\nQuoting: double quotes around URL, grep pattern with escaped quotes — the whitelist might choke on complex quotes. Simplify: grep -E \"full_name|description|stargazers|pushed_at|archived\". Fine without inner quotes.\n\nLet me also prepare the follow-ups in parallel? They're independent — can batch multiple curl commands in one run_command with `&&`? No — each prints a lot; separate calls better for readability. I'll do two searches first (xiaohongshu, then xhs), then decide."}
