s+crawler / q=小红书 percent-encoded.\n\nNext probes:\n1. q=MediaCrawler (get stats)\n2. q=xhs&sort=stars&per_page=8 (Spider_XHS, xhs lib, XHS-Downloader dupes fine)\n3. Agent-Reach details — README to see how it accesses XHS (login? cookies?) — this is the most relevant one. Fetch its README via API: https://api.github.com/repos/Panniantong/Agent-Reach/readme with Accept: application/vnd.github.raw — pipe to head -80.\n4. xpzouying/xiaohongshu-mcp README head.\n\nBatch: run these as separate commands. First the two searches (independent) + then READMEs (independent too — I know the repo names already). I can run them in parallel tool calls? run_command calls in same block execute in order — fine, all four are independent. But output size — READMEs head -100 each. OK.\n\nChinese in URLs: avoid; use ASCII queries. 小红书 percent-encoded = %E5%B0%8F%E7%BA%A2%E4%B9%A6. For MediaCrawler search just q=MediaCrawler."}
