s_mcp` 后端 + 测试一起交付。"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789632354.9955342, "id": "d8784c9d9c8b", "content": "好的，那开始修改代码，注意这里可以考虑做成模块化+多态的插件模式，为后面部署其他mcp做好接口；同时这个功能应该是泛用性的：不能再某台没有部署这个mcp的主机上污染任何的用户体验（例如不能说“请安装小红书mcp”）或者任何诸如此类的东西，本系统的所有接口都应该是泛化的，可以设计一套统一的接口和完善的注册机制"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789632458.6149569, "id": "c1af219ecb3c", "content": "当前是 **chat 模式(只读)**，我不能改文件——请用 Run 旁边的模式按钮切到 work mode,我立即开工。先把完整设计定稿，切过去就能直接照单实现；你要的三条要求(模块化+多态、无部署也不污染体验、泛化接口+注册机制)分别落在下面三层：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_f0bcc02b41d847208b71c609", "name": "save_memory", "arguments": "{\"content\":\"Approved design for the MCP plugin backend (user said start coding; chat mode blocked it — needs work mode). Goals: modular+polymorphic plugin seam for future MCPs; zero UX footprint on hosts without a given MCP (never \\\"please install X\\\"); generalized interface + registration. Plan: NEW agent/tools/mcpprovider.py — frozen McpProvider dataclass (name, label, url config key, search_tool, search_args builder, map_results callable, optional detail_tool) + MCP_PROVIDERS registry {\\\"xiaohongshu\\\": spec mapping search_feeds -> {title,url,snippet}, url = explore/{id}?xsec_token=...}. websearch.py: wrap the 4 existing backends + MCP ones into a uniform Backend protocol (name, available(config), search(q,limit,config,get)); add _mcp_call JSON-RPC client (initialize -> notifications/initialized -> tools/call, capture Mcp-Session-Id); _available_backends = registry AND configured (mcp_urls in Config, key prefix mcp_, env CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL, settings.json same key); error text and web_search.md prompt $backends render DYNAMICALLY from configured set only (factual absence, no install advice). server.py: settings POST/GET allow mcp_* keys; /api/mcp_status per-provider reachable+login (check_login_status). UI: settings modal renders MCP rows dynamically + status dot (has_api_key precedent). Degradation matrix: unconfigured host -> backend absent from chain, unknown-backend error lists only real ones; configured+down -> BackendError \\\"MCP unreachable at <url>\\\"; not logged in -> status via settings UI, tool surface unaffected. Code text English-only; tests self-run via .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m tests.X.\",\"title\":\"MCP plugin backend design (approved, pending work mode)\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user says: \"好的,那开始修改代码\" — start modifying code. But I'm in CHAT MODE (read-only). I cannot write files. The system prompt says: \"If the task requires writing or editing files, running mutating commands, or changing anything in the workspace, do not attempt it: tell the user clearly that the task needs work mode, and that they can switch with the mode button next to Run.\"\n\nWait — let me re-read the current mode. The system prompt at the start says \"Current mode: chat (read-only).\" and gives the chat mode instructions. So yes, I must tell the user to switch to work mode.\n\nBut wait — in the first turn of this conversation, I DID successfully edit files (`edit_file` on websearch.py, tests, README). Let me re-check... In turn 1, I used `edit_file` and it worked (\"OK: edited C:\\...\\websearch.py\"). So at that point the mode must have been work mode? The system prompt says \"Current mode: chat (read-only)\" — hmm, but the first turn used edit_file successfully. Actually looking at the conversation, the first assistant turn used `edit_file` and it returned \"OK: edited\". And `run_command` ran tests. So the session started in work mode.\n\nBut NOW — the last tool calls (greps) worked (read-only). The mode header in the system prompt says \"Current mode: chat (read-only)\" and includes the whole chat-mode block: \"You are in chat mode: you can READ project files and analyze the workspace, but you must never modify it... The write_file and edit_file tools are not available, and run_command rejects anything that could write files\".\n\nThat explains why my python -c probes got rejected later (\"CHAT MODE: this command was rejected\")! The mode switched from work to chat at some point (the user toggled it, or the UI mode is per-turn?). Actually the first turn had edit_file working... then later \"CHAT MODE: this command was rejected\". So the user switched to chat mode somewhere in between (maybe after the websearch completion report). The system prompt describes the current mode as chat.\n\nSo now the user asks to start modifying code. I cannot — chat mode. I must tell them to switch to work mode with the mode button next to Run.\n\nBut I can still do useful preparation in this turn:\n1. Design the architecture concretely (modular + polymorphic plugin design) — this is valuable design work I can present now, so that when they switch to work mode, implementation is immediate.\n2. Lay out the exact file changes.\n\nThe user's requirements:\n- 模块化+多态的插件模式 (modular + polymorphic plugin pattern) — for future MCP deployments\n- 泛用性: on hosts WITHOUT this MCP deployed, zero UX pollution — never say \"请安装小红书mcp\"\n- 泛化的接口: unified interface + registration mechanism\n\nThis maps to a design:\n\n**Design: MCP backend plugin system for websearch**\n\n1. **Generic MCP tool backend** (not xiaohongshu-specific): a `_mcp_backend` class/module that can talk to ANY HTTP MCP server. Registry entries map a \"provider name\" → MCP server config (URL, tool names, result mapping).\n\n2. **Registration mechanism**: \n   - `agent/tools/mcpbackends.py` (or extend websearch.py) with a registry: `_MCP_PROVIDERS: dict[str, McpProvider]` where McpProvider is a dataclass: name, url_config_key (which Config field holds the URL), list_tools (search tool name), search_args builder, result mapper (polymorphic — each provider maps its JSON to the unified {title,url,snippet} shape), detail tool (optional), login check tool (optional).\n   - Config: generic storage — instead of `xhs_mcp_url` hardcoded, use a generic pattern? Options:\n     a. Per-provider config field `mcp_xiaohongshu_url` etc. — simple but hardcodes each new provider in Config\n     b. Generic dict `config.mcp_urls: dict[str, str]` populated from env `CLUTCH_MCP_XIAOHONGSHU_URL` + settings.json key `mcp_xiaohongshu` — provider registration declares the key name; Config holds a generic mapping. This is the \"泛化\" way: adding a new MCP = adding one McpProvider entry + (optionally) one settings-modal row... but wait, settings modal rows are hardcoded in UI. Hmm — to be fully generic, settings.json can hold arbitrary keys; the UI can render MCP URLs from a registry endpoint (`/api/mcp_providers`) — dynamic UI! That might be overkill for v1. \n   \n   Given 泛用性 requirement, the core insight: **backend availability is config-driven; absence degrades silently**. The backend chain is built from `_available_backends(config)` — MCP providers just join this function: a provider is in the chain only if its URL is configured. If not configured → simply not in chain → zero UX footprint. The model never sees \"install xiaohongshu mcp\" — web_search's error message lists only actually-available backends. The `backend` param description is dynamic: \"pin one backend: tavily | searxng | bing | ddg | xiaohongshu\" — built from registered∧configured.\n\n   Also prompts: web_search.md must be generated from the registry (it already renders $max; add $backends list dynamically).\n\n3. **Polymorphism**: \n   - Current `_BACKENDS: dict[str, callable]` — functions with uniform signature `(q, limit, config, get)`. MCP backends fit the same protocol; but with per-provider mapping logic, better to make a small class hierarchy:\n     ```python\n     class Backend(Protocol):\n         name: str\n         def available(self, config) -> bool\n         def search(self, query, limit, config, get) -> list[dict]\n     ```\n     Existing four become thin adapters; new McpBackend(base) takes a Provider spec. Actually simpler: keep function-based registry (already polymorphic via signature) and add `McpProvider` dataclass with mapper functions — the \"polymorphism\" is the uniform call signature + per-provider mapper. Don't over-engineer: the refactor skill would say keep it simple. But user explicitly asked 模块化+多态插件. So introduce a `Backend` dataclass/protocol with fields: name, available(config), search(...) — a clean seam without rewriting the 4 existing backends heavily (wrap them).\n\n4. **MCP client (JSON-RPC)**: `_mcp_call(url, tool, args)` — initialize → tools/call. MCP streamable HTTP specifics: POST JSON-RPC; need `initialize` first, capture `Mcp-Session-Id` header; then `notifications/initialized`; then `tools/call`. Some servers tolerate stateless. Must handle: connection refused (service down) → BackendError(\"xiaohongshu MCP unreachable at ...\"), auth, timeout (config.web_search_timeout), response parse → mapper. All errors as BackendError so chain falls through / error-as-data listing stays factual.\n\n5. **Xiaohongshu provider spec**:\n   - config key: `mcp_xiaohongshu` (URL)\n   - search tool: `search_feeds` {keyword, limit?} → results[].{id,title,desc,xsec_token,...} → url `https://www.xiaohongshu.com/explore/{id}?xsec_token=...&source=web_search_result_note`? The exact URL shape — xiaohongshu explore URLs include xsec_token param. Mapper: title=title, snippet=_clean_snippet(desc), url=explore link with token.\n   - optional `detail` tool: get_feed_detail (v2)\n\n6. **Login UX without polluting**: the login status check belongs to the SETTINGS UI (server endpoint `/api/mcp_status` or extend settings GET), NOT to the model's tool surface. The model-facing prompt only mentions configured backends. If service down → backend simply absent from chain or returns BackendError → factual error \"xiaohongshu: MCP unreachable at <url>\" — never instructs installing anything. Chat mode constraint: in chat mode, is web_search available? Yes (registered in both modes).\n\n7. **Settings modal**: new \"联网服务\" section rendering MCP provider rows. V1: static field for xiaohongshu (fastest); or data-driven: GET /api/settings already returns flat dict; add `mcp_providers: [{key,label,placeholder}]` from registry so UI renders dynamically — this is the 泛化 UI. Worth doing: one loop in app.js.\n\n8. **Registration mechanism completeness**: adding provider = one entry in `mcpproviders.py` + nothing else (config key discovered dynamically, UI renders from /api endpoint, web_search prompt auto-updates). That's the \"统一的接口和完善的注册机制\".\n\nAlso tests: offline tests with fake JSON-RPC (monkeypatch _mcp_post), availability gating (unconfigured → not in chain, not in prompt), error-as-data when service down, mapper unit tests, settings roundtrip.\n\nPlan of file changes (for work mode):\n1. `agent/tools/mcpprovider.py` (NEW): McpProvider dataclass + PROVIDERS registry + xiaohongshu spec (or put in websearch.py? Modular → separate module, websearch imports it. registry.py imports websearch only).\n2. `agent/tools/websearch.py`: \n   - refactor `_BACKENDS` dict entries into `Backend` records with `available()` (tavily/searxng gain their key/url checks moved in — dedup with web_search's inline checks)\n   - `_mcp_call` JSON-RPC client\n   - chain assembly from registry ∧ config; dynamic backend list in errors and prompt render\n   - `web_search` returns unified; `detail` passthrough for providers that define it? Keep v1: search only; detail via follow-up? get_feed_detail needs feed_id+xsec_token which search results carry in URL; a `web_fetch` on that URL won't work (JS). So map... The model could call web_search(backend=\"xiaohongshu\", query, detail_of=...)? Cleaner: keep v1 search-only, detail later. State this.\n3. `agent/config.py`: generic `mcp_urls: dict` assembled in factory from env + settings (or explicit fields xhs_mcp_url; generic dict better matches 泛化: `mcp_xiaohongshu` key).\n4. `agent/server.py`: settings POST/GET allow `mcp_*` keys generically (prefix-based allowlist) + `/api/mcp_status` endpoint returning per-provider reachable+login state.\n5. `ui/index.html`/`app.js`/`main.js`: dynamic MCP rows from settings GET (`mcp_providers` meta) + status dots.\n6. `agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md`: render `$backends` dynamically.\n7. `tests/websearch_test.py` (extend) or `tests/mcpbackend_test.py`: mapper, gating, errors, JSON-RPC handshake with fake server.\n8. README update.\n\nThe critical \"no UX pollution\" guarantees:\n- Unconfigured host: provider absent from chain; `backend=xiaohongshu` → \"unknown backend ...; available: tavily | searxng | bing | ddg\" — factual, no installation advice.\n- Configured but down: \"xiaohongshu: MCP unreachable at http://...\" — factual. Model decides.\n- Prompt text: lists only configured backends; tool schema description built dynamically.\n- Settings UI: status dot neutral (\"未配置\" not \"请安装\").\n\nSo my reply: cannot edit in chat mode → ask to switch; but deliver the full design blueprint now (architecture diagram, interfaces, file-by-file plan, degradation matrix) so work mode starts instantly. Also maybe save_memory the design so it persists. Yes — save_memory with the design. That's allowed (memory tool, not workspace).\n\nMermaid diagram of plugin architecture:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    subgraph reg[\"注册层(唯一扩展点)\"]\n        R[\"MCP_PROVIDERS: McpProvider 数据类<br/>name / url_key / search tool / mapper\"]\n    end\n    subgraph core[\"websearch 核心(不认识任何具体平台)\"]\n        AVAIL[\"_available_backends: 注册 ∧ 已配置\"]\n        CHAIN[\"回退链\"]\n        CALL[\"_mcp_call: JSON-RPC initialize + tools/call\"]\n    end\n    subgraph surf[\"呈现层(全部动态生成)\"]\n        P[\"web_search 提示词 $backends\"]\n        S[\"设置弹窗 MCP 行(/api 动态)\"]\n    end\n    R --> AVAIL --> CHAIN\n    R --> P\n    R --> S\n    CHAIN --> CALL --> X[\"任意 HTTP MCP 服务\"]\n```\n\nCareful with mermaid rules: no nested double quotes; use single quotes inside labels. \"web_search 提示词 $backends\" fine.\n\nInterface sketch:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass McpProvider:\n    name: str                      # \"xiaohongshu\"\n    label: str                     # settings-modal label\n    search_tool: str               # \"search_feeds\"\n    search_args: Callable[[str, int], dict]\n    map_results: Callable[[Any], list[dict]]   # -> [{title,url,snippet}]\n    detail_tool: str | None = None # \"get_feed_detail\" (v2)\n\nMCP_PROVIDERS: dict[str, McpProvider] = {\"xiaohongshu\": XIAOHONGSHU}\n```\n\nConfig: `mcp_urls: dict[str,str]` — populated from settings.json/env prefix `mcp_` / `CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL`. Backend available iff provider.name in config.mcp_urls.\n\nDegradation matrix table.\n\nAlso mention: no pytest, self-run tests; English-only text in code (project convention).\n\nKeep response focused: 1) state mode limitation clearly, 2) deliver design, 3) exact implementation order for work mode. Save memory too."}
