n_status. Generic: provider.status_tool + status_args? McpProvider: status_check: Callable[[json], str] mapping response to one of \"ok\"/\"not_logged_in\". Reachable = RPC succeeds. v1: reachable = initialize handshake ok; login = call check_login_status → parse.\n\nUI: keep it modest — settings modal gets a dynamic section \"MCP 服务\" listing providers from GET /api/settings (add meta: mcp_providers: [{key:\"mcp_xiaohongshu\", label:\"小红书 MCP\", placeholder:\"http://localhost:18060/mcp\"}]) + one input each + status text fetched from /api/mcp_status. main.js mirror: need to see how settings.json mirror is built (renderer copy → file). app.js 2765-2793 area.\n\nwebsearch.py changes in detail:\n\nCurrent structure (to confirm after reads):\n- _BACKENDS: dict[str, callable], _DEFAULT_CHAIN: tuple\n- _available_backends(config) -> tuple (checks tavily key, searxng url)\n- web_search: backend param validation against _BACKENDS, per-backend key checks inline (lines 456-459), chain loop with BackendError/WebError catch\n\nNew:\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass HttpBackend:  # or generic Backend record\n    name: str\n    search: Callable  # (q, limit, config, get) -> list\n    available: Callable[[Config], bool] = lambda c: True\n\n_BACKENDS: dict[str, Backend] = {...tavily, searxng, bing, ddg, + mcp ones from provider registry}\n```\nAnd mcp backend factory: `_mcp_backend(provider) -> Backend`.\n\n_available_backends: [b.name for b in _BACKENDS.values() if b.available(config)] — dynamic chain. bing/ddg always available; tavily if key; searxng if url; xiaohongshu if url.\n\nweb_search backend param: if backend not in available → error lists available (factual). If backend given but not registered at all → same message. Never mention unconfigured.\n\n_mcp_call details (stdlib urllib):\n```python\ndef _mcp_call(url, tool, args, timeout, cancel=None):\n    # initialize\n    body = {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2025-03-26\",\"capabilities\":{},\"clientInfo\":{\"name\":\"clutch\",\"version\":\"0.1\"}}}\n    resp = _http_get? no — POST. _http_get is GET-only. Need _http_post or extend _http_get with method/body — _http_get already has method/body params! (line 123-124: method: str = \"GET\", body: bytes | None = None). \n```\n_http_get(url, timeout, cancel, method, body, headers, max_bytes) — it accepts POST already. But _assert_public_host rejects localhost! For MCP calls to localhost we must bypass. Options: separate thin poster that skips public-host guard (guard is for model-controlled URLs). Write `_mcp_post(url, payload, timeout, session_id)` using urllib directly with its own error→WebError mapping. Reuse _drain? Keep simple: dedicated small function.\n\nJSON-RPC response: MCP streamable HTTP may respond with SSE (text/event-stream) for notifications... For requests with id, server responds application/json typically (mcp-go supports both). xiaohongshu-mcp curl example suggests plain JSON responses. Handle content-type json primarily; if SSE, parse `data:` lines — add minimal fallback parsing for robustness.\n\nSession: initialize response headers → Mcp-Session-Id; then send notifications/initialized (notification = no id) with header; then tools/call with header.\n\nAlso each call new session — fine (13 tools, stateless-ish). Cache per-call: helper `_mcp_session(url, timeout)` returns (post_fn) doing init once; then tools/call. For web_search one call per search — init+call = 2 round trips, acceptable (localhost).\n\ntools/call result shape: {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"result\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<json string>\"}],...}} — mcp servers return text content usually JSON-encoded. Mapper: parse result.content[0].text as JSON → list of feeds. Need defensive: text may be JSON array or object with data key. Xiaohongshu-mcp returns? Unknown exactly. Make map_results defensive: accept list, or dict with \"data\"/\"items\"/\"feeds\" key. I'll write tolerant extraction: find first list under common keys.\n\nURL construction: need real field names from search_feeds response. I don't know exactly (id/note_id? title? desc? xsec_token?). Defensive mapper: id = item.get(\"id\") or item.get(\"note_id\"); title = item.get(\"title\") or \"\"; desc = item.get(\"desc\") or item.get(\"description\") or \"\"; token = item.get(\"xsec_token\"); url = f\"https://www.xiaohongshu.com/explore/{id}\" + (f\"?xsec_token={token}\" if token). user nickname optional in snippet? Keep title/snippet.\n\nlive test for xiaohongshu: not required (service not installed here). Offline tests with fake POST monkeypatched.\n\nTests: tests/mcpbackend_test.py:\n- mapper maps feed dict → result (title/url/snippet, token in url)\n- mapper tolerates nested {\"data\": [...]}\n- _mcp_call handshake: fake server via monkeypatched _mcp_post capturing payloads: assert initialize then tools/call with session id propagated; parse response\n- gating: Config(mcp_urls={}) → xiaohongshu not in available backends; web_search(backend=\"xiaohongshu\") → unknown-backend error listing only real ones (no \"install\" wording)\n- configured: Config with mcp_urls → chain includes it; _mcp_post error → BackendError → error-as-data with factual message\n- registry/prompt: render web_search.md includes only configured backends? prompt render happens in registry.py build_default_tools — test that chat/work tools' web_search description contains \"bing\" always but \"xiaohongshu\" only when configured.\n\nserver_test extension? /api/mcp_status + settings POST mcp key — maybe add to mcpbackend_test via direct function calls instead of HTTP e2e (server_test exists for e2e; adding there is heavier). Keep unit-level: test _settings allowlist function if factored. I'll factor settings key filtering into a helper `_mergeable_settings(data)`.\n\nUI: app.js settings modal — need to read the settings modal HTML in index.html and app.js settings save/load. Add dynamic section. main.js mirro