sion: flatten untouched.)\n\nAll recon done. Now write the new module first. \n[Assistant tool call]: write_file({\"path\":\"agent/tools/mcpprovider.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Registry of external MCP tool servers that extend web search.\\n\\nOne entry per platform turns a generic HTTP MCP server into a web_search\\nbackend: the provider names its config key, the tool to call, and how to map\\nits results onto the uniform {title, url, snippet} shape. Adding a platform\\nmeans adding one McpProvider here — the search chain, the rendered prompt and\\nthe settings UI all pick it up without further changes.\\n\\nHosts without a given service configured simply leave the URL empty: the\\nbackend is then absent from the chain and nothing in the UI or the prompts\\nmentions it. This module must stay import-safe from anywhere (stdlib only,\\nno agent-package imports).\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport os\\nimport urllib.parse\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\\nfrom typing import Any, Callable\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass McpProvider:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Declarative spec for one MCP-backed search source.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    name: str                                   # backend name (web_search backend=<name>)\\n    label: str                                  # human label for the settings modal\\n    search_tool: str                            # MCP tool invoked for searches\\n    search_args: Callable[[str, int], dict]     # (query, limit) -> tool arguments\\n    map_results: Callable[[Any], list[dict]]    # parsed tool result -> [{title,url,snippet}]\\n    placeholder: str = \\\"\\\"                       # example URL shown in the settings modal\\n    status_tool: str = \\\"\\\"                       # optional MCP tool reporting login state\\n\\n    def url_for(self, config: Any) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Configured endpoint for this provider ('' = not configured here).\\n\\n        Settings-modal values land in Config.mcp_urls under the provider name;\\n        CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL is the env-only equivalent.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        v = config.mcp_urls.get(self.name) or os.environ.get(\\n            f\\\"CLUTCH_MCP_{self.name.upper()}_URL\\\", \\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        return v.rstrip(\\\"/\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _mcp_providers_registry() -> dict[str, McpProvider]:\\n    ...\\n\"}])\n[Tool result]: ERROR: write_file content has an invalid JSON string escape (\\n inside... acceptable? Actually error: \"content has an invalid escape\". Retry with literal newlines via the tool's content field — the harness passes content as a real string; my \\n were fine before in edit_file... The previous write_file calls this session used real newlines. The failure: I embedded \\\" escaped quotes plus \\\\n — mixed. Resend with plain text content (real newlines, normal quotes). \n\nRetry with clean content (no \\\" escaping issues — write content directly): \n[Assistant tool call]: write_file({\"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Registry of external MCP tool servers that extend web search.\\n\\nOne entry per platform turns a generic HTTP MCP server into a web_search\\nbackend: the provider names its config key, the tool to call, and how to map\\nits results onto the uniform {title, url, snippet} shape. Adding a platform\\nmeans adding one McpProvider here — the search chain, the rendered prompt and\\nthe settings UI all pick it up without further changes.\\n\\nHosts without a given service configured simply leave the URL empty: the\\nbackend is then absent from the chain and nothing in the UI or the prompts\\nmentions it. This module must stay import-safe from anywhere (stdlib only,\\nno agent-package imports).\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport os\\nimport urllib.parse\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom typing import Any, Callable\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass McpProvider:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Declarative spec for one MCP-backed search source.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    name: str                                   # backend name (web_search backend=<name>)\\n    label: str                                  # human label for the settings modal\\n    search_tool: str                            # MCP tool invoked for searches\\n    search_args: Callable[[str, int], dict]     # (query, limit) -> tool arguments\\n    map_results: Callable[[Any], list[dict]]    # parsed tool result -> [{title,url,snippet}]\\n    placeholder: str = \\\"\\\"                       # example URL shown in the settings modal\\n    status_tool: str = \\\"\\\"                       # optional MCP tool reporting login state\\n\\n    def url_for(self, config: Any) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Configured endpoint ('' = not configured on this machine).\\n\\n        Settings-modal values land in Config.mcp_urls under the provider name;\\n        CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL is the env-only equivalent.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        v = config.mcp_urls.get(self.name) or os.environ.get(\\n            f\\\"CLUTCH_MCP_{self.name.upper()}_URL\\\", \\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        return v.rstrip(\\\"/\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ---- result mapping helpers --------------------------------------------------\\n\\n\\ndef _first_list(data: Any) -> list:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pull the first list value out of a tool result (bare list or wrapped).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if isinstance(data, list):\\n        return data\\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\\n        for key in (\\\"data\\\", \\\"items\\\", \\\"feeds\\\", \\\"results\\\", \\\"notes\\\"):\\n            if isinstance(data.get(key), list):\\n                return data[key]\\n    return []\\n\\n\\n# ---- concrete providers ------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n\\ndef _xhs_args(query: str, limit: int) -> dict:\\n    return {\\\"keyword\\\": query, \\\"limit\\\": limit}\\n\\n\\ndef _xhs_map(data: Any) -> list[dict]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"search_feeds results -> uniform rows. Keeps xsec_token in the URL:\\n    follow-up detail calls (and the site itself) require it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rows = []\\n    for it in _first_list(data):\\n        if not isinstance(it, dict):\\n            continue\\n        note_id = str(it.get(\\\"id\\\") or it.get(\\\"note_id\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n        if not note_id:\\n            continue\\n        url = f\\\"https://www.xiaohongshu.com/explore/{note_id}\\\"\\n        token = str(it.get(\\\"xsec_token\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n        if token:\\n            url += \\\"?\\\" + urllib.parse.urlencode({\\\"xsec_token\\\": token})\\n        rows.append(\\n            {\\n                \\\"title\\\": str(it.get(\\\"title\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip(),\\n                \\\"url\\\": url,\\n                \\\"snippet\\\": str(it.get(\\\"desc\\\") or it.get(\\\"description\\\") or \\\"\\\").strip(),\\n            }\\n        )\\n    return rows\\n\\n\\ndef _xhs_status_args() -> dict:\\n    return {}\\n\\n\\nXIAOHONGSHU = McpProvider(\\n    name=\\\"xiaohongshu\\\",\\n    label=\\\"Xiaohongshu MCP\\\",\\n    search_tool=\\\"search_feeds\\\",\\n    search_args=_xhs_args,\\n    map_results=_xhs_map,\\n    placeholder=\\\"http://localhost:18060/mcp\\\",\\n    status_tool=\\\"check_login_status\\\",\\n)\\n\\n# The registry. Extension point: add one entry, everything else follows\\n# (search chain, rendered prompt, settings modal rows).\\nMCP_PROVIDERS: dict[str, McpProvider] = {\\n    \\\"xiaohongshu\\\": XIAOHONGSHU,\\n}\\n\", \"path\":\"agent/tools/mcpprovider.py\"})\n[Tool result]: OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\agent\\tools\\mcpprovider.py (91 lines)\n\n(_xhs_status_args is unused — drop it on the next edit to keep the module clean. Now the websearch.py refactor: imports, Backend record, _mcp_rpc/_mcp_call, MCP backend join, dynamic available, unified factual errors.) \n[Assistant tool call]: edit_file({\"new_string\":\"from dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom html import unescape\\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\\n\\nfrom .mcpprovider import McpProvider, MCP_PROVIDERS\",\"old_string\":\"from dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom html import unescape\\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\",\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"})\n[Tool result]: OK: edited (+2 -0 lines). Now the Backend record + registry rewrite. Replace lines 414-435 block: \n[Assistant tool call]: edit_file({\"new_string\":\"# ---- registry ---------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Backend:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One search source: uniform call shape, plus its own gating rule.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    name: str\\n    search: Callable[[str, int, Any, Callable[..., HttpResp]], list[dict[str, str]]]\\n    available: Callable[[Any], bool] = lambda config: True\\n\\n\\n_BACKENDS: dict[str, Backend] = {\\n    \\\"tavily\\\": Backend(\\\"tavily\\\", _tavily, lambda c: bool(c.tavily_api_key)),\\n    \\\"searxng\\\": Backend(\\\"searxng\\\", _searxng, lambda c: bool(c.searxng_url)),\\n    \\\"bing\\\": Backend(\\\"bing\\\", _bing),\\n    \\\"ddg\\\": Backend(\\\"ddg\\\", _ddg),\\n}\\n_DEFAULT_CHAIN = tuple(_BACKENDS)\\n\\n\\ndef _mcp_backend(provider: McpProvider) -> Backend:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Adapt an MCP provider to the uniform Backend shape.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def search(q: str, limit: int, config: Any, get) -> list[dict[str, str]]:\\n        data = _mcp_call(\\n            provider.url_for(config),\\n            provider.search_tool,\\n            provider.search_args(q, limit),\\n            config.web_search_timeout,\\n        )\\n        rows = provider.map_results(data)\\n        if not rows:\\n            raise BackendError(f\\\"{provider.name}: no results\\\")\\n        return rows[:limit]\\n\\n    return Backend(provider.name, search, lambda c, p=provider: bool(p.url_for(c)))\\n\\n\\nfor _p in MCP_PROVIDERS.values():\\n    _BACKENDS[_p.name] = _mcp_backend(_p)\\n\\n\\n# Try order, filtered by what is configured on this machine. Kept as a function\\n# so the description in prompts can be rendered from it too.\\ndef _available_backends(config: Config) -> tuple[str, ...]:\\n    return tuple(b.name for b in _BACKENDS.values() if b.available(config))\", \"old_string\":\"# ---- registry ---------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n\\n_BACKENDS: dict[str, Any] = {\\n    \\\"tavily\\\": _tavily,\\n    \\\"searxng\\\": _searxng,\\n    \\\"bing\\\": _bing,\\n    \\\"ddg\\\": _ddg,\\n}\\n_DEFAULT_CHAIN = tuple(_BACKENDS)\\n\\n\\n# Try order, filtered by what is configured on this machine. Kept as a function\\n# so the description in prompts can be rendered from it too.\\ndef _available_backends(config: Config) -> tuple[str, ...]:\\n    out = []\\n    for name in _DEFAULT_CHAIN:\\n        if name == \\\"tavily\\\" and not config.tavily_api_key:\\n            continue\\n        if name == \\\"searxng\\\" and not config.searxng_url:\\n            continue\\n        out.append(name)\\n    return tuple(out)\", \"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"})\n[Tool result]: OK: edited. Note: _DEFAULT_CHAIN now unused inside websearch (used by turn-1-era error text at line 453 and possibly tests) — keep it as the documented base order; it still equals the first four names. Now the JSON-RPC client, inserted before the registry section: \n[Assistant tool call]: edit_file({\"new_string\":\"# ---- HTTP MCP (JSON-RPC over POST) ------------------------------------------\\n\\n_MCP_PROTO = \\\"2025-03-26\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _mcp_rpc(\\n    url: str,\\n    payload: dict,\\n    session: str | None,\\n    timeout: float,\\n    cancel: Any = None,\\n) -> tuple[dict, str | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One JSON-RPC POST to an HTTP MCP server; returns (response, session id).\\n\\n    Deliberately NOT routed through _http_get: the SSRF guard exists for\\n    model-controlled URLs, while this endpoint comes from operator config and\\n    is typically loopback. Errors become WebError so callers treat MCP\\n    failures like any other backend failure.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if cancel is not None and cancel.is_set():\\n        raise WebError(\\\"aborted by user\\\")\\n    body = json.dumps(payload).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    headers = {\\n        \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\",\\n        \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json, text/event-stream\\\",\\n    }\\n    if session:\\n        headers[\\\"Mcp-Session-Id\\\"] = session\\n    request = urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=headers, method=\\\"POST\\\")\\n    try:\\n        resp = urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=timeout)\\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"HTTP {e.code} from MCP server {url}\\\") from e\\n    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\\n        reason = getattr(e, \\\"reason\\\", e)\\n        if isinstance(reason, (socket.timeout, TimeoutError)):\\n            raise WebError(f\\\"MCP server timed out after {timeout:.0f}s: {url}\\\")\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"MCP server unreachable ({reason}): {url}\\\") from e\\n    except (ValueError, OSError) as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"MCP request failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n    with resp:\\n        raw = _drain(resp, cancel, _MAX_BYTES)\\n    sid = resp.headers.get(\\\"Mcp-Session-Id\\\") or session\\n    text = _decode_body(raw, resp.headers.get(\\\"Content-Type\\\", \\\"\\\"))\\n    if \\\"text/event-stream\\\" in text[:64] or text.startswith(\\\"event:\\\") or \\\"\\\\ndata:\\\" in text:\\n        # SSE-framed response: keep the last data frame (the JSON-RPC reply)\\n        frames = [ln[5:].strip() for ln in text.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\\\"data:\\\")]\\n        text = frames[-1] if frames else \\\"\\\"\\n    if not text.strip():\\n        return {}, sid  # e.g. 202 Accepted for notifications\\n    try:\\n        data = json.loads(text)\\n    except ValueError as e:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"MCP server returned non-JSON: {e}\\\") from e\\n    if isinstance(data, dict) and data.get(\\\"error\\\"):\\n        msg = data[\\\"error\\\"].get(\\\"message\\\", str(data[\\\"error\\\"])) if isinstance(data[\\\"error\\\"], dict) else str(data[\\\"error\\\"])\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"MCP error: {msg[:200]}\\\")\\n    return (data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}), sid\\n\\n\\ndef _mcp_call(\\n    url: str,\\n    tool: str,\\n    args: dict,\\n    timeout: float,\\n    cancel: Any = None,\\n) -> Any:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"initialize -> tools/call against an HTTP MCP server; returns the parsed\\n    tool output (JSON when it parses, else the plain text).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    hello = {\\n        \\\"jsonrpc\\\": \\\"2.0\\\",\\n        \\\"id\\\": 1,\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"initialize\\\",\\n        \\\"params\\\": {\\n            \\\"protocolVersion\\\": _MCP_PROTO,\\n            \\\"capabilities\\\": {},\\n            \\\"clientInfo\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"clutch\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.1\\\"},\\n        },\\n    }\\n    _, session = _mcp_rpc(url, hello, None, timeout, cancel)\\n    if session:\\n        _mcp_rpc(\\n            url,\\n            {\\\"jsonrpc\\\": \\\"2.0\\\", \\\"method\\\": \\\"notifications/initialized\\\"},\\n            session,\\n            timeout,\\n            cancel,\\n        )\\n    resp, _ = _mcp_rpc(\\n        url,\\n        {\\\"jsonrpc\\\": \\\"2.0\\\", \\\"id\\\": 2, \\\"method\\\": \\\"tools/call\\\", \\\"params\\\": {\\\"name\\\": tool, \\\"arguments\\\": args}},\\n        session,\\n        timeout,\\n        cancel,\\n    )\\n    result = resp.get(\\\"result\\\") or {}\\n    parts = result.get(\\\"content\\\") or []\\n    text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(\\n        p.get(\\\"text\\\", \\\"\\\") for p in parts if isinstance(p, dict) and p.get(\\\"type\\\") == \\\"text\\\"\\n    ).strip()\\n    if result.get(\\\"isError\\\") and text:\\n        raise WebError(f\\\"MCP tool error: {text[:200]}\\\")\\n    try:\\n        return json.loads(text)\\n    except ValueError:\\n        return text\\n\\n\\n# ---- registry ---------------------------------------------------------------\", \"old_string\":\"# ---- registry ---------------------------------------------------------------\", \"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"})\n[Tool result]: OK: edited. Now web_search's backend validation — unify to factual, dynamic messages: \n[Assistant tool call]: edit_file({\"new_string\":\"    limit = max(1, min(int(max_results or config.web_search_max_results), 20))\\n    available = _available_backends(config)\\n    if backend:\\n        if backend not in available:\\n            return {\\n                \\\"content\\\": f\\\"ERROR: backend {backend!r} is not available; \\\"\\n                           + \\\"available: \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(available),\\n                \\\"error\\\": True,\\n            }\\n        chain = (backend,)\\n    else:\\n        chain = available\", \"old_string\":\"    limit = max(1, min(int(max_results or config.web_search_max_results), 20))\\n    if backend:\\n        if backend not in _BACKENDS:\\n            return {\\n                \\\"content\\\": f\\\"ERROR: unknown backend {backend!r}; available: \\\"\\n                           + \\\", \\\".join(_DEFAULT_CHAIN),\\n                \\\"error\\\": True,\\n            }\\n        if backend == \\\"tavily\\\" and not config.tavily_api_key:\\n            return {\\\"content\\\": \\\"ERROR: tavily needs CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY\\\", \\\"error\\\": True}\\n        if backend == \\\"searxng\\\" and not config.searxng_url:\\n            return {\\\"content\\\": \\\"ERROR: searxng needs CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL\\\", \\\"error\\\": True}\\n        chain = (backend,)\\n    else:\\n        chain = _available_backends(config)\", \"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"})\n[Tool result]: OK: edited. And the loop now reads Backend records: \n[Assistant tool call]: edit_file({\"new_string\":\"    for name in chain:\\n        fn = _BACKENDS[name].search\", \"old_string\":\"    for name in chain:\\n        fn = _BACKENDS[name]\", \"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"})\n[T