{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789633542.0445745, "id": "801a24fe6984", "tool_call_id": "call_e7e641a90e0f48eb9f9480d7", "content": "[MCP plugin backend design (approved, pending work mode)]\nApproved design for the MCP plugin backend (user said start coding; chat mode blocked it — needs work mode). Goals: modular+polymorphic plugin seam for future MCPs; zero UX footprint on hosts without a given MCP (never \"please install X\"); generalized interface + registration. Plan: NEW agent/tools/mcpprovider.py — frozen McpProvider dataclass (name, label, url config key, search_tool, search_args builder, map_results callable, optional detail_tool) + MCP_PROVIDERS registry {\"xiaohongshu\": spec mapping search_feeds -> {title,url,snippet}, url = explore/{id}?xsec_token=...}. websearch.py: wrap the 4 existing backends + MCP ones into a uniform Backend protocol (name, available(config), search(q,limit,config,get)); add _mcp_call JSON-RPC client (initialize -> notifications/initialized -> tools/call, capture Mcp-Session-Id); _available_backends = registry AND configured (mcp_urls in Config, key prefix mcp_, env CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL, settings.json same key); error text and web_search.md prompt $backends render DYNAMICALLY from configured set only (factual absence, no install advice). server.py: settings POST/GET allow mcp_* keys; /api/mcp_status per-provider reachable+login (check_login_status). UI: settings modal renders MCP rows dynamically + status dot (has_api_key precedent). Degradation matrix: unconfigured host -> backend absent from chain, unknown-backend error lists only real ones; configured+down -> BackendError \"MCP unreachable at <url>\"; not logged in -> status via settings UI, tool surface unaffected. Code text English-only; tests self-run via .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m tests.X.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
