{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789633637.5535374, "id": "07dee403b02f", "tool_call_id": "call_8845245fd6934b3191aa0703", "content": "1: \"\"\"API-only HTTP + SSE server hosting the agent (the UI is a separate app).\n2: \n3: Endpoints (all JSON except SSE/NDJSON):\n4:   POST /api/project/new    {dir, name} -> create a .clc project file\n5:   POST /api/project/open   {path} -> load a .clc project (NDJSON stream)\n6:   POST /api/run            {task} -> start run on the active project (409 if busy)\n7:   POST /api/stop           cancel the running agent\n8:   GET  /api/events         SSE: replay active project history, then live events\n9:   GET  /api/workspace/tree   file tree under the project's working directory\n10:   GET  /api/health         {ok}\n11: \n12: CORS is wide open (Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *) so the decoupled UI can live\n13: on another origin/host. The API key travels in request bodies, not cookies, so a\n14: wildcard origin leaks nothing. Bind --host 0.0.0.0 to expose beyond localhost.\n15: \n16: The agent's existing sink is fed into a thread-safe broadcaster; each SSE subscriber\n17: gets a private queue. One run at a time; Stop sets a cancel flag checked by the loop.\n18: \"\"\"\n19: \n20: from __future__ import annotations\n21: \n22: import argparse\n23: import dataclasses\n24: import json\n25: import posixpath\n26: import queue\n27: import sys\n28: import threading\n29: from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n30: from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath\n31: from typing import Any\n32: from urllib.parse import parse_qs, urlparse\n33: \n34: from . import browsing\n35: from .base import BaseServer, Broadcaster, RunState\n36: from .config import REASONING_EFFORT_LEVELS, Config, flatten_settings\n37: from .core.project_lock import ProjectLock, ProjectOpenConflict\n38: from .events import (\n39:     Event,\n40:     FinalEvent,\n41:     PermissionRequestEvent,\n42:     StateUpdateEvent,\n43:     event_to_json,\n44: )\n45: from .project import Project, create_project, open_project_lazy\n46: from .tools.workspace import Workspace\n47: \n48: # a client hanging up mid-SSE surfaces as one of these on the socket write;\n49: # end cleanly, never let socketserver print a traceback. The class is host\n50: # dependent: POSIX gives BrokenPipeError (EPIPE) or ConnectionResetError\n51: # (ECONNRESET) when the peer is gone, Windows gives ConnectionAbortedError\n52: # (WSAECONNABORTED/WSAECONNRESET), so leaving it out spams one traceback per\n53: # closed window on Windows. ValueError covers a write on an already-closed\n54: # stream.\n55: _SSE_ERR = (BrokenPipeError, ConnectionResetError, ConnectionAbortedError, ValueError)\n... (showing lines 1-55 of 772; use offset=56 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
