{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789633864.2963266, "id": "9ee34dfe7b6d", "tool_call_id": "call_5904abf06ec44d42a6fc1ea4", "content": "38:   </div>\n39: \n40:   <div id=\"settings-modal\" class=\"modal hidden\">\n41:     <div class=\"modal-box\">\n42:       <h3>Settings</h3>\n43:       <label for=\"llm-profile-select\">Saved profiles</label>\n44:       <div class=\"fs-conn-row\" style=\"margin-bottom: 16px\">\n45:         <div id=\"llm-profile-select\" class=\"cselect\" title=\"pick a saved profile to apply it\"></div>\n46:         <button id=\"llm-profile-new\" title=\"add a new profile\">＋ New</button>\n47:         <button id=\"llm-profile-edit\" title=\"edit the selected profile\">Edit</button>\n48:         <button id=\"llm-profile-del\" title=\"delete the selected profile\">Delete</button>\n49:       </div>\n50:       <div class=\"modal-actions\">\n51:         <button id=\"settings-close\" class=\"ghost\">Cancel</button>\n52:       </div>\n53:     </div>\n54:   </div>\n55: \n56:   <div id=\"llm-profile-modal\" class=\"modal hidden\">\n57:     <div class=\"modal-box\">\n58:       <h3 id=\"llm-profile-title\">New LLM profile</h3>\n59:       <label for=\"llm-profile-name\">Profile name</label>\n60:       <input id=\"llm-profile-name\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" />\n61:       <p id=\"llm-profile-error\" class=\"llm-profile-error hidden\"></p>\n62:       <label for=\"llm-url-input\">LLM API base URL</label>\n63:       <input id=\"llm-url-input\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" />\n64:       <label for=\"api-key-input\">API key</label>\n65:       <input id=\"api-key-input\" type=\"password\" autocomplete=\"off\" />\n66:       <label for=\"model-input\">Model</label>\n67:       <input id=\"model-input\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" />\n68:       <label for=\"reasoning-effort-input\">Reasoning effort</label>\n69:       <div id=\"reasoning-effort-input\" class=\"cselect\"></div>\n70:       <div class=\"modal-actions\">\n71:         <button id=\"llm-profile-cancel\">Cancel</button>\n72:         <button id=\"llm-profile-save\" class=\"primary\">Save</button>\n73:       </div>\n... (showing lines 38-73 of 272; use offset=74 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789633864.3022246, "id": "cdeb2913f4a4", "tool_call_id": "call_2fb31092ae1a478186ef095d", "content": "244:         tunnelLog(`[backend] api:base failed: ${err && err.message}`);\n245:         return DEFAULT_API_BASE;\n246:       }\n247:     });\n248: \n249:     // The flat mirror file the backend + LLM proxy read; the UI's localStorage\n250:     // is the source of truth, this file is (re)written on every UI save.\n251:     function writeSettingsFile(data) {\n252:       const p = path.join(os.homedir(), \".clutch\", \"settings.json\");\n253:       let cur = {};\n254:       try {\n255:         cur = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p, \"utf-8\"));\n256:       } catch (e) {\n257:         /* first save: start from an empty file */\n258:       }\n259:       if (cur && cur.profiles) {\n260:         cur = cur.profiles[cur.active] || {}; // legacy map: keep the active profile's values\n261:       }\n262:       const upd = {};\n263:       for (const k of [\"base_url\", \"model\"]) {\n264:         if (data && data[k]) upd[k] = data[k];\n265:       }\n266:       if (data && data.api_key) upd.api_key = data.api_key;\n267:       // empty string clears the knob (provider default), undefined keeps it\n268:       if (data && data.reasoning_effort !== undefined) upd.reasoning_effort = data.reasoning_effort;\n269:       const flat = Object.assign({}, cur, upd);\n270:       fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(p), { recursive: true });\n271:       fs.writeFileSync(p, JSON.stringify(flat, null, 2), { mode: 0o600 });\n272:     }\n273: \n274:     ipcMain.handle(\"settings:save\", async (_e, data) => {\n275:       try {\n276:         writeSettingsFile(data);\n277:         return { ok: true };\n278:       } catch (e) {\n279:         return { ok: false, error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\n280:       }\n281:     });\n282: \n283:     // Self-heal the mirror: settings.json is derived state that session\n284:     // children (LLM config) and the LLM proxy read, but only a UI save\n285:     // recreates it — if it went missing/corrupt while localStorage still holds\n286:     // the config, the next session spawn silently boots with an EMPTY LLM\n287:     // config. Rebuild from the renderer's copy, but ONLY when the file is\n288:     // missing/blank: an existing file may hold intentional manual edits.\n289:     ipcMain.handle(\"settings:ensure\", async (_e, data) => {\n290:       try {\n291:         let cur = {};\n292:         try {\n293:           cur = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(os.homedir(), \".clutch\", \"settings.json\"), \"utf-8\"));\n294:         } catch (e) {\n295:           /* missing/corrupt: heal below */\n296:         }\n297:         if (cur && (cur.base_url || cur.api_key || cur.model)) return { ok: true, healed: false };\n298:         writeSettingsFile(data);\n299:         tunnelLog(\"[settings] mirror missing — rebuilt ~/.clutch/settings.json from the UI config\");\n300:         return { ok: true, healed: true };\n301:       } catch (e) {\n302:         return { ok: false, error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\n303:       }\n304:     });\n305: \n... (showing lines 244-305 of 338; use offset=306 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789633915.0179687, "id": "3fb18f8ba10b", "content": "核对最后两处（`apiFetch` 语义、测试约定），然后开写：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_e11e7e00f15246d187dea601", "name": "grep", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"ui/app.js\",\"pattern\":\"function apiFetch|async function apiFetch\"}"}, {"id": "call_7181906ba2d74158bfb75108", "name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"limit\":40,\"max_chars\":4600,\"path\":\"tests/websearch_test.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "Now I have the full picture. Important detail in `writeSettingsFile` (main.js 251-272): it rebuilds `flat` from `cur` (current file) merged with `upd` (only base_url/model/api_key/reasoning_effort). Since it preserves `cur` wholesale and merges `upd` on top, mcp_* keys already in settings.json are PRESERVED (cur keeps them). Good — no main.js change strictly needed: server-side saves persist mcp_* keys, and UI-side rewrites preserve them. The mirror only overwrites the four LLM keys. So the UI→server POST path is the way MCP URLs get saved (server writes settings.json itself).\n\nAlso note: `settings:ensure` self-heal — if file missing, rebuilds from data (only LLM keys) — fine.\n\nNow, everything's clear. Implementation plan (English-only code text):\n\n**1. agent/tools/mcpprovider.py (new)** — per approved design:\n- frozen `McpProvider` dataclass: name, label, search_tool, search_args, map_results, placeholder, status_tool\n- `url_for(config)`: config.mcp_urls.get(name) or env CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL, rstrip(\"/\")\n- `_first_list` helper\n- xiaohongshu spec: search_feeds, args {keyword, limit}, map keeping xsec_token in URL, placeholder http://localhost:18060/mcp, status_tool check_login_status\n- MCP_PROVIDERS registry\n- stdlib only\n\n**2. websearch.py edits**:\n- import MCP_PROVIDERS + McpProvider from .mcpprovider (same package: `from .mcpprovider import McpProvider, MCP_PROVIDERS`)\n- Backend frozen dataclass: name, search(q,limit,config,get), available(config) default True\n- _BACKENDS: dict[str, Backend] with the four wrapped\n- _DEFAULT_CHAIN stays as base order tuple\n- _mcp_rpc + _mcp_call JSON-RPC client before registry; errors → WebError; NOT via _http_get (SSRF guard is for model-controlled URLs; MCP endpoints are operator-configured, typically loopback)\n- _mcp_backend(provider) adapter\n- register MCP backends at import\n- _available_backends → uses Backend.available\n- web_search: backend validation unified — unknown/not-available → factual error listing only real available backends; no install advice, no naming unconfigured providers\n- loop: `fn = _BACKENDS[name].search` — actually keep `_BACKENDS[name](q, limit, config, get)` shape by making Backend callable? Cleaner: `results = _BACKENDS[name].search(q, limit, config, get)`.\n- mcp_status(url, provider, timeout) public for server\n\nNote the `get` partial includes cancel already; my _mcp_call signature should accept cancel — the MCP backend's search(q, limit, config, get) receives `get` it won't use, and needs config.web_search_timeout + cancel. Hmm — cancel isn't directly available in the backend signature; the existing backends use `get` which has cancel bound. For MCP, `_mcp_rpc` checks `cancel.is_set()`. I can pass cancel via... the Backend.search signature is (q, limit, config, get) — uniform. To honor cancel, I could extract cancel from the partial: `get.keywords.get(\"cancel\")` — hacky but works since functools.partial has .keywords. Cleaner: _mcp_rpc accepts cancel=None; in _mcp_backend.search, do `cancel = getattr(get, \"keywords\", {}).get(\"cancel\")`. That's a bit clever; alternatively just make _mcp_call accept cancel and pull from partial. Actually functools.partial objects have .args and .keywords attributes. `get.keywords` → {\"timeout\":..., \"cancel\":...}. That works. I'll write it defensively: `cancel = (getattr(get, \"keywords\", None) or {}).get(\"cancel\")`.\n\n**3. config.py**: add mcp_urls field after searxng_url.\n\n**4. server.py**:\n- import MCP_PROVIDERS as _MCP_PROVIDER_REGISTRY + websearch.mcp_status\n  - circular import check: server imports websearch — websearch imports ..config and .workspace only. server already imports .tools.workspace. Fine.\n- helper `mcp_providers()` returning list of providers\n- _settings_post: \n  - \"nothing to save\" guard must also consider mcp_* keys: change `if not any((base_url, model, api_key)) and \"reasoning_effort\" not in body:` → add `and not _mcp_keys(body)` or a small condition. Simplest: compute mcp updates first, then `if not any((base_url, model, api_key)) and \"reasoning_effort\" not in body and not mcp_updates: return nothing to save`.\n  - after saving flat keys, persist mcp_* into the RAW settings dict (raw = load_settings(); saved = flatten only for LLM fields). Careful: current code does `saved = flatten_settings(load_settings())` then updates and save_settings(saved) — flatten DROPS mcp_* keys! If a POST saves LLM settings after MCP URLs were configured, flatten would erase them. So I must merge: `saved = {**load_settings(), **flatten_settings(load_settings())}`? No — flatten_settings is for legacy migration; the raw dict IS flat already (plus mcp_* keys). Current code flattens to migrate legacy profiles on write. If raw has mcp_xiaohongshu key, flatten drops it → data loss on next settings POST.\n  \n  Fix: `raw = load_settings(); saved = flatten_settings(raw)` then `saved.update({k: v for k, v in raw.items() if k.startswith(\"mcp_\")})` — preserves MCP keys through flatten. Then apply mcp_* updates from body with validation (http(s) URL, '' clears, unknown providers kept).\n  - Apply to live config: `self._cfg.mcp_urls.update(...)` for set values; removal for cleared: `self._cfg.mcp_urls.pop(name, None)`.\n- _settings_get: include \"mcp_providers\": [{key, label, placeholder, value}] from RAW saved (not flatten) — value = raw.get(f\"mcp_{p.name}\", \"\").\n- GET route: add /api/mcp_status → _mcp_status handler (per-provider configured/reachable/login).\n- main(): after LLM endpoint resolution, load mcp_* from raw settings into config.mcp_urls.\n\n**5. registry.py**: \n- description render: add `backends=\" or \".join(websearch.available_backends(config))` — need `available_backends` alias in websearch.\n- backend param description: make dynamic: `f\"pin one backend: {' | '.join(websearch.available_backends(config))} (default: fall through the chain)\"`.\n- Check registry imports websearch module: line 161 uses `websearch.web_search` — so `websearch` module is imported. Good.\n\n**6. prompts/tools/web_search.md**: replace hardcoded chain sentence with `$backends`:\n\"Backends available here ($backends) are tried in order — the first that returns results wins; when all fail the error lists each backend's reason, and backend=<name> pins one.\"\n\n**7. UI**:\n- index.html: add `<div id=\"mcp-services\"></div>` before the modal-actions div in settings-modal (line 50).\n- app.js: append self-contained block at file end (file is a plain top-level script, 2811 lines). It renders rows from GET /api/settings mcp_providers, has its own Save button posting mcp_* keys, and refreshes status from /api/mcp_status. Hook rendering into openSettings? Simplest: render once at startup (IIFE) + refresh on every openSettings via hooking the settings-btn click (add another listener — multiple listeners fine).\n  - Need apiFetch semantics: from pushSettings usage: `apiFetch(\"/api/settings\", { method: \"POST\", body: payload })` and presumably GET `apiFetch(\"/api/...\")` returns parsed JSON. Check quickly? pushSettings does `await apiFetch(...)` without using return; openSettings elsewhere... I saw in the (lost) summary `const s = await apiFetch(\"/api/settings\")`. Let me verify apiFetch exists and returns json. grep app.js for \"function apiFetch\" — do that before writing.\n\n**8. tests/mcpbackend_test.py** (new) — offline, following testsupport.check. Need to check existing test conventions: read tests/websearch_test.py header + testsupport. And how tests handle Config import etc.\n\n**9. README.md** (Chinese) — add MCP services paragraph.\n\nOrder of work: mcpprovider.py → websearch.py edits → config.py → server.py → registry.py + prompt → UI → tests → README → run tests.\n\nLet me check apiFetch + tests conventions quickly (parallel greps/reads), then start writing."}
