{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789634151.810043, "id": "2899d90b213c", "tool_call_id": "call_2b5f46c600dc49009cfd0eb8", "content": "OK: edited C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\agent\\prompts\\tools\\web_search.md (+1 -1 lines)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/agent\\prompts\\tools\\web_search.md\n+++ b/agent\\prompts\\tools\\web_search.md\n@@ -1 +1 @@\n-Search the web for information the workspace cannot answer: current events, library versions and release notes, error messages, docs pages. Returns ranked results (title, URL, snippet); follow up with web_fetch on the 1-2 most relevant URLs for the full text. query is the search string — engine syntax like quoted phrases, site: and -term filters work; short factual queries beat long sentences. max_results caps entries (default $max). Backends try in order: tavily (needs CLUTCH_TAVILY_API_KEY), searxng (needs CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL), bing, duckduckgo — the first that returns results wins; when all fail the error lists each backend's reason, and backend=<name> pins one.\n+Search the web for information the workspace cannot answer: current events, library versions and release notes, error messages, docs pages. Returns ranked results (title, URL, snippet); follow up with web_fetch on the 1-2 most relevant URLs for the full text. query is the search string — engine syntax like quoted phrases, site: and -term filters work; short factual queries beat long sentences. max_results caps entries (default $max). Backends available on this machine ($backends) are tried in order — the first that returns results wins; when all fail the error lists each backend's reason, and backend=<name> pins one.\n"}
