h WOULD contain the name. So that old test would also fail — inconsistent memory; the summary's tests may never have run on disk. Ground truth: decide correct behavior.\n\nFactual, zero-pollution design: if the model pins `backend=\"xiaohongshu\"` on a host without it, saying \"backend 'xiaohongshu' is not available; available: bing, ddg\" is factual (the model introduced the name itself — likely from training, not from our surface). We must not: enumerate unconfigured providers, or advise installation. So the correct test assertion: content mentions the requested name (echoing the request is fine), does not suggest install/setup, and lists only real backends. But stronger: does echoing count as \"pollution\"? The model chose the name; echoing is unavoidable in any error format. Keep the factual echo.\n\nHmm — but could we avoid even echoing? `f\"ERROR: backend {backend!r} is not available\"` — standard. Echo is fine.\n\nFix the test: split into two checks:\n- pinned unconfigured backend → error whose \"available:\" list contains no mcp name... it can't (the list only has available ones). Check `\"available: \" in content` and `\"install\" not in content.lower()` and no \"needs CLUTCH_\" advice. And for the never-named property, use the FALL-THROUGH path: with no backends query, or the unknown-backend error — the message lists available only. Also check prompt/schema absence (section 7 covers).\n\nActually one more scenario worth locking: when the model pins an unconfigured MCP name, the response must not name any OTHER unconfigured service or give install advice. Keep it simple:\n\n```\nr = ws.web_search(None, plain, \"q\", backend=\"xiaohongshu\")\ncheck(r.get(\"error\") and \"available: \" in r[\"content\"], \"pinning an unconfigured backend errors factually\")\ncheck(\"install\" not in r[\"content\"].lower() and \"needs CLUTCH_\" not in r[\"content\"],\n      \"error never suggests installing or env vars\")\ncheck(\"searxng\" not in r[\"content\"], \"unconfigured siblings are not named either\")\n```\n\nWait — plain Config: searxng_url = \"\" → not available → not in the list; and the echo only names xiaohongshu. So \"searxng\" not in content holds... unless tavily env present: tavily would appear in the available list (that's fine, it's available). searxng won't appear either way (unless CLUTCH_SEARXNG_URL set in this shell — unlikely; test env). Use \"searxng\" absence as the no-sibling-pollution probe. Reasonably safe; if the CI env sets SEARXNG_URL it'd fail — acceptable for this repo's tests (websearch_test already assumes keyless env for chain tests? It has offline fallbacks. Fine.)\n\nApply the fix."}
