{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789810951.6994052, "id": "7a21ade7f11e", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_e20b010dbbc744ba809aebab", "name": "load_memory", "arguments": "{\"name\":\"Xiaohongshu open-source access landscape\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user asks: \"How do I now use this new feature to connect the agent to Xiaohongshu MCP?\"\n\nThis is a usage question — explain how to actually use the shipped feature. I should give concrete steps:\n\n1. Get xiaohongshu-mcp running (the community project — from memory: \"Xiaohongshu open-source access landscape\" memory mentions key projects like Panniantong's xiaohongshu-mcp). I should load that memory to give accurate setup instructions.\n\n2. Configure the URL in the settings modal (Web services section) or env var.\n\n3. How the agent uses it: web_search with backend=\"xiaohongshu\", login status check, etc.\n\nLet me load the memory about the Xiaohongshu open-source access landscape to give accurate instructions about the actual MCP server project (how to install/run it, e.g. `xiaohongshu-mcp` Go/Node project with a login QR code flow, default port 18060 per our placeholder).\n\nThen write a clear step-by-step guide in Chinese, with commands, maybe a mermaid diagram of the flow. Keep it practical:\n\n- Step 1: 启动 xiaohongshu-mcp 服务（real-browser + user login session; needs Chrome; run `xiaohongshu-mcp` binary; scan QR to log in; service serves MCP at http://localhost:18060/mcp)\n- Step 2: 在 Clutch 里配置：设置弹窗 → Web services → Xiaohongshu MCP URL 填 http://localhost:18060/mcp → Save web services。状态行会显示 connected · logged in / not logged in / unreachable\n- 或环境变量 CLUTCH_MCP_XIAOHONGSHU_URL\n- Step 3: 用法：对 agent 说\"在小红书搜...\" → agent 调 web_search(query=..., backend=\"xiaohongshu\")；得到 note URL（带 xsec_token）后可 web_fetch? Wait — web_fetch has SSRF guard and fetches text pages; xiaohongshu pages are JS-heavy and likely blocked. The MCP server itself has detail tools but our integration only exposes search_feeds as a search backend. Be honest: results give title/url/snippet; the snippet (desc) is the content we surface. Detail fetching would need more MCP tools mapped (future work) — actually per design only search is mapped. Don't overpromise.\n- Verify: run tests? Provide quick verification commands: curl the mcp_status endpoint, or check the settings modal status line.\n- Also mention: no restart needed — settings POST hot-updates the live config (cfg.mcp_urls.update in the same request). Actually the running server hot-applies (mcp_updates applied to self._cfg under lock). So no restart needed if the server is running. If configuring via env var, the env must be set before server start.\n- Troubleshooting table: unreachable → service not started/wrong port; not logged in → rescan QR; check_login_status.\n\nLet me load the memory first for accuracy about the xiaohongshu-mcp project (name, how to run, default port). This is a read-only memory load, cheap and relevant."}
