ver landed on disk (probably the session was interrupted/rolled back — perhaps they were in chat mode when the design was approved and \"start coding\" was blocked... actually the memory says \"user said start coding; chat mode blocked it — needs work mode\". Then a later session did it in work mode per the compaction summary, but the files weren't on disk — meaning that session's writes never persisted, OR the workspace got reverted).\n\nWait, let me reconstruct more carefully:\n\n- Memory: \"MCP plugin backend design (approved, pending work mode)\" — approved design, chat mode blocked coding.\n- Compaction summary: shows an implementation session that wrote files, ran tests successfully (COMPILE_OK, tests all passed). That session's final message was a completion report.\n- But at the start of THIS session: the files did NOT exist on disk.\n\nSo either:\n(a) The implementation session was in a different workspace/directory, or\n(b) The session's file writes were rolled back (user hit Undo, or workspace reset), or\n(c) The compaction summary described work that happened but was then lost somehow.\n\nMost important actionable fact: **The GitHub repo does not contain the new code.** Because:\n1. The workspace files didn't exist before today (verified at session start).\n2. I only re-created them today in this workspace.\n3. Unless the user commits and pushes THIS workspace's changes to GitHub, the CD will keep packaging the old source → no feature.\n\nAlso: is this workspace even a git repo connected to GitHub? Let me check `git status` / `git log` to see:\n- Whether agent/tools/mcpprovider.py, tests/mcpbackend_test.py etc. show as untracked/modified (uncommitted).\n- What the last commit is (probably the 0.1.13/0.0.13 release commit).\n- Whether there's a remote.\n\nThen the answer becomes concrete:\n1. 你 0.0.13 打包时上传的源码里本来就没有这个功能——因为实现它的代码今天才真正落到这份工作区（上一会话的实现没有保存到磁盘，我本次会话重新实现并测试通过）。\n2. 现在 GitHub 上的源码仍然是旧的（今天的改动还没有 commit/push）。\n3. CD 打包只打它看到的源码 → 打出来自然没有这个功能。\n4. 解决：把今天的改动 commit + push → 触发 CD → 产出新版本（0.1.14 或你 bump 的版本号）→ 安装新版。\n\nLet me verify with git commands (read-only, allowed): git status, git log --oneline -5, git remote -v. This will show untracked/modified files confirming the changes aren't pushed.\n\nAlso check the version in ui/package.json: 0.1.13 — user says 0.0.13. Maybe the GitHub repo's version differs. Whatever — the point stands.\n\nAlso possible: CD workflow details — check for .github/workflows to explain what triggers a build (tag push? release?). If the CD builds on tags, they need to bump version + tag. Let me look.\n\nPlan:\n1. Run git status + git log + git remote -v (read-only, allowed).\n2. Check .github/workflows for the CD trigger.\n3. Give the user a precise explanation + exact commands to ship: bump version, commit, push, tag → CD.\n\nThis is chat mode — I can't commit/push anyway (mutating). So the deliverable is: explanation + exact command list they can run themselves (or ask me to do it in work mode)."}
