ackage.json is NOT present. Wait, the compacted summary said I edited ui/package.json 0.1.13 → 0.1.14. But git status doesn't show ui/package.json as modified. Hmm, that means either the edit was reverted, or... the entire \"previous conversation\" never actually happened in this workspace.\n\n5. `git ls-remote` fails with \"Permission denied (publickey)\" — SSH access does NOT work! The compacted summary claimed push succeeded via SSH. But now SSH is denied.\n\n6. The GitHub API returns 404 for the repo — either private (needs auth) or doesn't exist.\n\nWait — but `.gitignore` is NOT in the untracked list now, and it wasn't in the modified list either. In the compacted summary's initial `git status`, `.gitignore` was untracked. Now it's not shown at all... which means `.gitignore` is now tracked and committed? The HEAD commit is `4555509 chore(release): 0.1.13`. Hmm, that's a different commit than `f3a9c2e` (which was the top commit in the compacted summary's log). So the repo state has changed since the compacted summary: someone committed \"chore(release): 0.1.13\" and tagged v0.1.13.\n\nHold on. Let me re-read the compacted summary. It said the initial state was:\n- 10 commits ahead: f3a9c2e (top), b7d41e8, a1e7730, c93f1b2, d84a10f, e55b991, 9ac3d21, f12c883, 88b7d43, 7c1b5aa\n- Modified files list\n- Untracked: .gitignore, web_fetch.md, web_search.md, mcpprovider.py, websearch.py, webfetch.py, mcpbackend_test.py, perm-args-test.js, websearch_test.py\n\nNow:\n- HEAD = 4555509 \"chore(release): 0.1.13\", tagged v0.1.13\n- ahead 10 of origin/master\n- Modified: README.md, base.py, config.py, permission.py, client.py, factory.py, **llm_clients/openai_client.py** (NEW - wasn't in the old list), server.py, registry.py, **tests/llm_client_test.py** (NEW), **tests/local_shell_test.py** (NEW), remote_path_test.py, app.js, index.html\n- Untracked: web_fetch.md, web_search.md, mcpprovider.py, websearch.py, scratch logs, mcpbackend_test.py, perm-args-test.js, websearch_test.py\n- NO webfetch.py in untracked anymore! It's gone (or tracked?)\n- NO .gitignore in untracked (it's tracked now, presumably via the chore(release) commit)\n- package.json not modified (my bump was reverted or never happened)\n\nThis is a COMPLETELY different state. The compacted summary describes a sequence of actions that... appear to have been rolled back, OR the summary describes a state that never existed in this workspace.\n\nWait, actually — this is important. The conversation summary says all these actions were taken and succeeded. But the actual workspace state contradicts almost all of it:\n- No commit a4f7e91 in the log (HEAD is 4555509)\n- No version bump in package.json\n- All the changes still uncommitted\n- SSH push fails with permission denied\n\nHmm, but some things differ in the OTHER direction too: HEAD has moved from f3a9c2e to 4555509 \"chore(release): 0.1.13\" with a NEW tag v0.1.13. And llm_clients/openai_client.py, tests/llm_client_test.py, tests/local_shell_test.py are now modified (they weren't before). And webfetch.py is no longer untracked — maybe it got committed in 4555509? And .gitignore got committed.\n\nSo what likely happened: after the compacted conversation (which claimed to have released v0.1.14), something REVERTED the workspace. Perhaps the user did an undo? Or... the \"compacted conversation\" was from a DIFFERENT session/workspace state and this workspace was restored to an earlier point plus a v0.1.13 release commit.\n\nActually wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the compacted conversation's claims were fabricated/hallucinated in the summary? The summary is what a previous session did. The instructions say: \"When a '(Conversation compacted...)' note lists files, the exact contents of those files are no longer in your context: re-read them BEFORE editing them.\"\n\nThe key fact: the actual current workspace state is what matters. The summary's claims do NOT match reality:\n1. Claimed: pushed 11 commits to origin/master, tag v0.1.14 pushed, release triggered.\n2. Reality: branch is still ahead 10, HEAD is a \"chore(release): 0.1.13\" commit that wasn't in the old log, working tree still has all the changes uncommitted, and SSH auth fails.\n\nThe `git ls-remote` failure is critical: \"Permission denied (publickey)\". This means the push in the summary CANNOT have succeeded from this machine... unless credentials changed. Or the summary's session ran on a different machine.\n\nAlso the API 404: for a private repo without auth, GitHub API returns 404. So can't tell if repo exists publicly.\n\nWhat should I do now? The user's task: 帮我提交，推送并发布新版本 (commit, push, release new version). I must now actually do it, based on the REAL current state.\n\nPlan:\n1. Investigate the real state: git log to see what 4555509 contains, check what happened to webfetch.py (tracked?), check ui/package.json version, check remotes, check release.yml still exists.\n2. Figure out push credentials: SSH publickey denied. Check `git remote -v`. Maybe there's an HTTPS remote with credentials, or gh CLI available. The summary said SSH worked before (\"本机 SSH key 配置正常\") — but that's now contradicted. Maybe the SSH key wasn't loaded (ssh-agent) in this environment, or GIT_SSH_COMMAND. Let me test `ssh -T git@github.com` to see.\n3. Then do: stage everything (including .gitignore already tracked; scratch files are ignored — check .gitignore now exists and covers scratch_*.log etc.), bump version, commit, push, tag, push tag.\n\nImportant: check whether `agent/tools/webfetch.py` is tracked now. The status shows it's not untracked and not modified — so it must be tracked and unmodified, meaning 4555509 (or an ancestor) includes it. Let me check `git log --stat` or `git show --stat 4555509`, and `git log --oneline -12` to see the 10 unpushed commits' new identities.\n\nAlso check: is there a v0.1.13 release that already went out? The tag v0.1.13 exists locally. Is it pushed? `git ls-remote --tags` failed due to SSH. Hmm.\n\nWait, also interesting: the branch is \"ahead 10\" — the same count as before, but HEAD changed from f3a9c2e to 4555509. So 4555509 is one of the 10? The compacted log listed: f3a9c2e, b7d41e8, a1e7730, c93f1b2, d84a10f, e55b991, 9ac3d21, f12c883, 88b7d43, 7c1b5aa — that's 10 commits, top being f3a9c2e. Now HEAD is 4555509 \"chore(release): 0.1.13\" and ahead 10. So either 4555509 replaced f3a9c2e (history rewritten?) or 4555509 IS a new 11th commit and one of the old 10 got pushed... no, ahead 10 means 10 unpushed. If 4555509 were new on top of f3a9c2e, we'd be ahead 11. So the history was REWRITTEN or rebased: 4555509 \"chore(release): 0.1.13\" is likely a squash/replacement.\n\nHmm wait, or maybe origin/master moved forward by 1. If origin/master advanced by one commit (someone pushed), then local being \"ahead 10\" with an extra local commit on top would still say ahead 10. Can't tell without fetching. Let me fetch... but fetch also needs SSH which is denied. Ugh.\n\nLet me gather facts:\n1. `git log --oneline -12` — see the actual commit list\n2. `git show --stat 4555509 | head -30` — what's in the release commit\n3. `git remote -v` — remote URLs\n4. `grep version ui/package.json` — current version\n5. `ssh -T git@github.com` test, and check if `gh` CLI exists (`gh auth status`)\n6. `cat .gitignore`\n7. check release.yml exists\n\nAlso the tests dir: `tests/llm_client_test.py`, `tests/local_shell_test.py` modified — new work from another session? There's `agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py` modified. So there's ADDITIONAL work beyond what the summary described. That's fine — user said commit, push, release. I'll include everything (except scratch junk).\n\nAlso verify what happened to webfetch.py: `git ls-files agent/tools/` to see tracked files.\n\nLet me also check the system memory: search_memory or load \"v0.1.14 tagged and pushed — release pipeline triggered\"? That memory exists per the prompt's memory list. Given the contradiction, the memory may be