log\nscratch_*.py?\n```\nHmm, patterns: scratch-launch-tests.py, scratch-relaunch-tests.py → `scratch-*.py`. Logs: `scratch_*.log`. Also server_smoke.log mentioned in summary — not present now. Keep it simple:\n```\n# local scratch test scripts and logs\n/scratch-*.py\n/scratch_*.log\n```\nAnchored to root — they're all root-level. Good.\n\nNow, the actual code changes to commit (from git status): 14 modified + 9 untracked source files (excluding scratch). Plus my .gitignore edit. Let me look at the diff for the new files I haven't seen in this repo: openai_client.py diff, local_shell_test.py diff, llm_client_test.py diff — to write an accurate commit message. The MCP stuff is known from memories (\"MCP web-search plugin shipped and verified\" — xiaohongshu). Let me load that memory too? The title says \"MCP web-search plugin shipped and verified\" — content may describe the work. It'd help write the commit message. Load both memories.\n\nBatch 2 (parallel):\n1. run_command: git log --oneline origin/master..master\n2. run_command: git ls-remote https (with GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0, timeout)\n3. run_command: cat VERSION && head -25 .github/workflows/release.yml && ls agent/tools/\n4. run_command: git diff --stat && echo ==== && git diff agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py | head -60\n5. load_memory: \"Project conventions and Windows environment quirks\"\n6. load_memory: \"MCP web-search plugin shipped and verified\"\n\n6 calls in one block — allowed since independent. Let me do it."}
