{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789812647.6777484, "id": "786953685444", "tool_call_id": "call_ab74850e628d43ffb2705ff5", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\n0.1.13\n====\n# Build the Clutch desktop releases on a tag push (vX.Y.Z) and attach them to\r\n# the GitHub release. Both artifacts are self-contained: bundled PyInstaller\r\n# backend + Electron GUI, click-to-use with no python/pip on the target machine.\r\n#  - deb  : Linux x86_64 (ubuntu-latest)\r\n#  - dmg  : macOS arm64 / Apple Silicon (macos-latest), UNSIGNED — first launch\r\n#           is blocked by Gatekeeper with a misleading \"damaged\" notice (macOS 15\r\n#           removed the right-click -> Open bypass); clear it with\r\n#           `xattr -cr /Applications/Clutch.app` until the project picks up\r\n#           Developer ID signing + notarization.\r\n#  - win  : Windows x64 NSIS (windows-latest), UNSIGNED — SmartScreen warns on\r\n#           the first run (\"Windows protected your PC\" -> More info -> Run\r\n#           anyway). This job must run on Windows: the bundled backend is a\r\n#           PyInstaller onefile .exe and PyInstaller cannot cross-compile.\r\nname: release\r\n\r\non:\r\n  push:\r\n    tags:\r\n      - \"v*\"\r\n\r\npermissions:\r\n  contents: write\r\n\r\njobs:\r\n  deb:\r\n====\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\nfilesystem.py\nlocalshell.py\nmcpprovider.py\nregistry.py\nshell.py\ntransport.py\nwebsearch.py\nworkspace.py\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789812647.9137523, "id": "a5e2cd1a833a", "tool_call_id": "call_4694675652dc4baba92a6a84", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\n README.md                              |  12 ++-\n agent/base.py                          |   1 +\n agent/config.py                        |  27 +++++++\n agent/core/permission.py               |   8 +-\n agent/llm/client.py                    |  18 ++++-\n agent/llm/factory.py                   |   1 +\n agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py |  12 ++-\n agent/server.py                        | 116 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n agent/tools/registry.py                |  51 +++++++++++-\n tests/llm_client_test.py               |  12 ++-\n tests/local_shell_test.py              |  38 ++++++---\n tests/remote_path_test.py              |   6 +-\n ui/app.js                              | 141 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n ui/index.html                          |   1 +\n 14 files changed, 411 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)\n====\ndiff --git a/agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py b/agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py\nindex 06ec29f..d142125 100644\n--- a/agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py\n+++ b/agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py\n@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ class OpenaiLlmClient(LlmClient):\n         base_url: str,\n         model: str,\n         request_timeout: float = 60.0,\n+        read_timeout: float = 240.0,\n         max_retries: int = 3,\n         retryable_status: Collection[int] = frozenset({429, 500, 502, 503, 504}),\n         reasoning_effort: str | None = None,\n@@ -23,12 +24,21 @@ class OpenaiLlmClient(LlmClient):\n         self.api_key = api_key\n         self.handlers = get_default_handlers()\n         self.request_timeout = request_timeout\n+        self.read_timeout = read_timeout\n         self.max_retries = max_retries\n         self.retryable_status = retryable_status\n         self.reasoning_effort = reasoning_effort\n \n         proxy = get_proxy_for_url(base_url)\n-        http_client = httpx2.Client(proxy=proxy, trust_env=False, timeout=self.request_timeout)\n+        # split budgets (a single float would set read=connect): connect fails\n+        # fast on dead routes, read tolerates long streaming chunk gaps — the\n+        # \"good network, frequent request timed out\" case is a read-budget\n+        # problem, not a connect one (see Config.llm_read_timeout)\n+        timeout = httpx2.Timeout(\n+            self.request_timeout, connect=min(15.0, self.request_timeout), read=self.read_timeout\n+        )\n+        http_client = httpx2.Client(proxy=proxy, trust_env=False, timeout=timeout)\n+        self.timeout = timeout\n         self.client = OpenAI(api_key=self.api_key, base_url=base_url, http_client=http_client)\n         self.model = model\n \n\nstderr:\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in README.md.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/base.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/config.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/core/permission.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/llm/client.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/llm/factory.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/server.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/tools/registry.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in tests/llm_client_test.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in tests/local_shell_test.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in tests/remote_path_test.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in ui/app.js.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in ui/index.html.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789812647.9147496, "id": "58b2fc5c7f03", "tool_call_id": "call_f5dc4a865d8049ed8b5f323b", "content": "[Project conventions and Windows environment quirks]\nClutch coding agent repo (C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch): all text in code (comments, tool descriptions, error messages) MUST be English — user explicitly corrected me on this; README.md is Chinese (project convention). Tests are self-running modules (no pytest): `.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m tests.X` with tests/testsupport.py check(); system python lacks deps (ModuleNotFoundError); `uv run` times out under the 30s command-timeout limit — use .venv/Scripts/python.exe directly. Windows console mangles CJK stdout (GBK); to verify Chinese output write to a UTF-8 file or sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\"). Command-line Chinese args get GBK-garbled through curl — percent-encode manually. Chat mode whitelist misjudges piped sed/grep as writes; bare curl|head, python -c, direct grep -rn work. Long streaming write_file args can trigger WinError 10054 — write big files in several small chunks.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789812647.9172578, "id": "051b77085732", "tool_call_id": "call_a3853d5a808a44a9832ae8ca", "content": "[MCP web-search plugin shipped and verified]\nShipped in work mode (all tests green, incl. live): MCP plugin backend for web_search. (1) NEW agent/tools/mcpprovider.py — frozen McpProvider dataclass (name/label/search_tool/search_args/map_results/placeholder/status_tool) + MCP_PROVIDERS registry, xiaohongshu spec (search_feeds -> {title,url,snippet}, url keeps xsec_token, status_tool check_login_status); stdlib-only, import-safe. (2) websearch.py — Backend frozen record (name/search/available) wraps 4 native backends, _mcp_rpc/_mcp_call JSON-RPC client (initialize -> notifications/initialized -> tools/call, Mcp-Session-Id, SSE-frame fallback, all errors -> WebError; deliberately bypasses the SSRF guard because MCP endpoints are operator-configured loopback), _mcp_backend adapter joins the chain, _available_backends = registered AND configured, public available_backends alias + mcp_status(). (3) config.mcp_urls dict field. (4) server.py — _split_mcp_fields/_mcp_keys_from/_login_state helpers; settings POST accepts mcp_* (http(s) validated, '' clears, unknown providers kept; \"nothing to save\" guard extended; flatten_settings would DROP mcp_* keys so persistence merges them back from raw); _settings_get returns mcp_providers metadata; GET /api/mcp_status (reachable+login, best-effort normalization); main() loads mcp_* at boot. (5) registry renders prompt $backends + schema backend param from the live available set; prompts/tools/web_search.md uses $backends. (6) UI: #mcp-services div in settings modal + self-contained initMcpServices block at end of ui/app.js (renders rows, own Save button, status text connected·logged in/unreachable/blank); main.js writeSettingsFile needs NO change (merges into existing file, mcp_* preserved). (7) tests/mcpbackend_test.py — 30+ checks incl. real loopback MCP server (json/SSE/text/202/rpcerror/500 paths). Gotcha discovered: an error echoing the model's own pinned backend name is FINE (factual echo); pollution = naming unconfigured services or install advice. Smoke-tested over HTTP and restored ~/.clutch/settings.json afterwards.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789812713.8483636, "id": "0f1205effaf4", "content": "远端真相大白：**HTTPS 匿名可读**，真实的 `origin/master` 就在 `4555509`（v0.1.13）——本地其实**并不落后也不领先**，\"ahead 10\" 只是陈旧的 tracking ref。所以任务收敛为：**把工作树里的 MCP 插件 + LLM 超时改动提交 → 推送 → 发 v0.1.14**。仓库约定清晰：功能 commit + `chore(release): 0.1.x` bump（VERSION/package.json/package-lock）+ 打 `v*` tag 触发 release.yml。\n\n继续并行：看剩余 diff 内容（写准确的 commit message）、诊断 SSH 和 HTTPS 凭据：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_71d21661e2194e089c12d0e3", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"git diff agent/base.py agent/core/permission.py agent/llm/factory.py agent/llm/client.py tests/remote_path_test.py tests/local_shell_test.py tests/llm_client_test.py 2>/dev/null | head -175\"}"}, {"id": "call_a8d6387a8e014423bfc41b25", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"git diff agent/config.py 2>/dev/null | head -70; echo ====; git diff agent/tools/registry.py 2>/dev/null | head -95\"}"}, {"id": "call_a3997241a22640e082b78c9b", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"git diff agent/server.py 2>/dev/null | head -150\"}"}, {"id": "call_1e5e1a49679140f496b65390", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"git diff README.md ui/index.html 2>/dev/null | head -55; echo ====; grep -rn \\\"web_fetch\\\\|webfetch\\\" agent/ README.md 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\"prompts/tools\\\" | head -12; echo ====; git diff ui/app.js 2>/dev/null | grep \\\"^+\\\" | head -30\"}"}, {"id": "call_ab6f787d30854f79b7e7df2e", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"ssh -v -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=8 -T git@github.com 2>&1 | grep -i \\\"offering\\\\|denied\\\\|authenticated\\\\|identity file\\\" | head -8\"}"}, {"id": "call_b204cd6f51614926af3a1f6b", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"printf \\\"protocol=https\\\\nhost=github.com\\\\n\\\\n\\\" | GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 GCM_INTERACTIVE=never git credential fill 2>&1 | sed -e 's/^password=.*/password=PRESENT/' -e 's/^oauth_refresh_token=.*/oauth_refresh_token=REDACTED/' -e 's/^refresh_token=.*/refresh_token=REDACTED/' | head -8\"}"}], "reasoning": "Now I have a much clearer picture:\n\n**Real repo**: github.com/Ethereal1024/Clutch (public! anonymous ls-remote worked via HTTPS)\n- origin/master = 4555509 = local HEAD (chore(release): 0.1.13, tagged v0.1.13). So the 10 \"ahead\" is wrong? Wait — `git ls-remote` via HTTPS shows refs/heads/master = 4555509 = local HEAD. But git status said \"ahead 10\". That means the local remote-tracking ref `origin/master` is STALE (last fetch was old). Actually no — if origin/master (remote-tracking) = some older commit and actual remote master = local HEAD, then local is NOT ahead at all; it's up to date with the real remote but the tracking ref is stale.\n\nWait, let me think again. `git log origin/master..master` showed exactly the 10 commits listed. So remote-tracking origin/master points to the parent of 4289473 (10 commits back). The REAL remote master is at 4555509 (= local HEAD). So actually: everything up to v0.1.13 IS pushed. Local just hasn't fetched. The \"ahead 10\" is stale tracking info. \n\nSo the real task: commit the current working-tree changes (MCP plugin + openai_client timeout work + UI), push, release v0.1.14.\n\n**Auth**: SSH denied, but HTTPS anonymous read works. Push via HTTPS needs credentials — credential.helper=manager (Windows Credential Manager). GCM might have stored a PAT/token from previous pushes (the repo has 13 releases, so pushes HAVE happened from this machine, likely via SSH before... or HTTPS). Worth trying: `git push https://github.com/Ethereal1024/Clutch.git` — if GCM has creds, works silently. If not, GCM may try to pop an interactive browser window — in a non-TTY subprocess that might fail or hang. I'll set GCM_INTERACTIVE=Never / GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 to fail fast rather than hang.\n\nAlternatively fix SSH: the key exists (~/.ssh/id_ed25519) but GitHub rejects it. Maybe the key was regenerated and the pub key not uploaded, or it's registered to a different account. Can't fix that from here (needs GitHub web UI). HTTPS is the path.\n\nTest order:\n1. `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 GCM_INTERACTIVE=never git ls-remote https://github.com/Ethereal1024/Clutch.git` worked (anon). For auth test, need an operation that requires auth: ls-remote on a private repo would need auth, but this repo is public so ls-remote succeeds anonymously. To test push creds without pushing: `git credential fill`! \n   `printf \"protocol=https\\nhost=github.com\\n\\n\" | GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git credential fill` — if GCM has stored credentials, it prints username/password (a token). If not, it tries to prompt (GCM might pop UI; with GCM_INTERACTIVE=never it fails). Let me be careful: output would contain a secret — it'll be in my transcript. That's ok-ish but better to avoid printing the secret. Use: `... | grep -c password` or check exit code and only print whether password exists:\n   `printf ... | git credential fill 2>&1 | sed 's/^password=.*/password=<redacted>/'`\n   \n   Simpler: just attempt the real push later; but if creds are missing it might hang with a GUI popup. Guard with env vars to fail fast.\n\n2. **Release conventions** (from real history): feature/fix commits, then `chore(release): 0.1.X` commit bumping VERSION + ui/package.json + ui/package-lock.json, then tag `v0.1.X` on that commit, push master + tag. release.yml triggers on `v*` tag push. \n\n3. **What's in the working tree** (the changes to commit):\n   - MCP web-search plugin (memories detail it thoroughly): mcpprovider.py, websearch.py, prompts/tools/web_search.md + web_fetch.md, config mcp_urls, server settings/mcp_status, registry $backends, UI settings modal, tests/mcpbackend_test.py.\n   - webfetch: prompts/tools/web_fetch.md exists; agent/tools/webfetch.py does NOT exist in this repo (ls agent/tools shows no webfetch.py!). But there's a prompt for web_fetch... and the memory says only web_search MCP plugin. The untracked files: prompts web_fetch.md + web_search.md, mcpprovider.py, websearch.py, tests. webfetch.py isn't in agent/tools — so the web_fetch prompt might be for a future/other tool, or the fetch tool lives elsewhere. Need to check registry diff & prompt content to write accurate commit message. Actually the registry diff (+51) will show what's registered. Let me check quickly: grep webfetch in registry.py and prompts.\n   - openai_client.py: split connect/read timeouts (llm_read_timeout config) — new work: config.py +27, client.py +18, llm_client_test +12.\n   - local_shell_test.py +38/-? — related to what? Maybe scratch test cleanups. Need a peek.\n   - base.py +1, permission.py +8, remote_path_test.py +6, factory.py +1, app.js +141, index.html +1, README.md +12.\n\n   Hmm, there might be multiple logical changes here. Ideally split into separate commits (repo convention: focused commits). Candidate split:\n   a. feat(agent): MCP web-search plugin (mcpprovider, websearch, prompts, config mcp_urls, server, registry, UI settings modal, mcpbackend_test, README)\n   b. fix(llm): split connect/read timeouts (openai_client, client, factory, config llm_read_timeout, llm_client_test)\n   c. misc: permission.py, base.py, local_shell_test.py, remote_path_test.py — unknown; need to inspect before deciding.\n\n   Given effort, maybe 2-3 commits. Let me inspect the remaining diffs I haven't seen: base.py, permission.py, factory.py, client.py, config.py (non-mcp part), local_shell_test.py, remote_path_test.py, app.js summary. Let me view diffs compactly.\n\n4. **Tests before commit**: run the python suites with .venv: llm_client_test, local_shell_test, remote_path_test, mcpbackend_test, websearch_test + perm-args-test.js (node). Also py_compile everything changed.\n\n5. **Version bump to 0.1.14**: VERSION file, ui/package.json, ui/package-lock.json (2 spots: top version + maybe packages.\"\" version). Release commit style: `chore(release): 0.1.14`.\n\n6. **Tag v0.1.14** on release commit, push master + tag via HTTPS (if creds work). Then verify workflow triggered — repo is public so I CAN check Actions via API anonymously! `curl https://api.github.com/repos/Ethereal1024/Clutch/actions/runs?per_page=3`.\n\nWait — first, does release.yml in THIS repo have a windows job? The head shows jobs: deb: ... (comment mentions deb/dmg/win). Fine.\n\nAlso check .gitignore: scratch files are NOT ignored here. Current untracked scratch: scratch-launch-tests.py, scratch-relaunch-tests.py, scratch_*.log (5 logs). I'll add ignore rules for scratch junk to .gitignore as part of a chore commit (matches repo's style of documenting why). Actually — keep it simple: add a short section. The repo's .gitignore has detailed comments; I'll add:\n\n```\n# local scratch scripts/logs from ad-hoc testing sessions\n/scratch-*.py\n/scratch_*.log\n```\n\nWait, careful: are there legit tracked files matching? No tracked scratch files. Good.\n\nBut hold on — should I commit scratch-*.py? No — they're ad-hoc test scripts (launch/relaunch tests). The .gitignore approach keeps them local. Good.\n\nAlso: `git ls-files agent/tools` earlier showed prompts only because head -30 cut it. Now ls agent/tools shows: filesystem, localshell, mcpprovider (untracked? no wait — ls shows the FILESYSTEM, mcpprovider.py IS there on disk), registry, shell, transport, websearch, workspace. Tracked vs untracked: git status says mcpprovider.py + websearch.py untracked; the rest tracked. No webfetch.py in this repo. But prompts/tools/web_fetch.md is untracked and exists. Is there a webfetch implementation somewhere else? Let me grep for \"webfetch\" / \"web_fetch\" in agent/ to understand what it is. The registry diff will reveal.\n\nAlso ui/app.js +141: includes MCP settings block (initMcpServices) per memory. index.html +1: #mcp-services div. OK.\n\nPlan next batch:\n1. Inspect remaining diffs (compact):\n   - `git diff agent/base.py agent/core/permission.py agent/llm/factory.py agent/llm/client.py tests/remote_path_test.py tests/local_shell_test.py | head -150`\n   - `git diff agent/config.py | head -60`\n   - `git diff agent/server.py | head -120` (big, +116)\n   - `git diff agent/tools/registry.py | head -80`\n   - grep -rn \"web_fetch\\|webfetch\" agent/ README.md | head\n2. Check whether README.md diff mentions new stuff (for release notes).\n\nLet me batch 4 commands (independent). Then tests. Then commits.\n\nActually also confirm remote-tracking staleness: after push I'll `git fetch origin` — but fetch via SSH will fail... I can fetch via HTTPS anonymously: `git fetch https://github.com/Ethereal1024/Clutch.git master` hmm, that doesn't update origin/master. Alternative: `git remote set-url origin https://github.com/Ethereal1024/Clutch.git`? If HTTPS push works with GCM creds, switching origin to HTTPS entirely is the cleanest (future pushes just work). And anonymous fetch works for a public repo. I'd say: test `git credential fill`; if it has creds → set-url to HTTPS, push, done. If not → try SSH with verbose to diagnose, or fall back to asking user. \n\nHmm wait, one more SSH possibility: the key might need to be the one registered; maybe there are multiple keys and ssh tries the wrong one? Only id_ed25519 exists. ssh -v would show \"Offering public key: id_ed25519\" then \"Permission denied\". The key is just not on the GitHub account (maybe account changed). I'll quickly run ssh -v to confirm which key is offered — useful for the user report. `ssh -v -o BatchMode=yes -T git@github.com 2>&1 | grep -i \"offering\\|denied\\|authenticated\"`. Cheap to include.\n\nBatch now (all independent):\nA. diffs of small files: `git diff agent/base.py agent/core/permission.py agent/llm/factory.py agent/llm/client.py tests/remote_path_test.py tests/local_shell_test.py tests/llm_client_test.py | head -170`\nB. `git diff agent/config.py | head -70; echo ====; git diff agent/tools/registry.py | head -90`\nC. `git diff agent/server.py | head -140`\nD. `git diff README.md ui/index.html | head -60; echo ====; grep -rn \"web_fetch\\|webfetch\" agent tools docs README.md 2>/dev/null | grep -v Binary | head -15; echo ====; grep -n \"mcp\\|web_search\\|webfetch\" ui/app.js | head -25`\nE. ssh -v diagnosis\nF. credential fill test: `printf \"protocol=https\\nhost=github.com\\n\\n\" | GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 GCM_INTERACTIVE=never git credential fill 2>&1 | sed -e 's/^password=.*/password=PRESENT/' -e 's/^oauth_refresh_token=.*/oauth=<redacted>/' | head -6`\n\nThat's 6 parallel calls. OK."}
