order commits so each state is as green as possible. Simplest: make the test fixes commit 1 (chore/test), then web tools, then llm, then perm. \n\n   Eh — actually let me not over-engineer. Plan: run full test suite now (this validates the FINAL tree). Commit sequence:\n   1. `test(transport): pin the real Popen spawn/decode contract` — local_shell_test.py + remote_path_test.py (if related to transport/decode)\n   2. `feat(tools): web_search/web_fetch + MCP backends` — everything web\n   3. `fix(llm): connect/read timeout split` — llm files\n   4. `refactor(perm): ask reason without args dump` — permission.py\n   Then chore(release): 0.1.14 bump + tag v0.1.14.\n\n   Hmm, 4 feature commits + release commit = matches repo style nicely.\n\n   But wait: permission.py — what about \"ask reasons must stay a reason\" app.js part... it's in commit 2's app.js. Mention in commit 2 body: \"ui: settings Web services rows; ask-dialog arg unwrap (extractCommand) + legacy-reason strip\". OK.\n\n4. **Remaining unknowns to check**: remote_path_test diff (+6) — need to see it to classify. And client.py diff tail + llm_client_test diff (covered by omitted chunk) — I know the gist (ConnectTimeout vs ReadTimeout classification). factory.py +1 (passes read_timeout presumably). Fine.\n\n5. **Tests to run**: \n   - py_compile all changed py files\n   - .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m tests.llm_client_test, local_shell_test, remote_path_test, mcpbackend_test, websearch_test (+ maybe server_test? server.py changed significantly — run it too; also ui_fonts_check? app.js changed... ui_fonts_check checks fonts, unrelated but cheap... skip. perm tests? there's no perm test listed... tests/perm-args-test.js is NEW (node). Run node tests/perm-args-test.js too.)\n   - Also config change → any config_test? Let me list tests dir.\n\n6. **Release mechanics**: \n   - VERSION: 0.1.13 → 0.1.14\n   - ui/package.json: 0.1.13 → 0.1.14 (single-line JSON)\n   - ui/package-lock.json: 2 spots (\"version\": \"0.1.13