{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789812950.1941469, "id": "b3022c737806", "content": "全绿 ✅（compile + 6 套件 + node 测试）。开始执行提交序列。先把 remote 切到 HTTPS（SSH key 已被 GitHub 拒绝，HTTPS 凭据可用），同时确认 package-lock 的版本字段位置：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_928a0577a1c14e74b382625d", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"git remote set-url origin https://github.com/Ethereal1024/Clutch.git && git remote -v\"}"}, {"id": "call_d9f8360053c341a8a06c35e9", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"grep -n '\\\"version\\\"' ui/package-lock.json | head -4\"}"}], "reasoning": "All tests pass. Now execute the commit sequence:\n\n1. Switch origin to HTTPS (SSH key is dead, HTTPS creds exist): `git remote set-url origin https://github.com/Ethereal1024/Clutch.git`\n2. Add scratch ignore rules to .gitignore (small edit)\n3. Commit 1: `test(transport): pin the real spawn/decode contracts` — tests/local_shell_test.py, tests/remote_path_test.py\n4. Commit 2: `feat(tools): web_search + web_fetch (native chain + MCP providers)` — agent/tools/websearch.py, agent/tools/mcpprovider.py, agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md, agent/prompts/tools/web_fetch.md, agent/tools/registry.py, agent/config.py, agent/server.py, ui/index.html, ui/app.js, README.md, tests/websearch_test.py, tests/mcpbackend_test.py\n   - app.js includes the ask-UX helpers (extractCommand/permReason) — mention in body.\n   - config.py includes llm_read_timeout — hmm, it's needed by commit 3's base.py; putting full config.py in commit 2 means commit 2 carries an unused-until-3 field. Alternatively put config.py in commit 3 (llm) — but then commit 2's registry reads config.web_search_* which wouldn't exist → commit 2 would be BROKEN (registry imports websearch, uses config.web_search_max_results). So config.py MUST be in commit 2. The llm_read_timeout field rides along; mention in commit 2 body? No — mention in commit 3 body \"config field landed with the web config commit\". Fine.\n5. Commit 3: `fix(llm): split connect/read timeout budgets` — agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py, agent/llm/client.py, agent/llm/factory.py, agent/base.py, tests/llm_client_test.py\n6. Commit 4: `refactor(perm): ask reason is a reason, args live in the args box` — agent/core/permission.py\n7. Release: bump VERSION, ui/package.json, ui/package-lock.json + .gitignore scratch rules → `chore(release): 0.1.14`\n8. Tag v0.1.14 (lightweight, matching previous)\n9. Push master + tag via HTTPS\n10. Verify CI via public API\n\nLet me check ui/package-lock.json version spots first: grep '\"version\"' — two spots typically: line 3-ish top and packages.\"\".version. Let me check and edit all.\n\n.gitignore edit: append a section:\n```\n\n# local scratch scripts/logs from ad-hoc testing sessions\n/scratch-*.py\n/scratch_*.log\n```\nWait — scratch-launch-tests.py and scratch-relaunch-tests.py match /scratch-*.py ✓. Logs: scratch_loop_test.log etc. match /scratch_*.log ✓. Also add /scratch_*.py in case. And server_smoke.log? Not present; skip (or include — harmless: `/server_smoke.log`? no, keep minimal, only what exists).\n\nEdit .gitignore via edit_file appending after the last line. The last line of .gitignore is:\n```\n/agent/skills/humanize-writing/\n/agent/skills/humanizer-document-zh/\n/agent/skills/humanizer-zh/\n/agent/skills/wudao-humanize/\n```\nI'll append after `/agent/skills/wudao-humanize/`.\n\nNow VERSION file: contains \"0.1.13\" (with or without newline?). `cat VERSION` printed \"0.1.13\" then ==== on same line? Output was \"0.1.13\\n====\" — cat output ended with newline probably. Use write_file? write_file for VERSION content \"0.1.14\\n\" — write_file probably adds content as given; I'll include trailing newline. Actually safer: `printf '0.1.14\\n' > VERSION` via run_command. Hmm, run_command writing files — allowed (shell). Fine.\n\nui/package.json: edit_file \"version\":\"0.1.13\" → \"version\":\"0.1.14\" (exact string `\"version\":\"0.1.13\"` appears once — top-level; desktopName etc. don't contain it).\n\nui/package-lock.json: `\"version\": \"0.1.13\"` appears twice (root + packages[\"\"]). edit_file replaces ONE occurrence — need two edits or sed. Use sed: `sed -i 's/\"version\": \"0.1.13\"/\"version\": \"0.1.14\"/g' ui/package-lock.json`. Check spacing first: package-lock is usually pretty-printed 2-space with `\"version\": \"0.1.13\"`. Verify with grep.\n\nSequence of commands (respecting dependencies):\n\nBatch A (independent):\n1. `git remote set-url origin https://github.com/Ethereal1024/Clutch.git && git remote -v`\n2. grep package-lock version spots: `grep -n '\"version\"' ui/package-lock.json | head -5`\n\nBatch B (after A confirms):\n3. edit_file .gitignore (append scratch section)\n4. edit_file package.json version\n5. run_command sed package-lock + printf VERSION\n6. commits 1-4 (sequential in one command? Each git add + git commit — can chain with && in one run_command; output shows each commit line)\n7. release commit + tag\n8. push\n9. CI check via curl\n\nCommits one command:\n```\ngit add tests/local_shell_test.py tests/remote_path_test.py && git commit -q -m \"test(transport): pin the real spawn/decode contracts\" -m \"- local_shell: Popen is the spawn path (Stop must kill the tree), fake a\n  pipe-like process and assert run()'s manual utf-8/replace decode on\n  mixed CJK + invalid bytes\n- remote_path: FakeBridge accepts cancel for parity with real transports\" && git add agent/tools/websearch.py agent/tools/mcpprovider.py agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md agent/prompts/tools/web_fetch.md agent/tools/registry.py agent/config.py agent/server.py ui/index.html ui/app.js README.md tests/websearch_test.py tests/mcpbackend_test.py && git commit -q -m \"feat(tools): web_search + web_fetch with pluggable backends\" -m \"...\" && ...\n```\n\nLong commit messages with -q -m multiple times. Careful with quoting in bash -c: use double quotes carefully, avoid ! and $. Messages in English (convention: code/comments English — commit messages in repo are English). \n\nLet me draft the messages:\n\nCommit 1:\n```\ntest(transport): pin the real spawn/decode contracts\n\n- local_shell: LocalTransport spawns via Popen (not run) so Stop can kill\n  the process tree; fake a pipe-like process and assert run()'s manual\n  utf-8/replace decode on CJK + invalid bytes\n- remote_path: FakeBridge.run accepts cancel, matching the real transport\n  signature (a remote exec just finishes on its own)\n```\n\nCommit 2:\n```\nfeat(tools): web_search + web_fetch with pluggable backends\n\n- tools/websearch.py: uniform backend chain — Bing RSS and DDG HTML are\n  keyless defaults; Tavily / SearXNG activate via env; web_fetch extracts\n  page text behind a SSRF guard (loopback/LAN refused, redirects re-checked)\n- tools/mcpprovider.py: declarative MCP tool-server registry; a configured\n  provider (e.g. xiaohongshu-mcp) joins the search chain over JSON-RPC\n  (initialize -> tools/call, session id, SSE fallback); unconfigured\n  providers are named nowhere and never suggested\n- registry: both tools available in chat + work (read-only network);\n  prompt/schema backends rendered from the live available set\n- server: settings POST/GET carry mcp_* keys (http(s) validated, '' clears,\n  flatten would drop them so persistence merges raw back); GET /api/mcp_status\n  reports reachability + login state per configured provider\n- ui: settings modal Web services rows with per-provider status; ask dialog\n  unwraps double-encoded run_command payloads (extractCommand) and strips\n  legacy \"... with args\" tails from reasons (permReason)\n- config: web_search_timeout/max_results, tavily/searxng env knobs, mcp_urls\n- tests: websearch_test (offline + --live), mcpbackend_test (loopback MCP\n  server: json/SSE/text/202/rpc-error/500 paths)\n```\n\nCommit 3:\n```\nfix(llm): split connect/read timeout budgets so slow streams survive\n\nA single float gave read the same 60s as connect, killing any stream whose\nprovider stalls (or whose buffering relay flushes only at the end) — the\n\"classic network is fine yet request timed out\". Now connect stays tight\n(<=15s, fail fast on dead routes) while read gets its own generous budget\n(Config.llm_read_timeout, default 240s; httpx read bounds the GAP between\nchunks, not total response time). Timeout errors now name their phase:\nconnect points at routing/proxy/base_url, read at the provider.\n```\n\nCommit 4:\n```\nrefactor(perm): ask reasons are reasons, not args dumps\n\nThe ask dialog renders args_repr in a dedicated box and the tool name in\nits header; embedding both in the reason string produced brace soup and\nduplicated names. The reason is now just \"permission ask\".\n```\n\nRelease commit:\n```\nchore(release): 0.1.14\n```\nplus .gitignore scratch rules — hmm, folding an ignore change into the release commit is a bit off-convention. Look at previous release commits: they touched VERSION, package-lock, package.json only. Cleaner: separate tiny chore commit:\n```\nchore: ignore local scratch test scripts and logs\n```\nThen release commit purely bumps. Good — matches repo hygiene style.\n\nOrder: commits 1-4, chore(.gitignore), chore(release) + tag v0.1.14.\n\nTag: `git tag v0.1.14` (lightweight, matches v0.1.13 which ls-remote showed as commit sha directly).\n\nPush: `git push origin master v0.1.14` — with credential manager it should use the stored PAT non-interactively. Set GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 to fail fast if something's off.\n\nThen verify: `git fetch origin && git status -sb` should show up to date. And curl the Actions API.\n\nLet me start: Batch A (remote set-url + grep package-lock). Then edits, then commits."}
