{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789812984.4988432, "id": "2393ea9645f9", "content": "bump 完成（VERSION / package.json / package-lock 三处 0.1.14，.gitignore 补了 scratch 规则）。按仓库惯例分逻辑提交——先提交测试修正 + web 工具链两组：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_9e50a9745c1f458c92fcf2fa", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"git add tests/local_shell_test.py tests/remote_path_test.py && git commit -q -m \\\"test(transport): pin the real spawn/decode contracts\\\" -m \\\"- local_shell: LocalTransport spawns via Popen (not run) so Stop can kill the\\n  process tree; fake a pipe-like process and assert run()'s manual\\n  utf-8/replace decode on CJK plus invalid bytes\\n- remote_path: FakeBridge.run accepts cancel, matching the real transport\\n  signature (a remote exec just finishes on its own)\\\" && git add agent/tools/websearch.py agent/tools/mcpprovider.py agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md agent/prompts/tools/web_fetch.md agent/tools/registry.py agent/config.py agent/server.py ui/index.html ui/app.js README.md tests/websearch_test.py tests/mcpbackend_test.py && git commit -q -m \\\"feat(tools): web_search + web_fetch with pluggable backends\\\" -m \\\"- tools/websearch.py: uniform backend chain - Bing RSS and DDG HTML are the\\n  keyless defaults; Tavily / SearXNG activate via env; web_fetch extracts page\\n  text behind a SSRF guard (loopback/LAN refused, redirects re-checked)\\n- tools/mcpprovider.py: declarative MCP tool-server registry; a configured\\n  provider (e.g. xiaohongshu-mcp) joins the search chain over JSON-RPC\\n  (initialize -> tools/call, session id, SSE fallback); unconfigured\\n  providers are named nowhere and never suggested\\n- registry: both tools in chat + work (read-only network); prompt/schema\\n  backends rendered from the live available set\\n- server: settings POST/GET carry mcp_* keys (http(s) validated, empty\\n  clears; flatten would drop them so persistence merges the raw file back);\\n  GET /api/mcp_status reports reachability + login per configured provider\\n- ui: settings modal Web services rows with per-provider status; ask dialog\\n  unwraps double-encoded run_command payloads (extractCommand) and strips\\n  legacy 'with args' tails from reasons (permReason)\\n- config: web_search_timeout/max_results, tavily/searxng env knobs, mcp_urls\\n- tests: websearch_test (offline, --live opts in) + mcpbackend_test (loopback\\n  MCP server: json/SSE/text/202/rpc-error/500 paths)\\\" && git log --oneline -2\"}"}], "reasoning": "All bumped. Now the commit sequence — 4 logical commits + 1 chore + 1 release commit, then tag. Chain them carefully with && in one or two run_commands. Long messages: use multiple -m flags. Watch out for bash quoting: use single... the command string itself is JSON; inside I use double quotes for -m args; avoid embedded double quotes in messages (use none or escape). My drafted messages contain no double quotes — check: commit 2 has `\"... with args\"` — yes it does! Rewrite without double quotes: use 'with args' in single quotes inside double-quoted string — fine in bash. Also \"classic network is fine yet request timed out\" in commit 3 — use single quotes inside.\n\nAlso parentheses fine. Backticks — none. `$` — none. Good.\n\nCommit 1+2 in one command, 3+4+chore+release+tag in another (to stay under limits). Actually chain all in one? Output manageable. Let me do two commands to be safe, sequential dependency — must run in ORDER (same block executes in order, but if commit 1 fails, command 2 would still run — bad). So run command 1 first, verify, then command 2. Sequential blocks.\n\nCommand 1:\n```\ngit add tests/local_shell_test.py tests/remote_path_test.py && git commit -q -m \"test(transport): pin the real spawn/decode contracts\" -m \"- local_shell: LocalTransport spawns via Popen (not run) so Stop can kill the\n  process tree; fake a pipe-like process and assert run()'s manual\n  utf-8/replace decode on CJK plus invalid bytes\n- remote_path: FakeBridge.run accepts cancel, matching the real transport\n  signature (a remote exec just finishes on its own)\" && git add agent/tools/websearch.py agent/tools/mcpprovider.py agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md agent/prompts/tools/web_fetch.md agent/tools/registry.py agent/config.py agent/server.py ui/index.html ui/app.js README.md tests/websearch_test.py tests/mcpbackend_test.py && git commit -q -m \"feat(tools): web_search + web_fetch with pluggable backends\" -m \"- tools/websearch.py: uniform backend chain - Bing RSS and DDG HTML are the\n  keyless defaults; Tavily / SearXNG activate via env; web_fetch extracts page\n  text behind a SSRF guard (loopback/LAN refused, redirects re-checked)\n- tools/mcpprovider.py: declarative MCP tool-server registry; a configured\n  provider (e.g. xiaohongshu-mcp) joins the search chain over JSON-RPC\n  (initialize -> tools/call, session id, SSE fallback); unconfigured\n  providers are named nowhere and never suggested\n- registry: both tools in chat + work (read-only network); prompt/schema\n  backends rendered from the live available set\n- server: settings POST/GET carry mcp_* keys (http(s) validated, empty\n  clears; flatten would drop them so persistence merges the raw file back);\n  GET /api/mcp_status reports reachability + login per configured provider\n- ui: settings modal Web services rows with per-provider status; ask dialog\n  unwraps double-encoded run_command payloads (extractCommand) and strips\n  legacy 'with args' tails from reasons (permReason)\n- config: web_search_timeout/max_results, tavily/searxng env knobs, mcp_urls\n- tests: websearch_test (offline, --live opts in) + mcpbackend_test (loopback\n  MCP server: json/SSE/text/202/rpc-error/500 paths)\" && git log --oneline -2\n```\n\nCommand 2:\n```\ngit add agent/llm/llm_clients/openai_client.py agent/llm/client.py agent/llm/factory.py agent/base.py tests/llm_client_test.py && git commit -q -m \"fix(llm): split connect/read timeout budgets so slow streams survive\" -m \"One float gave read the same 60s as connect, killing any stream whose\nprovider stalls (or whose buffering relay flushes only at the end) - the\n'classic network is fine yet request timed out'. Connect now stays tight\n(<=15s, fail fast on dead routes) while read gets its own generous budget\n(Config.llm_read_timeout, default 240s; httpx read bounds the gap between\nchunks, not total response time). Timeout errors name their phase: connect\npoints at routing/proxy/base_url, read at the provider.\" && git add agent/core/permission.py && git commit -q -m \"refactor(perm): ask reasons are reasons, not args dumps\" -m \"The ask dialog renders args_repr in a dedicated box and the tool name in\nits header; embedding both in the reason string produced brace soup and\nduplicated names. The reason is now just 'permission ask'.\" && git add .gitignore && git commit -q -m \"chore: ignore local scratch test scripts and logs\" && git add VERSION ui/package.json ui/package-lock.json && git commit -q -m \"chore(release): 0.1.14\" && git tag v0.1.14 && git log --oneline -7\n```\n\nThen push. Then CI check."}
