{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789813264.3810606, "id": "d26d080c78a4", "name": "load_memory", "arguments": "{\"name\":\"Xiaohongshu open-source access landscape\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_dcd5b64cc1b1498eac96b371"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789813264.3967986, "id": "c08f9bd57c65", "tool_call_id": "call_7c11f7349850426e9a701df4", "content": "\"\"\"Registry of external MCP tool servers that extend web search.\n\nOne entry here turns a generic HTTP MCP server into a web_search backend: the\nprovider names its config key, the tool to call, and how to map its results\nonto the uniform {title, url, snippet} shape. Adding a platform means adding\none McpProvider to MCP_PROVIDERS — the search chain, the rendered prompt and\nthe settings UI all pick it up without further changes.\n\nHosts without a given service configured simply leave the URL empty: the\nbackend is then absent from the chain, and nothing in the prompts, the error\ntexts or the UI mentions it (no \"please install X\" advice, ever).\n\nImport-safe from anywhere: stdlib only, no agent-package imports.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport urllib.parse\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Any, Callable\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass McpProvider:\n    \"\"\"Declarative spec for one MCP-backed search source.\"\"\"\n\n    name: str                                # backend name (web_search backend=<name>)\n    label: str                               # human label for the settings modal\n    search_tool: str                         # MCP tool invoked for searches\n    search_args: Callable[[str, int], dict]  # (query, limit) -> tool arguments\n    map_results: Callable[[Any], list[dict]]  # parsed tool result -> [{title,url,snippet}]\n    placeholder: str = \"\"                    # example URL shown in the settings modal\n    status_tool: str = \"\"                    # optional MCP tool reporting login state\n\n    def url_for(self, config: Any) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Configured endpoint ('' = not configured on this machine).\n\n        Settings-modal values land in Config.mcp_urls under the provider name;\n        CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL is the env-only equivalent.\n        \"\"\"\n        urls = getattr(config, \"mcp_urls\", None) or {}\n        value = urls.get(self.name) or os.environ.get(\n            f\"CLUTCH_MCP_{self.name.upper()}_URL\", \"\"\n        )\n        return str(value).strip().rstrip(\"/\")\n\n\ndef _first_list(data: Any) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Pull the first list value out of a tool result (bare list or wrapped).\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(data, list):\n        return data\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        for key in (\"data\", \"items\", \"feeds\", \"results\", \"notes\"):\n            if isinstance(data.get(key), list):\n                return data[key]\n    return []\n\n\n# ---- concrete providers ------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _xhs_args(query: str, limit: int) -> dict:\n    return {\"keyword\": query, \"limit\": limit}\n\n\ndef _xhs_map(data: Any) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"search_feeds rows -> uniform rows. Keeps xsec_token in the URL:\n    follow-up detail calls (and the site itself) require it.\"\"\"\n    rows: list[dict] = []\n    for it in _first_list(data):\n        if not isinstance(it, dict):\n            continue\n        note_id = str(it.get(\"id\") or it.get(\"note_id\") or \"\").strip()\n        if not note_id:\n            continue\n        url = f\"https://www.xiaohongshu.com/explore/{note_id}\"\n        token = str(it.get(\"xsec_token\") or \"\").strip()\n        if token:\n            url += \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode({\"xsec_token\": token})\n        rows.append(\n            {\n                \"title\": str(it.get(\"title\") or \"\").strip(),\n                \"url\": url,\n                \"snippet\": str(it.get(\"desc\") or it.get(\"description\") or \"\").strip(),\n            }\n        )\n    return rows\n\n\nXIAOHONGSHU = McpProvider(\n    name=\"xiaohongshu\",\n    label=\"Xiaohongshu MCP\",\n    search_tool=\"search_feeds\",\n    search_args=_xhs_args,\n    map_results=_xhs_map,\n    placeholder=\"http://localhost:18060/mcp\",\n    status_tool=\"check_login_status\",\n)\n\n# The registry. Extension point: add one entry, everything else follows\n# (search chain, rendered prompt, settings modal rows).\nMCP_PROVIDERS: dict[str, McpProvider] = {\n    \"xiaohongshu\": XIAOHONGSHU,\n}\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789813264.40379, "id": "db4ca2b8e4c6", "tool_call_id": "call_6dc212621fab456c8eeef6ba", "content": "ui\\app.js:\n  Line 2814: // Rendered from GET /api/settings mcp_providers metadata: a host without a\n  Line 2817: (function initMcpServices() {\n  Line 2818:   const box = document.getElementById(\"mcp-services\");\n  Line 2833:       input.id = \"mcp-input-\" + p.key;\n  Line 2836:       input.placeholder = p.placeholder || \"http://localhost:port/mcp\";\n  Line 2840:       status.dataset.mcpStatus = p.key;\n  Line 2855:     save.id = \"mcp-services-save\";\n  Line 2866:         const el = document.getElementById(\"mcp-input-\" + p.key);\n  Line 2881:       const st = await apiFetch(\"/api/mcp_status\");\n  Line 2883:       for (const row of (st && st.providers) || []) byKey[\"mcp_\" + row.name] = row;\n  Line 2884:       box.querySelectorAll(\"[data-mcp-status]\").forEach((el) => {\n  Line 2885:         const row = byKey[el.dataset.mcpStatus];\n  Line 2902:       render(s.mcp_providers || [], {});", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789813264.4093404, "id": "9b08c96cdadc", "tool_call_id": "call_94613241359249868833b9d2", "content": "Search the web for information the workspace cannot answer: current events, library versions and release notes, error messages, docs pages. Returns ranked results (title, URL, snippet); follow up with web_fetch on the 1-2 most relevant URLs for the full text. query is the search string — engine syntax like quoted phrases, site: and -term filters work; short factual queries beat long sentences. max_results caps entries (default $max). Backends available on this machine ($backends) are tried in order — the first that returns results wins; when all fail the error lists each backend's reason, and backend=<name> pins one.\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789813264.410573, "id": "901a617c589a", "tool_call_id": "call_dcd5b64cc1b1498eac96b371", "content": "[Xiaohongshu open-source access landscape]\nXHS (xiaohongshu) access survey (2026-09, via GitHub API): community consensus is real-browser + user's own login session; pure-HTTP signature reversing has been marginalized. Key projects: Panniantong/Agent-Reach 82.6k stars (agent-facing CLI, XHS route = OpenCLI desktop-session > xpzouying/xiaohongshu-mcp server > xhs-cli; deliberately never logs in itself nor reads browser cookies, only user-controlled sessions / manual Cookie-Editor export; per-platform multi-backend fallback + `agent-reach doctor` — same design as our websearch chain). xpzouying/xiaohongshu-mcp 15.8k (Go+Playwright, QR login, cookies in ./data, read AND publish, HTTP MCP on :18060; author: 1.5yr no bans, only cookie expiry). NanmiCoder/MediaCrawler 65.1k (Playwright crawler, notes+comments). JoeanAmier/XHS-Downloader 12.7k (single-note download, often login-free). Integration options for Clutch: (a) zero-code — call agent-reach via run_command; (b) thin backend — CLUTCH_XHS_CLI external-command backend in websearch chain; (c) Tier-1 cookie injection (~50 lines) same as xhs-cli approach.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
