{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789813437.3275187, "id": "71d8ec258eb5", "content": "不是——设计上就是**多 MCP 后端并存**的，现在只有一个纯粹是因为注册表里只写了小红书这一个条目。让我把关键代码段调出来给你看证据：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_0a61bafde5c04b3c83db6e84", "name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"limit\":36,\"offset\":548,\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user asks: \"那从设计上来说是只能有一个mcp后端吗\" — \"By design, can there only be one MCP backend?\"\n\nFrom the code I've read:\n\n1. `mcpprovider.py`: `MCP_PROVIDERS: dict[str, McpProvider]` — it's a **registry/dict**, explicitly designed as an extension point: \"Adding a platform means adding one McpProvider to MCP_PROVIDERS — the search chain, the rendered prompt and the settings UI all pick it up without further changes.\" Currently only `xiaohongshu` is registered, but the design supports MANY MCP providers.\n\n2. Each provider gets:\n   - Its own config key: `mcp_<name>` in settings.json (`mcp_xiaohongshu`), env `CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL`\n   - Its own backend in the chain: `websearch.py` line 570: `for _p in MCP_PROVIDERS.values(): _BACKENDS[_p.name] = _mcp_backend(_p)` — appended after native backends\n   - Its own settings UI row: server `_settings_get` returns `mcp_providers` list, UI renders one row per provider\n   - Its own status entry in /api/mcp_status\n\n3. So no — the design supports N MCP backends simultaneously. Currently only one is REGISTERED (xiaohongshu), because that's the only platform someone wrote a spec for. Adding another (e.g. bilibili, zhihu, weibo MCP servers) = one McpProvider entry.\n\nImportant nuance: multiple providers can each point to a DIFFERENT MCP server (one URL per provider). Can one MCP server host multiple search tools? Each provider spec names exactly one search_tool. If one MCP server exposes multiple useful search tools, you'd add multiple providers (with different names) pointing to the same URL. Is that possible? `url_for` reads `mcp_urls.get(self.name)` — each provider has its own name → own key → own URL. Two providers could have the same URL with different search_tool. Yes, that works — the key is per-provider.\n\nLet me double check the websearch.py code at lines 549-583 to be precise about how MCP backends join the chain. I saw:\n- Line 549: `_mcp_backend(provider)` \n- Line 570: `_BACKENDS[_p.name] = _mcp_backend(_p)` (in some loop over MCP_PROVIDERS)\n\nI should verify the loop quickly to answer precisely. Also the search chain order: MCP backends appended AFTER native ones (dict order: tavily, searxng, bing, ddg, then MCP providers in registry order).\n\nLet me read lines 548-600 of websearch.py to confirm.\n\nAlso the UI: one row per provider (the `for (const p of providers)` loop in app.js render()).\n\nAlso per-provider settings: `_split_mcp_fields` accepts ANY `mcp_<name>` key (\"names are free-form so a newer UI can configure providers this build does not know\") — forward compatible.\n\nAnd /api/mcp_status returns per-provider status.\n\nSo the answer structure:\n1. 不是 — 注册表设计就是多后端（dict，循环展开），现在只有一个是因为只写了小红书一个 spec\n2. 机制:每个 provider 一行 UI、一个 mcp_<name> 配置键、链尾一个 backend、独立状态探测\n3. 一个 MCP 服务器也可以拆成多个 provider(同 URL 不同 search_tool)\n4. 扩展成本: 加一个 McpProvider 即可,三处自动跟上\n5. 设计边界: 每个 provider 固定一个 search_tool + 一个结果映射 — 平台差异(字段、登录态工具)都在 spec 里\n\nLet me verify the loop code first (lines 548-583) — one quick read. I read 539-548 already; continue from 549."}
