{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789815331.0962183, "id": "51e288240e90", "tool_call_id": "call_d641ed27fbeb41e29cf32c7d", "content": "[MCP plugin backend design (approved, pending work mode)]\nApproved design for the MCP plugin backend (user said start coding; chat mode blocked it — needs work mode). Goals: modular+polymorphic plugin seam for future MCPs; zero UX footprint on hosts without a given MCP (never \"please install X\"); generalized interface + registration. Plan: NEW agent/tools/mcpprovider.py — frozen McpProvider dataclass (name, label, url config key, search_tool, search_args builder, map_results callable, optional detail_tool) + MCP_PROVIDERS registry {\"xiaohongshu\": spec mapping search_feeds -> {title,url,snippet}, url = explore/{id}?xsec_token=...}. websearch.py: wrap the 4 existing backends + MCP ones into a uniform Backend protocol (name, available(config), search(q,limit,config,get)); add _mcp_call JSON-RPC client (initialize -> notifications/initialized -> tools/call, capture Mcp-Session-Id); _available_backends = registry AND configured (mcp_urls in Config, key prefix mcp_, env CLUTCH_MCP_<NAME>_URL, settings.json same key); error text and web_search.md prompt $backends render DYNAMICALLY from configured set only (factual absence, no install advice). server.py: settings POST/GET allow mcp_* keys; /api/mcp_status per-provider reachable+login (check_login_status). UI: settings modal renders MCP rows dynamically + status dot (has_api_key precedent). Degradation matrix: unconfigured host -> backend absent from chain, unknown-backend error lists only real ones; configured+down -> BackendError \"MCP unreachable at <url>\"; not logged in -> status via settings UI, tool surface unaffected. Code text English-only; tests self-run via .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m tests.X.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789815331.0981324, "id": "a9a3d13cedbe", "tool_call_id": "call_b3276922373540b0a1549176", "content": "[MCP web-search plugin shipped and verified]\nShipped in work mode (all tests green, incl. live): MCP plugin backend for web_search. (1) NEW agent/tools/mcpprovider.py — frozen McpProvider dataclass (name/label/search_tool/search_args/map_results/placeholder/status_tool) + MCP_PROVIDERS registry, xiaohongshu spec (search_feeds -> {title,url,snippet}, url keeps xsec_token, status_tool check_login_status); stdlib-only, import-safe. (2) websearch.py — Backend frozen record (name/search/available) wraps 4 native backends, _mcp_rpc/_mcp_call JSON-RPC client (initialize -> notifications/initialized -> tools/call, Mcp-Session-Id, SSE-frame fallback, all errors -> WebError; deliberately bypasses the SSRF guard because MCP endpoints are operator-configured loopback), _mcp_backend adapter joins the chain, _available_backends = registered AND configured, public available_backends alias + mcp_status(). (3) config.mcp_urls dict field. (4) server.py — _split_mcp_fields/_mcp_keys_from/_login_state helpers; settings POST accepts mcp_* (http(s) validated, '' clears, unknown providers kept; \"nothing to save\" guard extended; flatten_settings would DROP mcp_* keys so persistence merges them back from raw); _settings_get returns mcp_providers metadata; GET /api/mcp_status (reachable+login, best-effort normalization); main() loads mcp_* at boot. (5) registry renders prompt $backends + schema backend param from the live available set; prompts/tools/web_search.md uses $backends. (6) UI: #mcp-services div in settings modal + self-contained initMcpServices block at end of ui/app.js (renders rows, own Save button, status text connected·logged in/unreachable/blank); main.js writeSettingsFile needs NO change (merges into existing file, mcp_* preserved). (7) tests/mcpbackend_test.py — 30+ checks incl. real loopback MCP server (json/SSE/text/202/rpcerror/500 paths). Gotcha discovered: an error echoing the model's own pinned backend name is FINE (factual echo); pollution = naming unconfigured services or install advice. Smoke-tested over HTTP and restored ~/.clutch/settings.json afterwards.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789815331.099658, "id": "8d8b4e75637e", "tool_call_id": "call_dd2d6484c433488aa2930c4b", "content": "[No-bias principle: no hardcoded platform names in code]\nUser principle (reiterated as a violation report): \"代码不应该有任何具备偏向性的设计\" — no hardcoded platform/service names in Clutch's code. The shipped v0.1.14 MCP design violates it: MCP_PROVIDERS registry contains exactly one concrete entry (XIAOHONGSHU with bespoke _xhs_args/_xhs_map code) — user calls this 掉价/dressed-up hardcode. Agreed refactor direction (chat-mode discussion, not yet implemented): core keeps ONLY a generic declarative MCP engine — config-driven McpServiceSpec {name,url,search_tool,args template {query}/{limit},list_key auto,fields map,url_template with {id}/{xsec_token} placeholders,status_tool,login_field}; xiaohongshu is fully expressible as such a record (proven: _xhs_map = list unwrap + url template + desc|description fallback). UI gets \"+ add service\" rows. Any built-in platform presets must be editable/deletable DATA (e.g. presets.json), never code; shipping zero presets is acceptable. Migration: old mcp_xiaohongshu settings key converted one-time via preset. Long-tail payloads that defeat declaration (signing, pagination, second-hop detail fetches) get an escape hatch, default empty. Note: narrow neutrality (no service names in prompts/errors/UI unless configured) WAS honored; the broader no-bias principle was not.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
