{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789817128.921553, "id": "f58af0a8feb3", "content": "这个问题值得查官方一手资料来答（而不是凭记忆）。让我拉一下 MCP 官方规范：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_ea21a0312cb644b98eb47073", "name": "web_fetch", "arguments": "{\"url\":\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/getting-started/intro\",\"max_chars\":8000}"}, {"id": "call_6f087e933c1d404ca567012d", "name": "web_fetch", "arguments": "{\"url\":\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/architecture\",\"max_chars\":12000}"}], "reasoning": "The user asks: \"从正统定义来说，什么是mcp？\" — \"From the orthodox/official definition, what is MCP?\"\n\nThis is asking about the official definition of MCP (Model Context Protocol). The previous conversation has been about the project's own MCP integration. Now they want the canonical/official definition — i.e., what Anthropic's Model Context Protocol actually is, from the spec's perspective.\n\nThis is a factual question about current external knowledge. I should search the web for the official MCP definition (modelcontextprotocol.io, spec) to give an accurate, grounded answer rather than from memory. MCP was announced by Anthropic in November 2024. The official definition: \"MCP is an open protocol that standardizes how applications provide context to LLMs. Think of MCP like a USB-C port for AI applications.\"\n\nKey concepts from the official spec:\n- Open protocol, open-sourced (MIT), originally by Anthropic (Nov 25, 2024), later adopted by OpenAI (March 2025) and Google DeepMind.\n- Standardizes how applications provide context to LLMs — client-server architecture.\n- Hosts (LLM applications like Claude Desktop, IDEs), Clients (connectors inside the host, 1:1 with servers), Servers (external programs exposing capabilities).\n- Core primitives: Tools (model-controlled), Resources (app-controlled data), Prompts (user-controlled templates), plus Sampling, Roots, Elicitation (newer), Notifications, Logging.\n- Transports: stdio, Streamable HTTP (replaced HTTP+SSE in 2025-03-26 revision).\n- JSON-RPC 2.0 as wire format.\n- Life cycle: initialization (version negotiation, capability discovery), operation, shutdown.\n- \"USB-C for AI applications\" analogy.\n\nI should fetch the official spec/docs to be precise and cite. Let me do a web search and fetch modelcontextprotocol.io.\n\nThe user is Chinese-speaking, so answer in Chinese, but quote the official English definitions.\n\nLet me search and fetch the official pages."}
