{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789817357.5178201, "id": "e84fa48810d8", "tool_call_id": "call_06beb5945d8143718fe4c87d", "content": "415: # ---- HTTP MCP client (JSON-RPC over POST) ------------------------------------\n416: \n417: \n418: _MCP_PROTO = \"2025-03-26\"  # protocol version announced in the initialize call\n419: \n420: \n421: def _mcp_rpc(\n422:     url: str,\n423:     payload: dict,\n424:     session: str | None,\n425:     timeout: float,\n426:     cancel: Any = None,\n427: ) -> tuple[dict, str | None]:\n428:     \"\"\"One JSON-RPC POST to an HTTP MCP server; returns (response, session id).\n429: \n430:     Deliberately NOT routed through _http_get: the private-network guard exists\n431:     for model-controlled URLs, while this endpoint comes from operator config\n432:     and is typically loopback. Every failure surfaces as WebError so callers\n433:     treat MCP problems like any other backend failure.\n434:     \"\"\"\n435:     if cancel is not None and cancel.is_set():\n436:         raise WebError(\"aborted by user\")\n437:     body = json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\")\n438:     headers = {\n439:         \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n440:         \"Accept\": \"application/json, text/event-stream\",\n441:     }\n442:     if session:\n443:         headers[\"Mcp-Session-Id\"] = session\n444:     request = urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=headers, method=\"POST\")\n445:     try:\n446:         resp = urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=timeout)\n447:     except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n448:         raise WebError(f\"HTTP {e.code} from MCP server {url}\") from e\n449:     except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n450:         reason = getattr(e, \"reason\", e)\n451:         if isinstance(reason, (socket.timeout, TimeoutError)):\n452:             raise WebError(f\"MCP server timed out after {timeout:.0f}s: {url}\")\n453:         raise WebError(f\"MCP server unreachable ({reason}): {url}\") from e\n454:     except (ValueError, OSError) as e:\n455:         raise WebError(f\"MCP request failed ({e}): {url}\") from e\n456:     with resp:\n457:         raw = _drain(resp, cancel, _MAX_BYTES)\n458:     sid = resp.headers.get(\"Mcp-Session-Id\") or session\n459:     text = _decode_body(raw, resp.headers.get(\"Content-Type\", \"\"))\n460:     if text.startswith(\"event:\") or text.startswith(\"data:\") or \"\\ndata:\" in text[:2048]:\n461:         # SSE-framed reply: keep the last data frame (the JSON-RPC response)\n462:         frames = [ln[5:].strip() for ln in text.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\"data:\")]\n463:         text = frames[-1] if frames else \"\"\n464:     if not text.strip():\n465:         return {}, sid  # e.g. 202 Accepted for a notification\n466:     try:\n467:         data = json.loads(text)\n468:     except ValueError as e:\n469:         raise WebError(f\"MCP server returned non-JSON: {_short(e)}\") from e\n470:     if isinstance(data, dict) and data.get(\"error\") is not None:\n471:         err = data[\"error\"]\n472:         msg = err.get(\"message\", str(err)) if isinstance(err, dict) else str(err)\n473:         raise WebError(f\"MCP error: {_short(msg)}\")\n474:     return (data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}), sid\n475: \n476: \n... (showing lines 415-476 of 702; use offset=477 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789817412.5668375, "id": "120eb3b04796", "content": "批评收到，而且它有一半是真的。先把账算清楚，再回答“二选一”——因为我认为这是个**假两难**，真正的选项是“把话说准 + 把负担砍到最小”。\n\n## 一、批评里成立的部分（必须承认）\n\n| 缺口 | 事实 |\n|---|---|\n| **只支持 HTTP 传输** | 生态里大量现成 MCP 服务器是 stdio（npx/uvx 启动的），Clutch 只说 Streamable HTTP。指望“接任意 MCP 服务器”的人会失望——这就是“阉割版”指责里最实在的一点 |\n| **没有 `tools/list` 发现** | 操作者必须手填 `search_tool` 和 `args` 模板，而真正的 MCP 客户端会自己发现。**这才是真正的“累赘”**——它压在操作者的配置数据上，不在运行时 |\n| **措辞邀请过度期待** | README 说“外部 MCP 服务可以接入”，会让人以为 resources/prompts/任意工具都通 |\n\n## 二、批评里不成立的部分（需要反驳）\n\n**1. “阉割版”不是协议违规，是协议允许的形态。** 规范自己的设计原则写着：*capability-based negotiation*——客户端声明只支持 `tools`，就只走 `tools/call`，这是**完全合法的 client**。MCP 被刻意设计成渐进采用（\"Features can be added progressively… Backwards compatibility is maintained\"）。所以架构没有病，病的是**没把范围说出口**。\n\n**2. “自拟协议”不是简化，是成本置换。** 拿数字说话：\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph now[\"现状: 协议成本已付清\"]\n        A[\"协议切片 ~135 行<br/>_mcp_rpc + _mcp_call<br/>一次性, 已测 59 项\"] \n        B[\"声明式映射引擎 ~330 行<br/>记录/模板/字段链<br/>与协议无关, 哪条路都要写\"]\n    end\n    subgraph alt[\"自拟协议后\"]\n        C[\"删掉 135 行协议代码\"] --> D[\"换来: 每个现成 MCP 服务器<br/>前面架一个适配层<br/>永久成本, 操作者承担\"]\n    end\n    A -.换成.-> D\n    B --> E[\"原样保留\"]\n```\n\n关键矛盾：**这个功能的立项理由本身就是现成的 MCP 服务器**（xiaohongshu 搜索服务就是生态里的 MCP server）。自拟 Clutch-Protocol™ 意味着每个现成服务器前面都要架 shim——用 135 行已付清的一次性成本，换永久性的生态不兼容。\n\n**3. “自拟接口”这条路项目里其实已经有了。** Tavily、SearXNG 就是直连函数（`_tavily`/`_searxng`，各约 20 行）——对已知服务用自有接口，对操作者自建的长尾服务用 MCP。二分法里被漏掉的正是这个分层：**两者本来就不互斥**。\n\n## 三、我的建议：不二选一，做三件小事\n\n1. **把话说准（近零成本）**：README/docstring 从“支持 MCP”改为精确表述——*“MCP 客户端：仅 Tools 原语 / 仅 Streamable HTTP 传输，不支持 stdio 服务器”*。“阉割版”的刺痛感来自信息不对称，说破就不痛了。\n\n2. **用 `tools/list` 砍掉真累赘（有界，~30 行 + 测试）**：`mcp_status` 本来就会探测服务器，顺手调一次 `tools/list`：\n   - 状态行从 `connected` 变成 `connected · 3 tools: search_feeds, …`\n   - 恰好只有一个工具时，UI 预填 `search_tool`，记录缩到 `{name, url}` 两个字段\n   - 操作者负担降到理论最小值，而运行时一行协议代码不加\n\n3. **把非目标写下来（防未来滑坡）**：明确不做 stdio、不做 resources/prompts/sampling、**尤其不做**“任意 MCP 服务器的一切工具自动变成 agent 工具”——那才是真正的大累赘（schema 翻译、逐工具注册、安全面扩大）。目前 135 行的切片之所以轻，恰恰因为拒绝了它。\n\n## 四、决策判据（如果你仍想推倒）\n\n只有一种情况 Horn B（自拟协议）是诚实的：**你确定今后永远不再接任何现成 MCP 服务器**，且嫌那 135 行握手代码碍眼。那时自拟协议就长这样——\n\n```\nPOST <url>          {\"query\": q, \"limit\": n}\n→ 200  [{\"title\": …, \"url\": …, \"snippet\": …}]     # 或用 fields 映射适配\n```\n\n映射引擎 330 行原封保留，删 135 行协议代码，架构确实更干净。但请意识到你同时删掉的是这个功能存在的理由。\n\n---\n\n如果你认可方案三，切到工作模式我就动手：改动是 README 两处措辞 + `mcp_status` 加 `tools/list` 探测 + UI 状态行与预填 + `mcpbackend_test.py` 补几项检查。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "Now I have all the facts:\n\n- MCP protocol slice in websearch.py: `_mcp_rpc` (lines 421-474, ~54 lines), `_mcp_call` (477-527, ~51 lines), `_mcp_backend` (553-570, ~18 lines), `mcp_status` (~14 lines). Total ≈ 135 lines, all tested (59 checks in mcpbackend_test.py).\n- Protocol-agnostic engine (mcpprovider.py, ~330 lines): records, parse/validate, args templates, field chains, url templates, list unwrap, login normalization. This part is needed under EITHER horn.\n\nNow let me compose the answer. The user poses a dilemma:\n- A: don't saddle search with MCP; either don't claim MCP (because it's a \"castrated version\")\n- B: or define own interface/protocol, drop MCP entirely, simplify architecture\n\nMy answer, honestly argued:\n\n**1. Where the critique lands (the true parts):**\n- HTTP-only: most published MCP servers are stdio (npx/uvx). Clutch only speaks Streamable HTTP. So \"supports MCP\" would mislead someone expecting to point it at any MCP server from the registry.\n- No `tools/list`: operator must hand-declare tool name + args template — a real MCP client discovers this. That's the actual \"累赘\" (burden), and it's on the *operator data*, not on the runtime.\n- The word \"MCP\" in README invites fuller expectations (resources, prompts, generic tool surfacing) that will never come.\n\n**2. Where it doesn't land (the false parts):**\n- \"阉割版\" implies spec violation. But the spec's own design principles bless this: capability-based negotiation — a client declaring only `tools` capability and using only `tools/call` is a fully legitimate conforming client. MCP was explicitly designed for progressive adoption (\"Features can be added progressively... Backwards compatibility is maintained\"). The 135-line slice is not a broken implementation of MCP; it's a minimal conformant one. The honest defect is *wording/scope disclosure*, not architecture.\n- Horn B is not cheaper, it's a cost *swap*: protocol cost (~135 lines, already written and tested, one-time) becomes adapter cost (per-service, forever, borne by the operator). The founding use case — xiaohongshu — exists as an MCP server in the wild. Inventing Clutch-Protocol™ would force a shim in front of every existing MCP server. \"彻底简化运行逻辑\" saves ~135 lines of already-stable code and buys permanent incompatibility with the ecosystem that made this worthwhile.\n- Also note: the project ALREADY has the \"own protocol\" pattern for HTTP JSON search services — they're called native backends (tavily, searxng: `_tavily`, `_searxng`, ~20 lines each, direct functions). So the dichotomy is false in practice: direct interfaces for known services, MCP for the long tail of operator-run servers.\n\n**3. What actually deserves doing (bounded, small):**\n- (a) Wording honesty (near-zero cost): README + docstring say \"MCP 客户端（仅 Tools 原语 / 仅 Streamable HTTP；不支持 stdio 服务器）\". Never bare-claim \"支持 MCP\".\n- (b) tools/list discovery (bounded): `mcp_status` already probes the server — have it also call `tools/list` and report tool names (and input-schema required fields). Then a well-behaved server needs only `{name, url}`: UI can prefill search_tool when exactly one tool exists, and the status dot can show \"3 tools: search_feeds, check_login_status…\". Operator burden drops to the true minimum without new protocol surface. ~20-30 lines + tests.\n- (c) Explicit non-goals, written down: no stdio, no resources/prompts/sampling, no generic \"any MCP server's tools become agent tools\" (that's the real burden — schema translation, per-tool registry, security surface — and it's the thing to refuse even if someday asked).\n\n**4. The decision rule** (give the user a crisp criterion):\n- If the set of services you'll ever connect = services that already speak MCP → keep the slice, fix wording, add tools/list. \n- If you'll never touch an existing MCP server again → then Horn B is honest: a `POST {\"query\",\"limit\"}` → rows convention + the existing fields mapping engine would delete the 135 protocol lines. But you'd also delete the reason this feature exists.\n\nAlso worth one sharp observation: the protocol-agnostic mapping engine (the actual complexity, ~330 lines) survives both horns. The debate is about 135 lines of handshake code and one honest sentence. Framing it that way shows the stakes are smaller than the rhetoric.\n\nShould I offer to implement (b)? Yes — but chat mode; say switching to work mode is needed. Keep it as an offer.\n\nLength: substantial but tight. Use a small table for A vs B costs. Maybe a compact mermaid? Probably not needed; tables + numbers carry it. Keep code identifiers in English, prose in Chinese."}
{"type": "final", "timestamp": 1789817412.5695493, "id": "e2968ddd6b67", "status": "completed", "summary": "批评收到，而且它有一半是真的。先把账算清楚，再回答“二选一”——因为我认为这是个**假两难**，真正的选项是“把话说准 + 把负担砍到最小”。\n\n## 一、批评里成立的部分（必须承认）\n\n| 缺口 | 事实 |\n|---|---|\n| **只支持 HTTP 传输** | 生态里大量现成 MCP 服务器是 stdio（npx/uvx 启动的），Clutch 只说 Streamable HTTP。指望“接任意 MCP 服务器”的人会失望——这就是“阉割版”指责里最实在的一点 |\n| **没有 `tools/list` 发现** | 操作者必须手填 `search_tool` 和 `args` 模板，而真正的 MCP 客户端会自己发现。**这才是真正的“累赘”**——它压在操作者的配置数据上，不在运行时 |\n| **措辞邀请过度期待** | README 说“外部 MCP 服务可以接入”，会让人以为 resources/prompts/任意工具都通 |\n\n## 二、批评里不成立的部分（需要反驳）\n\n**1. “阉割版”不是协议违规，是协议允许的形态。** 规范自己的设计原则写着：*capability-based negotiation*——客户端声明只支持 `tools`，就只走 `tools/call`，这是**完全合法的 client**。MCP 被刻意设计成渐进采用（\"Features can be added progressively… Backwards compatibility is maintained\"）。所以架构没有病，病的是**没把范围说出口**。\n\n**2. “自拟协议”不是简化，是成本置换。** 拿数字说话：\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph now[\"现状: 协议成本已付清\"]\n        A[\"协议切片 ~135 行<br/>_mcp_rpc + _mcp_call<br/>一次性, 已测 59 项\"] \n        B[\"声明式映射引擎 ~330 行<br/>记录/模板/字段链<br/>与协议无关, 哪条路都要写\"]\n    end\n    subgraph alt[\"自拟协议后\"]\n        C[\"删掉 135 行协议代码\"] --> D[\"换来: 每个现成 MCP 服务器<br/>前面架一个适配层<br/>永久成本, 操作者承担\"]\n    end\n    A -.换成.-> D\n    B --> E[\"原样保留\"]\n```\n\n关键矛盾：**这个功能的立项理由本身就是现成的 MCP 服务器**（xiaohongshu 搜索服务就是生态里的 MCP server）。自拟 Clutch-Protocol™ 意味着每个现成服务器前面都要架 shim——用 135 行已付清的一次性成本，换永久性的生态不兼容。\n\n**3. “自拟接口”这条路项目里其实已经有了。** Tavily、SearXNG 就是直连函数（`_tavily`/`_searxng`，各约 20 行）——对已知服务用自有接口，对操作者自建的长尾服务用 MCP。二分法里被漏掉的正是这个分层：**两者本来就不互斥**。\n\n## 三、我的建议：不二选一，做三件小事\n\n1. **把话说准（近零成本）**：README/docstring 从“支持 MCP”改为精确表述——*“MCP 客户端：仅 Tools 原语 / 仅 Streamable HTTP 传输，不支持 stdio 服务器”*。“阉割版”的刺痛感来自信息不对称，说破就不痛了。\n\n2. **用 `tools/list` 砍掉真累赘（有界，~30 行 + 测试）**：`mcp_status` 本来就会探测服务器，顺手调一次 `tools/list`：\n   - 状态行从 `connected` 变成 `connected · 3 tools: search_feeds, …`\n   - 恰好只有一个工具时，UI 预填 `search_tool`，记录缩到 `{name, url}` 两个字段\n   - 操作者负担降到理论最小值，而运行时一行协议代码不加\n\n3. **把非目标写下来（防未来滑坡）**：明确不做 stdio、不做 resources/prompts/sampling、**尤其不做**“任意 MCP 服务器的一切工具自动变成 agent 工具”——那才是真正的大累赘（schema 翻译、逐工具注册、安全面扩大）。目前 135 行的切片之所以轻，恰恰因为拒绝了它。\n\n## 四、决策判据（如果你仍想推倒）\n\n只有一种情况 Horn B（自拟协议）是诚实的：**你确定今后永远不再接任何现成 MCP 服务器**，且嫌那 135 行握手代码碍眼。那时自拟协议就长这样——\n\n```\nPOST <url>          {\"query\": q, \"limit\": n}\n→ 200  [{\"title\": …, \"url\": …, \"snippet\": …}]     # 或用 fields 映射适配\n```\n\n映射引擎 330 行原封保留，删 135 行协议代码，架构确实更干净。但请意识到你同时删掉的是这个功能存在的理由。\n\n---\n\n如果你认可方案三，切到工作模式我就动手：改动是 README 两处措辞 + `mcp_status` 加 `tools/list` 探测 + UI 状态行与预填 + `mcpbackend_test.py` 补几项检查。"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789817502.1484451, "id": "58f51fd54505", "content": "问题在于MCP是否定义了接口的形态？这个形态对于所有的MCP服务器都是通用的吗"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789817557.6730976, "id": "cab74b91f808", "content": "这个问题问到了整个争论的地基。让我先查规范原文确认“定义/不定义”的精确边界，再回答：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_cab6acf5e150482ead301919", "name": "web_fetch", "arguments": "{\"max_chars\":10000,\"url\":\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/server/tools\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user is asking a sharp, foundational question: \"Does MCP define the *shape* of the interface? Is this shape universal across all MCP servers?\"\n\nThis is the crux of the earlier debate. The user is probing: if MCP defines the interface shape (protocol level), why did our project need per-service declarative records (search_tool name, args templates, field mappings)? Is that per-service customization because MCP *doesn't* define the interface shape?\n\nLet me think carefully about what MCP actually defines vs. doesn't define:\n\n**What MCP DOES define (protocol/universal layer):**\n1. The wire format: JSON-RPC 2.0 messages\n2. The lifecycle: initialize → capability negotiation → operation → shutdown\n3. The discovery mechanism: `tools/list` returns tool descriptors with JSON Schema input schemas\n4. The invocation envelope: `tools/call` with `{name, arguments}` and a standardized *response envelope*: `{content: [{type: \"text\"|\"image\"|\"audio\"|\"resource\", ...}], isError, structuredContent?}`\n5. Transports: stdio framing, Streamable HTTP\n6. Session management, notifications, etc.\n\nSo MCP defines the interface shape **at the protocol/envelope level**: how you find tools, how you call them, what the reply *container* looks like. This IS universal — every conformant MCP server speaks this.\n\n**What MCP does NOT define (payload/semantic layer):**\n1. What tools exist (domain-specific names: `search_feeds`, `query`, `get_notes`)\n2. The arguments' names and shapes (each server's inputSchema is its own: `{keyword, limit}` vs `{q, n}` vs `{query, max_results}`)\n3. The **business payload** inside the text content: MCP says `content[0].text` is a string — it does NOT say that string is JSON, nor what shape the JSON takes. One server returns `[{\"id\",\"title\",\"desc\",\"note_id\"}]`, another returns `{\"results\": [...]}`, another returns markdown prose. The `structuredContent` field (added in 2025-06-18 spec) allows JSON output validation against outputSchema, but it's optional and servers rarely declare outputSchema.\n4. Semantics: what \"a result row\" even means — search results vs. notes vs. calendar events vs. rows in a DB.\n\nSo the answer to the user's question is nuanced and actually illuminating for the design debate:\n\n- **Yes**, MCP defines a universal interface shape — but only the **envelope** (transport + lifecycle + discovery + call/reply container). That's exactly why our 135-line client works against *every* MCP server unchanged.\n- **No**, it deliberately does NOT define the **payload** shape — that's each server's domain semantics. This is by design (servers should be extremely easy to build; focused capabilities; no central schema registry for business objects).\n\nThe consequence: any generic client that wants to *interpret* results (not just relay them to the LLM) must bridge the last mile: which tool to call, with which argument names, and how to read rows out of an arbitrary payload. THAT is what our declarative records (search_tool, args templates, fields mapping, list_key) are for. And this last mile is exactly the part MCP intentionally leaves open.\n\nNow — is that a flaw in my earlier argument? Let me reconsider the user's implicit challenge: \"if the shape were universal, records would be just {name, url}. The fact we need per-service mapping templates proves MCP doesn't define the interface shape, which supports the 'own protocol' horn.\"\n\nKey insight to articulate: there are TWO interfaces stacked here:\n1. The **protocol interface** (universal, MCP's job) — our client implements it once, generically. 135 lines, works with all servers.\n2. The **data interface** (necessarily per-service, NOT MCP's job) — the declarative record. This is data, not code — and crucially, it's needed under ANY protocol, including a self-invented one. Even `POST {\"query\",\"limit\"} → [{title,url,snippet}]` convention is itself \"a record + a fixed mapping\" — you've just hard-coded the template into the protocol. Real services (xiaohongshu: `keyword` not `query`; returns `note_id` not `id`; url needs assembling with `xsec_token`) would then need *adapters in code* — that's exactly the per-service customization returning in a worse form.\n\nActually wait — let me steelman: a self-defined protocol COULD mandate `{\"query\",\"limit\"}` args and `[{title,url,snippet}]` replies. Then records shrink to {name, url}. That's true! But then existing MCP servers don't speak it — the adapter shim has to translate. The adapter is precisely the per-service knowledge that our records express as data. So the invariant is: **per-service knowledge is conserved** — it either lives in a data record (our approach), in an adapter shim (own protocol), or in server-side changes to fit your convention (impossible for third-party servers you don't own).\n\nAlso worth noting: MCP *does* have a mechanism pointing toward payload universality — `tools/list` inputSchema (machine-readable arg shapes → could auto-fill args templates, hence my tools/list suggestion) and `structuredContent`/outputSchema (2025-06-18) for typed outputs. But adoption is thin, and outputSchema is validation, not a semantic convention for \"search results\".\n\nAnother point of universality worth mentioning: for the ORIGINAL intended consumer (the LLM), payload shape doesn't need to be universal — the model reads whatever JSON and understands it in context. MCP is designed so that raw tool output flows to the model, and the MODEL is the universal interpreter. Our case is special: web_search needs to extract {title,url,snippet} to merge with other backends' uniform rows and to present in UI — so WE need structure where MCP's normal consumer wouldn't. That's a genuine insight: our mapping engine exists because Clutch treats MCP servers as *rows providers* (mergeable backend chain), not as free-form context for the LLM. If MCP output went straight into the prompt, no mapping would be needed at all.\n\nThat's a really clean resolution of the whole debate arc:\n- MCP defines the universal envelope → one generic client works everywhere (fact).\n- MCP intentionally does not define payload semantics → the last-mile is per-service (fact).\n- The last-mile knowledge is conserved under any design: data record / adapter / server change (analysis).\n- Our records = that last-mile knowledge as *data*, colocated with operator config (design choice, arguably the best of the three).\n- And the reason we need the last mile at all is our own requirement (uniform rows for a mergeable search chain), not MCP's requirement (MCP's normal consumer is the model, which needs no mapping).\n\nLet me verify the structuredContent detail from the spec to be accurate. I recall: 2025-06-18 spec added `structuredContent` to tool results and optional `outputSchema` in tool descriptors, and `title` in Tool objects. Yes — Tool has name, title, description, inputSchema (required), outputSchema (optional), annotations. CallToolResult has content[], structuredContent, isError. Tools MUST return structuredContent conforming to outputSchema when outputSchema is declared. I'm fairly confident. I could fetch the spec page on tools to be precise. Since this is a factual protocol question and I've been citing the spec, one targeted fetch is worth it.\n\nLet me fetch the tools spec page (2025-06-18 revision) to confirm structuredContent/outputSchema details. Actually the docs site redirected earlier to /docs/2026-07-28/ for intro. The spec pages: modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/server/tools exists. There may be a newer dated revision (2026-07-28?). The earlier architecture fetch I did was .../specification/2025-06-18/architecture and it worked. Let me fetch the tools page.\n\nThen compose the answer:\n\nStructure:\n1. Direct answer: MCP 定义了接口形态 — 但只定义\"信封\"层；业务载荷刻意不定义。所以\"对所有 MCP 服务器通用\"的答案是分层的：协议层通用（是），数据层不通用（刻意）。\n2. 两层拆解表：信封层（传输/生命周期/tools-list/call-信封/结构化字段）universal vs 载荷层（工具名/参数名/业务对象语义）per-server。\n3. 证据：同是\"搜索\"，xiaohongshu 是 {keyword, limit} → [{id, title, desc, note_id, xsec_token}]，另一个服务器可能是 {query, n} → {results: [...]}. 引用我们自己的两条记录就是证据（预置 xiaohongshu vs NOTES 测试记录）。\n4. 为什么 MCP 刻意不定义载荷：设计原则\"服务器极容易写/职责单一\"；正常消费者是 LLM 本身——模型就是万能解释器，MCP 只需把原始输出递给模型。CLAUDE/ChatGPT 的 MCP 客户端没有映射引擎！\n5. 反转点：我们为什么需要映射引擎？不是 MCP 缺陷，是 Clutch 自己的需求——把 MCP 服务器当作\"可合并后端链里的行提供者\"，需要统一 {title,url,snippet} 行。这个\"最后一公里\"知识守恒：数据记录(现状) / 适配shim(自拟协议) / 改服务器(第三方不可能)。自拟协议只是把模板硬编码进协议——碰上 keyword≠query 就得写代码适配。\n6. 规范里的前瞻: inputSchema (tools/list 机器可读 → 可自动填参数模板), structuredContent/outputSchema (2025-06-18, 类型化输出但可选、采用率低、且是校验不是语义约定)。\n7. 收束到设计: 这回答了上一轮争论——MCP 的通用性买到了(135行客户端对所有服务器有效), 非通用性是领域本质+我们自己的行格式需求, 无论选哪条协议都逃不掉。→ 加强 tools/list 建议的合理性。\n\nLet me fetch the tools spec page first."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789817557.6730745, "id": "ea28f2a16a69", "name": "web_fetch", "arguments": "{\"max_chars\":10000,\"url\":\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/server/tools\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_cab6acf5e150482ead301919"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789817559.713981, "id": "c914382d7dbe", "tool_call_id": "call_cab6acf5e150482ead301919", "content": "# Tools - Model Context Protocol\n\nDocumentation Index\nFetch the complete documentation index at: /llms.txt\nUse this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\nSkip to main content\nModel Context Protocol home page\nDocumentation\nSpecification\nExtensions\nRegistry\nSEPs\nCommunity\nServer Features\nTools\nThe Model Context Protocol (MCP) allows servers to expose tools that can be invoked by\nlanguage models. Tools enable models to interact with external systems, such as querying\ndatabases, calling APIs, or performing computations. Each tool is uniquely identified by\na name and includes metadata describing its schema.\n​\nUser Interaction Model\nTools in MCP are designed to be model-controlled, meaning that the language model can\ndiscover and invoke tools automatically based on its contextual understanding and the\nuser’s prompts.\nHowever, implementations are free to expose tools through any interface pattern that\nsuits their needs—the protocol itself does not mandate any specific user\ninteraction model.\nFor trust & safety and security, there SHOULD always\nbe a human in the loop with the ability to deny tool invocations.Applications SHOULD:\nProvide UI that makes clear which tools are being exposed to the AI model\nInsert clear visual indicators when tools are invoked\nPresent confirmation prompts to the user for operations, to ensure a human is in the\nloop\n​\nCapabilities\nServers that support tools MUST declare the tools capability:\n{\n\"capabilities\": {\n\"tools\": {\n\"listChanged\": true\n}\n}\n}\nlistChanged indicates whether the server will emit notifications when the list of\navailable tools changes.\n​\nProtocol Messages\n​\nListing Tools\nTo discover available tools, clients send a tools/list request. This operation supports\npagination.\nRequest:\n{\n\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n\"id\": 1,\n\"method\": \"tools/list\",\n\"params\": {\n\"cursor\": \"optional-cursor-value\"\n}\n}\nResponse:\n{\n\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n\"id\": 1,\n\"result\": {\n\"tools\": [\n{\n\"name\": \"get_weather\",\n\"title\": \"Weather Information Provider\",\n\"description\": \"Get current weather information for a location\",\n\"inputSchema\": {\n\"type\": \"object\",\n\"properties\": {\n\"location\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"City name or zip code\"\n}\n},\n\"required\": [\"location\"]\n}\n}\n],\n\"nextCursor\": \"next-page-cursor\"\n}\n}\n​\nCalling Tools\nTo invoke a tool, clients send a tools/call request:\nRequest:\n{\n\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n\"id\": 2,\n\"method\": \"tools/call\",\n\"params\": {\n\"name\": \"get_weather\",\n\"arguments\": {\n\"location\": \"New York\"\n}\n}\n}\nResponse:\n{\n\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n\"id\": 2,\n\"result\": {\n\"content\": [\n{\n\"type\": \"text\",\n\"text\": \"Current weather in New York:\\nTemperature: 72°F\\nConditions: Partly cloudy\"\n}\n],\n\"isError\": false\n}\n}\n​\nList Changed Notification\nWhen the list of available tools changes, servers that declared the listChanged\ncapability SHOULD send a notification:\n{\n\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n\"method\": \"notifications/tools/list_changed\"\n}\n​\nMessage Flow\n​\nData Types\n​\nTool\nA tool definition includes:\nname: Unique identifier for the tool\ntitle: Optional human-readable name of the tool for display purposes.\ndescription: Human-readable description of functionality\ninputSchema: JSON Schema defining expected parameters\noutputSchema: Optional JSON Schema defining expected output structure\nannotations: optional properties describing tool behavior\nFor trust & safety and security, clients MUST consider\ntool annotations to be untrusted unless they come from trusted servers.\n​\nTool Result\nTool results may contain structured or unstructured content.\nUnstructured content is returned in the content field of a result, and can contain multiple content items of different types:\nAll content types (text, image, audio, resource links, and embedded resources)\nsupport optional\nannotations that\nprovide metadata about audience, priority, and modification times. This is the\nsame annotation format used by resources and prompts.\n​\nText Content\n{\n\"type\": \"text\",\n\"text\": \"Tool result text\"\n}\n​\nImage Content\n{\n\"type\": \"image\",\n\"data\": \"base64-encoded-data\",\n\"mimeType\": \"image/png\"\n\"annotations\": {\n\"audience\": [\"user\"],\n\"priority\": 0.9\n}\n}\nThis example demonstrates the use of an optional Annotation.\n​\nAudio Content\n{\n\"type\": \"audio\",\n\"data\": \"base64-encoded-audio-data\",\n\"mimeType\": \"audio/wav\"\n}\n​\nResource Links\nA tool MAY return links to Resources, to provide additional context\nor data. In this case, the tool will return a URI that can be subscribed to or fetched by the client:\n{\n\"type\": \"resource_link\",\n\"uri\": \"file:///project/src/main.rs\",\n\"name\": \"main.rs\",\n\"description\": \"Primary application entry point\",\n\"mimeType\": \"text/x-rust\",\n\"annotations\": {\n\"audience\": [\"assistant\"],\n\"priority\": 0.9\n}\n}\nResource links support the same Resource annotations as regular resources to help clients understand how to use them.\nResource links returned by tools are not guaranteed to appear in the results\nof a resources/list request.\n​\nEmbedded Resources\nResources MAY be embedded to provide additional context\nor data using a suitable URI scheme. Servers that use embedded resources SHOULD implement the resources capability:\n{\n\"type\": \"resource\",\n\"resource\": {\n\"uri\": \"file:///project/src/main.rs\",\n\"mimeType\": \"text/x-rust\",\n\"text\": \"fn main() {\\n println!(\\\"Hello world!\\\");\\n}\",\n\"annotations\": {\n\"audience\": [\"user\", \"assistant\"],\n\"priority\": 0.7,\n\"lastModified\": \"2025-05-03T14:30:00Z\"\n}\n}\n}\nEmbedded resources support the same Resource annotations as regular resources to help clients understand how to use them.\n​\nStructured Content\nStructured content is returned as a JSON object in the structuredContent field of a result.\nFor backwards compatibility, a tool that returns structured content SHOULD also return the serialized JSON in a TextContent block.\nstructuredContent is server-produced result data and is unrelated to LLM\n“structured outputs” (schema-constrained model generation).\n​\nOutput Schema\nTools may also provide an output schema for validation of structured results.\nIf an output schema is provided:\nServers MUST provide structured results that conform to this schema.\nClients SHOULD validate structured results against this schema.\nExample tool with output schema:\n{\n\"name\": \"get_weather_data\",\n\"title\": \"Weather Data Retriever\",\n\"description\": \"Get current weather data for a location\",\n\"inputSchema\": {\n\"type\": \"object\",\n\"properties\": {\n\"location\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"City name or zip code\"\n}\n},\n\"required\": [\"location\"]\n},\n\"outputSchema\": {\n\"type\": \"object\",\n\"properties\": {\n\"temperature\": {\n\"type\": \"number\",\n\"description\": \"Temperature in celsius\"\n},\n\"conditions\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"Weather conditions description\"\n},\n\"humidity\": {\n\"type\": \"number\",\n\"description\": \"Humidity percentage\"\n}\n},\n\"required\": [\"temperature\", \"conditions\", \"humidity\"]\n}\n}\nExample valid response for this tool:\n{\n\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n\"id\": 5,\n\"result\": {\n\"content\": [\n{\n\"type\": \"text\",\n\"text\": \"{\\\"temperature\\\": 22.5, \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Partly cloudy\\\", \\\"humidity\\\": 65}\"\n}\n],\n\"structuredContent\": {\n\"temperature\": 22.5,\n\"conditions\": \"Partly cloudy\",\n\"humidity\": 65\n}\n}\n}\nProviding an output schema helps clients and LLMs understand and properly handle structured tool outputs by:\nEnabling strict schema validation of responses\nProviding type information for better integration with programming languages\nGuiding clients and LLMs to properly parse and utilize the returned data\nSupporting better documentation and developer experience\n​\nError Handling\nTools use two error reporting mechanisms:\nProtocol Errors: Standard JSON-RPC errors for issues like:\nUnknown tools\nInvalid arguments\nServer errors\nTool Execution Errors: Reported in tool results with isError: true:\nAPI failures\nInvalid input data\nBusiness logic errors\nExample protocol error:\n{\n\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n\"id\": 3,\n\"error\": {\n\"code\": -32602,\n\"message\": \"Unknown tool: invalid_tool_name\"\n}\n}\nExample tool execution error:\n{\n\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n\"id\": 4,\n\"result\": {\n\"content\": [\n{\n\"type\": \"text\",\n\"text\": \"Failed to fetch weather data: API rate limit exceeded\"\n}\n],\n\"isError\": true\n}\n}\n​\nSecurity Considerations\nServers MUST:\nValidate all tool inputs\nImplement proper access controls\nRate limit tool invocations\nSanitize tool outputs\nClients SHOULD:\nPrompt for user confirmation on sensitive operations\nShow tool inputs to the user before calling the server, to avoid malicious or\naccidental data exfiltration\nValidate tool results before passing to LLM\nImplement timeouts for tool calls\nLog tool usage for audit purposes\nWas this page helpful?\nAssistant\nResponses are generated using AI and may contain mistakes.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789817617.4883358, "id": "d9529f4b5825", "content": "规范原文确认了。这个问题的答案是分层的，而且恰好解释了我们前面所有争论的根源：\n\n## 直接回答\n\n**MCP 定义了接口形态——但只定义“信封”层，这一层对所有服务器 100% 通用；它刻意不定义“载荷”层，这一层每家自有——而“不通用”本身是刻意的、写进设计原则的。**\n\n## 两层拆解（对照规范原文）\n\n| 层 | 内容 | 规范地位 | 通用性 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **信封层** | JSON-RPC 2.0 线格式、`initialize` 能力协商、`tools/list` 发现、`tools/call {name, arguments}` 调用、回执容器 `{content[], structuredContent?, isError}`、双错误通道（协议错误 vs `isError` 业务错误）、stdio/HTTP 传输、会话 | **MCP 定义，强制** | ✅ 100% 通用 |\n| **载荷层** | 工具叫什么（`search_feeds` vs `get_weather`）、参数叫什么（`keyword` vs `location`）、`content[0].text` 这个字符串里装什么 | **MCP 刻意不定义** | ❌ 每服务器自有 |\n\n规范原文的证据非常清楚：\n\n- Tool 描述符里的 `inputSchema` 是**每个工具自带的 JSON Schema**——“描述”自己的形状，而不是协议“规定”形状。schema 是关于这一个工具的数据，不是通用约定\n- 回执的 text 内容，规范自己的示例就是一段散文（`\"Current weather in New York:\\nTemperature: 72°F...\"`）——**任意文本是一等公民**。信封从不说 `text` 里是 JSON，更不说是什么形状的 JSON\n- `structuredContent`/`outputSchema`（2025-06-18 新增）看似通向统一，但它是**可选的**、每工具自declared的，而且职能是**校验**（\"Clients SHOULD validate\"）——协议里不存在“搜索结果行”的通用 schema\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph env[\"信封层: MCP 定义, 人人相同\"]\n        A[\"JSON-RPC / 会话 / initialize<br/>tools/list / tools/call / 回执容器\"]\n    end\n    subgraph pay[\"载荷层: MCP 刻意留空, 各家自有\"]\n        B[\"工具名 / 参数名 / text 里装什么\"]\n    end\n    A --> C{\"谁是载荷的读者?\"}\n    C -->|\"MCP 的默认答案: LLM 本身\"| D[\"模型是万能解释器<br/>Claude Desktop 等客户端<br/>根本没有映射引擎\"]\n    C -->|\"Clutch 自选的读者身份\"| E[\"要把行合并进统一搜索链<br/>title / url / snippet<br/>于是需要每服务一张映射记录\"]\n```\n\n## 为什么 MCP 刻意留空载荷层\n\n设计原则写得明白：*\"Servers should be extremely easy to build\"*。因为 MCP 的默认消费者是**模型**——模型就是那个万能解释器。Claude Desktop 的 MCP 客户端没有任何字段映射引擎：它把 `content` 原文塞进上下文，模型自己读懂任意形状。所以 MCP 的通用性契约是：**信封上任何客户端能对话任何服务器，语义上由读者负责消化**。\n\n## 关键反转：Clutch 为什么需要映射记录\n\n**不是 MCP 的缺陷，是 Clutch 自选的读者身份造成的。** 我们没有把载荷原文丢给模型，而是把 MCP 服务器当作“可合并后端链里的行提供者”——要和 bing/ddg/tavily 的结果合并、要在 UI 里渲染成链接。合并就要求统一行格式 `{title, url, snippet}`，于是必须有人把任意载荷翻译成行。这个翻译者就是 `search_tool` + `args` 模板 + `fields` 映射那张记录。\n\n## 由此看清上一轮争论的本质\n\n那份“每服务知识”（工具名、参数名、行形状）在**任何架构下都守恒**，区别只在它住在哪里：\n\n| 方案 | 知识住哪 | 代价 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 现状（MCP + 声明式记录） | **数据**：操作者的 settings 记录 | 加服务 = 改配置 |\n| 自拟协议（规定 `{\"query\",\"limit\"}` → `[{title,url,snippet}]`） | 被硬编码进协议——**但只对说你的协议的服务器消失**；对每个现成 MCP 服务器（`keyword≠query`、`note_id≠id`、`xsec_token` 要拼 URL），它原样变成每个服务器旁边的一个**代码适配层** | 翻译知识没有消失，只是从数据变成了代码 |\n\n所以“MCP 没把接口形态定义到载荷层”这件事，**不构成换协议的理由**——换了协议非通用性照样在，只是换了个更贵的存放位置。真正有原则的改进是利用信封层**本来就通用**的那份数据：`tools/list` 的 `inputSchema` 是机器可读的参数形状，通用客户端可以据此自动推导调用模板（`{query}` 填进那个 string 类型的必填参数）——这正是我上一轮建议 tools/list 的深层理由：**用协议定义的通用数据，去自动填掉记录里手写的那部分**，而不是发明新协议。\n\n一句话收束：**MCP 把“能对话”做成了通用，把“能读懂”外包给了读者。Clutch 因为亲自当了读者，才背上了映射记录——这是我们的需求，不是协议的债。**", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "Now I have the exact spec text. Let me compose the answer to the user's question: \"Does MCP define the shape of the interface? Is this shape universal across all MCP servers?\"\n\nThe precise answer:\n\n**MCP defines the interface shape — but only the envelope layer, and it's universal there. It deliberately does NOT define the payload/semantic layer, and that's universal in its non-universality (every server's payload is its own).**\n\nTwo layers:\n\n**Layer 1: Protocol envelope (defined by MCP, universal)**\n- Wire format: JSON-RPC 2.0\n- Lifecycle: initialize → capability negotiation → tools/list → tools/call\n- Tool descriptor shape: {name, title?, description, inputSchema, outputSchema?, annotations?}\n- Invocation envelope: tools/call {name, arguments}\n- Reply envelope: {content: [{type: \"text\"|\"image\"|\"audio\"|\"resource_link\"|\"resource\"}], structuredContent?, isError}\n- Error channels: protocol errors (JSON-RPC error) vs tool execution errors (isError: true)\n- Transports: stdio / Streamable HTTP, session management\n\nThis layer IS universal — and this is exactly why our 135-line generic client works unchanged against any conformant server.\n\n**Layer 2: Payload semantics (NOT defined, per-server by design)**\n- What tools exist and what they're named: `search_feeds` vs `get_weather` vs `query`\n- What the arguments are called: `{keyword, limit}` vs `{location}` vs `{q, n}`\n- What the text inside `content[0].text` means: the spec says text is a *string*; the xiaohongshu server stuffs a JSON array of note rows into it; another server would put prose. Nothing in the envelope says the text is JSON, let alone which JSON.\n- Even structuredContent/outputSchema: optional, server-declared, and it's *validation* (conformance checking), not a semantic convention — there is no standard schema for \"search result row\".\n\nEvidence from the spec text I just fetched:\n- inputSchema: per-tool JSON Schema — \"each tool includes metadata describing its schema\" — i.e., the shape is *described*, not *prescribed*. The schema is data about this one tool, not a protocol-mandated shape.\n- \"Tool results may contain structured or unstructured content\" — both allowed.\n- TextContent example: `\"Current weather in New York:\\nTemperature: 72°F...\"` — plain prose is a first-class valid reply.\n- outputSchema is optional and per-tool.\n\n**Why MCP deliberately leaves layer 2 open** (design principle from the architecture page: \"Servers should be extremely easy to build\", \"Servers focus on specific, well-defined capabilities\"): the normal consumer of the payload is the LLM itself. The model is the universal interpreter — Claude Desktop's MCP client has NO field-mapping engine. It just relays `content` text into the model's context and the model reads whatever shape. So MCP's universality contract is: *any client can talk to any server* (envelope), and *the model can understand any payload* (semantics deferred to the reader).\n\n**The reversal for Clutch's case:** we need layer-2 structure only because of OUR OWN requirement — not MCP's. Clutch doesn't relay payload to the model raw; it merges MCP rows into a uniform backend chain ({title,url,snippet}) alongside bing/ddg/tavily, presents them in UI, links them. That merge demands a common row shape, so someone must translate arbitrary payloads → uniform rows. That someone is the declarative record (search_tool, args template, fields mapping, list_key).\n\n**Knowledge conservation argument:** the per-service knowledge (tool name, arg names, row shape) is conserved under every architecture:\n- Our approach: it lives as *data* in the operator's record. Adding a service = editing config.\n- Own-protocol approach: you can hardcode `{\"query\",\"limit\"}` → `[{title,url,snippet}]` into your convention — records shrink to {name,url} — but only for servers that speak YOUR convention. For every existing MCP server (keyword≠query, note_id≠id, xsec_token in URL), the translation reappears as an adapter shim in *code*, deployed next to each server.\n- So: per-service knowledge never disappears; the only choice is where it lives — data record (ours), adapter code (own protocol), or server-side rewrite (impossible for third parties).\n\n**What MCP does offer toward layer 2 (and why it doesn't close the gap):**\n- `tools/list` inputSchema: machine-readable arg shapes → lets a generic client auto-build args ({query} → the string-typed required param). This is why my tools/list suggestion reduces records to {name,url} for well-behaved servers — it automates the CALL side using protocol-defined data.\n- structuredContent/outputSchema: could in principle carry typed rows, but adoption is thin, it's optional, it validates but doesn't standardize semantics (\"a search result\" has no universal schema).\n\nSo the direct answers:\n1. 是否定义了接口形态？ 定义了——信封层（传输、生命周期、发现、调用、回执容器）。\n2. 对所有服务器通用吗？ 信封层：是，100% 通用（这正是 135 行通用客户端成立的原因）。载荷层：刻意不通用——通用性被\"外包\"给了 LLM 这个读者。Clutch 因为要把行合并进统一链，亲自当了读者，才需要每服务一张映射记录。\n\nEnd with the design implication (brief, linking to previous turn): this is why \"own protocol\" doesn't escape the non-universality — it only relocates it; and why tools/list is the principled improvement: it uses layer-1's universal discovery data to auto-derive what we currently hand-write in records.\n\nFormat: layered table, evidence quotes, one mermaid diagram showing the two layers and where universality holds. Keep it tight. Chinese prose, English identifiers.\n\nMermaid caution: no double quotes inside labels. I'll use a simple diagram:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph env[\"信封层: MCP 定义, 100% 通用\"]\n        A1[\"JSON-RPC 2.0 / 传输 / 会话\"] \n        A2[\"initialize 能力协商 → tools/list 发现 → tools/call 调用\"]\n        A3[\"回执容器: content[] + structuredContent + isError\"]\n    end\n    subgraph pay[\"载荷层: MCP 刻意不定义, 每服务器自有\"]\n        B1[\"工具叫什么: search_feeds vs query\"]\n        B2[\"参数叫什么: keyword vs query\"]\n        B3[\"content[0].text 里装什么: 任意\"]\n    end\n    env -->|\"信封人人相同\"| pay\n    pay -->|\"通用读者 = LLM 本身\"| M[\"Claude Desktop 等客户端: 无映射引擎\"]\n    pay -->|\"Clutch 自选的读者身份\"| C[\"要合并进统一行格式 → 映射记录\"]\n```\n\nHmm \"content[0].text\" contains brackets and quotes? No quotes. Brackets fine in quoted label. OK.\n\nLength: medium. Let me write it."}
{"type": "final", "timestamp": 1789817617.4927924, "id": "77b3feaa4cd5", "status": "completed", "summary": "规范原文确认了。这个问题的答案是分层的，而且恰好解释了我们前面所有争论的根源：\n\n## 直接回答\n\n**MCP 定义了接口形态——但只定义“信封”层，这一层对所有服务器 100% 通用；它刻意不定义“载荷”层，这一层每家自有——而“不通用”本身是刻意的、写进设计原则的。**\n\n## 两层拆解（对照规范原文）\n\n| 层 | 内容 | 规范地位 | 通用性 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **信封层** | JSON-RPC 2.0 线格式、`initialize` 能力协商、`tools/list` 发现、`tools/call {name, arguments}` 调用、回执容器 `{content[], structuredContent?, isError}`、双错误通道（协议错误 vs `isError` 业务错误）、stdio/HTTP 传输、会话 | **MCP 定义，强制** | ✅ 100% 通用 |\n| **载荷层** | 工具叫什么（`search_feeds` vs `get_weather`）、参数叫什么（`keyword` vs `location`）、`content[0].text` 这个字符串里装什么 | **MCP 刻意不定义** | ❌ 每服务器自有 |\n\n规范原文的证据非常清楚：\n\n- Tool 描述符里的 `inputSchema` 是**每个工具自带的 JSON Schema**——“描述”自己的形状，而不是协议“规定”形状。schema 是关于这一个工具的数据，不是通用约定\n- 回执的 text 内容，规范自己的示例就是一段散文（`\"Current weather in New York:\\nTemperature: 72°F...\"`）——**任意文本是一等公民**。信封从不说 `text` 里是 JSON，更不说是什么形状的 JSON\n- `structuredContent`/`outputSchema`（2025-06-18 新增）看似通向统一，但它是**可选的**、每工具自declared的，而且职能是**校验**（\"Clients SHOULD validate\"）——协议里不存在“搜索结果行”的通用 schema\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph env[\"信封层: MCP 定义, 人人相同\"]\n        A[\"JSON-RPC / 会话 / initialize<br/>tools/list / tools/call / 回执容器\"]\n    end\n    subgraph pay[\"载荷层: MCP 刻意留空, 各家自有\"]\n        B[\"工具名 / 参数名 / text 里装什么\"]\n    end\n    A --> C{\"谁是载荷的读者?\"}\n    C -->|\"MCP 的默认答案: LLM 本身\"| D[\"模型是万能解释器<br/>Claude Desktop 等客户端<br/>根本没有映射引擎\"]\n    C -->|\"Clutch 自选的读者身份\"| E[\"要把行合并进统一搜索链<br/>title / url / snippet<br/>于是需要每服务一张映射记录\"]\n```\n\n## 为什么 MCP 刻意留空载荷层\n\n设计原则写得明白：*\"Servers should be extremely easy to build\"*。因为 MCP 的默认消费者是**模型**——模型就是那个万能解释器。Claude Desktop 的 MCP 客户端没有任何字段映射引擎：它把 `content` 原文塞进上下文，模型自己读懂任意形状。所以 MCP 的通用性契约是：**信封上任何客户端能对话任何服务器，语义上由读者负责消化**。\n\n## 关键反转：Clutch 为什么需要映射记录\n\n**不是 MCP 的缺陷，是 Clutch 自选的读者身份造成的。** 我们没有把载荷原文丢给模型，而是把 MCP 服务器当作“可合并后端链里的行提供者”——要和 bing/ddg/tavily 的结果合并、要在 UI 里渲染成链接。合并就要求统一行格式 `{title, url, snippet}`，于是必须有人把任意载荷翻译成行。这个翻译者就是 `search_tool` + `args` 模板 + `fields` 映射那张记录。\n\n## 由此看清上一轮争论的本质\n\n那份“每服务知识”（工具名、参数名、行形状）在**任何架构下都守恒**，区别只在它住在哪里：\n\n| 方案 | 知识住哪 | 代价 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 现状（MCP + 声明式记录） | **数据**：操作者的 settings 记录 | 加服务 = 改配置 |\n| 自拟协议（规定 `{\"query\",\"limit\"}` → `[{title,url,snippet}]`） | 被硬编码进协议——**但只对说你的协议的服务器消失**；对每个现成 MCP 服务器（`keyword≠query`、`note_id≠id`、`xsec_token` 要拼 URL），它原样变成每个服务器旁边的一个**代码适配层** | 翻译知识没有消失，只是从数据变成了代码 |\n\n所以“MCP 没把接口形态定义到载荷层”这件事，**不构成换协议的理由**——换了协议非通用性照样在，只是换了个更贵的存放位置。真正有原则的改进是利用信封层**本来就通用**的那份数据：`tools/list` 的 `inputSchema` 是机器可读的参数形状，通用客户端可以据此自动推导调用模板（`{query}` 填进那个 string 类型的必填参数）——这正是我上一轮建议 tools/list 的深层理由：**用协议定义的通用数据，去自动填掉记录里手写的那部分**，而不是发明新协议。\n\n一句话收束：**MCP 把“能对话”做成了通用，把“能读懂”外包给了读者。Clutch 因为亲自当了读者，才背上了映射记录——这是我们的需求，不是协议的债。**"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789817704.0789666, "id": "bd879e729ccd", "content": "那么就目前的实现而言，clutch现在可以接入任意mcp服务器吗"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789817788.1020024, "id": "f15a8b0ca70e", "content": "这个问题现在可以给出精确回答了——结合这轮讨论的分层框架和已核实的代码，答案是：\n\n## 判决：不能“任意”。能接的是一个边界清晰的子集\n\n> **Clutch 目前可以接：HTTP 单端点、免鉴权、单搜索工具、JSON 载荷的 MCP 服务器。**\n> 一句话：说得通 Streamable HTTP、不需要身份验证、你叫得动它一个工具、它吐得回 JSON 行——四关全过的才能接。\n\n一台 MCP 服务器要过四道闸门：\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    S[\"一台 MCP 服务器\"] --> G1{\"闸门 1: 传输\"}\n    G1 -->|\"Streamable HTTP 单端点 POST\"| G2\n    G1 -->|\"stdio (npx/uvx 大多数官方服务器)<br/>或老式双端点 SSE\"| X1[\"接不了\"]\n    G2{\"闸门 2: 鉴权\"} --> G2b\n    G2b -->|\"免鉴权 / 裸 loopback\"| G3\n    G2b -->|\"OAuth 或 Bearer token<br/>(record 没有 headers 字段)\"| X2[\"接不了\"]\n    G3{\"闸门 3: 调用形态\"} --> G3b\n    G3b -->|\"单工具, 动态参数只有 query/limit<br/>(常量可硬编码在 args 里)\"| G4\n    G3b -->|\"要更多动态参数 / 嵌套对象<br/>/ 多步调用 / resources / sampling\"| X3[\"接不了\"]\n    G4{\"闸门 4: 载荷形状\"} --> G4b\n    G4b -->|\"text 里是 JSON 数组或常见信封<br/>(data/items/feeds/results/notes)\"| OK[\"✅ 接入, 通用映射引擎读行\"]\n    G4b -->|\"散文 / 图片 / 嵌套结构<br/>(映射结果为空)\"| X4[\"接上但搜不到东西\"]\n```\n\n## 四道闸门对应的事实（已核实）\n\n| 闸门 | 代码事实 | 卡掉了谁 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **传输** | `_mcp_rpc` 是 urllib POST，声明 `2025-03-26`；能容忍 SSE 帧的**应答**，但不会做老式 `GET /sse` + `POST /messages` 双端点舞步，也没有任何 stdio 子进程管理 | **生态里最大的一块**：官方示例和 npx/uvx 一键启动的服务器多数是 stdio（filesystem、github、sqlite…） |\n| **鉴权** | `McpService` 没有 `headers` 字段，请求只带 `Content-Type`/`Accept`/`Mcp-Session-Id`；record 无处填 token；2025-06-18 的 OAuth 流程完全没实现 | 任何挂着 bearer token 的远程服务器（恰恰是“远程”服务器的常态） |\n| **调用** | `search_args` 的动态值只有 `{\"query\", \"limit\"}`；没有 `tools/list`（工具名和参数名全靠手填）；每次搜索重新握手，一次搜索 3 个往返，无会话复用/重连 | 参数表复杂的工具、需要多轮状态的工具 |\n| **载荷** | 映射引擎吃任意 JSON（字段链、URL 模板、`list_key`、常见信封自动解包）——这部分**确实通用**；但散文式返回会映射为空 → `no results` | 非结构化返回 |\n\n## 回到分层框架，这句话就精确了\n\n- **信封层**：“任意”成立——只要服务器肯用 Streamable HTTP 说协议，那 135 行通用客户端原封不动对谁都有效（你的 xiaohongshu 和测试里的假服务器走的就是同一段代码）\n- **传输/鉴权层**：“任意”不成立——这是当前实现的真实边界，也是“阉割版”指责里最硬的部分\n- **载荷层**：MCP 本来就不保证通用（上一轮的结论），Clutch 用映射记录接住了 JSON 形状的多样性，接不住非 JSON\n\n## 如果想扩大边界，按性价比排序\n\n1. **record 加 `headers` 字段**（~5 行 + 测试）——解锁所有 bearer token 服务器，性价比最高\n2. **`tools/list` 发现**（~30 行）——状态接口顺带列出工具名，单工具服务器免手填 `search_tool`；用信封层自带的通用数据消灭手写配置\n3. **`inputSchema` 自动推导 args**——单 string 参数时免手填模板，记录缩到 `{name, url}`\n4. **stdio 桥**——真正的大件（子进程管理、跨平台、生命周期），除非你自己的服务就是 stdio，否则不值得\n5. **OAuth**——明确不做；真有需求时操作者用网关/反代解决，客户端保持零 OAuth 面\n\n## 收束\n\n所以对这个问题的完整回答是：**“接入任意 MCP 服务器”从来不是这个功能的目标——目标是“接任意搜索后端”。** 在“搜索后端”这个小集合里（你自己的 xiaohongshu 服务这类本地、免鉴权、单工具、吐 JSON 的 HTTP 服务器），当前实现是完整可用的；对 MCP 服务器全集，它是一个诚实的窄子集——而边界在哪里，现在有了准确的描述和一份按性价比排好的扩边清单。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "The user asks the original question again (this conversation started with a compacted summary of that same question — \"那么就目前的实现而言，clutch现在可以接入任意mcp服务器吗\"). Now, after the full discussion about MCP's envelope vs payload layers, the question comes back with new depth. The user wants a precise, honest answer given the current implementation.\n\nLet me think about what the precise answer is, grounded in the code I've read:\n\n**Current implementation facts:**\n\n1. **Transport**: HTTP POST only (Streamable HTTP + SSE-framed responses tolerated). `_mcp_rpc` does JSON-RPC over POST with `Mcp-Session-Id`, Accept: application/json, text/event-stream. NO stdio support. So any stdio-based server (npx/uvx launched — which is a large share of published MCP servers: filesystem, everything, github via npx, etc.) cannot be connected directly. The operator would have to put an HTTP bridge (e.g. supergateway / mcp-proxy) in front.\n\n2. **Protocol slice**: initialize → notifications/initialized → tools/call. `_MCP_PROTO = \"2025-03-26\"`. Session id captured from `Mcp-Session-Id` header. Handles: JSON replies, SSE frames, HTTP 500, jsonrpc errors, empty 202, timeouts, unreachable. Does NOT handle: session expiry/re-negotiation (404 with session invalid), `notifications/tools/list_changed`, OAuth/Authorization header flows (2025-06-18 spec has auth), `tools/list` (not called at all), pagination.\n\n3. **Auth**: none. No Authorization header support in records. Servers requiring OAuth or even static bearer tokens can't be authenticated... wait, let me check — the record doesn't have a headers field. `_mcp_rpc` builds headers: Content-Type, Accept, Mcp-Session-Id. No auth. So HTTP servers behind a token (very common: `Authorization: Bearer ...`) are NOT connectable. Only open loopback servers like the local xiaohongshu one.\n\n4. **Tool discovery**: none (`tools/list` not implemented). Operator must hand-declare search_tool name and args template.\n\n5. **Payload interpretation**: generic mapping engine (fields chains, url templates, list_key, auto-unwrap). Works on arbitrary JSON payloads. If payload is unstructured prose, mapping yields nothing → BackendError \"no results\".\n\nSo the answer to \"可以接入任意 MCP 服务器吗\":\n\n**No — precisely scoped:**\n- ✅ Any MCP server that: speaks Streamable HTTP (POST), needs no auth (or is on a trusted loopback), exposes ONE tool whose arguments you can express as templates of {query}/{limit}, returns its rows as JSON inside text content (or a common envelope).\n- ❌ stdio servers (the majority of published ones) — no.\n- ❌ servers requiring auth (OAuth or bearer) — no headers field.\n- ❌ servers whose tool args don't fit {query}/{limit} templates (e.g., needs a date range, or a boolean flag, or nested objects — args templates only interpolate query/limit; values dict = {\"query\",\"limit\"} only). Actually `search_args` values only has query and limit. So a tool requiring e.g. `{\"category\": \"news\", \"query\": ...}` can't be expressed... well, you could hardcode \"category\": \"news\" as a literal string in args — non-template values pass through (`_interpolate_value` returns non-string as-is; a string without placeholders interpolates to itself). So literal constants ARE expressible. But multiple dynamic params beyond query/limit are not.\n- ❌ stateful flows: tools that need multi-step calls, resource reads, sampling, elicitation.\n- ❌ session-expiry re-handshake: if the server invalidates the session mid-use, current code doesn't re-initialize. (One search = one fresh handshake actually — `_mcp_call` does initialize→initialized→tools/call per invocation. So session issues are mostly moot: each search establishes a new session. That's wasteful (3 round trips per search) but robust. Worth noting as a cost: 3 RTTs per search.)\n\nWait — actually that's an important implementation detail: `_mcp_call` does the full handshake per search call. No connection reuse. That means: (a) robust to stateless servers (many Streamable HTTP servers are stateless and don't even need session), (b) costs 3 round trips per search.\n\nHmm, also \"initialize\" declares protocolVersion \"2025-03-26\" — newer servers on 2025-06-18 will accept? Per spec, if server doesn't support the requested version it SHOULD respond with a supported version... but our client ignores the negotiated version in the reply (just takes result). Most servers accept. Fine.\n\nSo the honest answer structure:\n\n**一句话**: 不能\"任意\"，能接的是一个小而明确的子集。给判定表。\n\n**判定表**（什么样的服务器能接）:\n| 条件 | 现状 |\n- 传输: HTTP POST (Streamable HTTP) ✅ / stdio ❌ — 而生态里大量官方服务器是 stdio\n- 鉴权: 无 auth 头字段 → 只能接无需鉴权的服务器（典型就是本地 loopback）\n- 工具调用: 需手声明 search_tool + args 模板；动态参数只有 {query}/{limit}，常量可硬编码；需要更多动态参数/嵌套对象/多步调用的工具 ❌\n- 回执: text 里是 JSON（或常见信封 data/items/feeds/results/notes）→ 通用映射引擎能读；散文/非 JSON → 映射为空 → \"no results\"\n- 生命周期: 每次搜索重新握手（3 RTT），无 tools/list、无会话重连、无 OAuth\n\n**量化**: 拿官方 registry/生态说：stdio + OAuth 的服务器占比相当大。我可以说\"生态中相当大比例（尤其官方 examples 和 npx 一键启动的）是 stdio\"。不过别乱编数字。\n\n**缩小后的准确表述**: \"可以接任意 **HTTP 传输、免鉴权、单工具、JSON 载荷** 的 MCP 服务器\" — 即\"Clutch 定义的那类搜索型 MCP 服务器\"。\n\n**与前面讨论的呼应**: \"任意\"在信封层成立（对说得通 HTTP 的服务器，135 行客户端通用），在传输/鉴权/载荷层不成立。这正是上一轮\"阉割版\"讨论的精确化：现在给出可操作的边界。\n\n**如果要迈向\"任意\"，差距清单**（按性价比排序）:\n1. tools/list 发现（信封层数据，已有原则性论证）→ 免手填 search_tool\n2. record 加 headers 字段（~5 行）→ 解锁 bearer token 服务器\n3. inputSchema 自动推导 args → 免手填模板\n4. stdio 桥（真正的大件：子进程管理、跨平台、生命周期）→ 除非真实需求，否则不做\n5. OAuth → 明确不做（操作者可用反向代理/网关解决）\n\nAlso the honest conclusion: \"接入任意 MCP 服务器\"从来不是这个功能的目标——目标是\"接任意**搜索后端**\"。对搜索后端这个小集合，当前实现覆盖率还行；对 MCP 全集，它是窄子集。\n\nShould I do any code verification? I've read all relevant code in this conversation already (mcpprovider.py fully, websearch.py 415-596, server.py sections, app.js section, config.py grep, tests fully). I know:\n- No headers/auth field in McpService (fields: name,url,search_tool,enabled,label,args,fields,list_key,status_tool,login_field) — confirmed from the dataclass.\n- No tools/list anywhere — confirmed (grep of test + websearch read).\n- stdio: nothing in code spawns processes for MCP; transport is urllib POST — confirmed.\n- args values: `search_args` builds `values = {\"query\": query, \"limit\": limit}` — confirmed, so only those two dynamic params.\n\nI have everything. No need for more tool calls. This is the third time the user asks this exact question (first at conversation start pre-fix, now post-discussion) — they want the definitive, honest answer integrating everything. I should answer decisively with the precise boundary, a decision table, and the gap list. Keep it tight and well-structured. No new tool calls needed — answer directly.\n\nFormat: \n- 开门见山一句话: 不能。能接的是一个精确定义的子集。\n- 一张判定表: 维度 / 现状 / 后果\n- mermaid? Maybe a small diagram of the four gates (传输/鉴权/调用/载荷) a server must pass. A checklist flow could be nice but tables may suffice. Let me do one compact mermaid gate diagram — it visualizes \"任意\" nicely. Careful with quotes in labels.\n- 呼应: 信封层 vs 传输/鉴权/载荷层\n- 若要迈向\"任意\": 差距清单按性价比\n- 收束: 功能目标是搜索后端不是 MCP 全集\n\nActually let me double-check one thing — the OAuth/auth claim. The 2025-06-18 spec added OAuth 2.1 authorization for HTTP transports. Our client sends no Authorization header and the record has no headers field — confirmed from McpService dataclass and _mcp_rpc headers. Good.\n\nAnd one more nuance: 2025-03-26 was actually the revision that INTRODUCED Streamable HTTP (replacing the old HTTP+SSE dual-endpoint transport). Old servers on 2024-11-05 use the dual-endpoint SSE transport (GET /sse + POST /messages?sessionId=...). Our client only POSTs JSON-RPC to one URL — it does NOT do the old GET-SSE dance. So pre-2025-03-26 HTTP servers are also not supported. Worth one line: 只支持 Streamable HTTP（2025-03-26 起的单端点 POST），老式双端点 SSE 传输不支持. Our `_mcp_rpc` tolerates SSE-framed *responses* on the POST endpoint, but doesn't do GET /sse stream + POST /messages. Correct.\n\nAlso: session handling — some Streamable HTTP servers are stateless (no Mcp-Session-Id) — handled (sid falls back to session/None). Fine.\n\nLet me also mention the 3-RTT-per-search cost as a design note (fresh handshake per search — robust but chatty).\n\nNow compose. Length: moderate — this deserves a thorough but tight answer. The user asked a yes/no question with depth; give the verdict, the precise boundary, gates, gap list, and the reframed goal."}
{"type": "final", "timestamp": 1789817788.1054366, "id": "78054eb07641", "status": "completed", "summary": "这个问题现在可以给出精确回答了——结合这轮讨论的分层框架和已核实的代码，答案是：\n\n## 判决：不能“任意”。能接的是一个边界清晰的子集\n\n> **Clutch 目前可以接：HTTP 单端点、免鉴权、单搜索工具、JSON 载荷的 MCP 服务器。**\n> 一句话：说得通 Streamable HTTP、不需要身份验证、你叫得动它一个工具、它吐得回 JSON 行——四关全过的才能接。\n\n一台 MCP 服务器要过四道闸门：\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    S[\"一台 MCP 服务器\"] --> G1{\"闸门 1: 传输\"}\n    G1 -->|\"Streamable HTTP 单端点 POST\"| G2\n    G1 -->|\"stdio (npx/uvx 大多数官方服务器)<br/>或老式双端点 SSE\"| X1[\"接不了\"]\n    G2{\"闸门 2: 鉴权\"} --> G2b\n    G2b -->|\"免鉴权 / 裸 loopback\"| G3\n    G2b -->|\"OAuth 或 Bearer token<br/>(record 没有 headers 字段)\"| X2[\"接不了\"]\n    G3{\"闸门 3: 调用形态\"} --> G3b\n    G3b -->|\"单工具, 动态参数只有 query/limit<br/>(常量可硬编码在 args 里)\"| G4\n    G3b -->|\"要更多动态参数 / 嵌套对象<br/>/ 多步调用 / resources / sampling\"| X3[\"接不了\"]\n    G4{\"闸门 4: 载荷形状\"} --> G4b\n    G4b -->|\"text 里是 JSON 数组或常见信封<br/>(data/items/feeds/results/notes)\"| OK[\"✅ 接入, 通用映射引擎读行\"]\n    G4b -->|\"散文 / 图片 / 嵌套结构<br/>(映射结果为空)\"| X4[\"接上但搜不到东西\"]\n```\n\n## 四道闸门对应的事实（已核实）\n\n| 闸门 | 代码事实 | 卡掉了谁 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **传输** | `_mcp_rpc` 是 urllib POST，声明 `2025-03-26`；能容忍 SSE 帧的**应答**，但不会做老式 `GET /sse` + `POST /messages` 双端点舞步，也没有任何 stdio 子进程管理 | **生态里最大的一块**：官方示例和 npx/uvx 一键启动的服务器多数是 stdio（filesystem、github、sqlite…） |\n| **鉴权** | `McpService` 没有 `headers` 字段，请求只带 `Content-Type`/`Accept`/`Mcp-Session-Id`；record 无处填 token；2025-06-18 的 OAuth 流程完全没实现 | 任何挂着 bearer token 的远程服务器（恰恰是“远程”服务器的常态） |\n| **调用** | `search_args` 的动态值只有 `{\"query\", \"limit\"}`；没有 `tools/list`（工具名和参数名全靠手填）；每次搜索重新握手，一次搜索 3 个往返，无会话复用/重连 | 参数表复杂的工具、需要多轮状态的工具 |\n| **载荷** | 映射引擎吃任意 JSON（字段链、URL 模板、`list_key`、常见信封自动解包）——这部分**确实通用**；但散文式返回会映射为空 → `no results` | 非结构化返回 |\n\n## 回到分层框架，这句话就精确了\n\n- **信封层**：“任意”成立——只要服务器肯用 Streamable HTTP 说协议，那 135 行通用客户端原封不动对谁都有效（你的 xiaohongshu 和测试里的假服务器走的就是同一段代码）\n- **传输/鉴权层**：“任意”不成立——这是当前实现的真实边界，也是“阉割版”指责里最硬的部分\n- **载荷层**：MCP 本来就不保证通用（上一轮的结论），Clutch 用映射记录接住了 JSON 形状的多样性，接不住非 JSON\n\n## 如果想扩大边界，按性价比排序\n\n1. **record 加 `headers` 字段**（~5 行 + 测试）——解锁所有 bearer token 服务器，性价比最高\n2. **`tools/list` 发现**（~30 行）——状态接口顺带列出工具名，单工具服务器免手填 `search_tool`；用信封层自带的通用数据消灭手写配置\n3. **`inputSchema` 自动推导 args**——单 string 参数时免手填模板，记录缩到 `{name, url}`\n4. **stdio 桥**——真正的大件（子进程管理、跨平台、生命周期），除非你自己的服务就是 stdio，否则不值得\n5. **OAuth**——明确不做；真有需求时操作者用网关/反代解决，客户端保持零 OAuth 面\n\n## 收束\n\n所以对这个问题的完整回答是：**“接入任意 MCP 服务器”从来不是这个功能的目标——目标是“接任意搜索后端”。** 在“搜索后端”这个小集合里（你自己的 xiaohongshu 服务这类本地、免鉴权、单工具、吐 JSON 的 HTTP 服务器），当前实现是完整可用的；对 MCP 服务器全集，它是一个诚实的窄子集——而边界在哪里，现在有了准确的描述和一份按性价比排好的扩边清单。"}
