{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789818111.4120934, "id": "82a0c025e0c0", "content": "这个问题正好补上整个图景的最后一块。让我把 `websearch.py` 里 bing/ddg 的原生实现读出来（前面只读了 MCP 部分）：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_4a2bedc5dccf4f54b3cf9999", "name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"limit\":210,\"offset\":1,\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"}"}, {"id": "call_8f509691d4d44629a2d6fe22", "name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"limit\":107,\"offset\":596,\"path\":\"agent/tools/websearch.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user asks: \"那么bing/ddg在web search中的聚合是如何实现的？它们本来不也是要靠运行某个命令/脚本访问吗\" — \"So how is the bing/ddg aggregation in web search implemented? Don't they also need to run some command/script to access?\"\n\nThis is the exact question from the very first turn of this conversation (the original task before compaction). Interesting — the user is now asking it as a follow-up to the discussion about \"agent can talk to any service via shell\". The question: how do bing/ddg backends work in Clutch's web_search — aren't they also just... running commands/scripts to access?\n\nThe key insight the user is circling: everything ultimately reduces to \"make an HTTP request and parse the response\". bing/ddg are just built-in Python functions that make HTTP requests — they're the same \"curl-equivalent\" thing, just written as code inside the process. So the answer should:\n\n1. Show how _bing and _ddg are implemented in agent/tools/websearch.py — I haven't actually read those functions yet! I've read lines 415-596 (the MCP part and backend registry). I need to read the earlier part of websearch.py: _http_get, _bing, _ddg, _tavily, _searxng.\n\nLet me read the file's beginning through line ~415 to see the native backends.\n\nKey points I expect:\n- _ddg: hits DuckDuckGo's HTML/lite endpoint or the JSON \"instant answer\" API? More likely the html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q= endpoint and regex-parse results.\n- _bing: \"内置 Bing RSS 免 key 后端\" per README — Bing has an RSS feed: https://www.bing.com/search?q=...&format=rss — yes, Bing search supports RSS output format. So _bing fetches the RSS and parses XML. No API key needed.\n- _searxng: JSON API of self-hosted SearXNG (format=json).\n- _tavily: REST API with key.\n\nAnd the aggregation: web_search iterates the backend chain (available_backends), tries in order, collects/merges results? Or stops at first success? Need to check web_search function (line 613+). I read the signature area earlier but not the body. Let me read lines 596-702.\n\nThe answer's core philosophical point, connecting to the whole conversation arc:\n- Yes — bing/ddg ARE \"running some code to access\" — but the code runs IN the agent process as Python functions using urllib, not as external commands. The shell (curl) and the built-in backend (urllib in Python) are the same act at different integration depths.\n- The spectrum: shell command (agent improvises) → built-in function (in-process, zero-config) → declarative MCP layer (operator-configured external service).\n- bing/ddg are special because they need NO credentials and NO config: keyless backends. So \"接入\" them = the code ships with the product. They're not \"aggregated\" via any protocol — they're just functions in a try-chain.\n\nHow does the aggregation work exactly? Need to read:\n1. _http_get: shared HTTP with SSRF guard, cancel, etc.\n2. _bing: Bing RSS URL, XML parse (namespace? <item><title><link><description>)\n3. _ddg: probably html.duckduckgo.com HTML scraping with regex, or the lite version\n4. web_search: chain iteration, dedup?, limit allocation, error handling (does it try next backend on failure — \"degradation\"?)\n\nLet me read websearch.py lines 1-415 (or the relevant chunks). The file is 702 lines. I read 415-596 already. Let me read 1-415 in two chunks, plus 596-702.\n\nThen compose the answer:\n- 直答: 是的——bing/ddg 本质上也是\"跑代码去访问\", 只不过这段代码是编译进 agent 进程的 Python 函数 (urllib 直接发 HTTP), 不是外部命令。它们和 curl 的关系: 同一个动作, 不同的封装深度。\n- 展示 _bing/_ddg 的实际代码: _bing = Bing 官方 RSS 输出 (format=rss), XML 解析; _ddg = DDG 的 html/lite 端点 + 正则/解析。免 key。\n- 聚合机制: Backend 协议 (name, search, available) + _BACKENDS 注册表 + _DEFAULT_CHAIN 顺序 + available() 过滤 → web_search 按 try-chain 或 merge。\n- 三种接入深度的连续谱: 进程内函数 (bing/ddg/tavily/searxng) / 声明式 MCP (operator 配的外部服务) / agent 临时 shell (curl)。本质上都是\"发 HTTP, 解响应\"。\n- 呼应上一轮: bing/ddg 之所以能\"内置\", 因为它们是公共免 key 端点 — 无需操作者声明; xiaohongshu 那种需要登录态/本地起服务的, 就只能走后两条路。所以\"内置 vs 配置 vs 临时\"的选择标准是: 谁负责让服务可达 + 是否需要凭据。\n\nLet me read the code now."}
