{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789869442.104747, "id": "f8823d74c71d", "tool_call_id": "call_13708a4320e040abbf873abd", "content": "298:     \"\"\"Serve SKILL.md (or a sub-file) from the skill's directory; error-as-data.\"\"\"\n299:     lib = cached_library(config.skills_dir)\n300:     skill = lib.get(name)\n301:     if skill is None:\n302:         return {\n303:             \"content\": render(\"errors/skill_unknown.md\", skill=repr(name), available=\", \".join(lib.names()) or \"none\"),\n304:             \"error\": True,\n305:         }\n306:     root = skill.dir.resolve()\n307:     path = (skill.dir / file).resolve()\n308:     if not path.is_relative_to(root):\n309:         return {\"content\": render(\"errors/skill_escape.md\", file=repr(file)), \"error\": True}\n310:     if not path.is_file():\n311:         return {\n312:             \"content\": render(\"errors/skill_missing.md\", skill=repr(name), file=repr(file)),\n313:             \"error\": True,\n314:         }\n315:     try:\n316:         return {\"content\": path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")}\n317:     except OSError as e:\n318:         return {\"content\": render(\"errors/skill_read_failed.md\", error=e), \"error\": True}\n319: \n320: \n321: class ToolRegistry:\n322:     def __init__(self, tools: list[Tool]) -> None:\n323:         self._tools = {t.name: t for t in tools}\n324:         # a tool opts into Stop by declaring a `cancel` parameter on its func\n325:         # (run_command does); the rest get the exact same call as before\n326:         self._cancelable = {\n327:             name: \"cancel\" in inspect.signature(t.func).parameters for name, t in self._tools.items()\n328:         }\n329: \n330:     def schemas(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n331:         return [t.to_openai_schema() for t in self._tools.values()]\n332: \n333:     def names(self) -> list[str]:\n334:         return list(self._tools)\n335: \n336:     def execute(\n337:         self,\n338:         workspace: Workspace,\n339:         config: Config,\n340:         name: str,\n341:         args: dict[str, Any],\n342:         cancel: threading.Event | None = None,\n343:     ) -> dict[str, Any]:\n344:         tool = self._tools.get(name)\n345:         if tool is None:\n346:             return {\n347:                 \"content\": render(\"unknown_tool.md\", tool=name, available=\", \".join(self.names())),\n348:                 \"error\": True,\n349:             }\n350:         try:\n351:             args = self._coerce_types(tool, args)\n352:             if self._cancelable.get(name):\n353:                 result = tool.func(workspace, config, cancel=cancel, **args)\n354:             else:\n355:                 result = tool.func(workspace, config, **args)\n356:         except TypeError as e:\n357:             result = {\"content\": render(\"errors/invalid_arguments.md\", error=e), \"error\": True}\n358:         except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 -- tool boundary: report to model\n359:             result = {\"content\": render(\"errors/tool_exception.md\", error=e), \"error\": True}\n360:         # normalize: every tool result carries error/diff so callers can index them\n361:         result.setdefault(\"error\", False)\n362:         result.setdefault(\"diff\", \"\")\n363:         return result\n364: \n365:     @staticmethod\n366:     def _coerce_types(tool: Tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n367:         \"\"\"Coerce args to the declared JSON Schema types (models sometimes pass strings).\"\"\"\n368:         props = tool.parameters.get(\"properties\", {})\n369:         for key, spec in props.items():\n370:             if key not in args:\n371:                 continue\n372:             if spec.get(\"type\") == \"integer\" and not isinstance(args[key], int):\n373:                 try:\n374:                     args[key] = int(args[key])\n375:                 except (TypeError, ValueError):\n376:                     pass\n377:         return args", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789869515.5788784, "id": "d78035492fee", "content": "全部执行路径读完核验了。现在可以给出这个开场问题的终局答案——完整的工具调用与执行逻辑，从 schema 到结果回灌，一共七步：\n\n## 总览：一条事件驱动的 while 循环\n\n```\nrun(task):\n  while True:\n    ① 预算检查 (max_turns)\n    ② 从事件日志推导消息 (context.derive_messages)\n    ③ 接近窗口 → 压缩 (Compactor) → 重新推导\n    ④ 调 LLM (流式) → (content, tool_calls, finish_reason)\n    ⑤ 有 tool_calls → 逐个执行 → 结果回灌 → continue\n       无 tool_calls 且有正文 → 结束 (completed)\n       空回复不算完成 → 喂回错误 → 重试\n```\n\n`loop.py` 的 docstring 一句话点破设计：**Events are the single source of truth**——日志、GUI、上下文全部从事件流派生，所以回放、压缩、界面永远一致。\n\n## 七步流水线\n\n**① 装配（每次 run）** — `base.py:start_task`：workspace（本地或 SSH 桥）+ LLM 客户端 + `ToolRegistry(build_default_tools(cfg))` + PermissionGate + Agent。关键：`build_tools(project, cfg)` 接收**本次 run 的 config**——chat 模式和工作模式生成的是**不同的工具集**（registry.py:93 注释写明：“chat mode: no write tools. The model never sees write_file/edit_file — **the schema is the hard boundary**\"）。\n\n**② 定义（单一事实源）** — `Tool` 数据类（registry.py:26）：`name + description(从 prompts/*.md 渲染，可动态插值) + JSON Schema + func`。一个定义同时产出 OpenAI schema 和本地执行入口——前面几轮讨论的“动态渲染”（web_search 只列真实后端）就发生在这一步的 `render()` 里。\n\n**③ 暴露** — `registry.schemas()` 转成 function-calling 格式传给 `llm.stream(msgs, tools=...)`。模型看到的世界 = 名字 + 描述 + schema，仅此而已。\n\n**④ 流式回合** — `_llm_call`：增量接收 reasoning/text/tool_call 事件，`tool_call_start` 先到名字、`tool_call_delta` 流式累积参数（UI 实时显示调用生成过程），每个 chunk 之间检查 Stop。\n\n**⑤ 循环裁决与看门狗**（`Agent.run` 中）：\n- 先记 `AssistantMessageEvent` **再**记 `ToolCallEvent`（保证会话回放顺序 = 文本→调用→结果）\n- **doom-loop 双重检测**：警告后重复完全相同的调用 → 升级（中止或喂回警告）；执行后 `record_call(name, args, result)` —— **相同调用且相同结果**才报警，且保留真实结果只附加警告，让模型自我纠正\n- `finish_reason == \"length\"` → 丢弃不完整调用，注入“请简洁”消息重来\n\n**⑥ 单次执行**（`_execute_tool` → `registry.execute`）—— 四道闸门依序：\n\n| 闸门 | 代码 | 失败时的行为 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 参数解析 | `parse_arguments(原始JSON串)` | 错误数据回灌 |\n| **权限** | `gate.require(name, args, workspace)`（chat 分类器/询问用户/自动放行） | 拒绝理由作为错误数据 |\n| 类型纠正 | `_coerce_types`——模型传 `\"28\"` 时按 schema 纠成 int | 静默修复 |\n| **取消注入** | 反射检查 func 是否声明 `cancel` 参数（run_command 有）——有则把 Stop 事件递进去，命令在飞时被杀树 | — |\n\n然后统一约定调用：`tool.func(workspace, config, **args)` → 依赖注入两个环境对象，其余全靠 **kwargs。任何异常在工具边界被捕获转成错误数据（registry.py:358 注释：\"tool boundary: report to model\"）——**工具崩溃永远炸不毁循环**。`finally: workspace.clear_allowed()`：用户批准的越权只对这一次调用生效。\n\n**⑦ 回灌** — `ToolResultEvent`（content + is_error + diff）进日志、推 UI；下一轮 `derive_messages` 把它作为 `tool_call_id` 对应的工具消息拼回上下文。模型看到结果，决定继续调用还是作答。\n\n## 一张图\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"LLM 流式产出 tool_call<br/>(id + name + args JSON串)\"] --> B[\"parse_arguments\"]\n    B --> C[\"PermissionGate.require<br/>(chat分类器 / 询问 / 放行)\"]\n    C --> D[\"registry.execute<br/>类型纠正 + cancel注入\"]\n    D --> E[\"func(workspace, config, **args)<br/>统一返回 dict: content/error/diff\"]\n    E --> F[\"异常→错误数据<br/>(工具边界)\"]\n    F --> G[\"ToolResultEvent 进日志+推UI\"]\n    G --> H[\"下一轮 derive_messages<br/>结果回灌给模型\"]\n    H --> A\n```\n\n## 用上一轮的框架收束\n\n这场对话最后建立的“agent = 一台计算机”的比喻，现在每个部件都有了确切的代码坐标：\n\n| 计算机部件 | Clutch 实现 |\n|---|---|\n| 指令集 ROM | `build_default_tools`——固化层，11 个具名工具，随模式裁剪 |\n| 说明书 | JSON Schema + 渲染的 description——模型唯一的契约来源 |\n| CPU（控制单元） | **模型本身**——循环里没有任何编排/路由/规划逻辑 |\n| 时钟 | `while True` + 结果回灌 |\n| MMU（内存保护） | PermissionGate + chat 模式的工具集裁剪 |\n| 看门狗 | Terminator（回合预算 + 双重 doom-loop 检测） |\n| 中断线 | `threading.Event`，经反射注入声明了 cancel 的工具 |\n| 系统总线 | 事件流——日志/GUI/上下文的单一事实源 |\n\n而最优雅的对称：这套内部契约（name + JSON 参数 + content 结果 + error 标志）**正是 MCP 在网络上标准化的同一形状**——`ToolRegistry` 就是一个缩微的本地 MCP 服务器，`registry.execute` 就是它的 `tools/call`。这场对话从“Clutch 怎么消费 MCP”开始，到这里发现“Clutch 自己就是 MCP”——零足迹原则（未配置的服务不出现在 schema 里）、错误即数据、schema 即硬边界，内外是同一套哲学。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "Now I have every piece of the tool invocation/execution pipeline verified. Let me compose the definitive answer to \"现在工具的调用和执行是什么逻辑？\" — the question that opened this conversation, now answered with full architectural context.\n\nThe complete pipeline:\n\n**Phase 0 — 装配 (per run)**: `BaseServer.start_task` (base.py) assembles: workspace (local or remote SSH bridge) + LLM client + `ToolRegistry(build_default_tools(cfg, memories))` + PermissionGate + Agent. Crucially `build_tools(project, config)` takes the per-run config: **chat mode vs work mode produce different toolsets** — write_file/edit_file don't even exist in chat mode (schema is the hard boundary).\n\n**Phase 1 — 定义 (build_default_tools)**: One `Tool` dataclass = name + description (rendered from `agent/prompts/tools/*.md`, with dynamic interpolation like $backends) + JSON Schema parameters + func (`(workspace, config, **args) -> dict{content, error?, diff?}`). Single source of truth: schema and execution entry from one definition (to_openai_schema()).\n\n**Phase 2 — 暴露给模型**: `registry.schemas()` → OpenAI function-calling format → passed to `llm.stream(msgs, tools=...)`. The model never sees Python; it sees name/description/JSON-schema. Dynamic content: web_search's description lists only real backends; chat mode doesn't contain write_file at all — the toolset itself is mode/environment-dependent.\n\n**Phase 3 — 流式回合 (_llm_call)**: The LLM streams: reasoning deltas, text deltas, tool_call_start (id+name arrive first), tool_call_delta (args stream incrementally, accumulated by index), finish(reason). Events emitted live to UI (ToolCallDeltaEvent shows the call as it's being generated). Cancel checked between chunks.\n\n**Phase 4 — 循环裁决 (Agent.run)**: while True:\n- budget check (max_turns)\n- derive messages from event log (context.derive_messages — events are the single source of truth: log, GUI, context all derive from them)\n- compaction check (near window → compact → re-derive)\n- call LLM\n- finish_reason == \"length\" → drop incomplete tool calls, inject \"be concise\" user message, continue\n- **tool_calls present**: \n  1. record AssistantMessageEvent BEFORE ToolCallEvents (replay order: text → tools → results)\n  2. for each tool_call: doom-loop escalation check (terminator.should_escalate — repeating the exact same call after a warning → abort or error-as-data)\n  3. `_execute_tool(ev)`\n  4. result-aware doom check: record_call(name, args, result) — identical call AND identical result → warn (append doom_loop.md warning to the real result, let the model course-correct)\n  5. emit ToolResultEvent\n  6. `continue` — next turn, model sees results\n- **no tool_calls**: text = answer; empty text is NOT completion (fed back as error, retry)\n\n**Phase 5 — 单次执行 (_execute_tool)**:\n1. `parse_arguments(ev.arguments)` — the raw JSON string; ParseError → error-as-data\n2. `gate.require(name, args_repr, workspace)` — PermissionGate (chat-mode classifier / ask-user / auto-allow in non-interactive); PermissionRequired → denial as error data\n3. `registry.execute(workspace, config, name, args, cancel=self.cancel)`\n4. finally: `workspace.clear_allowed()` — a user-approved escape is scoped to exactly one call\n\n**Phase 6 — registry.execute**:\n1. unknown tool → error-as-data with available names (model can recover)\n2. `_coerce_types` — models sometimes pass \"28\" instead of 28; coerce to declared schema types\n3. cancel-injection by introspection: tools declaring a `cancel` parameter (run_command) get the Stop event; others unchanged\n4. `tool.func(workspace, config, **args)` — the uniform convention `(workspace, config, **args) -> dict`\n5. TypeError → invalid_arguments error data; any Exception → tool_exception error data (the tool boundary turns exceptions into data — a crash never kills the loop)\n6. normalize: every result carries error/diff keys\n\n**Phase 7 — 反馈**: ToolResultEvent appended to log + streamed to UI (with diff for write tools); next `derive_messages` includes it as the tool result message for tool_call_id.\n\nThen the synthesis connecting to the whole conversation arc:\n\n- The loop is deliberately dumb: no orchestration, no routing, no planning logic — **the model is the control unit**, the loop is just the clock (while True + feed results back). Tools are the instruction set, registry is the decoder.\n- Events as single source of truth: log/GUI/context all derive — this is why compaction, replay, UI all stay consistent.\n- Error-as-data at every boundary: parse errors, permission denials, unknown tools, exceptions, doom loops — everything becomes a string the model reads. The loop never crashes on a tool.\n- The previous turn's frame made concrete: registry = instruction set ROM (固化 layer), the schema = the only documentation the model has, PermissionGate = the MMU, doom-loop detector = watchdog timer, cancel = interrupt line.\n- And the MCP symmetry: the internal contract (name, JSON args, content result, error flag) is EXACTLY the shape MCP standardizes for the network — Clutch's ToolRegistry is a local MCP server in miniature. The zero-footprint gating (chat mode lacks write tools; unconfigured backends don't exist in schemas) applies at registry build time.\n\nA mermaid sequence-ish flowchart of the pipeline would help. Mermaid rules: no double quotes in labels, subgraph id+quoted title. Let me build a flowchart of one turn.\n\nKeep the answer comprehensive but organized. This is the definitive capstone. I'll write it in Chinese with the pipeline phases, key code citations (file:line), the design principles table, and the synthesis."}
