rce_types`——模型传 `\"28\"` 时按 schema 纠成 int | 静默修复 |\n| **取消注入** | 反射检查 func 是否声明 `cancel` 参数（run_command 有）——有则把 Stop 事件递进去，命令在飞时被杀树 | — |\n\n然后统一约定调用：`tool.func(workspace, config, **args)` → 依赖注入两个环境对象，其余全靠 **kwargs。任何异常在工具边界被捕获转成错误数据（registry.py:358 注释：\"tool boundary: report to model\"）——**工具崩溃永远炸不毁循环**。`finally: workspace.clear_allowed()`：用户批准的越权只对这一次调用生效。\n\n**⑦ 回灌** — `ToolResultEvent`（content + is_error + diff）进日志、推 UI；下一轮 `derive_messages` 把它作为 `tool_call_id` 对应的工具消息拼回上下文。模型看到结果，决定继续调用还是作答。\n\n## 一张图\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"LLM 流式产出 tool_call<br/>(id + name + args JSON串)\"] --> B[\"parse_arguments\"]\n    B --> C[\"PermissionGate.require<br/>(chat分类器 / 询问 / 放行)\"]\n    C --> D[\"registry.execute<br/>类型纠正 + cancel注入\"]\n    D --> E[\"func(workspace, config, **args)<br/>统一返回 dict: content/error/diff\"]\n    E --> F[\"异常→错误数据<br/>(工具边界)\"]\n    F --> G[\"ToolResultEvent 进日志+推UI\"]\n    G --> H[\"下一轮 derive_messages<br/>结果回灌给模型\"]\n    H --> A\n```\n\n## 用上一轮的框架收束\n\n这场对话最后建立的“agent = 一台计算机”的比喻，现在每个部件都有了确切的代码坐标：\n\n| 计算机部件 | Clutch 实现 |\n|---|---|\n| 指令集 ROM | `build_default_tools`——固化层，11 个具名工具，随模式裁剪 |\n| 说明书 | JSON Schema + 渲染的 description——模型唯一的契约来源 |\n| CPU（控制单元） | **模型本身**——循环里没有任何编排/路由/规划逻辑 |\n| 时钟 | `while True` + 结果回灌 |\n| MMU（内存保护） | PermissionGate + chat 模式的工具集裁剪 |\n| 看门狗 | Terminator（回合预算 + 双重 doom-loop 检测） |\n| 中断线 | `threading.Event`，经反射注入声明了 cancel 的工具 |\n| 系统总线 | 事件流——日志/GUI/上下文的单一事实源 |\n\n而最优雅的对称：这套内部契约（name + JSON 参数 + content 结果 + error 标志）**正是 MCP 在网络上标准化的同一形状**——`ToolRegistry` 就是一个缩微的本地 MCP 服务器，`registry.execute` 就是它的 `tools/call`。这场对话从“Clutch 怎么消费 MCP”开始，到这里发现“Clutch 自己就是 MCP”——零足迹原则（未配置的服务不出现在 schema 里）、错误即数据、schema 即硬边界，内外是同一套哲学。"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789869815.0487454, "id": "d32eb2919aa1", "content": "现在我想改一下工具层的抽象，把工具的执行和调用分离：模型调用的所有工具的执行方式都固定为执行某一条指令，所有工具都遵循这个模型。工具的实现变成指令的实现。例如，如果指令执行是通过python实现的，那么工具的调用最终结果就应该是“python xxx.py”，如果用sh实现的也同理。目前的项目逻辑可以修改成这样吗？"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789869958.3085148, "id": "640060a5ddf1", "content": "这是整场对话真正的起点问题——现在带着全部积累，可以给出决定性回答了。\n\n## 判决：可以。切口恰好只有一行\n\n上一轮核验的执行管线里，工具的实现介质只在一处登场：\n\n```python\n# registry.py:353-355\nresult = tool.func(workspace, config, cancel=cancel, **args)\n```\n\n`Tool` 数据类（name + description + schema + func）在模型侧是自足的：schema 进 prompt、权限门禁读 name+args、doom 检测读 name+args+result、事件流读结果——**全部只依赖调用契约，不依赖 func 是什么**。把 `func(...)` 换成“构造指令 → 执行 → 解析 stdout”，上游零改动。你要切的那条缝，项目已经天然留好了。\n\n## 先定位你的提议：它不是\"everything is shell\"\n\n上一轮我们论证过“模型直接 run_command 一切”的代价（权限模型塌缩、spawn 税、契约退化）。你的提议**不是**那个——它是更精确的东西：\n\n> **调用契约保持具名工具不变（模型继续 `read_file(path, offset, limit)`），实现介质统一为“执行一条指令”。**\n\n这正是 **git 的单二进制子命令模式**，也正是 **MCP stdio 服务器的形状**（stdin 收 JSON、stdout 吐 JSON 的子进程）。模型完全无感——它甚至无法分辨自己调的是进程内函数还是一个脚本。\n\n## 改造前后\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph before[\"现状\"]\n        A1[\"tool_call: read_file path=x offset=28\"] --> B1[\"parse → gate.require → coerce\"]\n        B1 --> C1[\"func(workspace, config, **args)<br/>进程内 Python 调用\"]\n        C1 --> D1[\"{content, error, diff}\"]\n    end\n    subgraph after[\"提议\"]\n        A2[\"tool_call: read_file path=x offset=28<br/>(模型侧完全不变)\"] --> B2[\"parse → gate.require → coerce<br/>(权限与看门狗不动)\"]\n        B2 --> C2[\"build_command(tool.exec, args)<br/>→ 子进程执行指令\"]\n        C2 --> D2[\"stdout JSON → 解析 → {content, error, diff}\"]\n    end\n```\n\n## 五个关键设计决定\n\n1. **单入口分派器（git 模式），不是每工具一个散脚本**：`python -m agent.tools.cli <tool_name>`。实现核心还是现有的 `filesystem.read_file` 等函数——CLI 只是壳。之后个别工具想变成独立 sh 脚本，声明 `exec: [\"bash\", \"tools/bin/foo.sh\"]` 即可，分派器无感。\n2. **参数走 stdin JSON，不走 argv**。两个血泪教训支持这条：Windows 命令行有 32K 字符上限（`write_file` 的大文件内容必炸）；本会话刚验证过中文参数经命令行会被 GBK 弄哑。`{\"args\": {...}, \"workspace\": \"...\"}` 从 stdin 喂 UTF-8 字节，全部绕开。\n3. **stdout 契约原样复用**：子进程打印现有的 `{content, error, diff}` JSON——下游的事件流、doom 检测、UI 渲染一行不改。非 JSON 输出降级为纯文本 content。\n4. **门禁必须留在派发器，绝不进子进程**。“一切皆指令”最大的诱惑是让某条指令绕过 gate——架构上要把 gate 钉死在 `registry.execute` 里，子进程生而不持权。\n5. **cancel 反而变好了**：现在是反射注入 Stop 事件 + run_command 内部轮询；改成子进程后，Stop = kill 进程树，按构造可杀。\n\n## 什么动、什么不动\n\n| | 处置 |\n|---|---|\n| schema / 描述 / 动态渲染 | 不动（模型侧零感知） |\n| PermissionGate、doom-loop、事件流、ToolResultEvent | 不动（全在父进程） |\n| `Tool.func` | 保留为实现核心，CLI 壳调用**同一个函数** |\n| `ToolRegistry.execute` 的分发行 | **唯一被替换的一行** |\n| Workspace/Config 引导 | 子进程内重建（读 settings.json、解析 workdir——都是文件支撑的，无进程内隐状态） |\n\n## 三个意想不到的红利\n\n1. **每个工具变成手上可调试的命令**：`python -m agent.tools.cli read_file --path x` 在终端里直接跑——开发和 eval 从此不需要模型在场（base.py 里 server 和 eval 走同一套 build_tools，注册表换芯对两者透明）。\n2. **SSH 远端统一执行**：workspace 层本来就有 RemoteWorkspace 桥。指令化的工具可以选择在**文件所在的主机**上执行，而不是永远在 agent 进程所在的主机——这是现状做不到的（进程内的 `web_search` Python 调用无法“搬”到远端）。\n3. **演化终点自动浮现**：spawn-per-call 在 Windows 上有百毫秒级税。解法是**常驻执行器**——一个 stdin/stdout 行式 JSON 的长驻子进程。而它，就是上一轮说的那个闭环：**一个本地 stdio MCP 服务器的形状**。走到这里，“Clutch 成为别人的 MCP 服务”（workspace 服务器形态）只剩一步之遥。\n\n## 诚实的成本\n\n| 成本 | 缓解 |\n|---|---|\n| spawn 税（Windows 百毫秒级 × 每次调用） | 常驻执行器（即红利 3） |\n| 子进程重建 Config/Workspace | 都是文件读取，毫秒级；或由常驻执行器摊销 |\n| 跨进程调试（栈迹断了、错误要序列化） | stdout 契约里加 `traceback` 字段 |\n| 自拟了一门小协议（stdin/stdout JSON） | 协议两端都在你手里——和之前“对外接 MCP”的争论不同，**这次自拟协议完全站得住**：没有生态互操作问题 |\n\n## 迁移路径（绞杀者模式，随时可停）\n\n1. 加 `agent/tools/cli.py`（分派壳，~60 行）+ `Tool` 加 `exec` 声明字段\n2. `registry.execute` 分支：`tool.exec` 存在则走子进程，否则走 func——**新旧共存**\n3. 先迁 `read_file` 一个工具，跑 `tests/selfcheck.py` + `local_shell_test` 全绿，实测延迟\n4. 依据延迟数据决定：spawn-per-call 够用，还是上常驻执行器\n5. 其余工具逐个声明 `exec`，`func` 降级为实现细节\n\n---\n\n**结论：不但可以，而且这条缝是项目里切得最干净的一刀**——调用与执行本来就只隔着一行代码，而你这四轮对话问下来的所有积累（MCP 的信封/载荷之分、git 模式、skill 携带脚本、缓存层级）都在指向同一个结论：统一实现介质是合法的演化方向，只要把门禁留在派发器、把参数放进 stdin、把常驻执行器当作对抗 spawn 税的预案。切到工作模式的话，Phase 1–3（分派壳 + read_file 试点 + 测试全绿）一次就能落地。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "The user is now asking THE original question from the very first message of this conversation. We've come full circle. After this entire long architectural dialogue — MCP, skills, bing/ddg internals, failover chains, everything-is-shell, the tool invocation/execution pipeline — the user returns to the exact question they started with:\n\n\"现在我想改一下工具层的抽象，把工具的执行和调用分离：模型调用的所有工具的执行方式都固定为执行某一条指令，所有工具都遵循这个模型。工具的实现变成指令的实现。例如，如果指令执行是通过python实现的，那么工具的调用最终结果就应该是\"python xxx.py\"，如果用sh实现的也同理。目前的项目逻辑可以修改成这样吗？\"\n\n(Now I want to change the tool layer abstraction, separating tool invocation from execution: the execution of all tools called by the model is fixed to executing a certain instruction/command, and all tools follow this model. Tool implementations become command implementations. For example, if a command is executed via python, the tool call's final result should be \"python xxx.py\", same for sh. Can the current project logic be modified this way?)\n\nNow, at the END of this conversation, after everything we've discussed, I can give the definitive answer. The whole conversation has been building the conceptual apparatus to answer this properly. The previous turns established:\n\n1. read_file etc. are just Python functions (42 lines each)\n2. The registry is (name, description, schema, func) — single source of truth\n3. The execution pipeline: parse_args → permission gate → coerce → func(workspace, config, **args) → normalize → error-as-data\n4. Shell-everything has real costs: permission model collapse (the classifier misjudged `ls a && ls b` twice this session), spawn latency (4 orders of magnitude), contract-as-documentation, composability wins\n5. The cache hierarchy frame: tools = L1, skills+scripts = L2, ad-hoc shell = L3\n6. MCP's envelope/payload split\n7. The \"everything is X\" historical pattern — reduction is always true, never the design endpoint\n\nNow the user's proposal is SPECIFIC and different from pure \"everything is shell\":\n\n**The proposal**: Keep the tool abstraction for INVOCATION (model still calls named tools with schemas — read_file, write_file, etc.), but separate EXECUTION: every tool's execution is dispatched through a UNIFORM instruction channel — literally constructing and running a command line (`python xxx.py` or `sh xxx.sh`). Tool implementations become command implementations. So:\n\n- Model calls `read_file(path=\"x\", offset=28, limit=33)` (unchanged UX for the model)\n- Registry maps it → `python agent/tools/impl/read_file.py x --offset 28 --limit 33` (or similar)\n- The command runs through the existing shell infrastructure\n- stdout (JSON?) becomes the tool result\n\nSo it's NOT \"everything is run_command from the model's perspective\" (the model keeps named tools). It's \"the tool layer becomes a thin CLI dispatcher\". The seam moves: instead of `func(workspace, config, **args)` direct Python calls, every func becomes a command-builder + runner.\n\nIs this what they mean? \"工具的调用和执行分离：模型调用的所有工具的执行方式都固定为执行某一条指令\" — yes: invocation (schema, model-facing) stays; execution becomes uniformly \"execute one instruction\". The tool implementation becomes an instruction implementation (a standalone script).\n\nThis is a real, known architecture! It's exactly:\n- **The git model**: single binary, subcommands\n- **The `clutch-workspace read_file start=28 end=33` CLI** the user mentioned two turns ago\n- **The ACI/SWE-agent approach**: everything through the computer interface (shell)\n- **MCP stdio servers**: tools implemented as processes speaking JSON-RPC on stdin/stdout — this is EXACTLY \"tool implementation as instruction execution\"! An MCP stdio server receives a JSON-RPC request on stdin, runs its tool, returns JSON on stdout. The user's proposal is essentially \"make every tool a tiny stdio process\" — or one dispatcher process.\n- **Claude Code skills with scripts**: SKILL.md tells the model `bash {baseDir}/scripts/scan-project.sh` — the skill pattern is the manual version of this.\n\nSo my answer: YES, it can be done, the architecture is proven (git, MCP stdio, ACI), and here's exactly how it would map onto the current code — plus the honest cost ledger, plus what I'd recommend.\n\nLet me think about the concrete design in Clutch's codebase:\n\n**Current execution path** (verified last turn):\n```\nmodel → tool_call(name, args JSON) \n  → Agent._execute_tool \n    → parse_arguments \n    → gate.require(name, args, workspace)      ← permission\n    → registry.execute \n      → _coerce_types \n      → tool.func(workspace, config, **args)   ← direct in-process call\n    → normalize {content, error, diff} \n  → ToolResultEvent → next turn\n```\n\n**Proposed path**:\n```\nmodel → tool_call(name, args JSON)\n  → Agent._execute_tool \n    → parse_arguments \n    → gate.require(...)                        ← permission unchanged\n    → registry.execute \n      → command = build_command(tool, args)    ← NEW: args → CLI invocation\n      → run_command_internal(command)          ← through shell infra\n      → stdout → parse JSON → {content, error, diff}\n  → ToolResultEvent → next turn\n```\n\nSo the change is localized to `ToolRegistry.execute` (and Tool gains a `command template` field instead of / in addition to `func`). Everything upstream (model-facing schema, permission gate, doom-loop detection, events) stays IDENTICAL. That's the beauty: the seam the user wants to cut is exactly one line — `tool.func(workspace, config, **args)`.\n\n**Design decisions to make:**\n\n1. **One dispatcher vs per-tool scripts:**\n   - Option A: one entry `python -m agent.tools.cli read_file --path x --offset 28` — a single binary with subcommands (git model). All implementations stay as Python functions; the CLI is a wrapper that calls the SAME functions.\n   - Option B: per-tool scripts `tools/bin/read_file.py` — truly standalone, must bootstrap workspace/config themselves (read settings, find workspace root).\n   - Option A is clearly better initially: no duplication of bootstrap logic; the Tool dataclass gains `cli: \"read_file\"` and execute builds `[\"python\", \"-m\", \"agent.tools.cli\", name, --json-args]`. Later, individual tools can graduate to standalone scripts.\n\n2. **Args passing**: pass JSON via argv or stdin? JSON string as one argv arg is fragile with quoting (Windows 8191 char limit for command lines! write_file content could be huge). → **stdin** for payload, argv for tool name. This matters: write_file with a big file cannot go through argv/命令行. Also CJK on Windows GBK — stdin with UTF-8 bytes avoids the mojibake we hit with curl this session.\n\n3. **Result protocol**: script prints JSON `{content, error, diff}` on stdout — the exact existing dict shape. Registry parses stdout, falls back to raw text if non-JSON. This reuses the existing contract untouched.\n\n4. **What stays in-process**: This is the critical honest part. Some things CANNOT move to the subprocess without loss:\n   - The PermissionGate — must stay in the parent (it's the MMU; a child can't guard itself)\n   - cancel/Stop injection — parent holds the process handle, kills the tree (actually BETTER: subprocess is killable by construction!)\n   - workspace/config bootstrap — must be re-established in the child (or passed via env/args)\n   - doom-loop detection — parent-side, unchanged\n   - schema rendering — parent-side, unchanged\n   - Event emission — parent-side, unchanged\n   - In-process state: the Workspace object (path protection), MemoryStore, cached skill library — child needs to rebuild these (cheap: they're file-backed)\n\n5. **Performance**: Windows process spawn ~50-150ms × every tool call. read_file called dozens of times per session → noticeable. Mitigations: (a) keep a persistent worker process (the \"instruction executor\" as a long-lived child speaking line-delimited JSON on stdin/stdout — basically becoming a local MCP stdio server!), (b) accept the tax, (c) hybrid: hot tools in-process, long-tail via instructions.\n\nWait — that last mitigation is THE punchline: **a persistent child process speaking line-delimited JSON-RPC = an MCP stdio server**. The user's proposed architecture, fully realized, converges to: Clutch's tools become an MCP server that Clutch itself talks to. We said this two turns ago (\"Clutch 把自己的工具暴露为一个 MCP server，就是 workspace 服务器形态的完全体\"). The user's proposal is the incremental path to that endpoint: step 1 = dispatch through commands (spawn per call), step 2 = persistent executor process, step 3 = that process IS an MCP stdio server, and then external agents can drive the same workspace.\n\n6. **What the model sees: NOTHING changes.** Schemas identical, names identical, results identical. This is the \"调用和执行分离\" the user wants — invocation contract decoupled from implementation medium. The model can't tell. Which also means: it can be done incrementally per-tool (strangler pattern) — registry.execute branches: `if tool.cmd: run subprocess else: call func`.\n\n7. **Benefits (honest ones):**\n   - Uniform implementation medium: every tool is a debuggable CLI — you can test ANY tool by hand: `python -m agent.tools.cli read_file --path x` in a terminal. Huge for development/eval (the eval harness could run tools without a model!).\n   - Language freedom: implementations can be any language (sh, python, node...) — the user explicitly wants this (\"如果用sh实现的也同理\")\n   - Process isolation: a crashing tool cannot corrupt the agent process (currently exceptions are caught, but memory/state corruption, global mutations are possible); kill-ability by construction\n   - The workspace-server path: persistent executor → external drivability\n   - Forced contract discipline: tool I/O must be JSON-serializable, no hidden in-process state — makes tools relocatable (remote workspace!)\n   - Actually — REMOTE: if tools execute as commands through the workspace layer, they could execute ON THE REMOTE via the existing SSH bridge! The workspace/transport layer already routes to remote (RemoteWorkspace with bridge_url). Tools-as-commands could run where the files are. This is a real architectural win for the SSH degradation mode: currently read_file goes through RemoteWorkspace routing, but a Python web_search runs LOCALLY. With command-dispatch, every tool could run on the remote host uniformly.\n\n   Hmm wait, careful: web_search needs network + API keys; running it remote may not be desired. But file tools running remote makes sense. The uniformity is optional per-tool.\n\n8. **Costs (honest):**\n   - Spawn tax (Windows!), mitigated by persistent worker\n   - Bootstrap cost per invocation unless persistent: rebuild Config (read settings.json), Workspace (resolve root, protections)\n   - The CJK/quoting hell moves INTO the protocol — solved by JSON-over-stdin, but it's now a protocol to version and maintain (that's literally what MCP is)\n   - Loss of in-process convenience: tools can't share cached state (skill library cache, memory store) without re-reading\n   - The permission model must NOT move into the child — and there's a subtle risk: once \"everything is a command\", someone will be tempted to let the MODEL compose commands directly (bypassing gate) — the architecture must keep the gate in the dispatcher\n   - Debugging: stack traces become cross-process; errors must be serialized\n   - This is essentially rebuilding MCP stdio in-house — the earlier critique \"要么自拟接口和协议\" — the user is now choosing the \"自拟协议\" horn, but for the INTERNAL tool layer, where it's much more defensible than for external services (you own both ends, no ecosystem needed)\n\n9. **Concrete migration plan (strangler, per-tool):**\n   - Phase 0: extract pure functions — most tools are already thin (`filesystem.read_file(workspace, config, **kw)`) — keep as the implementation core\n   - Phase 1: add `agent/tools/cli.py` — argparse/dict dispatch: `python -m agent.tools.cli <name>` + JSON stdin → loads Config, rebuilds Workspace, calls the SAME registry function, prints JSON stdout. Add `Tool.cmd = True` flag per tool.\n   - Phase 2: modify `ToolRegistry.execute`: when `tool.cmd`: build subprocess `[sys.executable, \"-m\", \"agent.tools.cli\", name]`, stdin=json{args, workspace_root, config overrides}, decode stdout JSON, propagate. Permission gate + doom detection + events unchanged in Agent.\n   - Phase 3: migrate one tool (read_file) → run tests → measure latency → decide persistent-worker vs spawn-per-call\n   - Phase 4: if persistent worker: the executor loop is ~30 lines (read line, dispatch, write line) — and it IS a stdio MCP server shape; consider speaking actual MCP so external clients work\n   - Tests: tests/local_shell_test.py, selfcheck exercise tools heavily; the eval harness equivalence (base.py docstring says server and eval both go through build_llm/build_tools — the registry swap is transparent to both)\n\n10. **Answer to \"目前的项目逻辑可以修改成这样吗？\"** — YES. The seam is exactly one line (`tool.func(workspace, config, **args)` in registry.execute:353-355). Everything the conversation established says the model-facing half is already cleanly separated: Tool = (name, description, schema, func). Swap func for cmd-builder+runner and nothing upstream notices. The gate, doom-loop, events, schemas — all stay.\n\nBut I should also give the honest recommendation informed by the whole conversation: \n- Do it for the RIGHT reasons (isolation, remote execution, external drivability, language freedom, hand-debuggability) — not for purity\n- Don't do it as \"everything through run_command's classifier\" — the gate must stay at the dispatcher\n- Consider that step 3 of the natural evolution = your own local MCP — at which point the earlier debates (build vs adopt MCP) come back, but now for a protocol you control on both ends, where inventing a tiny line-JSON protocol is perfectly fine\n- Spawn tax on Windows is the #1 practical risk — persistent worker is the answer, and it's also the bridge to the workspace-server form\n\nAlso worth noting: the eval/testing benefit is real and immediately valuable: today tools can only be tested through Python imports; with the CLI form, every tool becomes reproducible in a terminal — and the model can DISCOVER tools the same way (skills pattern). It also makes the \"工具的实现变成指令的实现\" literal: implementation = a script at a visible path, exactly what the user said two turns ago about skills.\n\nOne more important precision: the user says \"模型调用的所有工具的执行方式都固定为执行某一条指令\" — all tools' EXECUTION fixed as executing ONE instruction. I should design exactly what \"指令\" looks like: a command line. And note argv size limits (Windows ~32K chars; write_file content can exceed → stdin). And sh implementations: the dispatcher handles `sh`/`python` prefix per-tool declaration: Tool gains `exec: [\"python\", \"-m\", \"agent.tools.cli\", name]` or `exec: [\"bash\", \"tools/bin/foo.sh\"]`.\n\nShould I draw the mermaid diagram of before/after? Yes, compact. And a table of what moves / what stays.\n\nI'm in chat mode. The user asks \"可以修改成这样吗\" — a feasibility question + presumably wants the plan. I should answer with the design, costs, and offer to implement in work mode. Keep it structured and definitive. This is the capstone — the conversation has armed us to answer this in a way that wasn't possible at the start (at the start, the same question got answered with a test-bug fix, oddly — the summary suggests the original session went down a different path; now we give the real architectural answer).\n\nLength: substantial but disciplined. Structure:\n1. 直接回答：可以。切口正好是一行（registry.execute 353-355 行）。模型侧一切不变。\n2. 提议的本质定位：这不是\"everything is shell\"，而是\"调用契约不变、实现介质统一为指令\"——git 模式 / MCP stdio 的形状。上一轮的缓存层级里，这是把 L1 的实现介质统一到指令层。\n3. 改造前后的执行路径图\n4. 具体设计（五要素）：单入口 CLI + JSON-over-stdin（argv 的 Windows 限制和 GBK 教训）+ stdout JSON 契约复用 + per-tool exec 声明 + 门禁留在派发器\n5. 什么动、什么不动（表）\n6. 收益清单（含两个意外红利：手可调试/eval 无模型可测；SSH 远端统一执行）\n7. 成本清单（spawn 税→常驻执行器；bootstrap；跨进程调试）\n8. 演化的终点：常驻执行器 ≈ 本地 stdio MCP server → workspace 服务器形态（呼应前面）\n9. 迁移步骤（strangler，一工具一测）\n10. 判决 + 建议在 work mode 落地 Phase 1-2\n\nMake sure to cite exact code lines verified last turn. Keep it tight though — the conversation is long; the user wants the definitive feasibility answer."}
{"type": "final", "timestamp": 1789869958.3109605, "id": "710d7260b443", "status": "completed", "summary": "这是整场对话真正的起点问题——现在带着全部积累，可以给出决定性回答了。\n\n## 判决：可以。切口恰好只有一行\n\n上一轮核验的执行管线里，工具的实现介质只在一处登场：\n\n```python\n# registry.py:353-355\nresult = tool.func(workspace, config, cancel=cancel, **args)\n```\n\n`Tool` 数据类（name + description + schema + func）在模型侧是自足的：schema 进 prompt、权限门禁读 name+args、doom 检测读 name+args+result、事件流读结果——**全部只依赖调用契约，不依赖 func 是什么**。把 `func(...)` 换成“构造指令 → 执行 → 解析 stdout”，上游零改动。你要切的那条缝，项目已经天然留好了。\n\n## 先定位你的提议：它不是\"everything is shell\"\n\n上一轮我们论证过“模型直接 run_command 一切”的代价（权限模型塌缩、spawn 税、契约退化）。你的提议**不是**那个——它是更精确的东西：\n\n> **调用契约保持具名工具不变（模型继续 `read_file(path, offset, limit)`），实现介质统一为“执行一条指令”。**\n\n这正是 **git 的单二进制子命令模式**，也正是 **MCP stdio 服务器的形状**（stdin 收 JSON、stdout 吐 JSON 的子进程）。模型完全无感——它甚至无法分辨自己调的是进程内函数还是一个脚本。\n\n## 改造前后\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph before[\"现状\"]\n        A1[\"tool_call: read_file path=x offset=28\"] --> B1[\"parse → gate.require → coerce\"]\n        B1 --> C1[\"func(workspace, config, **args)<br/>进程内 Python 调用\"]\n        C1 --> D1[\"{content, error, diff}\"]\n    end\n    subgraph after[\"提议\"]\n        A2[\"tool_call: read_file path=x offset=28<br/>(模型侧完全不变)\"] --> B2[\"parse → gate.require → coerce<br/>(权限与看门狗不动)\"]\n        B2 --> C2[\"build_command(tool.exec, args)<br/>→ 子进程执行指令\"]\n        C2 --> D2[\"stdout JSON → 解析 → {content, error, diff}\"]\n    end\n```\n\n## 五个关键设计决定\n\n1. **单入口分派器（git 模式），不是每工具一个散脚本**：`python -m agent.tools.cli <tool_name>`。实现核心还是现有的 `filesystem.read_file` 等函数——CLI 只是壳。之后个别工具想变成独立 sh 脚本，声明 `exec: [\"bash\", \"tools/bin/foo.sh\"]` 即可，分派器无感。\n2. **参数走 stdin JSON，不走 argv**。两个血泪教训支持这条：Windows 命令行有 32K 字符上限（`write_file` 的大文件内容必炸）；本会话刚验证过中文参数经命令行会被 GBK 弄哑。`{\"args\": {...}, \"workspace\": \"...\"}` 从 stdin 喂 UTF-8 字节，全部绕开。\n3. **stdout 契约原样复用**：子进程打印现有的 `{content, error, diff}` JSON——下游的事件流、doom 检测、UI 渲染一行不改。非 JSON 输出降级为纯文本 content。\n4. **门禁必须留在派发器，绝不进子进程**。“一切皆指令”最大的诱惑是让某条指令绕过 gate——架构上要把 gate 钉死在 `registry.execute` 里，子进程生而不持权。\n5. **cancel 反而变好了**：现在是反射注入 Stop 事件 + run_command 内部轮询；改成子进程后，Stop = kill 进程树，按构造可杀。\n\n## 什么动、什么不动\n\n| | 处置 |\n|---|---|\n| schema / 描述 / 动态渲染 | 不动（模型侧零感知） |\n| PermissionGate、doom-loop、事件流、ToolResultEvent | 不动（全在父进程） |\n| `Tool.func` | 保留为实现核心，CLI 壳调用**同一个函数** |\n| `ToolRegistry.execute` 的分发行 | **唯一被替换的一行** |\n| Workspace/Config 引导 | 子进程内重建（读 settings.json、解析 workdir——都是文件支撑的，无进程内隐状态） |\n\n## 三个意想不到的红利\n\n1. **每个工具变成手上可调试的命令**：`python -m agent.tools.cli read_file --path x` 在终端里直接跑——开发和 eval 从此不需要模型在场（base.py 里 server 和 eval 走同一套 build_tools，注册表换芯对两者透明）。\n2. **SSH 远端统一执行**：workspace 层本来就有 RemoteWorkspace 桥。指令化的工具可以选择在**文件所在的主机**上执行，而不是永远在 agent 进程所在的主机——这是现状做不到的（进程内的 `web_search` Python 调用无法“搬”到远端）。\n3. **演化终点自动浮现**：spawn-per-call 在 Windows 上有百毫秒级税。解法是**常驻执行器**——一个 stdin/stdout 行式 JSON 的长驻子进程。而它，就是上一轮说的那个闭环：**一个本地 stdio MCP 服务器的形状**。走到这里，“Clutch 成为别人的 MCP 服务”（workspace 服务器形态）只剩一步之遥。\n\n## 诚实的成本\n\n| 成本 | 缓解 |\n|---|---|\n| spawn 税（Windows 百毫秒级 × 每次调用） | 常驻执行器（即红利 3） |\n| 子进程重建 Config/Workspace | 都是文件读取，毫秒级；或由常驻执行器摊销 |\n| 跨进程调试（栈迹断了、错误要序列化） | stdout 契约里加 `traceback` 字段 |\n| 自拟了一门小协议（stdin/stdout JSON） | 协议两端都在你手里——和之前“对外接 MCP”的争论不同，**这次自拟协议完全站得住**：没有生态互操作问题 |\n\n## 迁移路径（绞杀者模式，随时可停）\n\n1. 加 `agent/tools/cli.py`（分派壳，~60 行）+ `Tool` 加 `exec` 声明字段\n2. `registry.execute` 分支：`tool.exec` 存在则走子进程，否则走 func——**新旧共存**\n3. 先迁 `read_file` 一个工具，跑 `tests/selfcheck.py` + `local_shell_test` 全绿，实测延迟\n4. 依据延迟数据决定：spawn-per-call 够用，还是上常驻执行器\n5. 其余工具逐个声明 `exec`，`func` 降级为实现细节\n\n---\n\n**结论：不但可以，而且这条缝是项目里切得最干净的一刀**——调用与执行本来就只隔着一行代码，而你这四轮对话问下来的所有积累（MCP 的信封/载荷之分、git 模式、skill 携带脚本、缓存层级）都在指向同一个结论：统一实现介质是合法的演化方向，只要把门禁留在派发器、把参数放进 stdin、把常驻执行器当作对抗 spawn 税的预案。切到工作模式的话，Phase 1–3（分派壳 + read_file 试点 + 测试全绿）一次就能落地。"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789870103.436039, "id": "8fa4c41b93ba", "content": "你说话说着有种装装的感觉，充满了各种你自己拟定的黑话，我不需要你对方案发表感想，而是需要你说清楚到底改哪些地方，不要预先假设我清楚所有的项目细节"}
{"type": "compaction", "timestamp": 1789870227.4259682, "id": "dc487cdc27aa", "summary": "## Objective\n- 用户最初问“工具的调用和执行是什么逻辑”，经多轮架构讨论（MCP 定义与边界、skill、bing/ddg 实现、执行管线）后提出具体重构需求：把工具的调用与执行分离——所有工具的执行统一为“执行一条指令”（如 `python xxx.py` / `sh xxx.sh`），工具实现变成指令实现，询问现有项目逻辑能否改。\n- 用户最新消息批评回答风格（自造黑话、说教感），明确要求：只讲清楚具体改哪些地方，逐步说明，不预设用户熟悉项目细节。\n\n## Important Details\n- 项目：Clutch coding agent，路径 `C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch`。代码内文本（注释、工具描述、报错）必须英文；README.md 用中文。测试为自运行模块：`.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m tests.X`；系统 python 缺依赖；`uv run` 会超 30s 超时。\n- 会话内已核实的关键代码事实（重构计划的依据）：`agent/tools/registry.py` 的 `Tool` dataclass（约 L26）= name + description（从 `agent/prompts/tools/*.md` 渲染，含动态 `$backends` 插值）+ JSON Schema + func；`build_default_tools` 按模式裁剪工具集（chat 模式无 write_file/edit_file，“schema 即硬边界”）；`ToolRegistry.execute` 中唯一实现介质登场点为 `result = tool.func(workspace, config, cancel=cancel, **args)`（约 L353-355），其后异常在工具边界转 error-as-data（约 L358）；执行链为 parse_arguments → PermissionGate.require → _coerce_types → cancel 反射注入 → func 调用。`agent/loop.py` Agent.run：事件流为单一事实源、derive_messages、压缩、doom-loop Terminator（record_call 按 name/args/result）、finish_reason==\"length\" 处理。`agent/base.py` start_task/build_tools 为 server 与 eval 共用装配。11 个内置工具；`agent/tools/filesystem.py` 共 188 行（read_file L21、write_file L84、edit_file L114）。\n- 已定重构方案要点（需以朴素语言重述给用户）：新增分发入口 `python -m agent.tools.cli <tool_name>`，参数经 stdin 传 JSON（规避 Windows 命令行 32K 上限与中文 GBK 乱码，本会话已实测踩坑）；子进程 stdout 打印现有 `{content, error, diff}` JSON 契约，下游零改动；`Tool` 增加可选 `exec` 字段，`registry.execute` 按其分支（subprocess 或原 func），新旧共存可逐工具迁移；PermissionGate 与 doom 检测必须留在父进程派发器内；cancel 改为杀进程树；子进程需从文件重建 Config/Workspace；先迁 read_file 试点再跑全量测试；后续可选常驻执行器（形状即本地 stdio MCP 服务器）。\n- 交付中已修复并验证：`agent/mcp_presets.json` 已移至 `agent/tools/mcp_presets.json`（引擎按 `Path(__file__).with_name` 查找）；`tests/mcpbackend_test.py` 服务名 `notes`→`notedb`（避免撞 web_search.md 提示词中的自然语言 \"release notes\"）；README L45 路径同步；`mcpprovider.py` docstring 示例同步改名；已存项目记忆 \"MCP web-search plugin shipped and verified\"。\n- 架构讨论结论（对后续有用）：Clutch MCP 客户端仅支持 Streamable HTTP（`_MCP_PROTO = \"2025-03-26\"`）、无鉴权 headers 字段、无 tools/list、不支持 stdio——能接的精确子集为“HTTP 单端点、免鉴权、单搜索工具、JSON 载荷”；bing/ddg 为进程内 urllib 函数（Bing RSS `format=rss`+ElementTree；DDG html 端点+HTMLParser）；web_search 是 failover 链（首个成功者胜出）而非多源融合，MCP 服务排在链尾；skill 可携带可执行脚本（readme-crafter 即实例，SKILL.md 引用 `{baseDir}/scripts/scan-project.sh`，`load_skill` 的 file 参数可读子文件）；xiaohongshu 服务当前未运行（端口 18060 无监听）。\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- MCP 两处修复落地并全绿：`tests.mcpbackend_test` 59 项通过，`tests.websearch_test`、`tests.server_test`（full）通过。\n- 完整执行管线核验完毕（base.py / loop.py / registry.py / filesystem.py），确定用户提议的重构切口只有一处：`registry.py` 中 `tool.func(...)` 那一行。\n- 重构方案已口头给出（exec 字段 + cli 分发器 + stdin JSON + 门禁留派发器 + 绞杀式逐工具迁移），但表述被用户否定了风格。\n\n### Active\n- 按用户新要求重写回答：不谈理念/感想，逐文件、逐函数给出具体修改清单（含新建文件与代码骨架），并对每个涉及的文件作用做一句说明，不假设用户已知项目细节。回答前应先完整重读 `agent/tools/registry.py`（Tool 字段名、execute 全文）与 `agent/loop.py` 的 `_execute_tool`、PermissionGate 的确切签名以保证引用精确。\n\n### Blocked\n- 编辑与写入需切换到 work mode（当前 chat mode）。\n- chat mode 分类器本会话多次误判只读命令为写操作（`ls a && ls b`、带 `2>/dev/null` 的 ls、第二次 curl POST），不要重试被拒命令。\n\n## Next Move\n1. 重读 `agent/tools/registry.py` 全文（确认 Tool dataclass 字段名、`execute`/`_coerce_types`/`parse_arguments` 细节、L340-377）与 `agent/loop.py` 中 `_execute_tool`、PermissionGate 调用签名。\n2. 用朴素语言输出逐文件修改方案：① 新建 `agent/tools/cli.py`（stdin 收 `{args, workspace_root}` JSON → load_settings 重建 Config、按 root 重建 Workspace → 调用与现在相同的工具函数 → stdout 打印结果 JSON；子进程 `sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")`）；② `registry.py` 的 Tool 加可选 `exec` 字段；③ `ToolRegistry.execute` 增加分支：`tool.exec` 存在则 subprocess 执行（轮询 cancel、超时/取消杀进程、stdout JSON 解析为现有结果 dict），否则走原 func——其余（loop.py、base.py、PermissionGate、事件流、schema）全部不动；④ 首个迁移 read_file；⑤ 新增 `tests/toolcli_test.py` 并跑 `tests.selfcheck`、`tests.local_shell_test` 回归；说明每处“为什么改、改成什么样”，然后请用户切 work mode 落地。\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `agent/tools/registry.py`：核心修改对象——Tool dataclass（~L26）、build_default_tools（L56-277 各工具名）、`ToolRegistry.execute` 的 `tool.func(...)` 分发点（~L353-355）。\n- `agent/loop.py`：Agent.run/_execute_tool/_llm_call/Terminator——重构不改它，但方案需说明为何它不受影响。\n- `agent/base.py`：BaseServer 装配（server 与 eval 共用 build_tools）——不变，用于说明新 CLI 与其透明兼容。\n- `agent/tools/filesystem.py`：read_file（L21）/write_file（L84）/edit_file（L114），首个迁移试点。\n- `agent/tools/mcpprovider.py`、`agent/tools/mcp_presets.json`：MCP 引擎与已迁移到位的预设数据文件（本会话修复）。\n- `tests/mcpbackend_test.py`：notedb 改名后 59 项全绿的回归基线。\n- `agent/tools/websearch.py`：原生后端与 MCP 客户端实现，讨论中多次引用的代码事实来源。\n- `tests/local_shell_test.py`、`tests/selfcheck.py`：重构后必须保持全绿的回归套件。\n- `agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md`：工具描述渲染来源（含 \"release notes\" 自然语言，是 notedb 改名的原因）。"}
