{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789871256.8455298, "id": "746cfbaf20cf", "tool_call_id": "call_288c2b8c942b48978a2c85d1", "content": "84: def write_file(workspace: Workspace, config: Config, path: str, content: str) -> dict:\n85:     try:\n86:         p: Path = workspace.resolve(path)\n87:         if workspace.is_protected(p):\n88:             return _result(render(\"errors/protected_write.md\", path=path), error=True)\n89:         # capture the previous content (if any) to build a unified diff\n90:         old = \"\"\n91:         try:\n92:             old = workspace.read(str(p))\n93:         except FileNotFoundError:\n94:             pass\n95:         if old:\n96:             workspace.snapshot(p, old)\n97:         workspace.write(str(p), content)\n98:         # external paths (approved escapes): show the absolute path in the diff header\n99:         try:\n100:             rel = p.relative_to(workspace.root)\n101:         except ValueError:\n102:             rel = p\n103:         diff = _unified_diff(old, content, rel=rel)\n104:         adds = sum(1 for ln in diff.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\"+\") and not ln.startswith(\"+++\"))\n105:         dels = sum(1 for ln in diff.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\"-\") and not ln.startswith(\"---\"))\n106:         summary = f\"OK: wrote {p} (+{adds} -{dels} lines)\" if old else f\"OK: wrote {p} ({len(content)} chars)\"\n107:         return _result(summary, diff=diff)\n108:     except ValueError as e:\n109:         return _result(f\"ERROR: {e}\", error=True)\n110:     except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n111:         return _result(render(\"errors/write_failed.md\", error=e), error=True)\n112: \n113: \n114: def edit_file(workspace: Workspace, config: Config, path: str, old_string: str, new_string: str) -> dict:\n115:     \"\"\"Targeted string replacement: one occurrence of old_string becomes new_string\n116:     (tiny diffs keep the context small instead of re-emitting the whole file).\"\"\"\n117:     try:\n118:         p: Path = workspace.resolve(path)\n119:         if workspace.is_protected(p):\n120:             return _result(render(\"errors/protected_write.md\", path=path), error=True)\n121:         try:\n122:             text = workspace.read(str(p))\n123:         except FileNotFoundError:\n124:             return _result(f\"ERROR: file not found: {path} — use write_file to create it\", error=True)\n125:         if not old_string:\n126:             return _result(\"ERROR: old_string is required\", error=True)\n127:         count = text.count(old_string)\n128:         if count == 0:\n129:             return _result(\n130:                 f\"ERROR: old_string not found in {path}. The file's current content is in an \"\n131:                 f\"earlier read; re-read it if needed and provide a unique block of context.\",\n132:                 error=True,\n133:             )\n134:         if count > 1:\n135:             return _result(\n136:                 f\"ERROR: old_string appears {count} times in {path}. Include more surrounding \"\n137:                 \"lines so it matches exactly once.\",\n138:                 error=True,\n139:             )\n140:         new = text.replace(old_string, new_string, 1)\n141:         workspace.snapshot(p, text)\n142:         workspace.write(str(p), new)\n143:         try:\n144:             rel = p.relative_to(workspace.root)\n145:         except ValueError:\n146:             rel = p\n147:         diff = _unified_diff(text, new, rel=rel)\n148:         adds = sum(1 for ln in diff.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\"+\") and not ln.startswith(\"+++\"))\n149:         dels = sum(1 for ln in diff.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\"-\") and not ln.startswith(\"---\"))\n150:         return _result(f\"OK: edited {p} (+{adds} -{dels} lines)\", diff=diff)\n151:     except ValueError as e:\n152:         return _result(f\"ERROR: {e}\", error=True)\n153:     except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n154:         return _result(render(\"errors/write_failed.md\", error=e), error=True)\n155: \n156: \n157: def _unified_diff(old: str, new: str, rel: str | Path) -> str:\n158:     \"\"\"Return a unified diff string between old and new file contents.\"\"\"\n159:     old_lines = old.splitlines(keepends=True)\n160:     new_lines = new.splitlines(keepends=True)\n161:     diff_lines = list(difflib.unified_diff(old_lines, new_lines, fromfile=f\"a/{rel}\", tofile=f\"b/{rel}\", n=3))\n162:     return \"\".join(diff_lines)\n163: \n164: \n165: def grep(workspace: Workspace, config: Config, pattern: str, path: str = \".\", include: str = \"\") -> dict:\n166:     try:\n167:         hits = workspace.grep(pattern, path=path, include=include or None)\n168:     except re.error as e:\n169:         return _result(f\"ERROR: invalid regex: {e}\", error=True)\n170:     except ValueError as e:\n171:         return _result(f\"ERROR: {e}\", error=True)\n172:     except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n173:         return _result(f\"ERROR: {e}\", error=True)\n174:     if not hits:\n175:         return _result(\"(no matches)\")\n176:     lines: list[str] = []\n177:     current: str | None = None\n178:     for fpath, lineno, text in hits:\n179:         if current != fpath:\n180:             if current is not None:\n181:                 lines.append(\"\")\n182:             current = fpath\n183:             lines.append(f\"{fpath}:\")\n184:         lines.append(f\"  Line {lineno}: {text[:300]}\")\n185:     content = \"\\n\".join(lines)\n186:     if len(hits) >= 100:\n187:         content += \"\\n\\n(Results capped at 100; use a more specific pattern or path.)\"\n188:     return _result(content)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789871270.272258, "id": "6bfc297033ce", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_c05011ec781e46ed9c41fc71", "name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"limit\":30,\"offset\":75,\"path\":\"agent/events.py\"}"}, {"id": "call_8c417be11a7e4317a8b4bafb", "name": "grep", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"agent/server.py\",\"pattern\":\"asdict|ToolResultEvent|sse|_SSE\"}"}], "reasoning": "Now I have the exact return values:\n\n- `read_file`: `content` = whole file text (or directory listing, or error). No diff.\n- `write_file`: `content` = one summary line `OK: wrote p (+N -M lines)` or `OK: wrote p (N chars)`; `diff` = full unified diff of the change.\n- `edit_file`: `content` = `OK: edited p (+N -M lines)`; `diff` = unified diff.\n\nSo the answer to the user's question:\n- The collapsible code list you see for read: yes, that's `content` (the file text).\n- For write/edit: the code you see in the collapsible panel is NOT `content` — it's the separate `diff` field. `content` is just one short summary line. The model receives only the summary line; the UI separately renders `diff`.\n\nAlso there's the \"call\" side: the tool call arguments (e.g. write_file's `content` argument — the new file text the model generates) stream via ToolCallDeltaEvent — the UI can show those in the tool row too. That's outgoing data (model → tool), separate from the result dict.\n\nLet me also verify how the UI gets these — server.py SSE serialization of ToolResultEvent. Let me check events.py ToolResultEvent fields and how it's serialized to the frontend, to be able to say \"the frontend receives content + is_error + diff as separate fields\". Let me quickly grep events.py around L97 and see the dataclass fields, and maybe check server.py's event serialization.\n\nActually let me check events.py L90-105 and how the SSE layer serializes events (asdict?)."}
