{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789871276.1184335, "id": "a5caaa518e67", "tool_call_id": "call_90cada6b076e4cbfa1fb029b", "content": "539:     def _write_sse(self, ev: Event, offset: int | None = None) -> None:\n540:         \"\"\"Emit one SSE event; with ``offset`` the payload is {offset, event} (the\n541:         lazy replay/open wire shape), otherwise the bare event JSON. event_to_json\n542:         already returns a serialized string, so only the wrapped shape is\n543:         re-serialized (no double encoding).\"\"\"\n544:         if offset is not None:\n545:             payload = json.dumps({\"offset\": offset, \"event\": json.loads(event_to_json(ev))})\n546:         else:\n547:             payload = event_to_json(ev)\n548:         self.wfile.write(f\"data: {payload}\\n\\n\".encode())\n549:         self.wfile.flush()\n550: \n551:     def _write_sse_raw(self, obj: dict) -> None:\n552:         self.wfile.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(obj)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n553:         self.wfile.flush()\n... (showing lines 539-553 of 856; use offset=554 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789871320.3669872, "id": "4aaacfbf2ce1", "content": "不是全在 `content` 里。你看到的折叠代码列表，取自**两个不同的字段**，而且 write/edit 的代码根本不在 `content` 里。逐个拆开看代码。\n\n## read_file：是的，全在 `content`\n\n`filesystem.py` L51-56：文件文本（超出 `read_max_chars` 就截断并附上 \"use offset=N to continue\" 提示）整个塞进 `content`，`diff` 为空。UI 折叠列表里那段带行号的代码，就是这个字段。\n\n## write_file / edit_file：代码在另一个字段 `diff` 里\n\n看 `filesystem.py` write_file 的返回（L103-107）：\n\n```python\ndiff = _unified_diff(old, content, rel=rel)          # 统一 diff 文本\n...\nsummary = f\"OK: wrote {p} (+{adds} -{dels} lines)\" ...\nreturn _result(summary, diff=diff)\n```\n\n`edit_file` 同样（L147-150）：`return _result(f\"OK: edited {p} (+{adds} -{dels} lines)\", diff=diff)`。\n\n所以一次写入的返回 dict 实际是：\n\n```python\n{\n    \"content\": \"OK: wrote agent/loop.py (+3 -1 lines)\",   # 只有这一行摘要\n    \"error\": False,\n    \"diff\": \"diff --git a/agent/loop.py b/agent/loop.py\\n--- a/...\\n+ 新增的行\\n- 删掉的行\\n...\"\n}\n```\n\n两个字段的用途在 `events.py` L100-102 的注释里写得非常明确：\n\n```python\ncontent: str = \"\"  # model-visible content\ndiff: str = \"\"     # unified diff (UI display only, not model-visible)\n```\n\n- **`content`**：给**模型**看的。写文件给模型看的只是一行摘要（`OK: wrote ... (+3 -1 lines)`），不是整个文件——`context.py` L80 构造 `role=tool` 消息时只带这个字段，这样不会因为写了个大文件就把上下文撑爆。\n- **`diff`**：给 **UI** 看的。你折叠面板里那段红绿代码就是它（difflib 的 unified diff），模型完全看不到。\n\n前端能拿到这两个字段，是因为事件整颗序列化：`server.py` L539-548 的 `_write_sse` 把 `ToolResultEvent` 整个 dataclass 转 JSON 发给浏览器，`content`、`is_error`、`diff` 是**三个并列的 JSON 字段**，不是揉在 content 里的。\n\n## 还有第三路：调用参数的流式显示\n\n写入类工具的折叠面板其实可能显示三样东西，第三样来自**调用侧**而不是结果侧：\n\n`events.py` L82-88 `ToolCallDeltaEvent` 的 docstring：\n\n> the model's tool-call arguments arrive as a stream of deltas ... The UI renders these live so the user watches e.g. a write_file content being produced instead of waiting for the finished result.\n\n模型生成 `write_file` 的参数时（参数里的 `content` 就是要写入的全文），这些参数边生成边以 delta 事件流给 UI——你看到“正在写出的代码”走的是这条流。它跟工具的返回 dict 是两个方向的数据，互不相干。\n\n## 汇总\n\n| 你看到的 | 数据来自 | 谁能看到 |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| read 折叠面板里的文件代码 | 返回 dict 的 `content` | 模型 + UI |\n| write/edit 折叠面板里的红绿 diff | 返回 dict 的 `diff` | 只有 UI |\n| write/edit 行摘要（`OK: wrote ...`） | 返回 dict 的 `content` | 模型 + UI |\n| 正在流式生成的写入内容 | `ToolCallDeltaEvent`（调用参数） | 只有 UI（live 显示，不持久化） |\n\n## 对上次重构方案的影响：零\n\n`diff` 和 `content` 一样，是返回 dict 里的一个普通 `str` 字段，子进程边界上被同一个 `json.dumps` / `json.loads` 原样搬运，UI 照常拿到完整 diff。方案不需要为它加任何东西。\n\n顺带一个呼应：正因为 write_file 的**入参**（新文件全文）可能很大，上次方案里才坚持参数走 stdin 的 JSON 而不是 Windows 命令行——命令行有 32K 上限，一个稍大的文件就装不下了；stdin 流式写入没有这个限制。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "`event_to_json` serializes the whole event dataclass — so the frontend receives `tool_result` events with `content`, `is_error`, `diff` as three separate JSON fields. The frontend then renders:\n- the tool row's collapsible result: for read_file, `content` (the file text); for write/edit, `diff` (the unified diff, rendered as a code diff view). The `content` one-liner (\"OK: wrote ... +3 -1 lines\") shows as the row summary line.\n- The call side (arguments streaming) comes via tool_call_delta events — e.g., write_file's args include the new file content, which the UI may show live.\n\nI have everything to answer now. The question: \"但例如read和write都会有带有代码的折叠列表，它们的内容也都在content中吗\" — Do the contents of the collapsible code lists for read and write all live in `content`?\n\nAnswer: No. Precisely:\n\n1. **read_file**: yes — the collapsible code = `content` field (file text / directory listing / truncated text with offset hint). `diff` empty.\n\n2. **write_file / edit_file**: no — two different pieces:\n   - The collapsible code block you see (green/red diff view) = the `diff` field, a unified diff built by `_unified_diff` (filesystem.py L157-162). \n   - `content` = only one summary line: `OK: wrote path (+3 -1 lines)` / `OK: edited path (+3 -1 lines)` (L106-107, L150). This one-liner is what the model sees; the diff is explicitly marked \"UI display only, not model-visible\" (events.py L102).\n   \n3. There's also the call side: what the model *sends* (write_file's `content` argument = the new file text) streams to the UI via ToolCallDeltaEvent (events.py L82-93, docstring says the UI renders live so the user watches a write_file content being produced). That's a third channel, separate from the result dict entirely.\n\nSo the \"折叠列表\" draws from up to three places depending on tool:\n- read: result `content`\n- write/edit: result `diff` (code view) + result `content` (the summary line) + optionally the streamed arguments (what was written)\n\nWire shape to the frontend: SSE `tool_result` event with three separate fields (content, is_error, diff) — `_write_sse` serializes the whole event dataclass (server.py L539-548), not just content.\n\nTie back to the refactor question (implicit: does the subprocess change affect this?):\n- `diff` is a plain str in the same returned dict → JSON round-trip safe, covered by the same contract. cli.py's stdout JSON carries both keys; nothing extra needed.\n- One nuance worth stating: the JSON payload in stdin (for write_file) contains the full new file content as an argument — size is fine (stdin streaming, no 32K limit) — that was the reason for choosing stdin.\n- Another nuance: `content` for read is capped by read_max_chars (20K default) — so the collapsible list shows up to that much; truncation text is part of content.\n\nAlso note doom detection uses content only — for write/edit the model-visible content is the summary line, so a repeated identical edit with same summary... actually result content differs by path/line counts. Not asked; skip.\n\nKeep the answer focused and plain: answer the yes/no first, then the exact split with code citations, a small table, and one line on the refactor implication. No preaching."}
