{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789872418.8333855, "id": "ed7c8152b107", "tool_call_id": "call_457259b9c59c44e9a65ebf78", "content": "1: \"\"\"Transport: run a shell command against the environment the agent works in.\n2: \n3: Local now (subprocess); SSH (via the exec bridge) comes with the degradation\n4: layer. The workspace keeps exactly one handle on the environment, so tools stay\n5: transport-agnostic.\n6: \n7: Every run takes a ``cancel`` event (Stop): both transports poll it while the\n8: command is in flight and kill the command tree within ~0.2s of it being set —\n9: a Stop must not have to wait out a long build. Local kills the whole tree\n10: (POSIX process group / Windows ``taskkill /T``); remote abandons the bridge\n11: wait (the bridge's own deadline reaps the remote exec).\n12: \"\"\"\n13: \n14: from __future__ import annotations\n15: \n16: import base64\n17: import json\n18: import os\n19: import signal\n20: import subprocess\n21: import threading\n22: import time\n23: import urllib.error\n24: import urllib.request\n25: from abc import ABC, abstractmethod\n26: from typing import Any, NamedTuple\n27: \n28: from .localshell import local_shell\n29: \n30: # how often an in-flight run re-checks its deadline and the Stop event\n31: _CANCEL_POLL = 0.15\n32: \n33: \n34: class CommandResult(NamedTuple):\n35:     code: int\n36:     stdout: str\n37:     stderr: str\n38: \n39: \n40: class TransportError(RuntimeError):\n... (showing lines 1-40 of 242; use offset=41 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
