{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789872418.8476825, "id": "f37f5ce328c4", "tool_call_id": "call_f0c2c9bd16f14fb28e5f4034", "content": "1: \"\"\"Windows local-shell adaptation: ONE shell decision, every consumer agrees.\n2: \n3: localshell decides which shell local run_command text executes under (the\n4: host's POSIX sh / a detected Git Bash / cmd.exe). These tests PIN that decision\n5: (reset_cache) and verify every consumer follows it:\n6: \n7:   - split_command                    tokenizer flavor (backslash + quoting rules)\n8:   - LocalTransport.run               spawn shape (argv vs shell=True, utf-8 decode)\n9:   - shell.run_command/_blocked_reason  unparseable-command guard + REPL lexer\n10:   - PermissionEvaluator.escaped_paths  flavor comes from the WORKSPACE, so a\n11:                                      remote (SSH) workspace tokenizes POSIX even\n12:                                      on a host pinned to cmd\n13:   - context.derive_messages          the local-environment hint (and its absence\n14:                                      on posix-sh / remote workspaces)\n15:   - supervisor._SafeStdStream        the no-fcntl (Windows) stdio degradation\n16: \n17: Run: uv run python3 -m tests.local_shell_test\n18: \"\"\"\n19: \n20: from __future__ import annotations\n21: \n22: import io\n23: import subprocess\n24: import tempfile\n25: import threading\n26: import time\n27: \n28: from tests.testsupport import check\n29: \n30: from agent.config import Config\n31: from agent.core.context import derive_messages\n32: from agent.core.lazy import LazyEventLog\n33: from agent.core.permission import PermissionEvaluator\n34: from agent.supervisor import _SafeStdStream\n35: from agent.tools import shell as shell_mod\n36: from agent.tools.localshell import LocalShell, local_shell, reset_cache, split_command\n37: from agent.tools.transport import LocalTransport\n38: from agent.tools.workspace import LocalWorkspace, RemoteWorkspace\n39: \n40: # pinned decisions (argv here is never spawned except in the recorder test,\n41: # which intercepts subprocess.Popen)\n42: POSIX = LocalShell(argv=None, posix=True, name=\"posix-sh\")\n43: BASH = LocalShell(argv=(r\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe\", \"-c\"), posix=True, name=\"bash\")\n44: CMD = LocalShell(argv=None, posix=False, name=\"cmd\")\n45: \n46: \n47: def test_split_command() -> None:\n48:     # ---- 1. explicit flavors: the two tokenizers ----\n49:     check(split_command(\"echo 'a b'\", posix=True) == [\"echo\", \"a b\"], \"posix: single quotes group\")\n50:     check(\n51:         split_command(r\"echo C:\\Users\", posix=True) == [\"echo\", \"C:Users\"],\n52:         \"posix: unquoted backslash is an escape (shlex eats it)\",\n53:     )\n54:     check(\n55:         split_command(r'type \"C:\\Program Files\\x.txt\"', posix=False)\n56:         == [\"type\", r\"C:\\Program Files\\x.txt\"],\n57:         \"cmd: quoted backslash path survives intact\",\n58:     )\n59:     check(\n60:         split_command(r\"type C:\\Users\\x.txt\", posix=False) == [\"type\", r\"C:\\Users\\x.txt\"],\n... (showing lines 1-60 of 327; use offset=61 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789872428.469659, "id": "f8421884e893", "content": "确认完毕：`transport.py` 不反向导入 registry（无循环导入）、`_protected` 在基类 `__init__` 初始化、测试用 `tests.testsupport.check`。看一下测试的运行骨架：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_ab8fef42d7f54fc7bbbb0efb", "name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"tests/testsupport.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "Confirmed:\n- transport.py has no import from registry → no cycle if registry imports transport. ✓\n- `_protected` initialized at workspace.py L113 in base Workspace `__init__`. ✓\n- Classes: `Workspace(ABC)` L101, `LocalWorkspace` L313, `RemoteWorkspace` L443. ✓\n- `agent/tools/__init__.py` is just a docstring — no import side effects. ✓\n- Test style: modules with `test_xxx()` functions using `check(cond, msg)` from `tests.testsupport`, docstring header with \"Run: ...\". Let me peek at the end of a test file to see the main runner pattern (how tests get invoked — probably a `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` that calls all test functions, or testsupport has a runner).\n\nLet me check tests/testsupport.py for `check` and the runner pattern."}
