{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789872708.2439678, "id": "04d80c4e16df", "content": "全部通过。存一条项目记忆，然后总结：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_9d91285b453a4104bebb76b4", "name": "save_memory", "arguments": "{\"title\":\"Tool subprocess execution refactor shipped (pilot: read_file)\",\"content\":\"Refactor shipped: tool execution unified behind an opt-in subprocess path. `Tool.subprocess: bool = False` field on the registry dataclass; `ToolRegistry.execute` routes to `_exec_subprocess` when `tool.subprocess AND not frozen AND isinstance(workspace, LocalWorkspace)` (remote/frozen fall back to in-process). New `agent/tools/cli.py`: reads one JSON payload from stdin `{name, args, workspace_root, mode, read_max_chars, protected[]}`, rebuilds Config+LocalWorkspace, re-applies protect() from the parent's `workspace.protected()` snapshot (new 3-line method on base Workspace), calls the same tool func, prints the {content, error, diff} dict as JSON on stdout (exit 0 whenever JSON was produced; parent trusts JSON not exit code). Platform rules baked in: binary pipes (no text=True — Windows newline translation), payload via stdin (no argv 32K/GBK issues), `start_new_session=os.name == \\\"posix\\\"` (MANDATORY — without it _kill_tree's killpg would kill the agent's own process group), PYTHONUTF8=1 env for child tracebacks, frozen builds never route to subprocess (sys.executable isn't python). read_file is the first migrated tool (`subprocess=True` pilot). Memory tools (save/load/search) are closures over MemoryStore — never migrated. New `tests/toolcli_test.py` (11 checks incl. cancel tree-kill in ~0.5s, skipped on bash-less hosts via posix_shell_argv()). Regression green: toolcli_test, local_shell_test, selfcheck, server_test full, websearch_test. Downstream (loop.py/PermissionGate/doom-loop/events/{content,error,diff} contract) untouched — diff field is UI-only, content is model-visible.\"}"}], "reasoning": "All green. Save a project memory about this refactor (durable fact for future sessions), then write the final summary."}
