nder, save, status)\n\n**tests:** mcpbackend_test.py (delete). Also check websearch_test.py / server_test.py / settings-mirror.test.js for MCP references — grep showed only mcpbackend_test.py in tests. Wait, the grep output for tests only showed mcpbackend_test.py. But server_test full does settings tests — settings-mirror.test.js? No hits for (?i)mcp there per grep. Good. But `tests/server_test.py` might POST settings with mcp_services? grep says no.\n\n**README.md:** need to check for MCP mentions.\n**prompts:** agent/prompts/tools/web_search.md — the web_search description includes backends list dynamically (`available_backends`); check the md for MCP wording.\n**eval/, scripts/, dist/:** check for MCP mentions.\n\nAlso the root scratch files: scratch-launch-tests.py, scratch-relaunch-tests.py, scratch_loop_test.log, scratch_ls.log, scratch_rp.log, scratch_server_test.log, scratch_supervisor_test.log, fix.clc, net_fix.clc, win-clutch.clc — these are \"多余文件\" candidates but NOT MCP-related. The .clc files are project/session files (win-clutch.clc might be an actual project file for this repo opened as a project! deleting would lose memory — NO, don't touch .clc). scratch-* files are likely temporary debris from earlier sessions. I'll list them and let the user decide — or actually the user asked me to \"检查是否有多余的文件\" — I should check and report. For scratch logs/scripts, they're clearly scratch; but deleting things not asked... The user asked to check — I'll report them as candidates with a recommendation, and can delete on confirmation. Hmm, or given the instruction \"检查是否有多余的文件\" it's arguably authorization to clean obvious junk. But scratch-launch-tests.py might be referenced by something? Let me check if referenced anywhere (git-tracked?). Let me check git status to see what's tracked — if tracked, they were committed intentionally at some point. If untracked, they're local debris and safe-ish to flag.\n\nLet me also check: eval/, scripts/, dist/ for mcp; README; prompts.\n\nThen do the removal. Order:\n1. Read the exact regions in server.py, websearch.py, app.js, index.html to cut cleanly.\n2. Delete 3 files (rm via run_command).\n3. Edit config.py, server.py, websearch.py, app.js, index.html.\n4. Check README/prompts.\n5. Run regressions: selfcheck, websearch_test, server_test full, toolcli_test, local_shell_test.\n\nLet me continue the inventory: grep (?i)mcp in README.md, agent/prompts, eval, scripts, dist, pyproject.toml. And git status for tracked state of the 3 files + scratch files."}
