not any((base_url, model, api_key))\n            and \"reasoning_effort\" not in body\n            and services is None\n        ):\n```\n→\n```\n        api_key = (body.get(\"api_key\") or \"\").strip()\n        if not any((base_url, model, api_key)) and \"reasoning_effort\" not in body:\n```\n\n**Edit 4 — settings_post services save + legacy keys** (L363-377):\n```\n            # empty value clears the knob (provider default); None = unset\n            if \"reasoning_effort\" in body:\n                self._cfg.llm_reasoning_effort = reasoning_effort or None\n            if services is not None:\n                self._cfg.mcp_services = services\n        # flatten migrates legacy profile maps but only knows the LLM fields.\n        # Untouched services: carry the legacy mcp_<name> URL keys across so a\n        # plain save never wipes configured web services. A posted mcp_services\n        # list replaces everything — legacy keys die here so a deleted service\n        # cannot resurrect from its pre-migration key.\n        saved = flatten_settings(load_settings())\n        if services is None:\n            saved.update(_mcp_keys_from(load_settings()))\n        else:\n            saved[\"mcp_services\"] = services\n        if base_url:\n```\n→\n```\n            # empty value clears the knob (provider default); None = unset\n            if \"reasoning_effort\" in body:\n                self._cfg.llm_reasoning_effort = reasoning_effort or None\n        # flatten migrates legacy profile maps but only knows the LLM fields\n        saved = flatten_settings(load_settings())\n        if base_url:\n```\n\n**Edit 5 — settings_get mcp_services** (L394-404):\n```\n        saved = flatten_settings(load_settings())\n        services = _parse_mcp_services(self._cfg.mcp_services)[0]\n        self._json(\n            {\n                \"base_url\": self._cfg.base_url or saved.get(\"base_url\", \"\"),\n                \"model\": self._cfg.model or saved.get(\"model\", \"\"),\n                \"reasoning_effort\": self._cfg.llm_reasoning_effort or saved.get(\"reasoning_effort\", \"\"),\n                \"has_api_key\": bool(self._state.api_key or self._cfg.api_key or saved.get(\"api_key\")),\n                # MCP web-search services: the records this server actually\n                # runs, for the settings UI to render and round-trip\n                \"mcp_services\": [s.record() for s in services],\n            }\n        )\n```\n→\n```\n        saved = flatten_settings(load_settings())\n        self._json(\n            {\n                \"base_url\": self._cfg.base_url or saved.get(\"base_url\", \"\"),\n                \"model\": self._cfg.model or saved.get(\"model\", \"\"),\n                \"reasoning_effort\": self._cfg.llm_reasoning_effort or saved.get(\"reasoning_effort\", \"\"),\n                \"has_api_key\": bool(self._state.api_key or self._cfg.api_key or saved.get(\"api_key\")),\n            }\n        )\n```\n\n**Edit 6 — _mcp_status method** (L408-433 + blank):\n```\n    def _mcp_status(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Per-service MCP reachability + login state, for the settings modal.\n\n        Purely informational and only about services this machine's user chose\n        to configure: unconfigured services report configured=False and the UI\n        leaves the row blank — nothing here suggests installing anything.\n        \"\"\"\n        out = []\n        for s in _parse_mcp_services(self._cfg.mcp_services)[0]:\n            row: dict[str, Any] = {\n                \"name\": s.name,\n                \"configured\": bool(s.url),\n                \"enabled\": s.enabled,\n                \"reachable\": None,\n                \"login\": None,\n            }\n            if s.url:\n                try:\n                    state = _mcp_status_probe(s.url, s) if s.status_tool else None\n                    row[\"reachable\"] = True\n                    row[\"login\"] = _login_state(state, s.login_field)\n                except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — any failure is a status, not a crash\n                    row[\"reachable\"] = False\n                    row[\"detail\"] = str(e)[:160]\n            out.append(row)\n        self._json({\"services\": out})\n\n    def _permission_respond(self) -> None:\n```\n→\n```\n    def _permission_respond(self) -> None:\n```\n\n**Edit 7 — boot wiring** (L813-815):\n```\n    # MCP web-search services: declarative records in settings.json\n    # (\"mcp_services\"); legacy mcp_<name> URL keys fold in via the preset data\n    config.mcp_services = _mcp_service_records(load_settings())\n    api_key = config.api_key\n```\n→\n```\n    api_key = config.api_key\n```\n\nAfter edits: check leftover references to `_parse_mcp_services`, `_mcp_service_records`, `_mcp_status_probe`, `_login_state`, `load_settings` (still used? `saved = flatten_settings(load_settings())` remains in both handlers, and boot uses load_settings? — L815 was possibly the only boot user, but `saved` at L800ish comes from somewhere — fine, it's used in _settings_post/_settings_get regardless).\n\nAlso `_login_state` helper — defined somewhere in server.py; after removing _mcp_status, is it orphaned? Check with grep and remove if unused.\n\nApply edits 1-4 in one message, then 5-7 in the next (or all 7 at once — they're all verified; batch all 7, results are independent). Let me batch all 7."}
