coercion/execution dispatch — platform-blind\n- `cli.py`: subprocess runner — takes a payload, runs python child; mostly blind (inherits whatever python)\n\nSo the answer:\n\n**管跨平台的（平台差异被消化在这里）**:\n1. `localshell.py` — 专职平台适配：探测可用 POSIX shell（Git Bash/WSL 排除/probe），决定 argv 拆分方言（posix vs windows），产出统一的 `LocalShell` 记录\n2. `transport.py` 里的一小角 — `_kill_tree` 的 os.name 分支（killpg vs taskkill /T）——这是进程树语义的差异，不是命令方言\n\n**不管平台的（平台盲）**:\n- `registry.py`、`filesystem.py`、`websearch.py` — 完全没有平台分支\n- `shell.py` — 严格说是\"平台感知但不适配\"：它问 workspace 要 `posix` 标志并按方言分词/分类，但自己不做任何探测，答案来自 localshell\n- `workspace.py` — 抽象层本体平台盲（把本地/远程、Windows/POSIX 路径都归一化掉），只有它对 transport/localshell 的调用点接触平台\n\nDesign pattern: 平台差异被压到最底两层（localshell + transport 的 kill 分支），上面全部说\"POSIX 方言 + 逻辑路径\"。这就是为什么 filesystem/websearch 里看不到一个 `os.name`。\n\nWhere does exec_shell() come from? workspace.ExecShell presumably wraps localshell.local_shell(). Line 212: `posix = workspace.exec_shell().posix`. Good.\n\nAlso verify claim \"filesystem.py has zero os.name branches\": quick mental check — earlier read of imports: fnmatch/json/os/posixpath/re/tempfile/threading/time for workspace. filesystem.py imports I haven't seen fully. I'll phrase carefully: \"几乎没有/不需要\" or quickly grep os.name in agent/tools. Let me do one grep to be safe — cheap.\n\nActually let me grep `os\\.name|platform\\.|sys\\.platform` across agent/tools to give exact counts — that makes the answer concrete and verifiable."}
