{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789876916.9974768, "id": "ed753df2b966", "content": "核实完毕，你的直觉是对的——我上一张图确实漏了远程这条轴。而且远程方案的答案比“哪些模块参与”更彻底：**远程机器上根本不运行这个项目的任何部分**。\n\n## 远程方案（代号“SSH 降级层”）是怎么做的\n\n`SshTransport` 的文档串写明了设计约束：**\"The remote only needs an sshd (no python, no SFTP, no base64)\"**。一次远程调用的完整链路：\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    T[\"工具<br/>read_file / run_command\"] --> WS[\"RemoteWorkspace<br/>文件操作翻译成 sh 命令\"]\n    WS --> ST[\"SshTransport<br/>HTTP POST /exec\"]\n    ST --> B[\"Electron 桥<br/>本机进程，POST 转成 ssh\"]\n    B --> SSHD[\"远程 sshd<br/>只看到普通 shell 会话\"]\n    SSHD --> SH[\"/bin/sh -c ...<br/>cat / ls / printf\"]\n```\n\n关键事实：\n\n1. **“桥”在客户端**——`bridge_url` 指向本机 Electron 壳开的 HTTP 端点，它把 `POST /exec {\"command\":...}` 翻译成 `ssh host '...'`。远程不需要知道桥的存在。\n2. **文件操作降级为 shell 原语**——`RemoteWorkspace` 把读/写/列表全部翻译成 `cat`、`ls`、`printf '%s'`（分块发送以绕过 sshd 命令长度限制），任何能跑 sshd 的设备都行。\n3. **路径全部用 `PurePosixPath`**——`realpath` 是纯词法归一化，绝不调本地文件系统（文档里记录了一个真实事故：macOS 宿主的 autofs 把远程路径 `/home/...` 改写成了 `/System/Volumes/Data/home/...`）。\n\n## 谁知道远程存在，谁不知道\n\n| 知道远程 | 不知道远程 |\n|---|---|\n| `base.py` 的状态层：`backend_mode`/`bridge_url`/`build_workspace()` 工厂——**唯一的切换点** | `filesystem.py`：拿到的只是 `Workspace`，`read_file` 不知道背后是本地磁盘还是一条 `cat` over ssh |\n| `transport.py` 的 `SshTransport`（边界本身） | `shell.py`：问 `workspace.exec_shell()` 拿“命令该按什么方言解析”，自己不关心答案从哪来 |\n| `workspace.py` 的 `RemoteWorkspace`（翻译层） | `websearch.py`：搜索/抓取**永远从本地机器发 HTTP**，ssh 模式下远程根本不参与 |\n| `browsing.py`：显式 `isinstance(ws, RemoteWorkspace)` 分支 | 权限引擎、prompts、LLM 循环：只处理文本 |\n| `core/lazy.py`/`core/persist.py`/`memory.py`：`.clc` 的远程按区间读/追加 | LLM 客户端、设置存储 |\n| UI 的 `switchBackend` | 远程机器本身：**它不知道自己在当远程工具用**——sshd 只看到又一个登录会话，上面没有任何本项目代码、不需要 Python |\n\n## 你问的“远程服务器上哪些部分不知道自己是远程工具”\n\n答案的字面版本是：**全部**——因为远程上没有任何它的部分。没有伴随进程、没有守护程序、没有解释器要求。远程执行的每一条命令都是普通 POSIX shell 命令，由 sshd 的 exec 通道跑完就退。`RemoteWorkspace` 文档串称之为“degradation layer”的原因正在于此：用能力降级（文件操作退化成 shell 原语）换取零部署。\n\n## 接缝的两处多态\n\n这个架构最巧的是把“本地/远程”藏在**两个同名方法**后面，工具层完全无感：\n\n1. **`build_workspace()` 工厂**（`base.py:82`）：`ssh` 模式给 `RemoteWorkspace`，否则 `LocalWorkspace`——启动时选一次，之后所有工具只看见 `Workspace` 抽象。\n2. **`exec_shell()` 多态**（`workspace.py:221/508`）：`shell.py` 问“命令按什么方言解析”，本地实现回答“看宿主机（Git Bash/cmd）”，远程实现永远回答 `posix=True`——文档原话：\"**even on a Windows machine behind the UI, run_command text parses as POSIX sh on the REMOTE**\"。所以 Windows 本地 + Linux 远程时，同一条命令在本地按 Git Bash 语义审、在远程按 POSIX sh 执行，`shell.py` 对此一无所知。\n\n一个诚实的例外：`registry.py` 的子进程试点里有一行 `isinstance(workspace, LocalWorkspace)`——但它不是适配，而是**卫语句**（子进程会打本地盘，所以远程时禁用子进程执行、回退进程内调用）。\n\n和上一轮的跨平台结论合起来就是完整的二维矩阵：**跨平台差异沉在 `localshell.py`，本地/远程差异沉在 `Workspace` 工厂 + `SshTransport`，其余所有层在这两条轴上都是盲的**。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "Now I have the complete, verified picture. Let me assemble the answer.\n\n**The remote scheme (\"SSH degradation layer\")**:\n\n1. **Nothing is installed on the remote.** SshTransport docstring: \"The remote only needs an sshd (no python, no SFTP, no base64)\". RemoteWorkspace docstring: \"File operations are plain POSIX sh — cat, ls, and `printf '%s'` appends... so any device that can run an sshd shell works.\"\n\n2. **The \"bridge\" is client-side** (Electron shell): SshTransport POSTs `{\"command\",\"timeout\",\"binary\"}` to `bridge_url/exec`; the Electron bridge turns that into an `ssh exec` channel. So the chain is:\n   `tool → workspace.run() → SshTransport.run() → HTTP POST localhost:bridge/exec → Electron bridge → ssh host 'command' → remote sshd → /bin/sh`\n\n3. **Who KNOWS about remote:**\n   - `base.py` AgentState: backend_mode/bridge_url/remote_root + `build_workspace()` factory — the SWITCH\n   - `server.py`: /api/backend endpoint (set_backend), workspace construction (L571)\n   - `transport.py` SshTransport: the boundary (HTTP→ssh)\n   - `workspace.py` RemoteWorkspace: translates file ops to POSIX sh one-liners (cat/ls/printf), PurePosixPath spelling, lexical realpath (never local FS calls), chunked writes for sshd limits\n   - `browsing.py`: isinstance(RemoteWorkspace) branches, direct SshTransport ls\n   - `core/lazy.py`, `core/persist.py`, `memory.py`, `project.py`: .clc range-read/append via bridge\n   - UI app.js: switchBackend/reconciledBackendUrl\n\n4. **Who does NOT know:**\n   - `filesystem.py`, `shell.py`, `websearch.py` tool impls: receive `workspace`, call its methods. read_file doesn't know if it's hitting a local disk or a cat-over-ssh.\n   - `registry.py` executor: passes workspace through; subprocess pilot even explicitly falls back to in-process for non-Local workspaces (`use_child = ... and isinstance(workspace, LocalWorkspace)`) — interesting: registry DOES make one isinstance check, but only as a guard (the child would hit the LOCAL disk), i.e., it knows enough to NOT specialize.\n   - LLM loop, prompts, permission engine (mostly): operate on text\n   - shell.py: asks workspace.exec_shell() — a local decision point that's REMOTE-AWARE through polymorphism: RemoteWorkspace.exec_shell() returns posix=True always (\"even on a Windows machine behind the UI, run_command text parses as POSIX sh on the REMOTE\"). So shell.py itself doesn't know about remote; it just asks the workspace for the parsing flavor. This is the elegant bit: the local/remote difference is hidden behind the same LocalShell record type.\n   \n5. **The remote machine**: doesn't run ANY part of clutch. It receives ordinary `sh -c '...'` commands over sshd's exec channel. It doesn't know it's serving an AI agent — to sshd it's just another shell session. The \"remote parts that don't know they're running as remote tools\" = literally everything on the remote, because nothing of clutch is there: no python needed, no daemon, no SFTP.\n\n6. Design name: \"SSH degradation layer\" (降级方案) — file tools degrade to shell primitives so that any sshd works. All the remote-awareness concentrates in: state factory + RemoteWorkspace + SshTransport + .clc/storage modules. The polymorphic seam is Workspace: build_workspace() picks the class ONCE at workspace creation; tools see only Workspace.\n\nOne nuance: registry's subprocess pilot checks isinstance(workspace, LocalWorkspace) — so registry has a tiny bit of remote awareness (a guard, not adaptation). Worth mentioning honestly since the user asks precisely \"哪些知道、哪些不知道\".\n\nAlso websearch doesn't care at all (HTTP from the LOCAL machine — search/fetch always run locally even in ssh mode; the remote isn't used for web). Worth a line.\n\nDiagram: full remote call chain + know/don't-know table.\n\nMermaid caution: no double quotes inside labels; use subgraph with id + quoted title.\n\nLet me write the final answer in Chinese, well-structured:\n\n1. 远程方案怎么做的（一次调用的完整链路）\n2. 远程机器上跑的是什么（答案：什么都没有——只有 sshd）\n3. 知道远程存在的部分（表格）\n4. 不知道的部分（表格）\n5. 关键设计：接缝在 Workspace 多态 + exec_shell() 多态\n\nThe exec_shell polymorphism is the answer to a subtle part: shell.py is remote-blind because IT ASKS. And L508-513 docstring is gold: \"The remote host runs the POSIX shell stack regardless of the app host's OS: even on a Windows machine behind the UI, run_command text parses as POSIX sh on the REMOTE.\"\n\nKeep it focused and concrete."}
