{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789877012.6043286, "id": "9394e48862a9", "tool_call_id": "call_1b481ede62164ef2981786ca", "content": "ui\\ssh-tunnel.js:\n  Line 2: // process: local forward to the remote supervisor API + reverse forward to the\n  Line 6: const http = require(\"http\");\n  Line 7: const net = require(\"net\");\n  Line 8: const os = require(\"os\");\n  Line 9: const path = require(\"path\");\n  Line 10: const fs = require(\"fs\");\n  Line 11: const { Client } = require(\"ssh2\");\n  Line 12: const { startLlmProxy, stopLlmProxy } = require(\"./llm-proxy\");\n  Line 13: const { startExecBridge, stopExecBridge } = require(\"./exec-bridge\");\n  Line 14: const { platformTag, ensureBundle, ensurePyLibsTar } = require(\"./server-bundle\");\n  Line 16: const LOG_FILE = path.join(os.homedir(), \".clutch\", \"tunnel.log\");\n  Line 17: const REMOTE_API_PORT = 8890;\n  Line 18: const LLM_PROXY_REMOTE_PORT = 8892;\n  Line 19: const CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS = 15000;\n  Line 32: const endListeners = new Set();\n  Line 34: const HEAL_INTERVAL_MS = 15000;\n  Line 36: function tunnelLog(...args) {\n  Line 47: function freePort() {\n  Line 58: function listen(srv, port) {\n  Line 68: function waitForServer(url, timeoutMs) {\n  Line 86: function httpGetBody(url, timeoutMs) {\n  Line 100: async function probeSupervisorShape(base) {\n  Line 109: function defaultKey() {\n  Line 121: function friendlyError(e) {\n  Line 140: function remoteExec(command, timeoutMs = 60000, binary = false) {\n  Line 175: function getSftp() {\n  Line 191: function uploadFile(localPath, remotePath) {\n  Line 200: function checkExec(r) {\n  Line 208: const { exec_chunk_bytes: EXEC_CHUNK_BYTES } = require(\"./transport_defaults.json\");\n  Line 210: function shq(s) {\n  Line 215: function chunkText(s, cap) {\n  Line 236: function uploadFileViaExec(localPath, remotePath, timeoutMs = 120000, exec = remoteExec) {\n  Line 265: const PROBE_CMD = [\n  Line 279: function parseProbe(out) {\n  Line 300: function startCommand(strategy, home) {\n  Line 302:   const args = \"--port \" + REMOTE_API_PORT + \" --idle-timeout 25\";\n  Line 315: function remoteRunningCmd(probe) {\n  Line 317:     return `python3 -c \"import socket;s=socket.socket();s.settimeout(1);s.connect(('127.0.0.1',${REMOTE_API_PORT}));print('UP')\" 2>/dev/null || echo DOWN`;\n  Line 319:   return `(command -v ss >/dev/null && ss -ltn 2>/dev/null | grep -q ':${REMOTE_API_PORT} ' && echo UP) || echo DOWN`;\n  Line 327: function chooseStrategy(probe, localTag = platformTag()) {\n  Line 338: async function installServer(probe, { force, progress } = {}) {\n  Line 465:           \"the remote Clutch supervisor failed to start on port \" + REMOTE_API_PORT +\n  Line 475: function stopServerCmd(strategy) {\n  Line 486: async function stopTunnel() {\n  Line 516: function notifyEnd() {\n  Line 528: function onTunnelEnd(cb) {\n  Line 533: function tunnelStatus() {\n  Line 542: // ---- per-window session forwards ----\n  Line 543: // Each window gets its own forward to its session child's port; all die with the tunnel.\n  Line 546: function openSessionForward(remotePort) {\n  Line 552:           sshClient.forwardOut(\"127.0.0.1\", 0, \"127.0.0.1\", remotePort, (err, stream) => {\n  Line 554:               tunnelLog(\"[session] forwardOut failed: \" + (err && err.message));\n  Line 564:             tunnelLog(`[session] forward 127.0.0.1:${localPort} -> remote :${remotePort}`);\n  Line 586: // Health-check the forward, restart the backend via the tunnel, else tear down.\n  Line 587: async function collectRemoteDiagnostics() {\n  Line 600: async function restartRemoteServer() {\n  Line 608: async function healOnce() {\n  Line 623: function startHealing() {\n  Line 627: function stopHealing() {\n  Line 634: async function connectTunnel({ host, user, port, password }, progress) {\n  Line 689:       if (info.destPort !== LLM_PROXY_REMOTE_PORT) {\n  Line 730:     if (progress) progress(\"forward\");\n  Line 741: // Set up the bidirectional forwards and gate on the health check through the tunnel.\n  Line 742: async function establishForwardAndHealth(localPort) {\n  Line 744:     sshClient.forwardOut(\"127.0.0.1\", 0, \"127.0.0.1\", REMOTE_API_PORT, (err, stream) => {\n  Line 746:         tunnelLog(\"[error] forwardOut failed: \" + (err && err.message));\n  Line 754:   tunnelLog(`[phase] local forward listening 127.0.0.1:${localPort} -> remote 127.0.0.1:${REMOTE_API_PORT}`);\n  Line 755:   sshClient.forwardIn(\"127.0.0.1\", LLM_PROXY_REMOTE_PORT, (err) => {\n  Line 757:       tunnelLog(\"[phase] reverse forward failed: \" + err.message);\n  Line 758:       console.error(\"[tunnel] reverse forward failed:\", err.message);\n  Line 760:       tunnelLog(`[phase] reverse forward requested 127.0.0.1:${LLM_PROXY_REMOTE_PORT} -> client proxy :${llmProxyPort}`);", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789877012.6094801, "id": "1411149281ac", "tool_call_id": "call_972a830e661342b49a818665", "content": "[Clutch push/release conventions + auth reality]\nClutch repo (Ethereal1024/Clutch, public): release flow = focused commits (test:/feat:/fix:/refactor:/chore:) -> chore(release): X.Y.Z bumping VERSION + ui/package.json + ui/package-lock.json (2 spots) -> lightweight tag vX.Y.Z on that commit -> push; .github/workflows/release.yml triggers on v* tags, builds deb/dmg/unsigned-win with bundled PyInstaller backend. Check CI anonymously via api.github.com/repos/Ethereal1024/Clutch/actions/runs. AUTH: origin is now HTTPS (git@github.com SSH is Permission denied (publickey) — the ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 key is NOT registered on GitHub, only user can fix via web settings); credential.helper=manager holds a working github.com PAT for Ethereal1024, so push/fetch just work over HTTPS. Repo has a long-standing commented .gitignore (docs/, .claude/skills/, poll_ci.py etc. stay local); scratch-*.py + scratch_*.log now ignored too. 30s command timeout: run test suites ONE per command (server_test is the slow HTTP+SSE e2e). Tests: .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m tests.X, node tests/foo-test.js.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789877062.7732258, "id": "bbf0fe5f281f", "content": "全部查证完毕。你说得对——我之前只讲了降级层，漏了完整的第二条方案。`ui/ssh-tunnel.js` 里就是它：`installServer`、`restartRemoteServer`、反向隧道。先存档这个修正，再给你完整的双方案图景：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_a4152a235f8640a7a1461e74", "name": "save_memory", "arguments": "{\"title\":\"Two remote schemes: SSH degradation + remote server deploy\",\"content\":\"Clutch has TWO remote schemes (user corrected me for describing only one). (A) SSH degradation layer: full agent runs locally; RemoteWorkspace/SshTransport translate file ops to POSIX sh over the Electron exec-bridge (POST /exec → ssh exec); remote needs nothing but sshd; .clc locking degrades to noclobber+TTL because process and files live on different machines. (B) Remote server deployment (ui/ssh-tunnel.js): ssh2 client probes remote platform, uploads a PyInstaller server bundle (SFTP via getSftp, or uploadFileViaExec chunked), starts remote supervisor on :8890 (--idle-timeout 25); each UI window gets forwardOut to its session child port; LLM reached by REVERSE forward (remote :8892 forwardIn → local llm-proxy, key never leaves the machine, remote api_key placeholder \\\"proxy\\\" per server.py boot); self-healing via healOnce/restartRemoteServer. In (B) the remote agent is a stock LOCAL deployment (LocalWorkspace, kernel file locks) and does not know it is remote — remote-awareness lives only in ui/main.js, ssh-tunnel.js, llm-proxy.js, server-bundle.js and supervisor lifecycle args. Symmetry: (A) agent knows remote / remote knows nothing; (B) agent knows nothing / UI+tunnel know.\"}"}], "reasoning": "Now I have the full picture of the second remote scheme. Key evidence from `ui/ssh-tunnel.js`:\n\n1. **`installServer(probe, ...)`** (L338) — deploys the server bundle to the remote: `platformTag`, `ensureBundle`, `ensurePyLibsTar` from `./server-bundle` — it uploads a **PyInstaller-bundled server** via SFTP (`uploadFile`, `getSftp`) or via exec-chunked upload (`uploadFileViaExec`)!\n2. **`startCommand`** (L300): `python3 agent/supervisor.py --port 8890 --idle-timeout 25` (or the bundled binary) — starts the **supervisor on the remote** at REMOTE_API_PORT=8890\n3. **Forward structure**:\n   - Local forward: `forwardOut` 127.0.0.1:local → remote 127.0.0.1:8890 (supervisor API)\n   - Per-window session forwards: `openSessionForward(remotePort)` — each window gets its own forward to its session child's port\n   - **Reverse forward**: `forwardIn(\"127.0.0.1\", 8892)` — remote :8892 → client's local LLM proxy (`startLlmProxy`) — so the REMOTE agent reaches the LLM API through the user's local machine (\"no remote internet/key needed\")\n4. **`restartRemoteServer` / healOnce** — self-healing: health-check the forward, restart the backend via the tunnel\n5. **exec-bridge.js**: the SAME tunnel's ssh2 client also exposes `remoteExec` as a loopback HTTP bridge for SshTransport — so scheme A rides on the same ssh2 connection when active\n6. supervisor.py docstring (L3-6): \"the supervisor spawns one agent.server child (--port 0...) per session... The window then talks to its child DIRECTLY (locally, or over its own tunnel forward)\"\n7. supervisor.py:32-34: \"(noclobber+TTL remains only for the execBridge-degraded path, where the agent process and the project files live on different machines.)\" — meaning: in the remote-server path, agent process and files live on the SAME machine (normal local semantics).\n\nAnd `probeSupervisorShape` / `chooseStrategy(probe, localTag)` / `parseProbe` — it probes the remote: platform (glibc/musl?), python3 availability, existing install — then picks a bundle strategy (platformTag).\n\nSo the TWO remote schemes:\n\n**方案 A：SSH 降级层（exec bridge / RemoteWorkspace / SshTransport）**\n- agent 全套跑在本地用户机器上\n- 只有文件/命令操作被翻译成 sh 命令送过 ssh exec\n- 远程零部署（只要 sshd）\n- 跨机器的代价：.clc 锁降级为 noclobber+TTL、路径词法化、逐命令 shell 往返\n\n**方案 B：远程部署服务器（tunnel mode）**\n- 通过 ssh2 把 PyInstaller 打包的 server bundle 上传到远程（SFTP 或 exec 分块上传），probe 远程平台选策略\n- 远程跑起 supervisor（:8890），supervisor 在远程 spawn agent.server 会话子进程\n- UI 每窗口一条 forwardOut 到自己的会话子进程端口\n- LLM 反向隧道：远程 :8892 forwardIn → 本地 llm-proxy —— API key 和外网出口都留在本地\n- 远程上的 agent 是**普通本地部署**：LocalWorkspace、POSIX shell、内核文件锁——完全不知道自己是\"远程工具\"\n- 同一条 ssh2 连接顺带把 remoteExec 暴露成本地 loopback 桥（exec-bridge），所以降级模式的 SshTransport 也能复用它\n\nWho knows about scheme B:\n- ui/main.js (session reconcile, kind: \"tunnel\" vs local, fallback logic)\n- ui/ssh-tunnel.js (install/start/forward/heal — the whole scheme lives here)\n- ui/llm-proxy.js (reverse-forward LLM proxy)\n- ui/server-bundle.js (bundle construction, platform tags)\n- supervisor.py (it's the thing deployed; --idle-timeout, self-exit)\n- The app.js UI (connection progress, degraded marker, reconciledBackendUrl)\n\nWho doesn't know:\n- agent/server.py, tools, workspace, loop, LLM client — when running under scheme B they are a stock local deployment. agent/server.py doesn't know if it was spawned by a local supervisor or remote one. (One nuance: server.py L509 \"Reachable only via the local bind or the SSH tunnel\" — bind 127.0.0.1 assumption, not knowledge.)\n- The LLM proxy client-side: llm-proxy.js is local; the remote just sees an env var base_url pointing at 127.0.0.1:8892.\n\nInteresting subtlety: in scheme B, does the remote agent's config get the LLM base_url pointing at the reverse-forward port? llm-proxy.js:4 \"reaches it via the SSH -R tunnel (no remote internet/key needed)\". Yes — the remote session's LLM base_url = http://127.0.0.1:8892 (the remote end of the -R tunnel), and the local llm-proxy injects the real key. That's what server.py L817-821 comment mentioned: \"the client-side proxy injects the real key; the server only needs a placeholder... api_key = 'proxy'\".\n\nAlso the mode names in UI: \"degrade mode\" marker (app.js L1867-1894: \"local agent, remote exec bridge; true = degraded\") vs tunnel sessions. So UI vocabulary: \"tunnel\" = 远程服务器方案；\"degraded\" = SSH 降级方案. Actually both ride on the tunnel connection; \"degrade\" refers to workspace mode. From main.js: tunnel alive but \"supervisorless (degraded host or remote died): fall back to a local session\" — a host without the server deployed → sessions run locally + degraded RemoteWorkspace.\n\nSo the matrix:\n\n| | 方案 A：SSH 降级（exec bridge） | 方案 B：远程部署服务器（tunnel） |\n|---|---|---|\n| agent 代码跑在哪 | 本地用户机 | 远程服务器 |\n| 远程要装什么 | 什么都不装（sshd 即可） | PyInstaller bundle（安装器自动上传+probe） |\n| 文件操作 | 翻译成 sh（cat/ls/printf）over ssh | 本地原生（远程视角全是本地） |\n| .clc 锁 | noclobber+TTL（跨机器降级） | 内核文件锁（同机器） |\n| LLM 访问 | 本地直连 | 远程 via -R 反向隧道到本地 llm-proxy（key 不出本地） |\n| supervisor | 本地 | 远程（:8890，会话子进程 per 窗口） |\n| 失败回退 | — | 远程 supervisor 挂了→restartRemoteServer；无部署→退回本地会话+降级 |\n\nWho knows what:\n- 知道方案 B 存在的：全部在 ui/（main.js、ssh-tunnel.js、exec-bridge.js、llm-proxy.js、server-bundle.js）+ supervisor.py（被部署的对象）+ server.py 的 LLM proxy placeholder 逻辑（\"api_key = 'proxy'\" 那段就是为方案 B 准备的！L817-821: \"the client-side proxy injects the real key; the server only needs a placeholder\"）\n- 不知道的：跑在远程的那套 agent 全家（server/tools/workspace/loop）——它们就是一个普通本地部署。这正好精确回答了用户上一轮的问题：\"安装在远程的服务器哪些部分并不知道自己作为一个远程工具运行\"——**在方案 B 下，远程上的所有部分都不知道**；知道隧道的只有 Electron 侧和 supervisor 的生命周期参数。\n\nAnd the beautiful symmetry: 方案 A 里 agent 知道远程存在（RemoteWorkspace 显式分支），远程不知道 agent；方案 B 里 agent 不知道自己远程（普通本地部署），UI/隧道知道。两条方案是同一枚硬币的两面。\n\nEvidence for server.py L817-821: earlier read showed:\n```\n    api_key = config.api_key\n    if args.base_url and not api_key:\n        # the client-side proxy injects the real key; the server only needs a\n        # placeholder. No env fallback: the key comes from the UI settings\n        # (state.api_key) or an explicit config.api_key.\n        api_key = \"proxy\"\n```\nYes — that's for the tunneled remote server whose base_url points at the reverse-forward proxy.\n\nI have enough verified evidence. Should I check llm-proxy.js quickly to confirm the key injection? The header comment said \"reaches it via the SSH -R tunnel (no remote internet/key needed). Honors the...\" — good enough.\n\nAlso should I save a memory? The user corrected my understanding: there are TWO remote schemes. My previous answer only knew scheme A. This is a durable architecture fact worth remembering. Let me save a compact memory about the two remote schemes.\n\nThen write the final answer with a diagram showing both schemes, the know/don't-know matrix, and the design symmetry.\n\nMermaid: careful with quotes in labels. Use subgraph with id + quoted title, no nested double quotes."}
