{"title": "Two remote schemes: SSH degradation + remote server deploy", "content": "Clutch has TWO remote schemes (user corrected me for describing only one). (A) SSH degradation layer: full agent runs locally; RemoteWorkspace/SshTransport translate file ops to POSIX sh over the Electron exec-bridge (POST /exec → ssh exec); remote needs nothing but sshd; .clc locking degrades to noclobber+TTL because process and files live on different machines. (B) Remote server deployment (ui/ssh-tunnel.js): ssh2 client probes remote platform, uploads a PyInstaller server bundle (SFTP via getSftp, or uploadFileViaExec chunked), starts remote supervisor on :8890 (--idle-timeout 25); each UI window gets forwardOut to its session child port; LLM reached by REVERSE forward (remote :8892 forwardIn → local llm-proxy, key never leaves the machine, remote api_key placeholder \"proxy\" per server.py boot); self-healing via healOnce/restartRemoteServer. In (B) the remote agent is a stock LOCAL deployment (LocalWorkspace, kernel file locks) and does not know it is remote — remote-awareness lives only in ui/main.js, ssh-tunnel.js, llm-proxy.js, server-bundle.js and supervisor lifecycle args. Symmetry: (A) agent knows remote / remote knows nothing; (B) agent knows nothing / UI+tunnel know.", "updated": 1789877062.778673}
