a sb, cfg, **kw: filesystem.read_file(sb, cfg, **kw)`\n- cli.py `_run(payload: dict)` — subprocess execution with a payload dict\n- `_exec_subprocess(workspace, config, name, args, cancel)`\n\nTo answer thoroughly and accurately, I should look at:\n1. How the prompt/tools are rendered for the model (prompts.py render? registry builds tool descriptions?)\n2. How the model's tool-call output is parsed (the LLM client? base.py loop?)\n3. `_coerce_types` in registry.py\n4. The dispatch in execute()\n5. _exec_subprocess payload\n\nLet me grep for the relevant pieces:\n- `_coerce_types` in registry.py\n- How tools are presented to the model (grep \"parameters\" or the prompt template)\n- Where execute() is called from (base.py loop? agent loop)\n- How the model's response is parsed into name+args (maybe in llm client or base.py)\n\nLet me do parallel greps."}
