{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789879064.2796211, "id": "d186beb0930f", "tool_call_id": "call_534886fc6ab344bd86de075e", "content": "324:     def shell_path(self, token: str) -> str:\n325:         \"\"\"Windows + Git Bash: translate the POSIX scratch spellings the agent\n326:         writes (`> /tmp/out.log 2>&1`, `2> /dev/null`, `head -c 8 /dev/urandom`)\n327:         to what bash itself resolves them to — /tmp is %TEMP% under MSYS\n328:         (`cygpath -w /tmp`), /dev/null is the NUL device, and the REST of the\n329:         POSIX scratch surface (/dev/* device nodes, /var/tmp) is MSYS-internal,\n330:         so it is mapped into the host scratch dir too. Without this the verdict\n331:         engine joins the token with ntpath instead, lands on `C:\\\\tmp\\\\out.log`\n332:         or `C:\\\\dev\\\\urandom`, and rejects an ordinary redirect as a workspace\n333:         escape — which it is not on the POSIX side, where all those dirs are\n334:         scratch. Only reached when the local shell is the POSIX flavor: under\n335:         cmd.exe the very same token is a drive-relative path and must be judged\n336:         literally.\"\"\"\n337:         if os.name != \"nt\" or not local_shell().posix:\n338:             return token\n339:         tmp = tempfile.gettempdir()\n340:         if token == \"/dev/null\":\n341:             return os.devnull\n342:         tail = posix_scratch_tail(token)\n343:         if tail is None:\n344:             # not scratch — or a `..` climbed back out of it (an escape on\n345:             # POSIX too): judge the token as the host would, so it stays one\n... (showing lines 324-345 of 715; use offset=346 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789879064.2843807, "id": "a2b733339ed1", "tool_call_id": "call_8af2442ca3394bbeba62985b", "content": "185:     def shell_path(self, token: str) -> str:\n186:         \"\"\"The local path a SHELL token denotes (identity by default).\n187: \n188:         Command text is parsed by the shell, not by us, so its spelling can\n189:         denote something the host's own path rules never produce: on Windows\n190:         under Git Bash (the POSIX flavor the agent speaks) `/tmp` IS %TEMP% and\n191:         `/dev/null` IS the NUL device — both as harmless as on Linux. Everyone\n192:         who reasons about command TEXT (the permission engine's escape parser,\n193:         the shell guard's token rejection) asks here, so the verdict follows the\n194:         shell that will run the text instead of guessing from the OS. A tool's\n... (showing lines 185-194 of 715; use offset=195 to continue)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789879105.0142176, "id": "c0abd5604b58", "content": "对，但「同一套」要说精确：**统一的是命令语言方言和安全审判逻辑（POSIX），不是底层执行管道**。适配的设计目标就是让 agent 只会说一种方言——代码注释里原话 \"the agent speaks POSIX\"（transport.py:110）。分三层看：\n\n## 第一层：真正统一的部分（面向模型和审判）\n\n平台决策只有一个点，探测到 Git Bash 后 Windows 就挂上 POSIX 标记：\n\n```python\n# agent/tools/localshell.py:76-85\ndef _detect() -> LocalShell:\n    if os.name != \"nt\":\n        return LocalShell(argv=None, posix=True, name=\"posix-sh\")\n    ...\n    if _probe_bash(cand):\n        return LocalShell(argv=(cand, \"-c\"), posix=True, name=\"bash\")   # ← posix=True\n    return LocalShell(argv=None, posix=False, name=\"cmd\")\n```\n\n而方言判定**只**看这个标记，不看操作系统：\n\n```python\n# agent/tools/shell.py:210-212\n# the flavor of the shell that will PARSE this text: local host's decision\n# for local workspaces, always POSIX for a remote (SSH) workspace\nposix = workspace.exec_shell().posix\n```\n\n所以模型写的命令文本、`classify_command` 安全分类、`split_command`（shlex）拆词、路径越界审判——Linux 和 Win+Git Bash 走的是**同一套代码路径**，零分叉。\n\n## 第二层：形式不同、语义等价的执行管道\n\n```python\n# agent/tools/transport.py:124-126\nproc = subprocess.Popen(\n    [*shell.argv, command] if shell.argv else command,\n    shell=shell.argv is None,\n```\n\n| | Linux | Windows + Git Bash |\n|---|---|---|\n| spawn 方式 | `Popen(cmd, shell=True)` | `Popen([bash.exe, \"-c\", cmd])` |\n| 实际解析器 | `/bin/sh -c` | Git Bash 的 `bash.exe -c` |\n| 方言 | POSIX | POSIX（同一套） |\n\n语义等价：同一行文本、同一套引号/管道/重定向规则。（一个有趣的细节：Linux 上是 `/bin/sh`——在 Debian 系其实是 dash，Windows 上反而是**真 bash**，所以 Windows 侧对 bashisms 的容忍度其实更高。）\n\n## 第三层：真实的平台差异，被适配层吸收、不外漏\n\n这些是「同一套」承诺之下垫着的平台补丁，全部封在 transport/workspace/localshell 三个适配文件里，`shell.py` 的业务逻辑看不到它们：\n\n| 差异 | POSIX 实现 | Windows 实现 | 位置 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 杀进程树 | `start_new_session` + `os.killpg(SIGKILL)` | `taskkill /PID x /T /F` 走树杀 | transport.py:83-99 |\n| 输出解码 | 默认 | 固定 `utf-8/replace`（否则中文 Windows 按 GBK 解出乱码） | transport.py:112-113, 172-176 |\n| 命令里的路径审判 | `/tmp` 就是 scratch | `/tmp`→`%TEMP%`、`/dev/null`→NUL（跟随 MSYS 的映射视角） | workspace.py:324-338 |\n| bash 来源 | 系统自带 | `CLUTCH_BASH` 环境变量 → 5 个标准安装路径 → `which`，且须通过 `bash -c echo` 实测探针，WSL 的 System32\\bash.exe 刻意排除 | localshell.py:49-57, 80-96 |\n\n## 两个不成立「同一套」的例外\n\n1. **Windows 上探测不到可用 bash** → 落到 `posix=False, name=\"cmd\"`：cmd.exe 执行、CommandLineToArgvW 方言拆词审判。整条 POSIX 承诺只在这个降级分支失效。\n2. **远程 SSH workspace** → 无条件 POSIX（shell.py:210 注释 \"always POSIX for a remote\"），此时与本地主机是什么系统无关。\n\n## 结论\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    M[\"模型写命令文本\"] --> Q[\"shell.py:212<br/>问 exec_shell().posix\"]\n    Q -->|True| P[\"一套 POSIX 逻辑:<br/>shlex 拆词 + 分类 + 越界审判\"]\n    Q -->|False| C[\"cmd 降级分支<br/>(无 bash 时才走)\"]\n    P --> E1[\"Linux: sh -c\"]\n    P --> E2[\"Win: bash -c<br/>同一方言, 不同 binary\"]\n```\n\n所以你的说法基本成立，准确表述是：**「模型写什么」和「怎么审判」在 Win 上与 Linux 是同一套 POSIX 逻辑（有 Git Bash 的前提下）；「怎么把文本变成进程」是两个等价实现加一个 cmd 降级；剩下的平台差异（杀树、编码、`/tmp` 映射）被三个适配文件吸收在水面之下。**", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "Now I have all the evidence. Let me compose the answer.\n\nThe question: \"但是由于我们的适配，所以现在我们在win上使用的也是同一套shell逻辑是吗\"\n\nAnswer: 对，但要说准确——「同一套」的是**命令文本方言和审判逻辑**（POSIX），不是底层执行机制。分三层：\n\n**第一层：统一的部分（agent 的世界观）**\n- 决策唯一点 localshell.py:76-85 `_detect()`：Windows 上探测到 Git Bash → `LocalShell(argv=(bash.exe, \"-c\"), posix=True, name=\"bash\")`\n- shell.py:212: `posix = workspace.exec_shell().posix` — 判定方言唯从此处来\n- 所以模型写的命令、安全审判（classify_command、shlex 拆词、路径越界判定）全部按 POSIX 一套，Linux/Win 无差别\n- transport.py:110 注释直说 \"the agent speaks POSIX\"\n\n**第二层：形式不同、语义等价的执行管道**\n- Linux: `Popen(cmd_str, shell=True)` → `/bin/sh -c`\n- Windows: `Popen([bash.exe, \"-c\", cmd_str])`\n- 两个都是\"POSIX shell 解析文本\"，但 binary 不同（sh vs bash）、spawn 机制不同（shell=True vs argv 前缀）。语义等价——同一行文本，同一套分词/管道/重定向行为\n\n**第三层：真正的平台差异，被适配层吸收掉的部分**\n1. 杀进程树：POSIX `start_new_session` + `os.killpg(SIGKILL)`；Windows `taskkill /PID x /T /F`（transport.py:83-99）\n2. 文本解码：固定 utf-8/replace，否则中文 Windows 按 GBK 解（transport.py:112-113, 172-176）\n3. 路径审判：`/tmp`→%TEMP%、`/dev/null`→NUL 的映射（workspace.py:324-338），MSYS 自己做映射，审判引擎跟着 bash 的视角走\n4. WSL bash 被刻意排除（localshell.py:49-51, 88-96）\n\n**例外/兜底路径（不是同一套）**\n- Windows 上找不到可用 bash → `LocalShell(argv=None, posix=False, name=\"cmd\")` → cmd.exe + CommandLineToArgvW 方言审判。同一套逻辑的承诺只在有 bash 时成立\n- 探测机制：CLUTCH_BASH 环境变量 > 5 个标准安装路径 > which bash，还要 `_probe_bash` 实测 `echo clutch-bash-ok`（localshell.py:80-84, 99-108）\n- 远程 SSH workspace：永远 posix=True（shell.py:210-212 注释），与本地主机无关\n\n结论表述：对——**面向模型和命令语言的逻辑是一套（POSIX 方言）**，这正是适配的设计目标：\"the agent speaks POSIX\"；但**执行管道是三实现两等价一兜底**：posix-sh（shell=True）、Git Bash（bash -c）语义等价，cmd.exe 是不同方言的降级。平台差异（杀树、解码、/tmp 映射）在 transport/workspace/localshell 三个适配层里被吸收，不漏到 shell.py 的业务逻辑。\n\nAlso worth one nuance: \"同一套\"还要打个补丁 — Linux 上是 /bin/sh（可能是 dash），Windows 上是真 bash。所以严格说 Windows 上的 bash 功能可能比 Linux CI 上的 sh 更多(bashisms)。有趣但真实：模型在 Windows 上反而更自由。可以一句话带过。\n\nFormat: use a table for the three-layer summary, mermaid maybe not needed (previous answers had diagrams; a small table suffices). Keep it focused. Chinese. Include file:line."}
