erred.\n- Shared utilities (e.g. split_command): implementations stay independent (duplication accepted).\n- New repo may use pytest (host repo stays runner-less). Python 3.14 at /c/Python314 available for test harness.\n- Known C++ port risks flagged to user: std::regex ECMAScript dialect vs Python re (no lookbehind!); hand-written unified diff (LCS/Myers, n=3); forced UTF-8 on Windows (binary file I/O, CP_UTF8 argv/console); hand-rolled JSON writer; big args (write --content) vs Windows 32K cmdline limit — proposal: value `-` = read stdin, pending user confirm.\n- Exit-code-table & schema/argparse drift explained to user; drift mitigation (workspace schema subcmd / codegen / contract tests) deferred to integration phase.", "updated": 1789891270.182313}
