{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789892730.5589893, "id": "f6fe871e0706", "content": "开工。先取两个保真度参照：host 的 `pyproject.toml`（镜像工程约定）和 `LocalWorkspace.read/grep/list/write` 的实现体（M1 平移的语义基准）。", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_1678bd2a9d4c4c3d8669feea", "name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"pyproject.toml\"}"}, {"id": "call_a72776b96a5f483a8dd225b8", "name": "grep", "arguments": "{\"include\":\"workspace.py\",\"path\":\"agent/tools\",\"pattern\":\"    def (read|list|write|grep)\\\\(\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user says: \"就这样吧，现在开始，如果中途碰到需要决策的技术点一定让我决策而不是静默执行\" — \"OK let's go, start now. If any technical decision points come up midway, make me decide instead of silently executing.\"\n\nThis matches the original task title at the very top of the conversation: \"就这样吧，现在开始，如果中途碰到需要决策的技术点一定让我决策而不是静默执行\"\n\nSo now I should start M1. But wait — I need to check: am I in work mode or chat mode? The system prompt says \"Current mode: work (full access).\" — \"You are in work mode: you can read and modify the workspace, create and edit files, and run arbitrary commands.\"\n\nSo I'm in work mode now. The user has confirmed. Per the plan:\n\n**M1 plan:**\n1. Scaffold: `clutch-workspace/` subdirectory inside current workspace, own `git init`, pyproject.toml (zero deps), package `clutch_workspace/` with `__init__.py|cli.py|jsonio.py|exitcodes.py`, tests/ with pytest (subprocess black-box driving the CLI).\n2. read_file full semantics port: directory listing / line-range reads with line numbers / truncation with continue hints / over-budget range errors.\n3. --json envelope + sysexits mapping.\n4. Then M1b: grep, write_file, edit_file.\n\nDefault W2: scaffold in current workspace as subfolder with own git. User said \"就这样吧\" — proceed with defaults. W3: value `-` = stdin, confirmed by default. Distribution: v1 = standard Python package, console script `clutch-workspace`.\n\nLet me now carefully design the implementation.\n\n**First: check environment.** Is pytest available? Python 3.14 at /c/Python314. The host repo has .venv (from pyproject/uv). For the new project I need its own venv or use the global python. Since pytest may not be installed globally, I may need to create a venv in clutch-workspace and pip install pytest (network available). Let me plan: `cd clutch-workspace && python -m venv .venv && .venv/Scripts/python -m pip install pytest`. On Windows Git Bash, venv scripts are in .venv/Scripts/. Need `python` — which python is in PATH: /c/Python314/python (per earlier PATH listing: /c/Python314/Scripts:/c/Python314). So `python` works.\n\nWait — the memory says tests in host repo run via `PYTHONPATH=. timeout 25 .venv/Scripts/python.exe tests/xxx_test.py`. The host .venv exists. But new repo should have its own venv. pytest needs installing — network available (pip install works? Should be fine).\n\nAlternatively: keep zero-install by writing tests runner without pytest? But user said pytest allowed (Q23: 可以上). Let's do pytest in the new repo's own venv.\n\n**Design of the package:**\n\n```\nclutch-workspace/\n├── .git/                    (own git init)\n├── .gitignore\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── README.md               (minimal — internal component; user said 不用文档. Skip README? A minimal one-liner is harmless but Q29 said 不用文档. I'll skip README or add tiny one. Better skip — user explicitly said no docs. Actually a repo with zero README is odd; but respect the decision: no docs. Hmm, pyproject needs at least name/version. Skip README.)\n├── clutch_workspace/\n│   ├── __init__.py          (version)\n│   ├── exitcodes.py         (sysexits constants)\n│   ├── jsonio.py            (JSON envelope writer with proper escaping — json.dumps handles it; stdlib json is allowed, zero-dep means no third-party. json is stdlib.)\n│   ├── argsio.py?           (stdin reading for '-' values — can live in cli.py)\n│   ├── reads.py             (read_file + grep)  — or filesystem.py mirroring host naming\n│   ├── writes.py            (write_file