d run WITHOUT installing the package: run `python -m clutch_workspace` with cwd=tmp_path and env PYTHONPATH=repo root. That way no pip install needed for dev/test. But console script check: pip install -e . once in venv, test `clutch-workspace --json`? Simpler: tests always use `-m`. Provide both.\n\npyproject: needs [build-system] setuptools? Zero-dep: use hatchling? Host uses uv — check host pyproject build backend to mirror conventions. I'll peek at host pyproject.toml.\n\n**Encoding on Windows:** CLI writes to stdout — must force UTF-8: `sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")` (Python 3.7+). Also `sys.stderr`. File writes: `open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\")` — newline=\"\" prevents CRLF translation → byte-faithful LF writes. Reads: `open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")`? — with newline=\"\"? Host workspace.read — check. Python read_text default universal newlines translates \\r\\n → \\n. Host read via workspace.read... unknown; likely read_text default (universal newlines ON). For fidelity, match host. I'll read the host LocalWorkspace.read quickly.\n\nLet me also check: does the host repo's pyproject use hatchling or setuptools? Quick read of pyproject.toml (host).\n\n**Plan of action now (work mode):**\n\n1. Read host pyproject.toml (mirror conventions) + workspace.py LocalWorkspace.read/grep/list bodies (fidelity reference). \n2. Check pytest availability / create venv in new repo + install pytest.\n3. Scaffold files.\n4. Implement exitcodes.py, jsonio.py (trivial), filesystem.py (read_file first? or all four since I'm reading bodies anyway — incremental: M1 read_file, test; M1b rest, test).\n5. Tests for read_file, run pytest → green.\n6. M1b: grep/write/edit + tests → green.\n7. Report: what was built, test results, decision points I flagged (error-code assignments for ambiguous cases, argparse exit 2→64 override, path display in summaries, no README per Q29, etc.)\n\nActually to keep this response manageable: do M1 completely (scaffold + read_file + tests green), then M1b (3 commands + tests green), then final report. Let me start.\n\nFirst batch of reads (parallel):\n- read host pyproject.toml\n- grep workspace.py for \"def read\" body — better: read_file workspace.py around LocalWorkspace read. LocalWorkspace class starts somewhere ~line 300? The file is 715 lines. Grep \"def read(self\" gave line 278 abstract. LocalWorkspace methods later. Let me grep for \"def read\" in workspace.py with line numbers to find LocalWorkspace.read, then read that range. Also \"def grep\" and \"def list\" and \"def write\".\n\nDo: grep pattern \"def (read|list|write|grep|snapshot)\\(\" path agent/tools/workspace.py → get line numbers, then read the LocalWorkspace implementations."}
