{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789893121.4034436, "id": "9d3b03ae9040", "content": "pytest 9.1.1 就绪。现在写骨架与全部实现文件：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_9484ff2ff10e41a28973a50d", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/pyproject.toml\",\"content\":\"[project]\\nname = \\\"clutch-workspace\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.1.0\\\"\\ndescription = \\\"Standalone file-inspection CLI: read_file / grep / write_file / edit_file as plain flags-in, text-out commands.\\\"\\nrequires-python = \\\">=3.10\\\"\\nlicense = \\\"MIT\\\"\\ndependencies = []\\n\\n[project.scripts]\\nclutch-workspace = \\\"clutch_workspace.cli:main\\\"\\n\\n[build-system]\\nrequires = [\\\"hatchling\\\"]\\nbuild-backend = \\\"hatchling.build\\\"\\n\\n[tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel]\\npackages = [\\\"clutch_workspace\\\"]\\n\\n[dependency-groups]\\ndev = [\\\"pytest>=8.0\\\"]\\n\\n[tool.ruff]\\nline-length = 120\\ntarget-version = \\\"py310\\\"\\n\\n[tool.ruff.lint]\\nselect = [\\\"E\\\", \\\"F\\\", \\\"W\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"I\\\"]\\n\"}"}, {"id": "call_9eca028752fa4f6484d52e9c", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/.gitignore\",\"content\":\"__pycache__/\\n*.pyc\\n.venv/\\n.pytest_cache/\\ndist/\\nbuild/\\n\"}"}, {"id": "call_f4d6d52f570e45b98b09399d", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/__init__.py\",\"content\":\"__version__ = \\\"0.1.0\\\"\\n\"}"}, {"id": "call_a19ed439eb9f420c983ca5fa", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/exitcodes.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Exit codes: BSD sysexits.h plus POSIX signal convention.\\n\\nThis table IS the CLI's error contract — the caller classifies failures from\\nthese codes (and from stderr briefs), never from parsing prose.\\n\\n  0   ok\\n  64  EX_USAGE    bad flags / unknown subcommand / contradictory arguments\\n  65  EX_DATAERR  data-level failure (edit target not found or ambiguous,\\n                  requested line range exceeds the read budget, bad stdin bytes)\\n  66  EX_NOINPUT  input file (or search root) missing\\n  70  EX_SOFTWARE internal invariant broken (bug — report it)\\n  74  EX_IOERR    read/write I/O failure\\n  130 128+SIGINT  aborted by the caller\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nEX_OK = 0\\nEX_USAGE = 64\\nEX_DATAERR = 65\\nEX_NOINPUT = 66\\nEX_SOFTWARE = 70\\nEX_IOERR = 74\\nEX_SIGINT = 130\\n\"}"}, {"id": "call_ac97a531349c492b8f0d5382", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/envelope.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Output contract: human text vs the --json machine envelope.\\n\\nTwo modes, one Result shape:\\n- human:  content (+ diff) on stdout; errors go to stderr as `ERROR: <brief>`\\n- --json: ONE compact JSON line on stdout, always\\n          {\\\"content\\\": str, \\\"error\\\": bool, \\\"diff\\\": str}\\n          errors use the same envelope with error=true, diff=\\\"\\\", and a\\n          non-zero exit code — callers parse stdout, never prose.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Result:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A successful command outcome: content plus an optional unified diff.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    content: str\\n    diff: str = \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass CommandError(Exception):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A failed command: sysexits code (see exitcodes) plus a brief message.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, code: int, message: str) -> None:\\n        super().__init__(message)\\n        self.code = code\\n        self.message = message\\n\\n\\ndef _write_line(text: str) -> None:\\n    sys.stdout.write(text + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef emit_result(res: Result, as_json: bool) -> None:\\n    if as_json:\\n        _write_line(json.dumps({\\\"content\\\": res.content, \\\"error\\\": False, \\\"diff\\\": res.diff}, ensure_ascii=False))\\n        return\\n    sys.stdout.write(res.content + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n    if res.diff:\\n        sys.stdout.write(res.diff if res.diff.endswith(\\\"\\\\n\\\") else res.diff + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef emit_error(err: CommandError, as_json: bool) -> None:\\n    if as_json:\\n        _write_line(json.dumps({\\\"content\\\": err.message, \\\"error\\\": True, \\\"diff\\\": \\\"\\\"}, ensure_ascii=False))\\n        return\\n    sys.stderr.write(f\\\"ERROR: {err.message}\\\\n\\\")\\n\"}"}], "reasoning": "pytest 9.1.1 installed. Now write all the files. Let me write:\n\n1. pyproject.toml\n2. .gitignore\n3. clutch_workspace/__init__.py\n4. clutch_workspace/exitcodes.py\n5. clutch_workspace/envelope.py\n6. clutch_workspace/filesystem.py (all four commands, faithful port)\n7. clutch_workspace/cli.py\n8. clutch_workspace/__main__.py\n9. tests/conftest.py\n10. tests/test_cli.py\n11. tests/test_read.py\n12. tests/test_grep.py\n13. tests/test_write.py\n14. tests/test_edit.py\n\nWrite them in parallel batches. Let me carefully compose each file.\n\nfilesystem.py — the core port. All four functions + _read_range + _unified_diff + DEFAULT_MAX_CHARS.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"The four file commands: read_file / grep / write_file / edit_file.\n\nPure capability, zero policy: paths are used exactly as given, resolved against\nthe process's current working directory. There is no workspace, no protection\nlist, no snapshotting here — confinement and safety are the caller's job (it\nchooses the cwd this process runs under).\n\nFaithful port of clutch's agent/tools/filesystem.py + LocalWorkspace file ops:\n- reads are UTF-8/replace with universal newlines; writes are UTF-8 with\n  newline=\"\\n\" (byte-exact, never CRLF-translated)\n- read_file's char budget, truncation pointer, line-range numbering and the\n  continuation hints are part of the model-facing output contract — keep them\n  byte-identical\n- errors are CommandError(sysexits code, brief message): this CLI never\n  renders prose for a model, the caller does\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nFunctions as designed. Let me now write everything.\n\nOne detail in read_file: host wrapped everything in try/except ValueError → \"ERROR: {e}\". ValueError here would come from... resolve (dropped). Keep a guard for weird paths (embedded nulls raise ValueError on Windows open). I'll wrap core in try: except CommandError: raise; except ValueError → EX_USAGE \"invalid path\"; except OSError → EX_IOERR \"read failed: {e}\".\n\nCareful ordering in read_file: is_dir check first, then read.\n\ntest expectations for exit codes: 64 usage (no args, unknown cmd, dir+range, bad regex, empty old_string), 65 (edit not found/ambiguous, over-budget range), 66 (missing file read/edit), 74 (IO — hard to test portably; skip), 70 skip.\n\nWait — one more consideration on `--max-chars` name → argparse dest \"max_chars\". Host schema called it max_chars. ✓.\n\nAlso grep --path default \".\" and --include default \"\" (host: include=\"\" → None). \n\nNow writing. For cli.py, `_version()` — just import from __init__.\n\nAlso add epilog to parser help documenting the stdin '-' and --json position contract? Minimal help is fine.\n\nLet me write all files now — batch 1: pyproject, .gitignore, __init__, exitcodes, envelope. Batch 2: filesystem, cli, __main__. Batch 3: tests. Then run."}
