{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789893361.045504, "id": "6fd67d5c8456", "tool_call_id": "call_b9161cbd137c4d2db7523000", "content": "[clutch-workspace C++ spin-off: frozen decisions]\nDECISION REVERSED: clutch-workspace implementation language is now PYTHON (was C++). Reason: no compiler on machine (W1), and for an internal component the C++ single-binary advantage is worth less than zero-toolchain + exact semantic fidelity (clutch host is Python anyway; tools/cli.py pilot already pays interpreter startup).\n\nFROZEN (unchanged through the language flip):\n- Name/repo: `clutch-workspace`, independent repo, internal component, no docs, stays part of clutch ecosystem.\n- Scope: exactly 4 subcommands = read_file / grep / write_file / edit_file — faithful port of agent/tools/filesystem.py semantics. No web_search/web_fetch/memory/load_skill/run-sh.\n- Pure capability: NO containment/protected/snapshot logic in the CLI. Paths resolve against the process CWD; host transport sets cwd=workspace root when spawning. Security/classification stays in host.\n- CLI contract: `--path x` space style; global `--json` → {content, error, diff} envelope; human mode prints summary + unified diff (my delegated Q15 decision); CLI emits error code + brief message only (errors/*.md prose stays in host).\n- Exit codes (BSD sysexits, user chose \"unix standard\"): 0 ok / 64 EX_USAGE / 65 EX_DATAERR (edit old_string not found or ambiguous) / 66 EX_NOINPUT / 70 EX_SOFTWARE / 74 EX_IOERR / 130 reserved (128+SIGINT).\n- read truncation in CLI: --max-chars default 20000; v1 zero config files, all knobs are flags.\n- Big args: value `-` = read stdin (write_file --content, edit_file --old-string/--new-string) due to Windows 32K argv limit (W3, default-yes).\n- UTF-8 forced. Shared utilities (split_command etc.) duplicated, not shared (Q22). pytest allowed in new repo (host stays runner-less).\n- Host integration explicitly deferred (Q21 full-cut-with-tag-rollback later, Q31/32/33: clutch untouched, connection later). Remote: servers will install the tool later; with Python the install story = pip/uv package (PyInstaller single-file optional, deferred).\n- Python floor 3.10 stdlib-only, pyproject+uv conventions like host repo; dev machine has Python 3.14 (/c/Python314).\n\nOPEN: W2 repo physical location (default: scaffold clutch-workspace/ subfolder inside clutch workspace with own git init, push to own remote later).\n\nC++ era risks all dead with the flip: regex dialect (Python re IS the reference), hand-written unified diff (difflib), Windows UTF-8 layer, hand-rolled JSON.\n\nNEXT: switch to work mode → M1 scaffold (pyproject, no deps) + argparse + envelope + sysexits + read_file full semantics + pytest black-box tests driving the CLI via subprocess; M1b: grep/write/edit batch.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
