'/')\". ✓ matches.\n\nHuman mode write/edit output: emit_result prints content then diff. Human grep/read: content. Errors human: `ERROR: {message}` to stderr (envelope.py already does that). Note host human channel prints \"ERROR: ...\" INSIDE content on stdout (tool-boundary style); our CLI human mode → stderr per envelope.py. That's already frozen (\"human 模式错误走 stderr\").\n\nWait, one subtlety: host puts error text in content with error=true; our --json envelope: {\"content\": err.message, \"error\": true, \"diff\": \"\"} — envelope.py puts message in content field. OK frozen already.\n\nNow the message TEXTS: frozen says \"CLI 只出错误码+简讯\" and prose stays in host. But which 简讯? The host error messages are the natural briefs minus the prose-ish tails. E.g.:\n- file missing: host renders errors/file_missing.md with path. Brief: `file not found: {path}` (matches edit's inline message style).\n- dir+range: host has inline brief \"cannot read a line range of a directory; list it without offset/limit\" — use as-is.\n- range over budget: inline host message exists: \"the requested range (lines A-B) exceeds the read limit of N chars. Use a smaller limit, or search with grep instead.\" — keep as brief (it's already brief-ish; it's guidance prose but useful; keep byte-identical minus \"ERROR: \" prefix which our envelope adds).\n- edit 0次: host brief: \"old_string not found in {path}\" + prose tail. CLI brief: \"old_string not found in {path}\" (drop the prose tail — prose stays in host per Q16).\n- edit >1次: \"old_string appears {count} times in {path}\" (drop \"Include more surrounding lines...\"? that's guidance prose — drop per Q16? Hmm, Q16 said prose like errors/*.md stays in host; inline guidance... The frozen examples: \"CLI 只出错误码+简讯\". I'll keep briefs minimal: `old_string appears 3 times in {path}`. Hmm, but \"keep it actionable\"... The user reviews these in the report anyway — I'll list the exact brief strings in the final report table so they can veto. Good co