roken pipe test: monkeypatch sys.stdout AFTER main's reconfigure? main reconfigures then dispatch writes. Fake with reconfigure pass + write raises BrokenPipe + fileno raises ValueError → main → except BrokenPipeError → _on_broken_pipe: os.dup2(os.open(devnull), sys.stdout.fileno()) — sys.stdout is the fake → fileno raises ValueError → caught → return 74 ✓ no fd damage ✓.\n\nWait: in _on_broken_pipe I reference sys.stdout.fileno() — fake raises ValueError ✓ good.\n\n130 test: monkeypatch cli.filesystem.read_file to raise KeyboardInterrupt; human mode: emit_error writes stderr ✓ rc 130.\n\nHmm wait — for the 130/70 tests: monkeypatch.setattr(\"clutch_workspace.cli.filesystem.read_file\", fn) — cli does `from . import filesystem` so cli.filesystem IS the module; setattr on module attr read_file ✓ (filesystem.read_file rebound). Restore automatic via monkeypatch.\n\n70 test: raise RuntimeError(\"boom\") → except Exception → traceback → stderr contains \"Traceback\" & \"RuntimeError: boom\"; envelope json if --json → content \"internal error: boom\", rc 70 ✓ assert both human (traceback) and json variant? one human test enough + maybe json error field. Do human with capsys.\n\nNow argparse allow_abbrev=False and parse_args([\"--json\"]) alone → error \"the following arguments are required: command\" → our error() → usage+msg → 64 ✓.\n\nWait — one more thing: subparsers with allow_abbrev: sub parsers inherit? parser_class default → argparse.ArgumentParser (NOT _Parser!) — sub.add_parser creates parsers via parser_class which defaults to the CLASS of the calling parser? docs: add_subparsers(parser_class=...) defaults to the type of the parser? Actually default parser_class = type(self) — yes: \"parser_class - class which will be used to create sub-parser instances, by default the class of the current parser (e.g. ArgumentParser)\". So sub-parsers are _Parser too ✓ their error() → 64 ✓ (e.g. read_file missing --path → sub parser error → 64 ✓).\n\nAlso `--json` with subcommand alias \"-\" prefix conflicts? no.\n\nmetavar \"<command>\" fine.\n\nVersion action on _Parser: exit(0, msg) → default exit → SystemExit(0) → parse_args propagates → main()?? WAIT: parse_args raises SystemExit INSIDE main() before try block — version/help exits with code 0 fine; error exits 64 via our error(). main() propagates SystemExit → console script wrapper sys.exit(SystemExit(64)) → 64 ✓. python -m → raise SystemExit(main()) — SystemExit from inside propagates ✓ fine.\n\nBut hold on: main returns 0 on success; parse errors raise SystemExit(64) from parse_args — both fine for callers.\n\nNow — one concern: emit_result human for read of empty content \"\" writes \"\\n\" — fine.\n\ngrep empty file root: file root that's empty → open iterates nothing → out [] → \"(no matches)\" ✓.\n\nconftest run(): PYTHONUTF8=1 env — cli also reconfigures; both.\n\nAlso PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 keeps tmp/__pycache__ from OUR package only (package lives in repo, not tmp) — irrelevant for tmp dirs. skip it? harmless keep.\n\nOne more fidelity item: host grep line.rstrip(\"\\n\") — only \\n stripped, \\r kept! File with CRLF read in text mode → universal newlines → \\r gone anyway. ✓ same.\n\nHost hit line: `line.rstrip(\"\\n\")` — trailing \\r via universal newlines already handled. ✓ port rstrip(\"\\n\").\n\nNow filesystem.grep rel on Windows for tmp files: \"f1.txt\" simple names fine.\n\nTime to write. Also `.gitignore` exists (summary says) — includes .venv/ presumably (dir listing of repo showed .gitignore only + dirs). Fine.\n\nAfter writing: run pytest via .venv: `clutch-workspace/.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q` from repo root (workspace root). Use `python` preferred... venv python explicit path: `clutch-workspace/.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest clutch-workspace/tests -q`. cwd = workspace root; pytest rootdir detection fine.\n\nThen git init + commit — WAIT: user said decision points → ask first. My plan: implement + green tests, then PRESENT decision list, do NOT git init/commit yet? git init is harmless but the commit bakes choices into history; better ask first, then commit after rulings. Hmm — but a baseline commit of a green state is actually useful for incremental edits... The user cares about decisions, not commits. I'll hold the commit until after their rulings, per the \"must let me decide\" instruction. State that in the report.\n\nAlso I promised in memory NEXT: M1 scaffold... fine.\n\nWrite all 9 files in one batch now (independent). Let me compose carefully.\n\nfilesystem.py:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"The four commands, ported 1:1 from the host's agent/tools/filesystem.py.\n\nDeltas are exactly the frozen \"pure capability\" cuts — nothing else:\n- no Workspace object: paths resolve against the process CWD (`_resolve`),\n  so \"the workspace\" is whatever cwd the caller spawns us with\n- no protected set / snapshots / containment: every path is servable\n- no error prose templates: failures raise CommandError(code, brief); the\n  caller owns the long-form prose\n- output-channel formats (hit grouping, continuation hints, the grep cap\n  footer, \"(no matches)\", \"(empty directory)\") stay byte-identical to the\n  host so the host's prompt contract keeps holding verbatim\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport difflib\nimport fnmatch\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom .envelope import CommandError, Result\nfrom .exitcodes import EX_DATAERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\n\nREAD_MAX_CHARS = 20_000  # --max-chars default: the host's read budget\n_GREP_MAX_HITS = 100\n_GREP_LINE_MAX = 300\n```\n\nThen functions as planned.\n\nDocstrings copied spirit from host. Compose write/edit.\n\ncli.py as planned.\n\nLet me now also double check `Path.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\")` — newline param added 3.10 ✓ floor is 3.10.\n\nPotential Windows quirk: p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True) when parent == \".\" → exist_ok ✓.\n\n_edit write: p.write_text(new, ...) without mkdir — file exists (we read it) ✓.\n\ngrep `files = [root] if root.is_file() else _grep_files(root)` — after missing-root guard.\n\nOK writing now. Six test files + 3 source files. Keep tests thorough but not bloated.\n\nFor test_cli version test: run via fixture run(\"--version\")? cwd tmp fine.\n\nOne more: test \"--json first\" vs human default: assert human read stdout raw+newline.\n\nAnd envelope ordering test: `[\"--json\", \"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\"]` ok vs `[\"read_file\", \"--json\", ...]` rc 64.\n\nWriting conftest with sys.path insert:\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nif str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n```\n\nFixtures run/jok/jerr as planned.\n\nNow compose test_read exact strings:\n\nDATA = \"l1\\nl2\\nl3\\nl4\\nl5\\n\"\n- raw json content == DATA ✓\n- human stdout == DATA + \"\\n\" (write adds one) ✓\n- offset2 limit2 content: \"2: l2\\n3: l3\\n... (showing lines 2-3 of 5; use offset=4 to continue)\" ✓\n- offset 4: \"4: l4\\n5: l5\" ✓\n- offset 1 (no limit): \"1: l1\\n2: l2\\n3: l3\\n4: l4\\n5: l5\" ✓\n- limit 2 (no offset): \"1: l1\\n2: l2\\n... (showing lines 1-2 of 5; use offset=3 to continue)\" ✓ (start=0, shown=2 <5 → \"showing lines 1-2 of 5; use offset=3\") ✓\n- over budget: max-chars 10, offset 1 limit 4: body=\"1: l1\\n2: l2\\n3: l3\\n4: l4\" len = 5+5+5+5=20 > 10 → error msg \"the requested range (lines 1-4) exceeds the read limit of 10 chars. Use a smaller limit, or search with grep instead.\" code 65 ✓\n- offset 99: content \"\" rc 0 ✓\n\ntruncation single-line: text = \"x\" * 30000; expected content = \"x\"*20000 + \"\\n... [truncated, file is 30000 chars; use offset=1 to continue]\" ✓\n\ndir listing: entries \".hidden\"(file), \"A.txt\", \"b.txt\", \"sub/\" → sorted plain ✓\n\nNow write files. Also add README? Frozen: \"no docs\" — skip README. pyproject already has description.\n\n.gitignore — exists from last session; trust.\n\nLet me write everything now. Long batch of write_file calls — all independent (different paths).\n\nCareful in tests: `--max-chars` flag name with dest max_chars ✓ argparse auto.\n\nFor jerr on argparse errors: stderr has usage, stdout empty → json.loads fails! jerr only for envelope errors (not usage) — usage errors tested separately with raw run(). Note in tests.\n\ntest_cli human stderr exact: \"ERROR: file not found: nope.txt\\n\" ✓ envelope emit_error writes f\"ERROR: {msg}\\n\" ✓.\n\nEdge: Windows console for child stderr — reconfigured utf-8; message ASCII anyway.\n\nCompose everything.\n\ncli.py full text:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Flag wiring: argparse -> filesystem commands -> envelope out.\n\n  clutch-workspace [--json] <command> [flags]\n\n- human (default): content on stdout (plus the unified diff for\n  write/edit), `ERROR: <brief>` on stderr, sysexits code as exit status\n- --json: ONE compact {\"content\", \"error\", \"diff\"} line on stdout for\n  BOTH outcomes; callers parse stdout and the exit code, never prose.\n  It is a global flag and must precede the subcommand.\nA payload flag value of `-` reads the value from stdin (write_file\n--content, edit_file --old-string/--new-string) so bodies beyond the\nWindows 32K argv limit still get through. Only one flag per invocation\nmay use `-` — two would drain the same stream twice.\n\nUsage errors (bad flags, unknown command, contradictory arguments —\nargparse's own included) exit 64; I/O failures 74; a bug that escapes is\n70, never masquerading as caller error.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport traceback\n\nfrom . import __version__, filesystem\nfrom .envelope import CommandError, Result, emit_error, emit_result\nfrom .exitcodes import EX_IOERR, EX_SIGINT, EX_SOFTWARE, EX_USAGE\nfrom .filesystem import READ_MAX_CHARS\n\n\nclass _Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\n    def error(self, message: str):  # argparse's default is 2; our contract is 64\n        self.print_usage(sys.stderr)\n        self.exit(EX_USAGE, f\"{self.prog}: error: {message}\\n\")\n\n\ndef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n    parser = _Parser(\n        prog=\"clutch-workspace\",\n        description=\"Standalone file-inspection CLI: read_file / grep / write_file / edit_file.\",\n        allow_abbrev=False,\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--json\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"emit one JSON envelope line on stdout instead of human text\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--version\", action=\"version\", version=f\"clutch-workspace {__version__}\")\n    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", metavar=\"<command>\", required=True)\n\n    read = sub.add_parser(\"read_file\", help=\"read a file (or list a directory); numbered ranges with continuation hints\")\n    read.add_argument(\"--path\", required=True, help=\"file or directory, relative to the process CWD\")\n    read.add_argument(\"--offset\", type=int, default=0, metavar=\"N\", help=\"1-based first line\")\n    read.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=0, metavar=\"N\", help=\"max lines to return\")\n    read.add_argument(\"--max-chars\", type=int, default=READ_MAX_CHARS, metavar=\"N\", help=f\"char budget before truncation (default {READ_MAX_CHARS})\")\n\n    search = sub.add_parser(\"grep\", help=\"regex search over text files, capped at 100 hits\")\n    search.add_argument(\"--pattern\", required=True, help=\"Python regex\")\n    search.add_argument(\"--path\", default=\".\", help=\"file or directory to search (default: the CWD)\")\n    search.add_argument(\"--include\", default=\"\", metavar=\"GLOB\", help=\"fnmatch filter on file name or CWD-relative path\")\n\n    write = sub.add_parser(\"write_file\", help=\"create or overwrite a file (parents auto-created); prints a unified diff\")\n    write.add_argument(\"--path\", required=True)\n    write.add_argument(\"--content\", required=True, help=\"new file body; `-` reads stdin\")\n\n    edit = sub.add_parser(\"edit_file\", help=\"replace exactly one occurrence of old_string; prints a unified diff\")\n    edit.add_argument(\"--path\", required=True)\n    edit.add_argument(\"--old-string\", required=True, dest=\"old_string\", help=\"exact text to find; `-` reads stdin\")\n    edit.add_argument(\"--new-string\", required=True, dest=\"new_string\", help=\"replacement text; `-` reads stdin\")\n    return parser\n```\n\npayload:\n\n```python\ndef _payload(value: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"`-` = the value arrives on stdin (Windows argv caps at ~32K).\"\"\"\n    return sys.stdin.read() if value == \"-\" else value\n\n\ndef _check_args(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\n    if args.command != \"read_file\":\n        return\n    for name in (\"offset\", \"limit\", \"max_chars\"):\n        if getattr(args, name) < 0:\n            raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, f\"--{name.replace('_', '-')} must be >= 0\")\n```\n\nHmm max_chars attr: \"--max-chars\" → dest max_chars ✓.\n\ndispatch + main as planned. main:\n\n```python\ndef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n    for stream in (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr):\n        try:\n            stream.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        except (AttributeError, OSError, ValueError):\n            pass\n    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)  # usage errors exit 64 from here\n    try:\n        _check_args(args)\n        result = _dispatch(args)\n    except CommandError as err:\n        emit_error(err, as_json=args.json)\n        return err.code\n    except BrokenPipeError:\n        return _silence_broken_pipe()\n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n        emit_error(CommandError(EX_SIGINT, \"interrupted\"), as_json=args.json)\n        return EX_SIGINT\n    except OSError as err:\n        emit_error(CommandError(EX_IOERR, str(err)), as_json=args.json)\n        return EX_IOERR\n    except Exception as err:  # noqa: BLE001 - the one catch-all: name it a bug\n        traceback.print_exc()\n        emit_error(CommandError(EX_SOFTWARE, f\"internal error: {err}\"), as_json=args.json)\n        return EX_SOFTWARE\n    emit_result(result, as_json=args.json)\n    return 0\n\n\ndef _silence_broken_pipe() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Keep the interpreter's shutdown flush from re-raising on the dead pipe.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        os.dup2(os.open(os.devnull, os.O_WRONLY), sys.stdout.fileno())\n    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):\n        pass\n    return EX_IOERR\n```\n\nWait: reconfigure on stdin: TextIOWrapper.reconfigure fine. But when stdin closed (pytest capture?) — caught.\n\nCommandError for OSError: str(err) like \"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'x'\" ✓ acceptable brief.\n\nHmm — OSError catch also swallows socket stuff etc. fine for CLI.\n\n_dispatch as planned.\n\nNow filesystem.py final. Compose fully:\n\n(as drafted above, plus docstrings.)\n\nI'm confident. Write 9 files now in one batch.\n\nActually wait — one thing on `emit_result` human: prints content + \"\\n\". For read of file without trailing newline, content \"abc\" → \"abc\\n\" ✓. For dir listing etc. ✓.\n\nAnd json emit: json.dumps(...) with ensure_ascii=False → 中文 raw ✓ stdout utf-8 reconfigured ✓.\n\nTests list finalized. Writing now.\n\nOne more check on jerr usage for 65 range test: message text assert contains \"exceeds the read limit of 10 chars\" ✓ exact brief text: \"the requested range (lines 1-4) exceeds the read limit of 10 chars. Use a smaller limit, or search with grep instead.\"\n\nGo."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "f7a6a355f88a", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/filesystem.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"The four commands, ported 1:1 from the host's agent/tools/filesystem.py.\\n\\nDeltas are exactly the frozen \\\"pure capability\\\" cuts — nothing else:\\n- no Workspace object: paths resolve against the process CWD (`_resolve`),\\n  so \\\"the workspace\\\" is whatever cwd the caller spawns us with\\n- no protected set / snapshots / containment: every path is servable\\n- no error prose templates: failures raise CommandError(code, brief); the\\n  caller owns the long-form prose\\n- output-channel formats (hit grouping, continuation hints, the grep cap\\n  footer, \\\"(no matches)\\\", \\\"(empty directory)\\\") stay byte-identical to the\\n  host, so the host's prompt contract keeps holding verbatim\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport difflib\\nimport fnmatch\\nimport re\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nfrom .envelope import CommandError, Result\\nfrom .exitcodes import EX_DATAERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\\n\\nREAD_MAX_CHARS = 20_000  # --max-chars default: the host's read budget\\n_GREP_MAX_HITS = 100\\n_GREP_LINE_MAX = 300\\n\\n\\ndef read_file(path: str, offset: int = 0, limit: int = 0, max_chars: int = READ_MAX_CHARS) -> Result:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read a file (or, with no range flags, list a directory).\\n\\n    No range flags: raw text, truncated at the char budget with a hint that\\n    points at the first unread line. With range flags: 1-based numbered\\n    lines [offset, offset+limit) — a range that cannot fit the budget is an\\n    error, not a silent truncation.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    limit_chars = max_chars or READ_MAX_CHARS  # --max-chars 0 means \\\"the default\\\", like the host\\n    p = _resolve(path)\\n    if p.is_dir():\\n        if offset > 0 or limit > 0:\\n            # usage-level: the flags contradict the input kind (64, not 65)\\n            raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, \\\"cannot read a line range of a directory; list it without offset/limit\\\")\\n        # byte-identical to the host: suffixed names, plain lexicographic sort,\\n        # dotfiles INCLUDED (only grep hides them)\\n        entries = sorted(e.name + (\\\"/\\\" if e.is_dir() else \\\"\\\") for e in p.iterdir())\\n        return Result(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(entries) if entries else \\\"(empty directory)\\\")\\n    try:\\n        text = _read_text(p)\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        raise CommandError(EX_NOINPUT, f\\\"file not found: {path}\\\") from None\\n    if offset > 0 or limit > 0:\\n        return _read_range(text, offset, limit, limit_chars)\\n    if len(text) > limit_chars:\\n        # point the caller at the first unread line instead of re-serving the same head\\n        head = text[:limit_chars]\\n        next_offset = head.count(\\\"\\\\n\\\") + 1\\n        text = head + f\\\"\\\\n... [truncated, file is {len(text)} chars; use offset={next_offset} to continue]\\\"\\n    return Result(text)\\n\\n\\ndef _read_range(text: str, offset: int, limit: int, limit_chars: int) -> Result:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Lines [offset, offset+limit) (1-based) with line numbers; a range that\\n    cannot fit the char budget is an ERROR, not a silent truncation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    lines = text.splitlines()\\n    total = len(lines)\\n    start = max(0, offset - 1) if offset > 0 else 0\\n    end = start + limit if limit > 0 else total\\n    selected = lines[start:end]\\n    body = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(f\\\"{i + 1}: {ln}\\\" for i, ln in enumerate(selected, start=start))\\n    if len(body) > limit_chars:\\n        raise CommandError(\\n            EX_DATAERR,\\n            f\\\"the requested range (lines {start + 1}-{end}) exceeds the read limit of \\\"\\n            f\\\"{limit_chars} chars. Use a smaller limit, or search with grep instead.\\\",\\n        )\\n    shown = start + len(selected)\\n    if shown < total:\\n        body += f\\\"\\\\n... (showing lines {start + 1}-{shown} of {total}; use offset={shown + 1} to continue)\\\"\\n    return Result(body)\\n\\n\\ndef write_file(path: str, content: str) -> Result:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Create or overwrite a file (parents auto-created); summary plus a\\n    unified diff against the previous content, if there was one.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    p = _resolve(path)\\n    old = \\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        old = _read_text(p)\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        pass\\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    # newline=\\\"\\\\n\\\": byte-exact on every host (the host's LocalWorkspace rule —\\n    # Windows text mode must not expand \\\\n into \\\\r\\\\n)\\n    p.write_text(content, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\", newline=\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n    rel = _rel(p)\\n    diff = _unified_diff(old, content, rel)\\n    adds, dels = _count_changes(diff)\\n    # the path in the summary is echoed as given (not absolutized) — see review notes\\n    if old:\\n        return Result(f\\\"OK: wrote {path} (+{adds} -{dels} lines)\\\", diff=diff)\\n    return Result(f\\\"OK: wrote {path} ({len(content)} chars)\\\", diff=diff)\\n\\n\\ndef edit_file(path: str, old_string: str, new_string: str) -> Result:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Targeted string replacement: exactly one occurrence of old_string\\n    becomes new_string (tiny diffs keep the context small instead of\\n    re-emitting the whole file).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    p = _resolve(path)\\n    try:\\n        text = _read_text(p)\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        raise CommandError(EX_NOINPUT, f\\\"file not found: {path} — use write_file to create it\\\") from None\\n    if not old_string:\\n        raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, \\\"old_string is required\\\")\\n    count = text.count(old_string)\\n    if count == 0:\\n        raise CommandError(EX_DATAERR, f\\\"old_string not found in {path}\\\")\\n    if count > 1:\\n        raise CommandError(EX_DATAERR, f\\\"old_string appears {count} times in {path}\\\")\\n    new = text.replace(old_string, new_string, 1)\\n    p.write_text(new, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\", newline=\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n    diff = _unified_diff(text, new, _rel(p))\\n    adds, dels = _count_changes(diff)\\n    return Result(f\\\"OK: edited {path} (+{adds} -{dels} lines)\\\", diff=diff)\\n\\n\\ndef grep(pattern: str, path: str = \\\".\\\", include: str = \\\"\\\") -> Result:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Regex search over text files under path, capped at 100 hits, grouped\\n    per file with a blank line between groups.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        rx = re.compile(pattern)\\n    except re.error as e:\\n        # the pattern is caller-built input; a syntax error in it is a usage\\n        # fault (\\\"bad syntax in a parameter\\\" in sysexits terms) — 64, not 65\\n        raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, f\\\"invalid regex: {e}\\\") from None\\n    root = _resolve(path)\\n    if not root.is_file() and not root.is_dir():\\n        raise CommandError(EX_NOINPUT, f\\\"file not found: {path}\\\")\\n    files = [root] if root.is_file() else _grep_files(root)\\n    out: list[tuple[str, int, str]] = []\\n    for f in files:\\n        rel = _rel(f)\\n        if include and not (fnmatch.fnmatch(f.name, include) or fnmatch.fnmatch(rel, include)):\\n            continue\\n        if _is_binary(f):\\n            continue\\n        try:\\n            with open(f, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\") as fh:\\n                for i, line in enumerate(fh, 1):\\n                    if rx.search(line):\\n                        out.append((rel, i, line.rstrip(\\\"\\\\n\\\")))\\n                        if len(out) >= _GREP_MAX_HITS:\\n                            break\\n        except OSError:\\n            continue\\n        if len(out) >= _GREP_MAX_HITS:\\n            break\\n    if not out:\\n        return Result(\\\"(no matches)\\\")\\n    lines: list[str] = []\\n    current: str | None = None\\n    for fpath, lineno, text in out:\\n        if current != fpath:\\n            if current is not None:\\n                lines.append(\\\"\\\")\\n            current = fpath\\n            lines.append(f\\\"{fpath}:\\\")\\n        lines.append(f\\\"  Line {lineno}: {text[:_GREP_LINE_MAX]}\\\")\\n    content = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines)\\n    if len(out) >= _GREP_MAX_HITS:\\n        content += \\\"\\\\n\\\\n(Results capped at 100; use a more specific pattern or path.)\\\"\\n    return Result(content)\\n\\n\\ndef _grep_files(dirpath: Path) -> list[Path]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Recursive walk, sorted, skipping dot-entries and __pycache__ (the\\n    host's rule: hidden files are invisible to grep but visible to read).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    files: list[Path] = []\\n    for ent in sorted(dirpath.iterdir()):\\n        if ent.name.startswith(\\\".\\\") or ent.name == \\\"__pycache__\\\":\\n            continue\\n        if ent.is_dir():\\n            files.extend(_grep_files(ent))\\n        elif ent.is_file():\\n            files.append(ent)\\n    return files\\n\\n\\ndef _is_binary(p: Path) -> bool:\\n    try:\\n        with open(p, \\\"rb\\\") as f:\\n            return b\\\"\\\\x00\\\" in f.read(1024)\\n    except OSError:\\n        return True\\n\\n\\ndef _resolve(path: str) -> Path:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"cwd-flavored mirror of LocalWorkspace.resolve: anchor relative paths at\\n    the process CWD, resolve symlinks in the parent chain, keep the final\\n    component unresolved (a project-local symlink must still open as itself).\\n    No containment: whatever this returns is the file — the caller picked\\n    the cwd, so the caller picked the fence.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    base = Path.cwd().resolve() / path\\n    try:\\n        if base.name:\\n            return base.parent.resolve() / base.name\\n    except OSError:\\n        pass\\n    return base.resolve()\\n\\n\\ndef _read_text(p: Path) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The host's LocalWorkspace.read: a non-file (dir, missing) is\\n    FileNotFoundError; text is utf-8 with replacement, never an exception.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not p.is_file():\\n        raise FileNotFoundError(str(p))\\n    return p.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _rel(p: Path) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"CWD-relative display form (the host shows workspace-relative paths in\\n    diff headers and grep groups); outside the CWD it falls back to absolute.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        return str(p.relative_to(Path.cwd().resolve()))\\n    except ValueError:\\n        return str(p)\\n\\n\\ndef _unified_diff(old: str, new: str, rel: str) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Unified diff between old and new file contents (difflib, n=3 context).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    diff_lines = difflib.unified_diff(\\n        old.splitlines(keepends=True),\\n        new.splitlines(keepends=True),\\n        fromfile=f\\\"a/{rel}\\\",\\n        tofile=f\\\"b/{rel}\\\",\\n        n=3,\\n    )\\n    return \\\"\\\".join(diff_lines)\\n\\n\\ndef _count_changes(diff: str) -> tuple[int, int]:\\n    adds = sum(1 for ln in diff.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\\\"+\\\") and not ln.startswith(\\\"+++\\\"))\\n    dels = sum(1 for ln in diff.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\\\"-\\\") and not ln.startswith(\\\"---\\\"))\\n    return adds, dels\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_a59a02c77a2b43c790c202ff"}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "1751158eb4f0", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/cli.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Flag wiring: argparse -> filesystem commands -> envelope out.\\n\\n  clutch-workspace [--json] <command> [flags]\\n\\n- human (default): content on stdout (plus the unified diff for\\n  write/edit), `ERROR: <brief>` on stderr, sysexits code as exit status\\n- --json: ONE compact {\\\"content\\\", \\\"error\\\", \\\"diff\\\"} line on stdout for\\n  BOTH outcomes; callers parse stdout plus the exit code, never prose.\\n  It is a global flag and must precede the subcommand.\\nA payload flag value of `-` reads the value from stdin (write_file\\n--content, edit_file --old-string/--new-string) so bodies beyond the\\nWindows 32K argv limit still get through. Only ONE flag per invocation\\nmay use `-` — two would drain the same stream twice.\\n\\nUsage errors (bad flags, unknown command, contradictory arguments —\\nargparse's own included) exit 64; I/O failures 74; a bug that escapes is\\n70, never masquerading as caller error.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport traceback\\n\\nfrom . import __version__, filesystem\\nfrom .envelope import CommandError, Result, emit_error, emit_result\\nfrom .exitcodes import EX_IOERR, EX_SIGINT, EX_SOFTWARE, EX_USAGE\\nfrom .filesystem import READ_MAX_CHARS\\n\\n\\nclass _Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\\n    def error(self, message: str):  # argparse's default is 2; our contract is 64\\n        self.print_usage(sys.stderr)\\n        self.exit(EX_USAGE, f\\\"{self.prog}: error: {message}\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\\n    parser = _Parser(\\n        prog=\\\"clutch-workspace\\\",\\n        description=\\\"Standalone file-inspection CLI: read_file / grep / write_file / edit_file.\\\",\\n        allow_abbrev=False,\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--json\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"emit one JSON envelope line on stdout instead of human text\\\")\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--version\\\", action=\\\"version\\\", version=f\\\"clutch-workspace {__version__}\\\")\\n    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\\\"command\\\", metavar=\\\"<command>\\\", required=True)\\n\\n    read = sub.add_parser(\\\"read_file\\\", help=\\\"read a file (or list a directory); numbered ranges with continuation hints\\\")\\n    read.add_argument(\\\"--path\\\", required=True, help=\\\"file or directory, relative to the process CWD\\\")\\n    read.add_argument(\\\"--offset\\\", type=int, default=0, metavar=\\\"N\\\", help=\\\"1-based first line\\\")\\n    read.add_argument(\\\"--limit\\\", type=int, default=0, metavar=\\\"N\\\", help=\\\"max lines to return\\\")\\n    read.add_argument(\\\"--max-chars\\\", type=int, default=READ_MAX_CHARS, metavar=\\\"N\\\", help=f\\\"char budget before truncation (default {READ_MAX_CHARS})\\\")\\n\\n    search = sub.add_parser(\\\"grep\\\", help=\\\"regex search over text files, capped at 100 hits\\\")\\n    search.add_argument(\\\"--pattern\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Python regex\\\")\\n    search.add_argument(\\\"--path\\\", default=\\\".\\\", help=\\\"file or directory to search (default: the CWD)\\\")\\n    search.add_argument(\\\"--include\\\", default=\\\"\\\", metavar=\\\"GLOB\\\", help=\\\"fnmatch filter on file name or CWD-relative path\\\")\\n\\n    write = sub.add_parser(\\\"write_file\\\", help=\\\"create or overwrite a file (parents auto-created); prints a unified diff\\\")\\n    write.add_argument(\\\"--path\\\", required=True)\\n    write.add_argument(\\\"--content\\\", required=True, help=\\\"new file body; `-` reads stdin\\\")\\n\\n    edit = sub.add_parser(\\\"edit_file\\\", help=\\\"replace exactly one occurrence of old_string; prints a unified diff\\\")\\n    edit.add_argument(\\\"--path\\\", required=True)\\n    edit.add_argument(\\\"--old-string\\\", required=True, dest=\\\"old_string\\\", help=\\\"exact text to find; `-` reads stdin\\\")\\n    edit.add_argument(\\\"--new-string\\\", required=True, dest=\\\"new_string\\\", help=\\\"replacement text; `-` reads stdin\\\")\\n    return parser\\n\\n\\ndef _payload(value: str) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"`-` = the value arrives on stdin (Windows argv caps at ~32K).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return sys.stdin.read() if value == \\\"-\\\" else value\\n\\n\\ndef _check_args(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Flag combos argparse cannot express (negative numbers are caller bugs,\\n    not data problems — usage fault, 64).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if args.command != \\\"read_file\\\":\\n        return\\n    for name in (\\\"offset\\\", \\\"limit\\\", \\\"max_chars\\\"):\\n        if getattr(args, name) < 0:\\n            raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, f\\\"--{name.replace('_', '-')} must be >= 0\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _dispatch(args: argparse.Namespace) -> Result:\\n    if args.command == \\\"read_file\\\":\\n        return filesystem.read_file(args.path, offset=args.offset, limit=args.limit, max_chars=args.max_chars)\\n    if args.command == \\\"grep\\\":\\n        return filesystem.grep(args.pattern, path=args.path, include=args.include)\\n    if args.command == \\\"write_file\\\":\\n        return filesystem.write_file(args.path, content=_payload(args.content))\\n    if args.command == \\\"edit_file\\\":\\n        if args.old_string == \\\"-\\\" and args.new_string == \\\"-\\\":\\n            raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, \\\"only one of --old-string/--new-string may read stdin ('-')\\\")\\n        return filesystem.edit_file(\\n            args.path,\\n            old_string=_payload(args.old_string),\\n            new_string=_payload(args.new_string),\\n        )\\n    raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, f\\\"unknown command: {args.command}\\\")  # unreachable: subparsers required\\n\\n\\ndef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\\n    for stream in (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr):\\n        try:\\n            stream.reconfigure(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        except (AttributeError, OSError, ValueError):\\n            pass\\n    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)  # usage errors exit 64 straight from here\\n    try:\\n        _check_args(args)\\n        result = _dispatch(args)\\n    except CommandError as err:\\n        emit_error(err, as_json=args.json)\\n        return err.code\\n    except BrokenPipeError:\\n        return _silence_broken_pipe()\\n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\\n        emit_error(CommandError(EX_SIGINT, \\\"interrupted\\\"), as_json=args.json)\\n        return EX_SIGINT\\n    except OSError as err:\\n        emit_error(CommandError(EX_IOERR, str(err)), as_json=args.json)\\n        return EX_IOERR\\n    except Exception as err:  # noqa: BLE001 - the one catch-all: name it a bug\\n        traceback.print_exc()\\n        emit_error(CommandError(EX_SOFTWARE, f\\\"internal error: {err}\\\"), as_json=args.json)\\n        return EX_SOFTWARE\\n    emit_result(result, as_json=args.json)\\n    return 0\\n\\n\\ndef _silence_broken_pipe() -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Keep the interpreter's shutdown flush from re-raising on the dead pipe.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        os.dup2(os.open(os.devnull, os.O_WRONLY), sys.stdout.fileno())\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):\\n        pass\\n    return EX_IOERR\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_692745ea790d40e5b83862c8"}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "a390bd34c620", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/__main__.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"`python -m clutch_workspace` — the same entry the console script wraps.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom .cli import main\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    raise SystemExit(main())\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_6b6dd5083ee2459a8f4273de"}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "74b82468c18b", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/tests/conftest.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Black-box harness: every test drives the real CLI as a subprocess\\n(`python -m clutch_workspace`), the way the host transport will — no imports\\nof the module under test for behavior, only for the exit-code table.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport subprocess\\nimport sys\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nif str(ROOT) not in sys.path:  # lets tests import clutch_workspace for constants\\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\\n\\n\\ndef _run(*args: object, cwd: Path | str, stdin: str | None = None):\\n    env = dict(os.environ, PYTHONPATH=str(ROOT), PYTHONUTF8=\\\"1\\\")\\n    return subprocess.run(\\n        [sys.executable, \\\"-m\\\", \\\"clutch_workspace\\\", *(str(a) for a in args)],\\n        cwd=str(cwd),\\n        input=stdin,\\n        capture_output=True,\\n        text=True,\\n        encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\",\\n        env=env,\\n    )\\n\\n\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef run(tmp_path: Path):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Raw runner, cwd defaults to the test's tmp workspace.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def _run_cwd(*args: object, cwd: Path | str | None = None, stdin: str | None = None):\\n        return _run(*args, cwd=cwd if cwd is not None else tmp_path, stdin=stdin)\\n\\n    return _run_cwd\\n\\n\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef jok(run):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"--json run that must succeed: returns the parsed envelope dict.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def _jok(*args: object, **kw):\\n        proc = run(\\\"--json\\\", *args, **kw)\\n        assert proc.returncode == 0, f\\\"stdout={proc.stdout!r} stderr={proc.stderr!r}\\\"\\n        return json.loads(proc.stdout)\\n\\n    return _jok\\n\\n\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef jerr(run):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"--json run that must fail with an envelope: returns (exit_code, env).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def _jerr(*args: object, **kw):\\n        proc = run(\\\"--json\\\", *args, **kw)\\n        assert proc.returncode != 0, f\\\"stdout={proc.stdout!r} stderr={proc.stderr!r}\\\"\\n        assert proc.stdout.count(\\\"\\\\n\\\") == 1, f\\\"envelope must be one line, got {proc.stdout!r}\\\"\\n        return proc.returncode, json.loads(proc.stdout)\\n\\n    return _jerr\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_91fb5088b37944a1a3f76b67"}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "bf4560e1890f", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/tests/test_read.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"read_file: raw reads, numbered ranges, truncation hints, directory listings.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_DATAERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\\n\\nDATA = \\\"l1\\\\nl2\\\\nl3\\\\nl4\\\\nl5\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_raw_read_has_no_line_numbers(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == DATA\\n    assert env[\\\"error\\\"] is False and env[\\\"diff\\\"] == \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_human_read_prints_content_plus_newline(run, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"abc\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    proc = run(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == 0\\n    assert proc.stdout == \\\"abc\\\\n\\\"\\n    assert proc.stderr == \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_range_is_numbered_with_continuation_hint(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--offset\\\", 2, \\\"--limit\\\", 2)\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"2: l2\\\\n3: l3\\\\n... (showing lines 2-3 of 5; use offset=4 to continue)\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_range_from_middle_to_eof_has_no_hint(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--offset\\\", 4)[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"4: l4\\\\n5: l5\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_limit_only_starts_at_line_one(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--limit\\\", 2)\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"1: l1\\\\n2: l2\\\\n... (showing lines 1-2 of 5; use offset=3 to continue)\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_range_over_budget_is_dataerr_not_truncation(jerr, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--offset\\\", 1, \\\"--limit\\\", 4, \\\"--max-chars\\\", 10)\\n    assert code == EX_DATAERR\\n    assert env[\\\"error\\\"] is True\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == (\\n        \\\"the requested range (lines 1-4) exceeds the read limit of 10 chars. \\\"\\n        \\\"Use a smaller limit, or search with grep instead.\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef test_offset_past_eof_returns_empty_ok(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--offset\\\", 99)[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_whole_file_truncation_points_at_next_line(jok, tmp_path):\\n    text = \\\"x\\\" * 30000\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(text, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"x\\\" * 20000 + \\\"\\\\n... [truncated, file is 30000 chars; use offset=1 to continue]\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_truncation_hint_uses_first_unread_line(jok, tmp_path):\\n    text = \\\"0123456789\\\\n\\\" * 3000  # 33000 chars, 3000 lines\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(text, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    head = text[:20000]\\n    env = jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == head + f\\\"\\\\n... [truncated, file is {len(text)} chars; use offset={head.count(chr(10)) + 1} to continue]\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_max_chars_flag(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"0123456789ABCDEF\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--max-chars\\\", 10)\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"0123456789\\\\n... [truncated, file is 16 chars; use offset=1 to continue]\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_directory_lists_entries_dirs_get_slash(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"sub\\\").mkdir()\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"b.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"A.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    (tmp_path / \\\".hidden\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")  # read shows dotfiles; only grep hides them\\n    assert jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\".\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\".hidden\\\\nA.txt\\\\nb.txt\\\\nsub/\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_empty_directory(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"empty\\\").mkdir()\\n    assert jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"empty\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"(empty directory)\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_directory_with_range_flags_is_usage_error(jerr, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"sub\\\").mkdir()\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"sub\\\", \\\"--offset\\\", 1)\\n    assert code == EX_USAGE\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"cannot read a line range of a directory; list it without offset/limit\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_missing_file_is_noinput(jerr, tmp_path):\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"nope.txt\\\")\\n    assert code == EX_NOINPUT\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"file not found: nope.txt\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_undecodable_bytes_read_with_replacement(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"latin.txt\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"caf\\\\xe9\\\\n\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"latin.txt\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"caf\\\\ufffd\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_crlf_reads_as_lf(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"win.txt\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\\r\\\\n\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"win.txt\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"a\\\\nb\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_negative_flags_are_usage(jerr, tmp_path):\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--offset\\\", -1)\\n    assert code == EX_USAGE\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"--offset must be >= 0\\\"\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_9f8ae27bb3c341f5a88d2710"}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "5a9f1e74207d", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/tests/test_grep.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"grep: hit format, filters, skips, the 100 cap, error cases.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport os\\n\\nfrom clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\\n\\n\\ndef test_hits_grouped_per_file_with_blank_line_between(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"g1.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"hit_a\\\\nhit_b\\\\nnope\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"g2.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\\nhit_c\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    assert (\\n        jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"hit\\\")[\\\"content\\\"]\\n        == \\\"g1.txt:\\\\n  Line 1: hit_a\\\\n  Line 2: hit_b\\\\n\\\\ng2.txt:\\\\n  Line 2: hit_c\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef test_no_matches(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"nothing here\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"zzz\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"(no matches)\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_python_regex_dialect(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.py\\\").write_text(\\\"def  one():\\\\nreturn 1\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", r\\\"^def \\\\w+\\\\(\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"f.py:\\\\n  Line 1: def  one():\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_include_filters_by_name(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"a.py\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"a.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    content = jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"needle\\\", \\\"--include\\\", \\\"*.py\\\")[\\\"content\\\"]\\n    assert \\\"a.py:\\\" in content\\n    assert \\\"a.txt\\\" not in content\\n\\n\\ndef test_include_filters_by_relative_path(jok, tmp_path):\\n    sub = tmp_path / \\\"sub\\\"\\n    sub.mkdir()\\n    (sub / \\\"b.py\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"a.py\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    content = jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"needle\\\", \\\"--include\\\", \\\"sub/*\\\")[\\\"content\\\"]\\n    assert f\\\"sub{os.sep}b.py:\\\" in content\\n    assert \\\"a.py\\\" not in content\\n\\n\\ndef test_path_subdir_limits_search(jok, tmp_path):\\n    sub = tmp_path / \\\"sub\\\"\\n    sub.mkdir()\\n    (sub / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"top.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    content = jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"needle\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"sub\\\")[\\\"content\\\"]\\n    assert f\\\"sub{os.sep}f.txt:\\\" in content\\n    assert \\\"top.txt\\\" not in content\\n\\n\\ndef test_single_file_as_path(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"one\\\\ntwo needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"needle\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"f.txt:\\\\n  Line 2: two needle\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_hidden_and_pycache_are_skipped(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\".secrets.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    cache = tmp_path / \\\"__pycache__\\\"\\n    cache.mkdir()\\n    (cache / \\\"x.py\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"needle\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"(no matches)\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_explicit_dotfile_path_is_searched(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\".secrets.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"needle\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    content = jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"needle\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\".secrets.txt\\\")[\\\"content\\\"]\\n    assert content == \\\".secrets.txt:\\\\n  Line 1: needle\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_binary_file_skipped(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"bin.dat\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"ok\\\\x00binary\\\" + b\\\"\\\\nneedle\\\\n\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"needle\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"(no matches)\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_nul_after_first_1024_bytes_is_not_binary(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"late.bin\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"z\\\" * 1024 + b\\\"\\\\x00 and needle\\\\n\\\")\\n    content = jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"needle\\\")[\\\"content\\\"]\\n    assert \\\"  Line 1: \\\" in content\\n\\n\\ndef test_capped_at_100_with_footer(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"big.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"hit\\\\n\\\" * 120, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    content = jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"hit\\\")[\\\"content\\\"]\\n    assert content.endswith(\\\"(Results capped at 100; use a more specific pattern or path.)\\\")\\n    assert \\\"  Line 100: hit\\\" in content\\n    assert \\\"  Line 101:\\\" not in content\\n\\n\\ndef test_lines_truncated_at_300_chars(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"long.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"y\\\" * 400 + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    assert jok(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"y\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"long.txt:\\\\n  Line 1: \\\" + \\\"y\\\" * 300\\n\\n\\ndef test_bad_regex_is_usage_error(jerr):\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"(\\\")\\n    assert code == EX_USAGE\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"].startswith(\\\"invalid regex: \\\")\\n\\n\\ndef test_missing_search_root_is_noinput(jerr):\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"grep\\\", \\\"--pattern\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"nope_dir\\\")\\n    assert code == EX_NOINPUT\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"file not found: nope_dir\\\"\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_aa5192c20e014f84b6b74cc2"}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "2af2e5ee0773", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/tests/test_write.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"write_file: creation, overwrite diffs, newline law, error surface.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_IOERR\\n\\n\\ndef test_create_new_file(jok, tmp_path):\\n    env = jok(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"new.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"hello\\\\n\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"OK: wrote new.txt (6 chars)\\\"\\n    assert env[\\\"diff\\\"] == \\\"--- a/new.txt\\\\n+++ b/new.txt\\\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\\\n+hello\\\\n\\\"\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"new.txt\\\").read_bytes() == b\\\"hello\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_parents_auto_created(jok, tmp_path):\\n    env = jok(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"sub/dir/new.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"x\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"OK: wrote sub/dir/new.txt (1 chars)\\\"\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"sub\\\" / \\\"dir\\\" / \\\"new.txt\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") == \\\"x\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_overwrite_reports_added_removed_lines(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"old\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"new\\\\n\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"OK: wrote f.txt (+1 -1 lines)\\\"\\n    assert env[\\\"diff\\\"] == \\\"--- a/f.txt\\\\n+++ b/f.txt\\\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\\\n-old\\\\n+new\\\\n\\\"\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") == \\\"new\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_noop_rewrite_has_empty_diff(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"same\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"same\\\\n\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"OK: wrote f.txt (+0 -0 lines)\\\"\\n    assert env[\\\"diff\\\"] == \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_empty_content_new_file(jok, tmp_path):\\n    env = jok(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"empty.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"OK: wrote empty.txt (0 chars)\\\"\\n    assert env[\\\"diff\\\"] == \\\"\\\"\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"empty.txt\\\").read_bytes() == b\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_content_lf_normalized_on_disk(jok, tmp_path):\\n    jok(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\")\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_bytes() == b\\\"a\\\\nb\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_trailing_newline_preserved_exactly(jok, tmp_path):\\n    jok(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"no-newline\\\")\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_bytes() == b\\\"no-newline\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_human_mode_prints_summary_then_diff(run, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"old\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    proc = run(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"new\\\\n\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == 0\\n    assert proc.stdout == \\\"OK: wrote f.txt (+1 -1 lines)\\\\n--- a/f.txt\\\\n+++ b/f.txt\\\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\\\n-old\\\\n+new\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_stdin_payload_via_dash(run, tmp_path):\\n    proc = run(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"-\\\", stdin=\\\"from stdin\\\\n\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == 0\\n    assert \\\"OK: wrote f.txt (11 chars)\\\" in proc.stdout\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") == \\\"from stdin\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_parent_is_a_file_is_io_error(jerr, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"blocker\\\").write_text(\\\"just a file\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"blocker/child.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"x\\\")\\n    assert code == EX_IOERR\\n    assert env[\\\"error\\\"] is True\\n\\n\\ndef test_utf8_body_survives_json_roundtrip(jok, tmp_path):\\n    jok(\\\"write_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"cn.txt\\\", \\\"--content\\\", \\\"中文内容\\\\n\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"cn.txt\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"中文内容\\\\n\\\"\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_dac54e1489dc40dcbdd31ce6"}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "5c6537655fd7", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/tests/test_edit.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"edit_file: single-occurrence replacement and its error codes.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_DATAERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\\n\\n\\ndef test_unique_replacement(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"alpha\\\\nbeta\\\\ngamma\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"edit_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--old-string\\\", \\\"beta\\\", \\\"--new-string\\\", \\\"BETA\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"OK: edited f.txt (+1 -1 lines)\\\"\\n    assert \\\"-beta\\\\n+BETA\\\" in env[\\\"diff\\\"]\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") == \\\"alpha\\\\nBETA\\\\ngamma\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_multiline_old_and_new(jok, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    env = jok(\\\"edit_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--old-string\\\", \\\"a\\\\nb\\\", \\\"--new-string\\\", \\\"x\\\")\\n    assert env[\\\"diff\\\"] == \\\"--- a/f.txt\\\\n+++ b/f.txt\\\\n@@ -1,3 +1,2 @@\\\\n-a\\\\n-b\\\\n+x\\\\n c\\\\n\\\"\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") == \\\"x\\\\nc\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_zero_occurrences_is_dataerr_and_file_untouched(jerr, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"keep\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"edit_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--old-string\\\", \\\"zzz\\\", \\\"--new-string\\\", \\\"x\\\")\\n    assert code == EX_DATAERR\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"old_string not found in f.txt\\\"\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") == \\\"keep\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_ambiguous_occurrences_is_dataerr(jerr, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\\nx\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"edit_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--old-string\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"--new-string\\\", \\\"y\\\")\\n    assert code == EX_DATAERR\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"old_string appears 2 times in f.txt\\\"\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") == \\\"x\\\\nx\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_missing_file_is_noinput_with_hint(jerr):\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"edit_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"new.txt\\\", \\\"--old-string\\\", \\\"a\\\", \\\"--new-string\\\", \\\"b\\\")\\n    assert code == EX_NOINPUT\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"file not found: new.txt — use write_file to create it\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_empty_old_string_is_usage(jerr, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    code, env = jerr(\\\"edit_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--old-string\\\", \\\"\\\", \\\"--new-string\\\", \\\"y\\\")\\n    assert code == EX_USAGE\\n    assert env[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"old_string is required\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_stdin_payload_via_dash(run, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"count: 1\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    proc = run(\\\"edit_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--old-string\\\", \\\"-\\\", \\\"--new-string\\\", \\\"N\\\",\\n               stdin=\\\"count: 1\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == 0\\n    assert (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") == \\\"N\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_two_stdin_flags_rejected(run):\\n    proc = run(\\\"edit_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--old-string\\\", \\\"-\\\", \\\"--new-string\\\", \\\"-\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == 64\\n    assert \\\"only one of --old-string/--new-string may read stdin\\\" in proc.stderr\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_5ad41b227f4d43a885609177"}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789894127.5278153, "id": "dadf129a5ae8", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/tests/test_cli.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"CLI surface: envelope shape, --json placement, exit-code contract, exotic failures.\\n\\nThe black-box tests go through subprocesses; the three failure paths that are\\nawkward to provoke in a child (broken pipe, SIGINT, internal bug) run main()\\nin-process with patched streams/collaborators.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom clutch_workspace import cli\\nfrom clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_IOERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_SIGINT, EX_SOFTWARE, EX_USAGE\\n\\n\\ndef test_version(run):\\n    proc = run(\\\"--version\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == 0\\n    assert proc.stdout == \\\"clutch-workspace 0.1.0\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_no_args_prints_usage_and_exits_64(run):\\n    proc = run()\\n    assert proc.returncode == EX_USAGE\\n    assert proc.stderr.startswith(\\\"usage:\\\")\\n    assert \\\"error:\\\" in proc.stderr\\n\\n\\ndef test_unknown_command_is_64(run):\\n    assert run(\\\"frobnicate\\\").returncode == EX_USAGE\\n\\n\\ndef test_missing_required_flag_is_64(run):\\n    assert run(\\\"read_file\\\").returncode == EX_USAGE\\n\\n\\ndef test_json_must_precede_the_subcommand(run, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    assert run(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\", \\\"--json\\\").returncode == EX_USAGE\\n    assert run(\\\"--json\\\", \\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\").returncode == 0\\n\\n\\ndef test_envelope_success_shape(run, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    proc = run(\\\"--json\\\", \\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\")\\n    assert proc.stdout.count(\\\"\\\\n\\\") == 1  # ONE compact line\\n    env = json.loads(proc.stdout)\\n    assert set(env) == {\\\"content\\\", \\\"error\\\", \\\"diff\\\"}\\n    assert env == {\\\"content\\\": \\\"x\\\", \\\"error\\\": False, \\\"diff\\\": \\\"\\\"}\\n\\n\\ndef test_envelope_error_shape_and_exit_code(run):\\n    proc = run(\\\"--json\\\", \\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"nope.txt\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == EX_NOINPUT\\n    assert json.loads(proc.stdout) == {\\\"content\\\": \\\"file not found: nope.txt\\\", \\\"error\\\": True, \\\"diff\\\": \\\"\\\"}\\n\\n\\ndef test_human_errors_go_to_stderr(run):\\n    proc = run(\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"nope.txt\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == EX_NOINPUT\\n    assert proc.stdout == \\\"\\\"\\n    assert proc.stderr == \\\"ERROR: file not found: nope.txt\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_json_body_is_not_ascii_escaped(run, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"cn.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"中文\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    proc = run(\\\"--json\\\", \\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"cn.txt\\\")\\n    assert \\\"中文\\\" in proc.stdout  # ensure_ascii=False\\n    assert json.loads(proc.stdout)[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"中文\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_help_lists_all_four_commands(run):\\n    proc = run(\\\"--help\\\")\\n    assert proc.returncode == 0\\n    for command in (\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"grep\\\", \\\"write_file\\\", \\\"edit_file\\\"):\\n        assert command in proc.stdout\\n\\n\\nclass _DeadPipe:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"stdout stand-in whose writes fail like a closed pipe downstream.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def write(self, *_args):\\n        raise BrokenPipeError\\n\\n    def fileno(self):\\n        raise ValueError  # keeps the dup2 cleanup away from the real fd 1\\n\\n    def reconfigure(self, **_kw):\\n        pass\\n\\n\\ndef test_broken_pipe_is_ioerr(monkeypatch, tmp_path):\\n    (tmp_path / \\\"f.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"x\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sys, \\\"stdout\\\", _DeadPipe())\\n    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)\\n    assert cli.main([\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\"]) == EX_IOERR\\n\\n\\ndef test_keyboard_interrupt_is_130(monkeypatch, tmp_path):\\n    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(cli.filesystem, \\\"read_file\\\", lambda *_a, **_k: (_ for _ in ()).throw(KeyboardInterrupt()))\\n    assert cli.main([\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\"]) == EX_SIGINT\\n\\n\\ndef test_internal_bug_is_70_with_traceback(monkeypatch, tmp_path, capsys):\\n    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(cli.filesystem, \\\"read_file\\\", lambda *_a, **_k: (_ for _ in ()).throw(RuntimeError(\\\"boom\\\")))\\n    assert cli.main([\\\"read_file\\\", \\\"--path\\\", \\\"f.txt\\\"]) == EX_SOFTWARE\\n    assert \\\"RuntimeError: boom\\\" in capsys.readouterr().err\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_b723bbb80f5b4634ac99ffee"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.614113, "id": "bf9884742ef3", "tool_call_id": "call_a59a02c77a2b43c790c202ff", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\filesystem.py (9912 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\filesystem.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\filesystem.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,244 @@\n+\"\"\"The four commands, ported 1:1 from the host's agent/tools/filesystem.py.\n+\n+Deltas are exactly the frozen \"pure capability\" cuts — nothing else:\n+- no Workspace object: paths resolve against the process CWD (`_resolve`),\n+  so \"the workspace\" is whatever cwd the caller spawns us with\n+- no protected set / snapshots / containment: every path is servable\n+- no error prose templates: failures raise CommandError(code, brief); the\n+  caller owns the long-form prose\n+- output-channel formats (hit grouping, continuation hints, the grep cap\n+  footer, \"(no matches)\", \"(empty directory)\") stay byte-identical to the\n+  host, so the host's prompt contract keeps holding verbatim\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import difflib\n+import fnmatch\n+import re\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+from .envelope import CommandError, Result\n+from .exitcodes import EX_DATAERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\n+\n+READ_MAX_CHARS = 20_000  # --max-chars default: the host's read budget\n+_GREP_MAX_HITS = 100\n+_GREP_LINE_MAX = 300\n+\n+\n+def read_file(path: str, offset: int = 0, limit: int = 0, max_chars: int = READ_MAX_CHARS) -> Result:\n+    \"\"\"Read a file (or, with no range flags, list a directory).\n+\n+    No range flags: raw text, truncated at the char budget with a hint that\n+    points at the first unread line. With range flags: 1-based numbered\n+    lines [offset, offset+limit) — a range that cannot fit the budget is an\n+    error, not a silent truncation.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    limit_chars = max_chars or READ_MAX_CHARS  # --max-chars 0 means \"the default\", like the host\n+    p = _resolve(path)\n+    if p.is_dir():\n+        if offset > 0 or limit > 0:\n+            # usage-level: the flags contradict the input kind (64, not 65)\n+            raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, \"cannot read a line range of a directory; list it without offset/limit\")\n+        # byte-identical to the host: suffixed names, plain lexicographic sort,\n+        # dotfiles INCLUDED (only grep hides them)\n+        entries = sorted(e.name + (\"/\" if e.is_dir() else \"\") for e in p.iterdir())\n+        return Result(\"\\n\".join(entries) if entries else \"(empty directory)\")\n+    try:\n+        text = _read_text(p)\n+    except FileNotFoundError:\n+        raise CommandError(EX_NOINPUT, f\"file not found: {path}\") from None\n+    if offset > 0 or limit > 0:\n+        return _read_range(text, offset, limit, limit_chars)\n+    if len(text) > limit_chars:\n+        # point the caller at the first unread line instead of re-serving the same head\n+        head = text[:limit_chars]\n+        next_offset = head.count(\"\\n\") + 1\n+        text = head + f\"\\n... [truncated, file is {len(text)} chars; use offset={next_offset} to continue]\"\n+    return Result(text)\n+\n+\n+def _read_range(text: str, offset: int, limit: int, limit_chars: int) -> Result:\n+    \"\"\"Lines [offset, offset+limit) (1-based) with line numbers; a range that\n+    cannot fit the char budget is an ERROR, not a silent truncation.\"\"\"\n+    lines = text.splitlines()\n+    total = len(lines)\n+    start = max(0, offset - 1) if offset > 0 else 0\n+    end = start + limit if limit > 0 else total\n+    selected = lines[start:end]\n+    body = \"\\n\".join(f\"{i + 1}: {ln}\" for i, ln in enumerate(selected, start=start))\n+    if len(body) > limit_chars:\n+        raise CommandError(\n+            EX_DATAERR,\n+            f\"the requested range (lines {start + 1}-{end}) exceeds the read limit of \"\n+            f\"{limit_chars} chars. Use a smaller limit, or search with grep instead.\",\n+        )\n+    shown = start + len(selected)\n+    if shown < total:\n+        body += f\"\\n... (showing lines {start + 1}-{shown} of {total}; use offset={shown + 1} to continue)\"\n+    return Result(body)\n+\n+\n+def write_file(path: str, content: str) -> Result:\n+    \"\"\"Create or overwrite a file (parents auto-created); summary plus a\n+    unified diff against the previous content, if there was one.\"\"\"\n+    p = _resolve(path)\n+    old = \"\"\n+    try:\n+        old = _read_text(p)\n+    except FileNotFoundError:\n+        pass\n+    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n+    # newline=\"\\n\": byte-exact on every host (the host's LocalWorkspace rule —\n+    # Windows text mode must not expand \\n into \\r\\n)\n+    p.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\")\n+    rel = _rel(p)\n+    diff = _unified_diff(old, content, rel)\n+    adds, dels = _count_changes(diff)\n+    # the path in the summary is echoed as given (not absolutized) — see review notes\n+    if old:\n+        return Result(f\"OK: wrote {path} (+{adds} -{dels} lines)\", diff=diff)\n+    return Result(f\"OK: wrote {path} ({len(content)} chars)\", diff=diff)\n+\n+\n+def edit_file(path: str, old_string: str, new_string: str) -> Result:\n+    \"\"\"Targeted string replacement: exactly one occurrence of old_string\n+    becomes new_string (tiny diffs keep the context small instead of\n+    re-emitting the whole file).\"\"\"\n+    p = _resolve(path)\n+    try:\n+        text = _read_text(p)\n+    except FileNotFoundError:\n+        raise CommandError(EX_NOINPUT, f\"file not found: {path} — use write_file to create it\") from None\n+    if not old_string:\n+        raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, \"old_string is required\")\n+    count = text.count(old_string)\n+    if count == 0:\n+        raise CommandError(EX_DATAERR, f\"old_string not found in {path}\")\n+    if count > 1:\n+        raise CommandError(EX_DATAERR, f\"old_string appears {count} times in {path}\")\n+    new = text.replace(old_string, new_string, 1)\n+    p.write_text(new, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\")\n+    diff = _unified_diff(text, new, _rel(p))\n+    adds, dels = _count_changes(diff)\n+    return Result(f\"OK: edited {path} (+{adds} -{dels} lines)\", diff=diff)\n+\n+\n+def grep(pattern: str, path: str = \".\", include: str = \"\") -> Result:\n+    \"\"\"Regex search over text files under path, capped at 100 hits, grouped\n+    per file with a blank line between groups.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        rx = re.compile(pattern)\n+    except re.error as e:\n+        # the pattern is caller-built input; a syntax error in it is a usage\n+        # fault (\"bad syntax in a parameter\" in sysexits terms) — 64, not 65\n+        raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, f\"invalid regex: {e}\") from None\n+    root = _resolve(path)\n+    if not root.is_file() and not root.is_dir():\n+        raise CommandError(EX_NOINPUT, f\"file not found: {path}\")\n+    files = [root] if root.is_file() else _grep_files(root)\n+    out: list[tuple[str, int, str]] = []\n+    for f in files:\n+        rel = _rel(f)\n+        if include and not (fnmatch.fnmatch(f.name, include) or fnmatch.fnmatch(rel, include)):\n+            continue\n+        if _is_binary(f):\n+            continue\n+        try:\n+            with open(f, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as fh:\n+                for i, line in enumerate(fh, 1):\n+                    if rx.search(line):\n+                        out.append((rel, i, line.rstrip(\"\\n\")))\n+                        if len(out) >= _GREP_MAX_HITS:\n+                            break\n+        except OSError:\n+            continue\n+        if len(out) >= _GREP_MAX_HITS:\n+            break\n+    if not out:\n+        return Result(\"(no matches)\")\n+    lines: list[str] = []\n+    current: str | None = None\n+    for fpath, lineno, text in out:\n+        if current != fpath:\n+            if current is not None:\n+                lines.append(\"\")\n+            current = fpath\n+            lines.append(f\"{fpath}:\")\n+        lines.append(f\"  Line {lineno}: {text[:_GREP_LINE_MAX]}\")\n+    content = \"\\n\".join(lines)\n+    if len(out) >= _GREP_MAX_HITS:\n+        content += \"\\n\\n(Results capped at 100; use a more specific pattern or path.)\"\n+    return Result(content)\n+\n+\n+def _grep_files(dirpath: Path) -> list[Path]:\n+    \"\"\"Recursive walk, sorted, skipping dot-entries and __pycache__ (the\n+    host's rule: hidden files are invisible to grep but visible to read).\"\"\"\n+    files: list[Path] = []\n+    for ent in sorted(dirpath.iterdir()):\n+        if ent.name.startswith(\".\") or ent.name == \"__pycache__\":\n+            continue\n+        if ent.is_dir():\n+            files.extend(_grep_files(ent))\n+        elif ent.is_file():\n+            files.append(ent)\n+    return files\n+\n+\n+def _is_binary(p: Path) -> bool:\n+    try:\n+        with open(p, \"rb\") as f:\n+            return b\"\\x00\" in f.read(1024)\n+    except OSError:\n+        return True\n+\n+\n+def _resolve(path: str) -> Path:\n+    \"\"\"cwd-flavored mirror of LocalWorkspace.resolve: anchor relative paths at\n+    the process CWD, resolve symlinks in the parent chain, keep the final\n+    component unresolved (a project-local symlink must still open as itself).\n+    No containment: whatever this returns is the file — the caller picked\n+    the cwd, so the caller picked the fence.\"\"\"\n+    base = Path.cwd().resolve() / path\n+    try:\n+        if base.name:\n+            return base.parent.resolve() / base.name\n+    except OSError:\n+        pass\n+    return base.resolve()\n+\n+\n+def _read_text(p: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"The host's LocalWorkspace.read: a non-file (dir, missing) is\n+    FileNotFoundError; text is utf-8 with replacement, never an exception.\"\"\"\n+    if not p.is_file():\n+        raise FileNotFoundError(str(p))\n+    return p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+\n+\n+def _rel(p: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"CWD-relative display form (the host shows workspace-relative paths in\n+    diff headers and grep groups); outside the CWD it falls back to absolute.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        return str(p.relative_to(Path.cwd().resolve()))\n+    except ValueError:\n+        return str(p)\n+\n+\n+def _unified_diff(old: str, new: str, rel: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Unified diff between old and new file contents (difflib, n=3 context).\"\"\"\n+    diff_lines = difflib.unified_diff(\n+        old.splitlines(keepends=True),\n+        new.splitlines(keepends=True),\n+        fromfile=f\"a/{rel}\",\n+        tofile=f\"b/{rel}\",\n+        n=3,\n+    )\n+    return \"\".join(diff_lines)\n+\n+\n+def _count_changes(diff: str) -> tuple[int, int]:\n+    adds = sum(1 for ln in diff.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\"+\") and not ln.startswith(\"+++\"))\n+    dels = sum(1 for ln in diff.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\"-\") and not ln.startswith(\"---\"))\n+    return adds, dels\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.6301284, "id": "41b463fb973b", "tool_call_id": "call_692745ea790d40e5b83862c8", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\cli.py (6434 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\cli.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\cli.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@\n+\"\"\"Flag wiring: argparse -> filesystem commands -> envelope out.\n+\n+  clutch-workspace [--json] <command> [flags]\n+\n+- human (default): content on stdout (plus the unified diff for\n+  write/edit), `ERROR: <brief>` on stderr, sysexits code as exit status\n+- --json: ONE compact {\"content\", \"error\", \"diff\"} line on stdout for\n+  BOTH outcomes; callers parse stdout plus the exit code, never prose.\n+  It is a global flag and must precede the subcommand.\n+A payload flag value of `-` reads the value from stdin (write_file\n+--content, edit_file --old-string/--new-string) so bodies beyond the\n+Windows 32K argv limit still get through. Only ONE flag per invocation\n+may use `-` — two would drain the same stream twice.\n+\n+Usage errors (bad flags, unknown command, contradictory arguments —\n+argparse's own included) exit 64; I/O failures 74; a bug that escapes is\n+70, never masquerading as caller error.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import argparse\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import traceback\n+\n+from . import __version__, filesystem\n+from .envelope import CommandError, Result, emit_error, emit_result\n+from .exitcodes import EX_IOERR, EX_SIGINT, EX_SOFTWARE, EX_USAGE\n+from .filesystem import READ_MAX_CHARS\n+\n+\n+class _Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\n+    def error(self, message: str):  # argparse's default is 2; our contract is 64\n+        self.print_usage(sys.stderr)\n+        self.exit(EX_USAGE, f\"{self.prog}: error: {message}\\n\")\n+\n+\n+def build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n+    parser = _Parser(\n+        prog=\"clutch-workspace\",\n+        description=\"Standalone file-inspection CLI: read_file / grep / write_file / edit_file.\",\n+        allow_abbrev=False,\n+    )\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--json\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"emit one JSON envelope line on stdout instead of human text\")\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--version\", action=\"version\", version=f\"clutch-workspace {__version__}\")\n+    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", metavar=\"<command>\", required=True)\n+\n+    read = sub.add_parser(\"read_file\", help=\"read a file (or list a directory); numbered ranges with continuation hints\")\n+    read.add_argument(\"--path\", required=True, help=\"file or directory, relative to the process CWD\")\n+    read.add_argument(\"--offset\", type=int, default=0, metavar=\"N\", help=\"1-based first line\")\n+    read.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=0, metavar=\"N\", help=\"max lines to return\")\n+    read.add_argument(\"--max-chars\", type=int, default=READ_MAX_CHARS, metavar=\"N\", help=f\"char budget before truncation (default {READ_MAX_CHARS})\")\n+\n+    search = sub.add_parser(\"grep\", help=\"regex search over text files, capped at 100 hits\")\n+    search.add_argument(\"--pattern\", required=True, help=\"Python regex\")\n+    search.add_argument(\"--path\", default=\".\", help=\"file or directory to search (default: the CWD)\")\n+    search.add_argument(\"--include\", default=\"\", metavar=\"GLOB\", help=\"fnmatch filter on file name or CWD-relative path\")\n+\n+    write = sub.add_parser(\"write_file\", help=\"create or overwrite a file (parents auto-created); prints a unified diff\")\n+    write.add_argument(\"--path\", required=True)\n+    write.add_argument(\"--content\", required=True, help=\"new file body; `-` reads stdin\")\n+\n+    edit = sub.add_parser(\"edit_file\", help=\"replace exactly one occurrence of old_string; prints a unified diff\")\n+    edit.add_argument(\"--path\", required=True)\n+    edit.add_argument(\"--old-string\", required=True, dest=\"old_string\", help=\"exact text to find; `-` reads stdin\")\n+    edit.add_argument(\"--new-string\", required=True, dest=\"new_string\", help=\"replacement text; `-` reads stdin\")\n+    return parser\n+\n+\n+def _payload(value: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"`-` = the value arrives on stdin (Windows argv caps at ~32K).\"\"\"\n+    return sys.stdin.read() if value == \"-\" else value\n+\n+\n+def _check_args(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Flag combos argparse cannot express (negative numbers are caller bugs,\n+    not data problems — usage fault, 64).\"\"\"\n+    if args.command != \"read_file\":\n+        return\n+    for name in (\"offset\", \"limit\", \"max_chars\"):\n+        if getattr(args, name) < 0:\n+            raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, f\"--{name.replace('_', '-')} must be >= 0\")\n+\n+\n+def _dispatch(args: argparse.Namespace) -> Result:\n+    if args.command == \"read_file\":\n+        return filesystem.read_file(args.path, offset=args.offset, limit=args.limit, max_chars=args.max_chars)\n+    if args.command == \"grep\":\n+        return filesystem.grep(args.pattern, path=args.path, include=args.include)\n+    if args.command == \"write_file\":\n+        return filesystem.write_file(args.path, content=_payload(args.content))\n+    if args.command == \"edit_file\":\n+        if args.old_string == \"-\" and args.new_string == \"-\":\n+            raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, \"only one of --old-string/--new-string may read stdin ('-')\")\n+        return filesystem.edit_file(\n+            args.path,\n+            old_string=_payload(args.old_string),\n+            new_string=_payload(args.new_string),\n+        )\n+    raise CommandError(EX_USAGE, f\"unknown command: {args.command}\")  # unreachable: subparsers required\n+\n+\n+def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n+    for stream in (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr):\n+        try:\n+            stream.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+        except (AttributeError, OSError, ValueError):\n+            pass\n+    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)  # usage errors exit 64 straight from here\n+    try:\n+        _check_args(args)\n+        result = _dispatch(args)\n+    except CommandError as err:\n+        emit_error(err, as_json=args.json)\n+        return err.code\n+    except BrokenPipeError:\n+        return _silence_broken_pipe()\n+    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n+        emit_error(CommandError(EX_SIGINT, \"interrupted\"), as_json=args.json)\n+        return EX_SIGINT\n+    except OSError as err:\n+        emit_error(CommandError(EX_IOERR, str(err)), as_json=args.json)\n+        return EX_IOERR\n+    except Exception as err:  # noqa: BLE001 - the one catch-all: name it a bug\n+        traceback.print_exc()\n+        emit_error(CommandError(EX_SOFTWARE, f\"internal error: {err}\"), as_json=args.json)\n+        return EX_SOFTWARE\n+    emit_result(result, as_json=args.json)\n+    return 0\n+\n+\n+def _silence_broken_pipe() -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Keep the interpreter's shutdown flush from re-raising on the dead pipe.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        os.dup2(os.open(os.devnull, os.O_WRONLY), sys.stdout.fileno())\n+    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):\n+        pass\n+    return EX_IOERR\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.6441338, "id": "608a59c60181", "tool_call_id": "call_6b6dd5083ee2459a8f4273de", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\__main__.py (158 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\__main__.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\__main__.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+\"\"\"`python -m clutch_workspace` — the same entry the console script wraps.\"\"\"\n+\n+from .cli import main\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    raise SystemExit(main())\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.6583693, "id": "a815ea89742c", "tool_call_id": "call_91fb5088b37944a1a3f76b67", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\tests\\conftest.py (1923 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\tests\\conftest.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\tests\\conftest.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@\n+\"\"\"Black-box harness: every test drives the real CLI as a subprocess\n+(`python -m clutch_workspace`), the way the host transport will — no imports\n+of the module under test for behavior, only for the exit-code table.\"\"\"\n+\n+import json\n+import os\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n+if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:  # lets tests import clutch_workspace for constants\n+    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n+\n+\n+def _run(*args: object, cwd: Path | str, stdin: str | None = None):\n+    env = dict(os.environ, PYTHONPATH=str(ROOT), PYTHONUTF8=\"1\")\n+    return subprocess.run(\n+        [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"clutch_workspace\", *(str(a) for a in args)],\n+        cwd=str(cwd),\n+        input=stdin,\n+        capture_output=True,\n+        text=True,\n+        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n+        env=env,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture\n+def run(tmp_path: Path):\n+    \"\"\"Raw runner, cwd defaults to the test's tmp workspace.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def _run_cwd(*args: object, cwd: Path | str | None = None, stdin: str | None = None):\n+        return _run(*args, cwd=cwd if cwd is not None else tmp_path, stdin=stdin)\n+\n+    return _run_cwd\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture\n+def jok(run):\n+    \"\"\"--json run that must succeed: returns the parsed envelope dict.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def _jok(*args: object, **kw):\n+        proc = run(\"--json\", *args, **kw)\n+        assert proc.returncode == 0, f\"stdout={proc.stdout!r} stderr={proc.stderr!r}\"\n+        return json.loads(proc.stdout)\n+\n+    return _jok\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture\n+def jerr(run):\n+    \"\"\"--json run that must fail with an envelope: returns (exit_code, env).\"\"\"\n+\n+    def _jerr(*args: object, **kw):\n+        proc = run(\"--json\", *args, **kw)\n+        assert proc.returncode != 0, f\"stdout={proc.stdout!r} stderr={proc.stderr!r}\"\n+        assert proc.stdout.count(\"\\n\") == 1, f\"envelope must be one line, got {proc.stdout!r}\"\n+        return proc.returncode, json.loads(proc.stdout)\n+\n+    return _jerr\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.668946, "id": "07b24813cf49", "tool_call_id": "call_9f8ae27bb3c341f5a88d2710", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_read.py (4784 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_read.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_read.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@\n+\"\"\"read_file: raw reads, numbered ranges, truncation hints, directory listings.\"\"\"\n+\n+from clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_DATAERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\n+\n+DATA = \"l1\\nl2\\nl3\\nl4\\nl5\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_raw_read_has_no_line_numbers(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == DATA\n+    assert env[\"error\"] is False and env[\"diff\"] == \"\"\n+\n+\n+def test_human_read_prints_content_plus_newline(run, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"abc\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    proc = run(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == 0\n+    assert proc.stdout == \"abc\\n\"\n+    assert proc.stderr == \"\"\n+\n+\n+def test_range_is_numbered_with_continuation_hint(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--offset\", 2, \"--limit\", 2)\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"2: l2\\n3: l3\\n... (showing lines 2-3 of 5; use offset=4 to continue)\"\n+\n+\n+def test_range_from_middle_to_eof_has_no_hint(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    assert jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--offset\", 4)[\"content\"] == \"4: l4\\n5: l5\"\n+\n+\n+def test_limit_only_starts_at_line_one(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--limit\", 2)\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"1: l1\\n2: l2\\n... (showing lines 1-2 of 5; use offset=3 to continue)\"\n+\n+\n+def test_range_over_budget_is_dataerr_not_truncation(jerr, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    code, env = jerr(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--offset\", 1, \"--limit\", 4, \"--max-chars\", 10)\n+    assert code == EX_DATAERR\n+    assert env[\"error\"] is True\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == (\n+        \"the requested range (lines 1-4) exceeds the read limit of 10 chars. \"\n+        \"Use a smaller limit, or search with grep instead.\"\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def test_offset_past_eof_returns_empty_ok(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(DATA, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    assert jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--offset\", 99)[\"content\"] == \"\"\n+\n+\n+def test_whole_file_truncation_points_at_next_line(jok, tmp_path):\n+    text = \"x\" * 30000\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(text, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"x\" * 20000 + \"\\n... [truncated, file is 30000 chars; use offset=1 to continue]\"\n+\n+\n+def test_truncation_hint_uses_first_unread_line(jok, tmp_path):\n+    text = \"0123456789\\n\" * 3000  # 33000 chars, 3000 lines\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(text, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    head = text[:20000]\n+    env = jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == head + f\"\\n... [truncated, file is {len(text)} chars; use offset={head.count(chr(10)) + 1} to continue]\"\n+\n+\n+def test_max_chars_flag(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"0123456789ABCDEF\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--max-chars\", 10)\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"0123456789\\n... [truncated, file is 16 chars; use offset=1 to continue]\"\n+\n+\n+def test_directory_lists_entries_dirs_get_slash(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"sub\").mkdir()\n+    (tmp_path / \"b.txt\").write_text(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    (tmp_path / \"A.txt\").write_text(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    (tmp_path / \".hidden\").write_text(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\")  # read shows dotfiles; only grep hides them\n+    assert jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \".\")[\"content\"] == \".hidden\\nA.txt\\nb.txt\\nsub/\"\n+\n+\n+def test_empty_directory(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"empty\").mkdir()\n+    assert jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"empty\")[\"content\"] == \"(empty directory)\"\n+\n+\n+def test_directory_with_range_flags_is_usage_error(jerr, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"sub\").mkdir()\n+    code, env = jerr(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"sub\", \"--offset\", 1)\n+    assert code == EX_USAGE\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"cannot read a line range of a directory; list it without offset/limit\"\n+\n+\n+def test_missing_file_is_noinput(jerr, tmp_path):\n+    code, env = jerr(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"nope.txt\")\n+    assert code == EX_NOINPUT\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"file not found: nope.txt\"\n+\n+\n+def test_undecodable_bytes_read_with_replacement(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"latin.txt\").write_bytes(b\"caf\\xe9\\n\")\n+    assert jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"latin.txt\")[\"content\"] == \"caf\\ufffd\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_crlf_reads_as_lf(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"win.txt\").write_bytes(b\"a\\r\\nb\\r\\n\")\n+    assert jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"win.txt\")[\"content\"] == \"a\\nb\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_negative_flags_are_usage(jerr, tmp_path):\n+    code, env = jerr(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--offset\", -1)\n+    assert code == EX_USAGE\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"--offset must be >= 0\"\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.677327, "id": "973c5ebf90b5", "tool_call_id": "call_aa5192c20e014f84b6b74cc2", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_grep.py (4243 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_grep.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_grep.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@\n+\"\"\"grep: hit format, filters, skips, the 100 cap, error cases.\"\"\"\n+\n+import os\n+\n+from clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\n+\n+\n+def test_hits_grouped_per_file_with_blank_line_between(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"g1.txt\").write_text(\"hit_a\\nhit_b\\nnope\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    (tmp_path / \"g2.txt\").write_text(\"x\\nhit_c\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    assert (\n+        jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"hit\")[\"content\"]\n+        == \"g1.txt:\\n  Line 1: hit_a\\n  Line 2: hit_b\\n\\ng2.txt:\\n  Line 2: hit_c\"\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def test_no_matches(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"nothing here\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"zzz\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"(no matches)\"\n+\n+\n+def test_python_regex_dialect(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.py\").write_text(\"def  one():\\nreturn 1\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    assert jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", r\"^def \\w+\\(\")[\"content\"] == \"f.py:\\n  Line 1: def  one():\"\n+\n+\n+def test_include_filters_by_name(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"a.py\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    (tmp_path / \"a.txt\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    content = jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"needle\", \"--include\", \"*.py\")[\"content\"]\n+    assert \"a.py:\" in content\n+    assert \"a.txt\" not in content\n+\n+\n+def test_include_filters_by_relative_path(jok, tmp_path):\n+    sub = tmp_path / \"sub\"\n+    sub.mkdir()\n+    (sub / \"b.py\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    (tmp_path / \"a.py\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    content = jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"needle\", \"--include\", \"sub/*\")[\"content\"]\n+    assert f\"sub{os.sep}b.py:\" in content\n+    assert \"a.py\" not in content\n+\n+\n+def test_path_subdir_limits_search(jok, tmp_path):\n+    sub = tmp_path / \"sub\"\n+    sub.mkdir()\n+    (sub / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    (tmp_path / \"top.txt\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    content = jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"needle\", \"--path\", \"sub\")[\"content\"]\n+    assert f\"sub{os.sep}f.txt:\" in content\n+    assert \"top.txt\" not in content\n+\n+\n+def test_single_file_as_path(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"one\\ntwo needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    assert jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"needle\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\")[\"content\"] == \"f.txt:\\n  Line 2: two needle\"\n+\n+\n+def test_hidden_and_pycache_are_skipped(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \".secrets.txt\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    cache = tmp_path / \"__pycache__\"\n+    cache.mkdir()\n+    (cache / \"x.py\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    assert jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"needle\")[\"content\"] == \"(no matches)\"\n+\n+\n+def test_explicit_dotfile_path_is_searched(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \".secrets.txt\").write_text(\"needle\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    content = jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"needle\", \"--path\", \".secrets.txt\")[\"content\"]\n+    assert content == \".secrets.txt:\\n  Line 1: needle\"\n+\n+\n+def test_binary_file_skipped(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"bin.dat\").write_bytes(b\"ok\\x00binary\" + b\"\\nneedle\\n\")\n+    assert jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"needle\")[\"content\"] == \"(no matches)\"\n+\n+\n+def test_nul_after_first_1024_bytes_is_not_binary(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"late.bin\").write_bytes(b\"z\" * 1024 + b\"\\x00 and needle\\n\")\n+    content = jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"needle\")[\"content\"]\n+    assert \"  Line 1: \" in content\n+\n+\n+def test_capped_at_100_with_footer(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"big.txt\").write_text(\"hit\\n\" * 120, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    content = jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"hit\")[\"content\"]\n+    assert content.endswith(\"(Results capped at 100; use a more specific pattern or path.)\")\n+    assert \"  Line 100: hit\" in content\n+    assert \"  Line 101:\" not in content\n+\n+\n+def test_lines_truncated_at_300_chars(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"long.txt\").write_text(\"y\" * 400 + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    assert jok(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"y\")[\"content\"] == \"long.txt:\\n  Line 1: \" + \"y\" * 300\n+\n+\n+def test_bad_regex_is_usage_error(jerr):\n+    code, env = jerr(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"(\")\n+    assert code == EX_USAGE\n+    assert env[\"content\"].startswith(\"invalid regex: \")\n+\n+\n+def test_missing_search_root_is_noinput(jerr):\n+    code, env = jerr(\"grep\", \"--pattern\", \"x\", \"--path\", \"nope_dir\")\n+    assert code == EX_NOINPUT\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"file not found: nope_dir\"\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.6863272, "id": "4c470de0e6c8", "tool_call_id": "call_dac54e1489dc40dcbdd31ce6", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_write.py (3161 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_write.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_write.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@\n+\"\"\"write_file: creation, overwrite diffs, newline law, error surface.\"\"\"\n+\n+from clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_IOERR\n+\n+\n+def test_create_new_file(jok, tmp_path):\n+    env = jok(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"new.txt\", \"--content\", \"hello\\n\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"OK: wrote new.txt (6 chars)\"\n+    assert env[\"diff\"] == \"--- a/new.txt\\n+++ b/new.txt\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+hello\\n\"\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"new.txt\").read_bytes() == b\"hello\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_parents_auto_created(jok, tmp_path):\n+    env = jok(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"sub/dir/new.txt\", \"--content\", \"x\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"OK: wrote sub/dir/new.txt (1 chars)\"\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"sub\" / \"dir\" / \"new.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"x\"\n+\n+\n+def test_overwrite_reports_added_removed_lines(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"old\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--content\", \"new\\n\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"OK: wrote f.txt (+1 -1 lines)\"\n+    assert env[\"diff\"] == \"--- a/f.txt\\n+++ b/f.txt\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-old\\n+new\\n\"\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"new\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_noop_rewrite_has_empty_diff(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"same\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--content\", \"same\\n\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"OK: wrote f.txt (+0 -0 lines)\"\n+    assert env[\"diff\"] == \"\"\n+\n+\n+def test_empty_content_new_file(jok, tmp_path):\n+    env = jok(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"empty.txt\", \"--content\", \"\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"OK: wrote empty.txt (0 chars)\"\n+    assert env[\"diff\"] == \"\"\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"empty.txt\").read_bytes() == b\"\"\n+\n+\n+def test_content_lf_normalized_on_disk(jok, tmp_path):\n+    jok(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--content\", \"a\\r\\nb\")\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_bytes() == b\"a\\nb\"\n+\n+\n+def test_trailing_newline_preserved_exactly(jok, tmp_path):\n+    jok(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--content\", \"no-newline\")\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_bytes() == b\"no-newline\"\n+\n+\n+def test_human_mode_prints_summary_then_diff(run, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"old\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    proc = run(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--content\", \"new\\n\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == 0\n+    assert proc.stdout == \"OK: wrote f.txt (+1 -1 lines)\\n--- a/f.txt\\n+++ b/f.txt\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-old\\n+new\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_stdin_payload_via_dash(run, tmp_path):\n+    proc = run(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--content\", \"-\", stdin=\"from stdin\\n\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == 0\n+    assert \"OK: wrote f.txt (11 chars)\" in proc.stdout\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"from stdin\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_parent_is_a_file_is_io_error(jerr, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"blocker\").write_text(\"just a file\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    code, env = jerr(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"blocker/child.txt\", \"--content\", \"x\")\n+    assert code == EX_IOERR\n+    assert env[\"error\"] is True\n+\n+\n+def test_utf8_body_survives_json_roundtrip(jok, tmp_path):\n+    jok(\"write_file\", \"--path\", \"cn.txt\", \"--content\", \"中文内容\\n\")\n+    env = jok(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"cn.txt\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"中文内容\\n\"\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.692327, "id": "8e88ab423bd3", "tool_call_id": "call_5ad41b227f4d43a885609177", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_edit.py (2844 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_edit.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_edit.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@\n+\"\"\"edit_file: single-occurrence replacement and its error codes.\"\"\"\n+\n+from clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_DATAERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_USAGE\n+\n+\n+def test_unique_replacement(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"alpha\\nbeta\\ngamma\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"edit_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--old-string\", \"beta\", \"--new-string\", \"BETA\")\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"OK: edited f.txt (+1 -1 lines)\"\n+    assert \"-beta\\n+BETA\" in env[\"diff\"]\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"alpha\\nBETA\\ngamma\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_multiline_old_and_new(jok, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"a\\nb\\nc\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    env = jok(\"edit_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--old-string\", \"a\\nb\", \"--new-string\", \"x\")\n+    assert env[\"diff\"] == \"--- a/f.txt\\n+++ b/f.txt\\n@@ -1,3 +1,2 @@\\n-a\\n-b\\n+x\\n c\\n\"\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"x\\nc\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_zero_occurrences_is_dataerr_and_file_untouched(jerr, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"keep\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    code, env = jerr(\"edit_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--old-string\", \"zzz\", \"--new-string\", \"x\")\n+    assert code == EX_DATAERR\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"old_string not found in f.txt\"\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"keep\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_ambiguous_occurrences_is_dataerr(jerr, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"x\\nx\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    code, env = jerr(\"edit_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--old-string\", \"x\", \"--new-string\", \"y\")\n+    assert code == EX_DATAERR\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"old_string appears 2 times in f.txt\"\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"x\\nx\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_missing_file_is_noinput_with_hint(jerr):\n+    code, env = jerr(\"edit_file\", \"--path\", \"new.txt\", \"--old-string\", \"a\", \"--new-string\", \"b\")\n+    assert code == EX_NOINPUT\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"file not found: new.txt — use write_file to create it\"\n+\n+\n+def test_empty_old_string_is_usage(jerr, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"x\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    code, env = jerr(\"edit_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--old-string\", \"\", \"--new-string\", \"y\")\n+    assert code == EX_USAGE\n+    assert env[\"content\"] == \"old_string is required\"\n+\n+\n+def test_stdin_payload_via_dash(run, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"count: 1\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    proc = run(\"edit_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--old-string\", \"-\", \"--new-string\", \"N\",\n+               stdin=\"count: 1\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == 0\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"N\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_two_stdin_flags_rejected(run):\n+    proc = run(\"edit_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--old-string\", \"-\", \"--new-string\", \"-\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == 64\n+    assert \"only one of --old-string/--new-string may read stdin\" in proc.stderr\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894127.6973274, "id": "3081059dad44", "tool_call_id": "call_b723bbb80f5b4634ac99ffee", "content": "OK: wrote C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_cli.py (3789 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_cli.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\tests\\test_cli.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@\n+\"\"\"CLI surface: envelope shape, --json placement, exit-code contract, exotic failures.\n+\n+The black-box tests go through subprocesses; the three failure paths that are\n+awkward to provoke in a child (broken pipe, SIGINT, internal bug) run main()\n+in-process with patched streams/collaborators.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+import json\n+import sys\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from clutch_workspace import cli\n+from clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_IOERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_SIGINT, EX_SOFTWARE, EX_USAGE\n+\n+\n+def test_version(run):\n+    proc = run(\"--version\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == 0\n+    assert proc.stdout == \"clutch-workspace 0.1.0\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_no_args_prints_usage_and_exits_64(run):\n+    proc = run()\n+    assert proc.returncode == EX_USAGE\n+    assert proc.stderr.startswith(\"usage:\")\n+    assert \"error:\" in proc.stderr\n+\n+\n+def test_unknown_command_is_64(run):\n+    assert run(\"frobnicate\").returncode == EX_USAGE\n+\n+\n+def test_missing_required_flag_is_64(run):\n+    assert run(\"read_file\").returncode == EX_USAGE\n+\n+\n+def test_json_must_precede_the_subcommand(run, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    assert run(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\", \"--json\").returncode == EX_USAGE\n+    assert run(\"--json\", \"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\").returncode == 0\n+\n+\n+def test_envelope_success_shape(run, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    proc = run(\"--json\", \"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\")\n+    assert proc.stdout.count(\"\\n\") == 1  # ONE compact line\n+    env = json.loads(proc.stdout)\n+    assert set(env) == {\"content\", \"error\", \"diff\"}\n+    assert env == {\"content\": \"x\", \"error\": False, \"diff\": \"\"}\n+\n+\n+def test_envelope_error_shape_and_exit_code(run):\n+    proc = run(\"--json\", \"read_file\", \"--path\", \"nope.txt\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == EX_NOINPUT\n+    assert json.loads(proc.stdout) == {\"content\": \"file not found: nope.txt\", \"error\": True, \"diff\": \"\"}\n+\n+\n+def test_human_errors_go_to_stderr(run):\n+    proc = run(\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"nope.txt\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == EX_NOINPUT\n+    assert proc.stdout == \"\"\n+    assert proc.stderr == \"ERROR: file not found: nope.txt\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_json_body_is_not_ascii_escaped(run, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"cn.txt\").write_text(\"中文\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    proc = run(\"--json\", \"read_file\", \"--path\", \"cn.txt\")\n+    assert \"中文\" in proc.stdout  # ensure_ascii=False\n+    assert json.loads(proc.stdout)[\"content\"] == \"中文\"\n+\n+\n+def test_help_lists_all_four_commands(run):\n+    proc = run(\"--help\")\n+    assert proc.returncode == 0\n+    for command in (\"read_file\", \"grep\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\"):\n+        assert command in proc.stdout\n+\n+\n+class _DeadPipe:\n+    \"\"\"stdout stand-in whose writes fail like a closed pipe downstream.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def write(self, *_args):\n+        raise BrokenPipeError\n+\n+    def fileno(self):\n+        raise ValueError  # keeps the dup2 cleanup away from the real fd 1\n+\n+    def reconfigure(self, **_kw):\n+        pass\n+\n+\n+def test_broken_pipe_is_ioerr(monkeypatch, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"f.txt\").write_text(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(sys, \"stdout\", _DeadPipe())\n+    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)\n+    assert cli.main([\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\"]) == EX_IOERR\n+\n+\n+def test_keyboard_interrupt_is_130(monkeypatch, tmp_path):\n+    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(cli.filesystem, \"read_file\", lambda *_a, **_k: (_ for _ in ()).throw(KeyboardInterrupt()))\n+    assert cli.main([\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\"]) == EX_SIGINT\n+\n+\n+def test_internal_bug_is_70_with_traceback(monkeypatch, tmp_path, capsys):\n+    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(cli.filesystem, \"read_file\", lambda *_a, **_k: (_ for _ in ()).throw(RuntimeError(\"boom\")))\n+    assert cli.main([\"read_file\", \"--path\", \"f.txt\"]) == EX_SOFTWARE\n+    assert \"RuntimeError: boom\" in capsys.readouterr().err\n"}
