{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789894549.0119884, "id": "727af8e7f5cf", "tool_call_id": "call_45555b1f29b74b46ba2e8269", "content": "[Clutch push/release conventions + auth reality]\nClutch repo (Ethereal1024/Clutch, public): release flow = focused commits (test:/feat:/fix:/refactor:/chore:) -> chore(release): X.Y.Z bumping VERSION + ui/package.json + ui/package-lock.json (2 spots) -> lightweight tag vX.Y.Z on that commit -> push; .github/workflows/release.yml triggers on v* tags, builds deb/dmg/unsigned-win with bundled PyInstaller backend. Check CI anonymously via api.github.com/repos/Ethereal1024/Clutch/actions/runs. AUTH: origin is now HTTPS (git@github.com SSH is Permission denied (publickey) — the ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 key is NOT registered on GitHub, only user can fix via web settings); credential.helper=manager holds a working github.com PAT for Ethereal1024, so push/fetch just work over HTTPS. Repo has a long-standing commented .gitignore (docs/, .claude/skills/, poll_ci.py etc. stay local); scratch-*.py + scratch_*.log now ignored too. 30s command timeout: run test suites ONE per command (server_test is the slow HTTP+SSE e2e). Tests: .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m tests.X, node tests/foo-test.js.", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
