都算） |\n| 65 | 数据错（读超预算、old_string 找不到/不唯一） |\n| 66 | 文件或搜索根不存在 |\n| 70 | 内部 bug（遇到了算我的） |\n| 74 | I/O 错（权限、路径被占用等） |\n| 130 | 被中断（Ctrl+C） |\n\nhuman 模式下错误走 stderr，格式 `ERROR: 简讯`。\n\n## 四、大内容别塞命令行，走管道\n\nWindows 单参数上限约 32KB，大文件内容用 `-` 表示「从 stdin 读」：\n\n```bash\npython gen_report.py | clutch-workspace write_file --path out/report.md --content -\n```\n\n## 五、一句提醒\n\n它是**纯能力工具，没有围栏**：绝对路径也能指到当前目录之外。围栏由调用方决定——host 以后靠 `cwd` 圈，你手动用就靠自己 cd 的位置。写文件类操作不问确认，敲下去就落盘。\n\n---\n\n想现在就装好并看实跑效果的话，切到工作模式（Run 旁边的模式按钮）说一声，我把 ② 的安装跑完，再用仓库里的真实文件演示一遍读/搜/写/改。"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789896235.9197323, "id": "036b83050582", "content": "我改变主意了，把安全限制也下放到workspace，任务目录设置为可配置的参数。客户端ui对其有配置权，但tool封装没有配置入口。你清楚我的意思吗"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789896392.5218296, "id": "11da1f0a6192", "content": "清楚，而且这是一次方向性反转——先把我的理解复述给你验货，再说要你拍板的点。\n\n## 我理解的架构\n\n「安全围栏」从 host 搬进 clutch-workspace：任务目录从「隐式的进程 cwd」变成**显式可配置的参数**；配置权只在客户端 UI（人）手里；host 的 tool 封装层只能发起调用，**没有任何配置入口**——它既不能指定任务目录，也不能改安全策略，从结构上杜绝「被服务的 agent 自己给自己挪围栏」。\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph host[\"clutch host\"]\n        UI[\"客户端 UI（人）\"] --> CFG[\"配置：任务目录 + 安全限制\"]\n        TOOLS[\"tool 封装（read/grep/write/edit）\"]\n    end\n    CFG -->|\"唯一的配置通道\"| CLI[\"clutch-workspace CLI\"]\n    TOOLS -->|\"只发起调用，不能配置\"| CLI\n    CLI --> TASK[\"在任务目录围栏内执行四个命令\"]\n```\n\n一句话：**UI 定围栏，CLI 执围栏，tool 封装只敲门口禁上的铃。**\n\n## 这会推翻两条已冻结决策\n\n1. 「纯能力、无越界保护、cwd 即 workspace」→ 变成「CLI 内置围栏 + `--workspace` 参数」\n2. 相关的「安全/分类留在 host」→ 变成「围栏下放，host 只剩配置转发」\n\n拍板后我会同步更新冻结记忆，避免以后的会话拿旧契约说事。\n\n## 要你拍板的 6 个点（都带推荐）\n\n**① 「安全限制」具体搬哪些进来？** host 的 Workspace 现有四样安保：\n- 越界拒绝（路径解析后必须落在任务目录内）——**必搬**（核心）\n- protected 名单（对工具隐身/禁写的路径）——推荐**搬**，以参数形式传入\n- 外部路径白名单（host 权限引擎批过的例外路径）——推荐**搬**，否则审批流程无处落地\n- snapshot/undo 后悔药——推荐**不搬**（它是撤销机制不是围栏，先留在 host）\n\n**② 任务目录参数长什么样？**\n推荐：全局 `--workspace <dir>`（和 `--json` 并列、放子命令前）。**不传时默认 cwd**（向后兼容，已写的 64 个测试不炸）；host 将来永远显式传。传了之后，相对路径就锚在任务目录而不是 cwd。\n\n**③ UI 的配置怎么流到 CLI？** 两个方案：\n- **方案 A（推荐）**：CLI 保持零配置文件、无状态；host 传输层每次启动时把 UI 配置翻译成命令行参数（`--workspace X --protect y ...`）。「tool 封装无配置入口」= 配置只存在于 host 的 UI 设置层，tool 函数碰不到、传不了，传输层只做忠实转发。\n- 方案 B：CLI 自己读配置文件（如任务目录下的 `.clutch.json`），UI 只负责写文件。结构上更强（host 代码想配也配不了），但 CLI 从「零配置」变「有状态」，和你之前拍的 v1 零配置相反。\n\n**④ 违反围栏的退出码？** 现在的表（0/64/65/66/70/74/130）没有「越权」档。推荐**新增 77**（sysexits 标准成员 EX_NOPERM，语义正好）。\n\n**⑤ host 侧旧围栏去留？** Workspace 里的 resolve/protected/escape 逻辑：按你之前 Q21 的精神 **full-cut 删除**（唯一围栏在 CLI，出问题靠 tag 回滚）——但这是 host 改动，可以本轮只动 CLI、host 集成维持原计划后置。推荐后者（本轮不碰 host）。\n\n**⑥ 远程工作区（SSH bridge 那套）本轮管吗？** 推荐**不管**，围栏下放先只做本地 CLI，远程桥的安全语义单独一轮。\n\n---\n\n你可以逐条回（比如「①全搬除了undo ②同意 ③A ④77 ⑤本轮不碰host ⑥不管远程」），也可以「都按推荐」。拍板后我：改 CLI（围栏实现 + `--workspace` + 77 码）→ 补测试跑绿 → 提交 → 更新冻结记忆。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "The user says: \"我改变主意了，把安全限制也下放到workspace，任务目录设置为可配置的参数。客户端ui对其有配置权，但tool封装没有配置入口。你清楚我的意思吗\"\n\nTranslation: \"I changed my mind. Move the security restrictions down into the workspace too, and make the task directory a configurable parameter. The client UI has the right to configure it, but the tool wrapper (tool封装) has no configuration entry point. Do you understand what I mean?\"\n\nThis is a significant architecture reversal. The frozen contract was \"pure capability: NO containment in the CLI; paths resolve against process CWD; host sets cwd; security/classification stays in host.\"\n\nNow the user wants:\n1. Security restrictions (安全限制) moved INTO clutch-workspace (下放到workspace)\n2. The task directory (任务目录) becomes a configurable parameter (instead of implicit cwd)\n3. The client UI (clutch host's UI) has configuration rights over it (the UI can set/configure the task directory and presumably the security restrictions)\n4. But the tool封装 (tool wrapper — the host's tool layer, agent/tools/filesystem.py) has NO configuration entry — meaning the tools layer doesn't get to configure it; the boundary is: UI/config → workspace, tools layer just uses it.\n\nLet me parse more carefully in context of the clutch architecture:\n\n- clutch host has: agent/tools/filesystem.py (tool wrappers), agent/tools/workspace.py (Workspace abstraction with LocalWorkspace/RemoteWorkspace, containing protected sets, resolve with containment/escapes, snapshots)\n- agent/tools/transport.py spawns the tool subprocess with cwd=self.cwd (line 127)\n- clutch-workspace: the new standalone CLI we just built — pure capability, cwd-as-workspace\n\n\"把安全限制也下放到workspace\" — \"also\" (也) suggests moving security restrictions down into the workspace component. Which workspace? Two readings:\n\nReading A: clutch-workspace (the new CLI repo). Security restrictions (containment, protected paths, the fence) move INTO the CLI. Task directory becomes a CLI parameter (--workspace / --root flag). The host UI configures it (e.g., via config), but the host's tool wrapper layer (agent/tools/*.py) has no per-call configuration entry — it just passes the configured workspace path.\n\nReading B: \"workspace\" = the Workspace class in the host (agent/tools/workspace.py). Moving security down into workspace... but that's where it already lives (is_protected, resolve containment). Hmm, \"也下放\" (also delegate down) — down to where? \n\nContext clues: \"任务目录设置为可配置的参数\" — task directory as a configurable parameter. In the current CLI design, the task directory = process cwd, chosen by the caller (transport sets cwd). Making it a *parameter* means the CLI (or workspace component) takes --workspace <dir>. \"客户端ui对其有配置权\" — the client UI has the right to configure it. In clutch, there's a UI (ui/ directory, Node frontend). So the user wants: the task directory (and the security fence) configured at the UI/config level, flowing into the workspace component; the tool wrapper layer (filesystem.py in host, the 4-command wrappers) should NOT have a configuration entry point — i.e., tools don't decide or per-call override the workspace/security; they just operate within what's configured.\n\nSo the architecture becomes:\n\n```\n客户端 UI ──(配置: 任务目录 + 安全限制)──> workspace 组件（clutch-workspace）\ntool 封装（agent/tools/filesystem.py 4 个工具函数）──> 只是调 workspace，无配置入口\n```\n\nThis reverses the frozen \"pure capability, security stays in host\" decision. The security fence (containment: paths must stay inside task dir; possibly protected paths; maybe more) moves INTO clutch-workspace, parameterized:\n- --workspace/-C <dir> or --root: the task directory (default: cwd? or required?)\n- Security restrictions: containment enforcement (reject paths escaping the task dir), and possibly the protected-files concept.\n\n\"tool封装没有配置入口\" — the tool wrapper (host's tools/cli.py transport spawn, or the tool functions) has no config entry: meaning when the host's tool layer invokes clutch-workspace, it cannot pass arbitrary config/security overrides; those come only from the (UI-configured) workspace configuration. This prevents the agent (the LLM being served) from influencing the fence — the model only sees tools; the fence is set by the human via UI.\n\nThat's actually a coherent security posture: trust boundary — UI (human) configures the fence; tool wrapper (agent-facing) can't touch it.\n\nSo the user asks: \"你清楚我的意思吗\" — do you understand? Per the standing instruction from earlier (\"中途碰到需要决策的技术点必须让我决策而不是静默执行\"), and this being a major contract reversal, the right move is:\n\n1. Confirm understanding by restating the architecture precisely.\n2. Point out what changes: frozen decision \"pure capability / security stays in host / cwd-as-workspace\" is now reversed — need to restate the new contract.\n3. Identify the decision points and ambiguities that need user rulings BEFORE implementing.\n\nThis is a big design shift. I should NOT silently implement. I should:\n- Restate my understanding\n- Lay out the concrete design questions (decision points) for user拍板\n\nAlso per compaction note: re-read files before editing. But right now we're just discussing — no edits. I might want to check the host's current structure (agent/tools/workspace.py containment bits, protected sets, how UI config flows) to ground the questions. I have good context from earlier reads. Maybe quickly grep the host for how UI config reaches tools (config.py? ui settings?) to phrase the \"UI has configuration rights\" integration concretely. That would help me ask sharp questions. Let me do a bit of light reading: agent/config.py? agent/tools/transport.py:127 area (cwd=self.cwd), and how host spawns tools/cli.py subprocess (the tool subprocess pilot). Also \"MCP web-service feature fully removed\" memory etc. Hmm.\n\nActually the user just asks \"你清楚我的意思吗\" — the expected response is: confirm understanding + reflect back the design + list decision points. Light verification reading is fine but I should keep it lean. I already know the host side well enough from prior reads:\n\n- LocalWorkspace: root, resolve() with _allowed_escapes + _inside_or_scratch + scratch dirs, protected set (is_protected/protect()), visible_entries filters protected, snapshot/undo (_MAX_SNAPSHOTS_PER_FILE), escape_path for permission engine.\n- transport.py:127: spawns tool subprocess with cwd=self.cwd.\n- The tool subprocess (tools/cli.py) rebuilds a bare Workspace in child; parent ships protected set so child re-applies protect() (from workspace.py:157-161 comment).\n\nSo host currently: fence lives in Workspace (host-side), tools call workspace, UI/config... there's a Config object (config.read_max_chars referenced in filesystem.py).\n\nNew design per user:\n- clutch-workspace gains: --workspace (or similar) parameter = task directory (replacing/augmenting cwd semantics), and security enforcement INSIDE the CLI: containment (no escape), presumably protected paths, maybe read-only mode? What exactly are \"安全限制\"? In host Workspace today: (a) containment/escape verdicts, (b) protected set, (c) snapshots/undo (safety net), (d) approval flow for external paths (_allowed_escapes approved by permission engine).\n\nQuestions for the user (decision points):\n\n1. **参数形态**: task directory parameter shape — `--workspace <dir>` global flag? Default when absent: cwd (backward compat) or required-error? Position: before subcommand alongside --json?\n\n2. **安全限制具体指哪些**: which of the host's protections move in?\n   a. 越界拒绝 (containment: relative/absolute paths must resolve inside task dir; reject otherwise with new exit code? which code — new? 77 EX_NOPERM? 65? host uses ValueError→error prose)\n   b. protected 名单 (protected paths — ship as flag? config file? env? This conflicts with \"v1 zero config files\" frozen decision — now UI configures it, so maybe config via CLI flag or a workspace config file like .clc)\n   c. external escape approval (host's permission engine