{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789896810.12248, "id": "1ae56cc71ff1", "content": "能不能把workspace做成一个常驻子进程？"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789896952.3403904, "id": "9f873d2f1790", "content": "能做，而且这一问正好把上一轮 undo 的死结解开了。先把结论放前面：**技术上完全可行（仍然零依赖、纯标准库），而且「常驻」比「每次调用起一个进程」更能自洽地承载你刚定的两个方向（围栏下放 + undo 下放）**。但形态要选对，下面摊开讲。\n\n## 为什么「常驻」恰好是对症的\n\n上一轮 undo 卡住的根本原因是：现在的 CLI **一次调用一个进程、干完即退**，内存快照栈活不过一次调用，逼出「落盘存储」那串复杂设计。如果 workspace 变成常驻进程：\n\n- **undo 回到内存栈**——和今天 host 的行为完全一致（host 的 `_snapshots` 就是内存 dict，会话结束即失），不需要 `.clutch/undo/` 落盘方案了\n- **每次调用省掉一次 Python 解释器冷启动**（Windows 上单次约 100–200ms），agent 一个会话几百次工具调用，累积收益可观\n- **围栏配置收口得更彻底**：围栏在 daemon 启动时从 spawn 参数一次性注入，之后的协议里**根本没有 config 字段**——比「转发 flag」更强的「tool 封装无配置入口」，结构性做到\n- **和远程方案汇合**：你之前定过「远程 = 服务器部署 + SSH 桥」，常驻 server 化的 workspace 跟桥那套形态天然趋同，将来本地/远程可以是同一套协议\n\n## 推荐形态：`serve` 子命令 + stdio 行式 JSON\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph host[\"clutch host\"]\n        UI[\"客户端 UI\"] --> SERVER[\"server.py 会话\"]\n        TOOLS[\"tool 封装\"]\n    end\n    SERVER -->|\"spawn + 注入配置(仅此处)\"| D[\"clutch-workspace serve\"]\n    TOOLS -->|\"协议调用，无配置字段\"| D\n    D --> S[\"内存态：围栏 + undo 栈\"]\n    D --> DIR[\"任务目录\"]\n```\n\n- host 在**会话开始**时 spawn：`clutch-workspace serve --workspace X --protect ...`（UI 配置在此一次性注入）\n- 协议就是 stdin/stdout 上的一行 JSON 进、一行 JSON 出：\n\n```json\n→ {\"id\": 7, \"op\": \"edit_file\", \"params\": {\"path\": \"a.py\", \"old-string\": \"...\", \"new-string\": \"...\"}}\n← {\"id\": 7, \"ok\": true, \"content\": \"OK: edited a.py (+1 -1 lines)\", \"diff\": \"--- a/a.py...\"}\n← {\"id\": 9, \"ok\": false, \"code\": 66, \"error\": \"file not found: a.py\"}\n```\n\n- 会话结束 host 杀掉它；意外死亡由 host 重启（快照丢失 = 和今天 host 重启丢快照一个待遇，不是退步）\n- **单命令模式原样保留**（人手动用、脚本用、现有 64 个测试全都不动）——`serve` 只是复用同一个核心的第二个门面\n\n**为什么不推荐 TCP 端口版 daemon**：本机任何进程都能连上一个裸端口，围栏配置权就从「host 独有」泄漏成「本机谁都在场」，得再加 token 认证；还有端口分配、孤儿进程清理（Windows 上很烦）、防火墙首次弹窗。stdio 管道的信任边界和今天完全一样：管道另一头就是 host，不多不少。\n\n## 代价（说实话的部分）\n\n1. **host 要管生命周期**：spawn/杀/崩溃重启。host 的 supervisor 已有子孙进程清理机制（Toolhelp32 那套），有现成经验\n2. **状态陈旧风险**：daemon 记着 workspace 根，用户中途删目录/改配置会失配 → 每次调用前校验根目录仍存在 + 加一条 `configure` 协议消息支持中途改围栏\n3. **多了一层要冻结的契约**（协议格式）；好在错误语义可以直接搬 sysexits 码进 `code` 字段\n4. **并发模型要定**：推荐「一会话一 daemon」，两个会话开同一目录 = 两个 daemon、两套 undo 栈——和今天两个 host 进程各持一份内存栈的行为一致\n\n## 对上一轮待拍板项的影响\n\n| 上轮决策点 | 常驻后 |\n|---|---|\n| undo-① 存储位置（落盘 `.clutch/undo/`） | **作废** → daemon 内存栈，零落盘 |\n| undo-⑤ 节奏 | 仍建议与围栏同轮 |\n| 围栏-③ 配置通道 | 不变方向，但收口更狠：配置只存在于 spawn 参数，协议无 config 字段 |\n| 围栏-①②④⑥（搬哪些/`--workspace`/77 码/远程不管） | **不受影响，仍待你拍** |\n\n## 现在轮到你拍板的（新增 3 个）\n\n1. **做不做常驻**——推荐做；替代方案是维持 per-call + undo 落盘（更简单但慢、且要落盘设计）\n2. **形态**——推荐 stdio 行式 JSON 的 `serve` 子命令，随会话生死，单命令模式保留；不推荐 TCP daemon\n3. **undo 存储改判**——推荐从「落盘」改回「daemon 内存（会话级，与今天 host 行为对齐）」\n\n连同上一轮还挂着的围栏 ①②④⑥，你可以一起裁，比如「1做 2按推荐 3改内存；围栏①全搬除undo已解决 ②同意 ④77 ⑥不管远程」。裁完我一次做完：serve 协议 + 围栏 + `--workspace` + undo 栈 + 测试全绿 + 提交。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "The user asks: \"能不能把workspace做成一个常驻子进程？\" — \"Can we make the workspace a resident/long-lived subprocess (daemon)?\"\n\nThis is interesting. This connects DIRECTLY to the previous discussion: the reason undo was awkward to move into the CLI is that the CLI is a stateless per-call process. If the workspace became a resident (long-running) subprocess, then:\n\n- In-memory snapshot stacks become viable again (no on-disk store needed... or still optional)\n- The undo question changes shape entirely\n- Per-call spawn overhead (Python interpreter startup ~30-100ms per tool call) disappears\n- State can persist across calls: undo stacks, caches, etc.\n\nThis also connects to a memory: \"Two remote schemes: SSH degradation + remote server deploy\" — there's already a remote bridge concept (agent/tools/workspace.py RemoteWorkspace with SshTransport, bridge_url). The host already has a server.py (HTTP). The UI is Electron/Node.\n\nThe user is asking a feasibility/design question. Per the standing instruction: decision points go to the user; but first I should give a well-grounded technical analysis: what problems it solves, what it costs, what the design options are, and my recommendation. This is a \"能不能\" question — answer it honestly with trade-offs, then lay out decision points if we decide to do it.\n\nContext relevant facts from the conversation and memories:\n- clutch-workspace: Python CLI, 4 commands, stateless per-call, 64 black-box subprocess tests, just committed (M1)\n- The undo discussion: snapshots in host memory (workspace.py `_snapshots: dict[str, list[str]]`), depth 5; user wants undo moved into workspace\n- Host transport spawns tool subprocess per call (transport.py:127 cwd=self.cwd; \"Tool subprocess execution refactor shipped (pilot: read_file)\")\n- Windows host, Git Bash environment\n- Python 3.14 at /c/Python314\n- The frozen contract: --json envelope, sysexits codes, --path space style, UTF-8, zero config files (now being revised: fence下放 + --workspace parameter pending)\n- Previous round left OPEN: 6 fence decision points (①-⑥) + 5 undo decision points — user hasn't ruled on those yet! They pivoted to this question instead. This daemon question is actually RELATED to those pending decisions (especially undo storage: in-memory vs on-disk).\n\nSo this question is likely the user exploring: if workspace is resident, undo state can live in memory again, avoiding the on-disk snapshot store complexity. I should point that connection out — it changes the decision matrix from the last round.\n\nNow the technical analysis:\n\n**Can it be done? Yes, easily.** A resident subprocess = a small server process that reads commands from stdin (line-delimited JSON / LSP-style) or listens on a localhost TCP/Unix socket or named pipe, and responds per request. Python stdlib-only is still feasible (socketserver, or just a stdin/stdout loop). Windows named pipes work via stdlib? socket on localhost is simplest and cross-platform.\n\n**Architecture options:**\n\n1. **stdin/stdout protocol loop (child of host)**: host spawns `clutch-workspace serve` (or `--serve`); protocol: one JSON request per line on stdin, one JSON response per line on stdout. Host holds the pipe for the session. Pros: no port management, no auth needed (pipe is already the trust boundary), trivial lifecycle (kill process = cleanup), stdlib only. Cons: host must manage the child lifecycle (crash → restart), single-client.\n2. **localhost TCP socket daemon**: CLI or separate process listens on 127.0.0.1:port; host connects. Pros: multiple clients possible (UI and host both?); survives host restart; Cons: port allocation/ownership, needs an auth token (any local process could connect! security regression — the fence would be configurable by any local process unless token-authenticated), lifecycle (who owns the daemon? orphan cleanup on Windows is annoying), firewall prompts possible (localhost usually fine but Windows Defender may prompt), stale daemon cleanup.\n3. **Named pipe (Windows)**: stdlib support is weak (pywin32 needed) — violates zero-dependency. Cross-platform named pipes via stdlib not really. Skip.\n\nGiven clutch already has server.py (the host app server) and a remote bridge over SSH (bridge_url HTTP to remote), a TCP localhost server inside workspace would mirror the remote bridge pattern... but the trust model differs: remote bridge is authenticated by network topology; local TCP needs a token.\n\n**What the resident model buys:**\n\n1. **Undo in memory** — directly resolves the on-disk snapshot store dilemma from last round. The stack lives in the daemon; host restart → snapshots lost unless persisted (same as today's host behavior! Today's snapshots ARE in-memory and die on restart — so parity, no regression).\n2. **Performance**: eliminates per-call Python startup (~50-150ms on Windows per spawn) × every tool call. Agent makes MANY tool calls per session; meaningful latency win. Also the host transport currently pays subprocess spawn per call.\n3. **Session state**: cwd/workspace binding once at session start instead of per call; caches (directory stats, file mtimes) possible later.\n4. **Cleaner fence lifecycle**: fence configured once at daemon start from UI config; tool calls carry no config at all — even stronger version of \"tool封装没有配置入口\" (the tool calls literally cannot pass config because the protocol has no config field; only the spawn/attach step can, and that's host-side).\n5. **Future remote**: the resident server + the SSH bridge pattern converge (remote workspace = same protocol over the bridge). Actually this is a big one: the memory \"Two remote schemes: SSH degradation + remote server deploy\" — a resident workspace server could run remotely the same way, making local/remote uniform. The RemoteWorkspace already speaks HTTP to a bridge.\n\n**What it costs / risks:**\n\n1. **Lifecycle management**: who spawns it, when does it die, crash detection + auto-restart, orphan cleanup (especially on Windows — no clean process groups; supervisor.py already deals with descendant killing for the host). Host already has supervisor machinery for killing descendants — reusable knowledge.\n2. **State staleness**: a resident process holds cwd/fence config; if the UI changes the workspace mid-session → need a reconfigure message; if the user deletes/renames the task dir → daemon holds a stale root. Per-call spawn is stateless and thus immune to staleness. Mitigation: reconfigure command + root revalidation per call (cheap).\n3. **Concurrency**: multiple sessions on one workspace; single daemon per workspace? Per session? Decision needed. Simplest: one daemon per (host process, workspace) session, dies with session.\n4. **Protocol design**: new surface to freeze (request/response framing, error mapping — the sysexits codes move into protocol responses; exit codes become less relevant; the --json envelope becomes the protocol message basically). CLI keeps working for humans — dual mode (serve subcommand + one-shot commands) is fine, share the core.\n5. **Testing**: protocol tests instead of pure subprocess black-box (though we can keep black-box: spawn server, write lines to stdin, read lines). The existing 64 tests stay valid for the one-shot mode.\n6. **Security surface**: stdin-pipe model adds nothing (parent is host, same as today). TCP model adds a local network surface — needs token. Recommend stdin/stdout pipe model to keep the trust story identical to today.\n\n**Interaction with pending decisions:**\n- Undo storage: in-memory stack becomes viable (parity with today) → decision point from last round changes: \"存储位置\" would become \"daemon 内存（随会话）\" with optional later persistence. Recommend: in-memory in daemon, matching today's semantics exactly (dies with session), no on-disk store needed at all. Simpler than the on-disk plan.\n- The fence (--workspace etc.): config at daemon start; per-call no config. Strengthens ③.\n- ④ exit code 77: in resident mode, violations come back as protocol error field; exit codes still apply in one-shot mode. Keep both.\n- ② --workspace flag: still needed for one-shot mode; in serve mode it's a startup arg + reconfigure message.\n- ⑥ remote: defer still, but note convergence.\n\n**My recommendation**: Yes, feasible and actually a good fit — BUT as `serve` subcommand speaking line-delimited JSON over stdio, spawned by host per session, dying with it; one-shot CLI preserved for humans/scripts/tests. This resolves the undo question elegantly (memory stack, host parity) and keeps the trust model unchanged.\n\nWait — one more consideration: is the added complexity worth it NOW? The user asked \"能不能\" — feasibility + design. The agent makes many tool calls; per-call startup on Windows Python is genuinely noticeable (python startup ~30-80ms + import overhead; total maybe 100-200ms per call). Over a session with hundreds of tool calls that's seconds to minutes of cumulative latency. It's a real win but not urgent for correctness. The undo motivation is the real driver here.\n\nAlso relevant: the host already spawned per-call subprocess for tools (the refactor shipped with read_file pilot). A resident workspace changes the transport integration design (Q21 integration deferred anyway). So now is actually the right time to decide, BEFORE host integration lands, because it changes the integration shape.\n\nHonesty requires me to also present the \"keep per-call, use on-disk snapshots\" path as a legitimate alternative: simpler mental model, no lifecycle management, but pays spawn latency per call and needs the snapshot store design. I'll lay out both with a recommendation.\n\nAlso stdlib-only feasibility: yes. Line-delimited JSON over stdin/stdout loop is ~100 lines. No asyncio needed even (just loop reading stdin). Timeout handling: per-request watchdog optional; broken pipe → exit. Must handle: unknown request, exception per request → error response (don't kill loop), graceful shutdown on stdin EOF, signal handling.\n\nProtocol sketch:\n\nRequest: `{\"id\": 1, \"op\": \"read_file\", \"params\": {\"path\": \"a.py\", \"offset\": 2}}`\nResponse: `{\"id\": 1, \"ok\": true, \"content\": \"...\", \"diff\": \"\"}` or `{\"id\": 1, \"ok\": false, \"code\": 66, \"error\": \"file not found: a.py\"}`\nControl ops: `ping`, `shutdown`, `configure` (workspace/fence re-set).\n\nThe one-shot CLI becomes a thin client... no wait, one-shot stays as-is (direct execution). serve shares the filesystem.py core unchanged. The 64 tests keep passing; add protocol tests.\n\nLifecycle recommendation: host spawns at session start with `serve --workspace X --protect ...` (the UI config), reads/writes stdio, kills at session end; on unexpected child death → respawn (state loss = snapshots lost, acceptable, same as today's restart behavior); host already has supervisor descendant-kill machinery.\n\nWindows specifics: pipe I/O fine; no fork issues (spawn); kill via taskkill/terminate — supervisor handles.\n\nAlso: should the daemon be one per workspace or one per host session? Per session (each agent session binds one workspace) — matches transport's cwd per workspace today. Multiple sessions on same dir = separate daemons, snapshot stacks separate — fine, matches today (separate host processes would have separate stacks anyway).\n\nWhat about the UI talking directly to the daemon for undo? Simpler to keep: UI → host server.py → daemon protocol `undo` op. Keeps single writer.\n\nFormat of my answer:\n- 直接回答：能，而且它正好解开上一轮 undo 的死结。给出推荐形态（serve 子命令 + stdio 行式 JSON + 随会话生死）。\n- 常驻换来什么（4 点，结合 undo/potato latency/fence/remote convergence）\n- 代价与风险（lifecycle/staleness/protocol/双模式）\n- 两种形态对比小表：per-call（现状）vs resident；以及 TCP 模型为什么不用（本地信任面+token+孤儿进程）\n- 协议草图（简短 code block）\n- 对上一轮待拍板项的影响：undo 存储从「落盘 .clutch/undo」变成「daemon 内存，会话结束即失（与今天 host 行为完全一致）」；配置权在 spawn 参数处收口，tool 调用协议里根本没有 config 字段——比 flag 转发更强的「无配置入口」\n- 决策点（新批次）：做不做、形态（stdio vs TCP）、一 daemon 一会话？、undo 存储改判、one-shot 模式保留？、host 生命周期归谁（推荐 transport spawn/session kill + supervisor 兜底）\n- 明确说：上一轮的 6+5 个决策点里，哪些被这个改变影响（undo 的 #1 #5，围栏的 ③ 配置通道），哪些不变（①②④⑤⑥ 大部分）\n\nKeep it in Chinese, plain, structured, concrete. Include a small mermaid? Maybe an architecture sketch. Mermaid rules: quoted labels, no nested double quotes. A simple flowchart: host session → spawn serve → daemon holds workspace+fence+undo stack; tool封装 → protocol requests.\n\nActually a compact mermaid:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph host[\"clutch host\"]\n        UI[\"客户端 UI\"] --> SERVER[\"server.py / 会话\"]\n        TOOLS[\"tool 封装\"]\n    end\n    SERVER -->|\"spawn + 配置(仅此处)\"| D[\"clutch-workspace serve 常驻进程\"]\n    TOOLS -->|\"协议调用，无配置字段\"| D\n    D --> F[\"内存：围栏 + undo 栈\"]\n    D --> DIR[\"任务目录\"]\n```\n\nCareful: mermaid label with parentheses fine inside quotes; no nested quotes. OK.\n\nLength: this is a substantial design question — a thorough but tidy answer. End with the decision list, per user's standing rule. Don't implement anything yet (also chat mode: no writes anyway)."}
{"type": "final", "timestamp": 1789896952.346501, "id": "5102351a1115", "status": "completed", "summary": "能做，而且这一问正好把上一轮 undo 的死结解开了。先把结论放前面：**技术上完全可行（仍然零依赖、纯标准库），而且「常驻」比「每次调用起一个进程」更能自洽地承载你刚定的两个方向（围栏下放 + undo 下放）**。但形态要选对，下面摊开讲。\n\n## 为什么「常驻」恰好是对症的\n\n上一轮 undo 卡住的根本原因是：现在的 CLI **一次调用一个进程、干完即退**，内存快照栈活不过一次调用，逼出「落盘存储」那串复杂设计。如果 workspace 变成常驻进程：\n\n- **undo 回到内存栈**——和今天 host 的行为完全一致（host 的 `_snapshots` 就是内存 dict，会话结束即失），不需要 `.clutch/undo/` 落盘方案了\n- **每次调用省掉一次 Python 解释器冷启动**（Windows 上单次约 100–200ms），agent 一个会话几百次工具调用，累积收益可观\n- **围栏配置收口得更彻底**：围栏在 daemon 启动时从 spawn 参数一次性注入，之后的协议里**根本没有 config 字段**——比「转发 flag」更强的「tool 封装无配置入口」，结构性做到\n- **和远程方案汇合**：你之前定过「远程 = 服务器部署 + SSH 桥」，常驻 server 化的 workspace 跟桥那套形态天然趋同，将来本地/远程可以是同一套协议\n\n## 推荐形态：`serve` 子命令 + stdio 行式 JSON\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph host[\"clutch host\"]\n        UI[\"客户端 UI\"] --> SERVER[\"server.py 会话\"]\n        TOOLS[\"tool 封装\"]\n    end\n    SERVER -->|\"spawn + 注入配置(仅此处)\"| D[\"clutch-workspace serve\"]\n    TOOLS -->|\"协议调用，无配置字段\"| D\n    D --> S[\"内存态：围栏 + undo 栈\"]\n    D --> DIR[\"任务目录\"]\n```\n\n- host 在**会话开始**时 spawn：`clutch-workspace serve --workspace X --protect ...`（UI 配置在此一次性注入）\n- 协议就是 stdin/stdout 上的一行 JSON 进、一行 JSON 出：\n\n```json\n→ {\"id\": 7, \"op\": \"edit_file\", \"params\": {\"path\": \"a.py\", \"old-string\": \"...\", \"new-string\": \"...\"}}\n← {\"id\": 7, \"ok\": true, \"content\": \"OK: edited a.py (+1 -1 lines)\", \"diff\": \"--- a/a.py...\"}\n← {\"id\": 9, \"ok\": false, \"code\": 66, \"error\": \"file not found: a.py\"}\n```\n\n- 会话结束 host 杀掉它；意外死亡由 host 重启（快照丢失 = 和今天 host 重启丢快照一个待遇，不是退步）\n- **单命令模式原样保留**（人手动用、脚本用、现有 64 个测试全都不动）——`serve` 只是复用同一个核心的第二个门面\n\n**为什么不推荐 TCP 端口版 daemon**：本机任何进程都能连上一个裸端口，围栏配置权就从「host 独有」泄漏成「本机谁都在场」，得再加 token 认证；还有端口分配、孤儿进程清理（Windows 上很烦）、防火墙首次弹窗。stdio 管道的信任边界和今天完全一样：管道另一头就是 host，不多不少。\n\n## 代价（说实话的部分）\n\n1. **host 要管生命周期**：spawn/杀/崩溃重启。host 的 supervisor 已有子孙进程清理机制（Toolhelp32 那套），有现成经验\n2. **状态陈旧风险**：daemon 记着 workspace 根，用户中途删目录/改配置会失配 → 每次调用前校验根目录仍存在 + 加一条 `configure` 协议消息支持中途改围栏\n3. **多了一层要冻结的契约**（协议格式）；好在错误语义可以直接搬 sysexits 码进 `code` 字段\n4. **并发模型要定**：推荐「一会话一 daemon」，两个会话开同一目录 = 两个 daemon、两套 undo 栈——和今天两个 host 进程各持一份内存栈的行为一致\n\n## 对上一轮待拍板项的影响\n\n| 上轮决策点 | 常驻后 |\n|---|---|\n| undo-① 存储位置（落盘 `.clutch/undo/`） | **作废** → daemon 内存栈，零落盘 |\n| undo-⑤ 节奏 | 仍建议与围栏同轮 |\n| 围栏-③ 配置通道 | 不变方向，但收口更狠：配置只存在于 spawn 参数，协议无 config 字段 |\n| 围栏-①②④⑥（搬哪些/`--workspace`/77 码/远程不管） | **不受影响，仍待你拍** |\n\n## 现在轮到你拍板的（新增 3 个）\n\n1. **做不做常驻**——推荐做；替代方案是维持 per-call + undo 落盘（更简单但慢、且要落盘设计）\n2. **形态**——推荐 stdio 行式 JSON 的 `serve` 子命令，随会话生死，单命令模式保留；不推荐 TCP daemon\n3. **undo 存储改判**——推荐从「落盘」改回「daemon 内存（会话级，与今天 host 行为对齐）」\n\n连同上一轮还挂着的围栏 ①②④⑥，你可以一起裁，比如「1做 2按推荐 3改内存；围栏①全搬除undo已解决 ②同意 ④77 ⑥不管远程」。裁完我一次做完：serve 协议 + 围栏 + `--workspace` + undo 栈 + 测试全绿 + 提交。"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1789897112.5401618, "id": "75ed5667fbe7", "content": "常驻程序支持使用终端命令式的请求调用吗？还是说做成cli-srv模型使用本地http通信更好"}
{"type": "compaction", "timestamp": 1789897326.80495, "id": "3a9a5d8f651d", "summary": "# 直答：能，而且你这一问恰好修正了我上轮的推荐\n\n**stdio 常驻做不到终端直调**——那根 stdin/stdout 管子是宿主进程私有的，终端里敲命令根本够不着 daemon。要「终端命令式」地调用常驻进程，唯一路子就是你说的 **cli-srv**：daemon 监听本地端口，**CLI 变成薄客户端**，命令语法原样保留、请求转发给 daemon。所以两个选项不是并列关系：你要保留终端直调，cli-srv 就是必然形态。\n\n## cli-srv 的核心手法：一份语法，三条路径\n\n```bash\n# 终端敲的命令和今天一模一样，用户无感知：\nclutch-workspace read_file --path src/app.py\n```\n\nCLI 启动时按 `--workspace` 算出发现文件（用户级目录，按任务目录哈希命名，内含端口+token+pid）：\n\n| daemon 状态 | CLI 行为 |\n|---|---|\n| 在跑 | 转发 HTTP，收到 `{code,error}` 映射回原有退出码和信封，**UX 逐字节不变** |\n| 没在跑 | 懒启动 daemon（失败则静默回退本地直执） |\n| 强制本地 | `--no-server` 直执，测试和脚本兜底用 |\n\n现有 64 个测试自动变成「回退路径」的回归网，再补一组 daemon 模式测试即可。\n\n## 为什么本地 HTTP 优于裸协议\n\n- **调试零成本**：`curl 127.0.0.1:PORT/read_file?...` 就能打，行式自造协议做不到\n- **与远程桥收敛**：你之前定的远程方案就是「服务器部署 + HTTP 桥」——本地/远程同族协议，将来 RemoteWorkspace 可以薄到只是换个 base_url\n- **回环绑定不触发 Windows 防火墙弹窗**；keep-alive 下开销亚毫秒\n- 标准库 `http.server`（HTTP/1.1）+ `http.client` 足够，**零依赖仍然守住**\n- AF_UNIX + 行 JSON 虽然免端口免 token，但 Windows 版 Python 支持有历史坑，不做首选\n\n**安全账（必须说实话的部分）**：本地端口 = 本机任何进程都能连。防线 = 仅绑 127.0.0.1 + 随机端口 + token（写进发现文件）。单用户机器上这是合理强度，但和 stdio 管子的「宿主独占」比，信任面确实宽了一档——换来的是多客户端统一。\n\n## 这个模型白送的两个结构性保证\n\n1. **「tool 封装无配置入口」变得可审计**：围栏只在 daemon **启动参数**里（host 会话拉起时注入），HTTP API 干脆**不提供 reconfigure 端点**。想改围栏 = 重启 daemon。没有任何端点可调，比「纪律上不许传」硬得多。\n2. **undo 栈全局一致**：终端、脚本、host、UI 按钮打的都是同一个 daemon → 共享同一份内存 undo 栈（比 stdio 方案强：那方案里终端的一次性命令和 daemon 各持一套状态，互相看不见）。回退直执时的外部写入不被快照——和今天你用 vim 改文件 host 不知道，是同等语义，可接受。\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    T[\"终端 / 脚本\"] --> C\n    subgraph host[\"clutch host\"]\n        TOOLS[\"tool 封装（进程内 HTTP 调用，不再 spawn）\"] --> C[\"clutch-workspace CLI 薄客户端\"]\n        SERVER[\"server.py 会话\"] -->|\"spawn + 围栏配置（唯一入口）\"| D\n    end\n    C -->|\"HTTP 127.0.0.1 + token\"| D[\"daemon：围栏 + undo 内存栈\"]\n    D --> DIR[\"任务目录\"]\n    C -.->|\"daemon 缺席 → 本地直执\"| DIR\n```\n\n## 性能收益的真实分布\n\n- **host 侧是大头**：tool 调用从「每次 spawn 子进程（~100–200ms）」变成进程内 HTTP 调用（~1–5ms），一个会话几百次调用，累积可观\n- **终端侧**延迟不变（反正都要起一个薄客户端进程），买到的是**共享状态**而非速度\n\n## 待你拍板（含 carry-over）\n\n| # | 决策点 | 推荐 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 模型定型 | **cli-srv**（daemon + 薄客户端 + 回退直执），放弃 stdio 子进程方案 |\n| 2 | 协议 | 127.0.0.1 + 随机端口 + token + 发现文件；**不提供 reconfigure 端点**（围栏改动=重启 daemon） |\n| 3 | daemon 粒度 | 每 workspace 一个（发现文件按路径哈希寻址）；空闲超时自杀（如 10 分钟）+ pid 存活校验清理 |\n| 4 | 懒启动 | 终端首次调用自动拉起 daemon，失败静默回退直执 |\n| 5 | undo 存储改判 | daemon **内存栈**（随 daemon 生死；落盘 `.clutch/undo/` 方案正式作废）；`undo_file` 进 HTTP API，仍不映射给 agent 工具表 |\n| 6 | carry-over | 围栏上轮的 ①搬哪些 ②`--workspace` ④退出码77 ⑥远程不管——不受本轮影响，仍待裁 |\n\n逐条回或「都按推荐」。裁完我一次性落地：daemon + 薄客户端 + 围栏 + `--workspace` + undo 栈 + 双模式测试全绿 + 提交。"}
