{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789897749.7790287, "id": "cf799e99dc52", "content": "fix.clc 是项目对话日志，跳过。核心对象是 `agent/supervisor.py`，我把它完整读一遍，再看 UI 侧和测试是怎么消费它的。", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_a36d7344dbdf4b3397570c05", "name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"agent/supervisor.py\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":240}"}], "reasoning": "The fix.clc file is the project's conversation log — I should not read it. The key file is `agent/supervisor.py`. Let me read it fully to understand its current structure. It's ~760 lines. Let me read it in chunks.\n\nAlso relevant: `agent/server.py` (the session child), `ui/main.js` and `ui/server-bootstrap.js` (how UI talks to supervisor), `tests/supervisor_test.py`.\n\nThe user's task: \"把supervisor管理进程那套抽象分层出来，这部分以后广泛地管理所有和clutch有关的进程，在这层抽象的基础上如有必要再对会话进程管理这个特殊的需求做特化。\"\n\nSo: extract the process-management machinery from agent/supervisor.py into a general-purpose layered abstraction (process supervision: spawn, discover, health-check, kill-tree, idle reaping, stale cleanup, port waiting, job objects), which will later manage ALL clutch-related processes (workspace daemon from the cli-srv plan, LLM proxy, session servers, remote supervisor...). Then specialize on top for session management (the UI session lifecycle).\n\nI'm in chat mode — read-only. So my deliverable is the layered design + refactoring plan. But the refactor skill says: Phase 1 research → write REFACTORING.md... but I can't write files in chat mode. I should do the research and present the design in the response, then tell the user to switch to work mode for implementation.\n\nLet me read agent/supervisor.py in full (it's ~760 lines, read in 2-3 chunks), and glance at how ui/main.js uses it, and tests/supervisor_test.py."}
