supervisor_test spawns real agent.server children (~minutes? test 6 sleeps 7s, test 13 Job stuff, total maybe 60-90s). Then server_test full. Also quick import check of ui? No — Python only.\n\nAlso — verify nothing else references the old private names: grep `from agent.supervisor import|from .supervisor import` across repo (excluding fix.clc log!). fix.clc is the conversation log — grep will hit it; restrict path to agent/, scripts/, tests/, ui/ (ui is js — `-m agent.supervisor` subprocess only ✓). \n\nLet me write the files now. Order: procmgr package → supervisor.py rewrite → compile check → test edits → run.\n\nWriting kill.py — copy structures EXACTLY (ctypes field defs must not drift).\n\nFor stop_process docstring — preserve original _kill docstring substance, generalize \"session child\"→\"child\".\n\nJob block comment (lines 219-234) — I'll keep it nearly verbatim, replacing \"session child\"/\"session\" with \"managed child\" where it refers to the generic concept, and keeping the .clc-lock war story (it's the justification).\n\nTime to write. Also add procmgr to any packaging config? pyproject.toml — packages discovered how? Frozen build uses PyInstaller entry scripts (agent.supervisor module via entry py file with PYTHONPATH). pyproject may list [tool.pyinstaller] or packages. Check pyproject.toml quickly before finishing. If it uses hatchling with packages=[\"agent\"], subpackage auto-included ✓. I'll peek at pyproject.\n\nLet me start writing files. I'll do pyproject check + write stdio.py in parallel-ish (independent). Actually read pyproject first (tiny), then write files."}
