beyond the\\nWindows 32K argv limit still get through. Only ONE flag per invocation\\nmay use `-` — two would drain the same stream twice.\"}"}, {"id": "call_6d9af0bc521e48fc9311ca56", "name": "edit_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/cli.py\",\"old_string\":\"from . import __version__, filesystem\\nfrom .envelope import CommandError, Result, emit_error, emit_result\\nfrom .exitcodes import EX_IOERR, EX_SIGINT, EX_SOFTWARE, EX_USAGE\\nfrom .filesystem import READ_MAX_CHARS\",\"new_string\":\"from . import __version__, client, filesystem\\nfrom .envelope import CommandError, Result, emit_error, emit_result\\nfrom .exitcodes import EX_DATAERR, EX_IOERR, EX_NOPERM, EX_NOINPUT, EX_SIGINT, EX_SOFTWARE, EX_USAGE\\nfrom .filesystem import READ_MAX_CHARS\\n\\n# verdict codes the daemon may answer with — the CLI re-raises them as its\\n# own exit codes; anything else (400/403/404/5xx) is protocol trouble, not\\n# a verdict for the command, and falls back to direct execution\\n_CONTRACT_CODES = frozenset({EX_USAGE, EX_DATAERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_SOFTWARE, EX_IOERR, EX_NOPERM})\"}"}], "reasoning": "Now wire cli.py: docstring, parser flags, _prepare/_EXECUTE/_execute refactor, imports. Targeted edits.\n\nEdit 1 — docstring: add daemon paragraph. The docstring currently:\n\n```\n\"\"\"Flag wiring: argparse -> filesystem commands -> envelope out.\n\n  clutch-workspace [--json] <command> [flags]\n\n- human (default): ...\n- --json: ...\nA payload flag value of `-` reads ...\nmay use `-` — two would drain the same stream twice.\n\nUsage errors (bad flags, unknown command, contradictory arguments —\nargparse's own included) exit 64; I/O failures 74; a bug that escapes is\n70, never masquerading as caller error.\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nAdd after the --json bullet or before \"Usage errors\":\n\n```\n- daemon mode (default): the command rides a per-workspace HTTP daemon\n  when one is running (or can be lazy-started); the reply envelope is\n  re-emitted byte-identica