{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1789901214.7922273, "id": "ff91a9d0b02f", "name": "edit_file", "arguments": "{\"new_string\":\"def _verdict(result: Result) -> dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The CLI's envelope plus the verdict code — \\\"code\\\" is transport-only:\\n    sysexits numbers are illegal HTTP statuses, so they ride in the body.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return {\\\"content\\\": result.content, \\\"error\\\": False, \\\"diff\\\": result.diff, \\\"code\\\": 0}\\n\\n\\ndef _verdict_err(code: int, message: str) -> dict:\\n    return {\\\"content\\\": message, \\\"error\\\": True, \\\"diff\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"code\\\": code}\\n\\n\\ndef _transport_err(message: str) -> dict:\\n    return {\\\"content\\\": message, \\\"error\\\": True, \\\"diff\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"old_string\":\"def _err_envelope(message: str) -> dict:\\n    return {\\\"content\\\": message, \\\"error\\\": True, \\\"diff\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"path\":\"clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/daemon.py\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_38865bb86ac04d88beed124a"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789901214.8113344, "id": "95e1064c2f22", "tool_call_id": "call_4f02ee8977364dea85d5d7cd", "content": "OK: edited C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\daemon.py (+12 -9 lines)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\daemon.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\daemon.py\n@@ -12,15 +12,18 @@\n header (anything else is 403):\n \n     GET  /health      → {\"ok\": true, \"workspace\", \"pid\", \"undo\"}\n-    POST /read_file /grep /write_file /edit_file /undo\n-                      → the command verdict, envelope out\n-    POST /shutdown    → 200, then the daemon unpublishes and exits\n-\n-The HTTP status IS the command verdict: 200 ok, otherwise the BSD sysexits\n-code the CLI contract uses (64/65/66/74; 77 when a --protect glob fences\n-the path; 70 for a daemon bug). The body is the same {\"content\", \"error\",\n-\"diff\"} envelope the CLI emits, so the thin client re-emits it byte-\n-identically. /health and /shutdown answer plain {\"ok\": true, ...}.\n+    POST /read_file /grep /write_file /edit_file /undo /shutdown\n+                      → the command response\n+\n+Every command response rides HTTP 200; the VERDICT is the envelope's\n+\"code\" field: 0 ok, else the BSD sysexits code the CLI contract uses\n+(64/65/66/74; 77 when a --protect glob fences the path; 70 for a daemon\n+bug). The sysexits numbers are NOT HTTP statuses — 2-digit codes are\n+illegal status lines — so they travel in the body. The other three fields\n+are exactly the CLI's {\"content\", \"error\", \"diff\"} envelope, so the thin\n+client re-emits byte-identically and just maps code → exit status. The\n+transport statuses (403 bad token, 400 bad JSON, 404 unknown path) carry\n+no verdict: the client treats them as \"no usable daemon\" and falls back.\n \n Undo lives HERE (ratified: daemon memory, not disk): every write/edit that\n succeeds pushes {path, before, existed}, capped at the 100 most recent;\n"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789901214.8535905, "id": "bd017674ddc2", "tool_call_id": "call_38865bb86ac04d88beed124a", "content": "OK: edited C:\\Users\\12741\\Desktop\\临时文件\\Clutch\\clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\daemon.py (+11 -1 lines)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\daemon.py\n+++ b/clutch-workspace\\clutch_workspace\\daemon.py\n@@ -221,7 +221,17 @@\n     return out\n \n \n-def _err_envelope(message: str) -> dict:\n+def _verdict(result: Result) -> dict:\n+    \"\"\"The CLI's envelope plus the verdict code — \"code\" is transport-only:\n+    sysexits numbers are illegal HTTP statuses, so they ride in the body.\"\"\"\n+    return {\"content\": result.content, \"error\": False, \"diff\": result.diff, \"code\": 0}\n+\n+\n+def _verdict_err(code: int, message: str) -> dict:\n+    return {\"content\": message, \"error\": True, \"diff\": \"\", \"code\": code}\n+\n+\n+def _transport_err(message: str) -> dict:\n     return {\"content\": message, \"error\": True, \"diff\": \"\"}\n \n \n"}
{"type": "compaction", "timestamp": 1789901281.1946895, "id": "b04b14288b9f", "summary": "## Objective\n- Implement the workspace daemon (ratified cli-srv model) in `clutch-workspace`: HTTP daemon + CLI thin client (transparent forwarding, lazy start, `--no-server` fallback), dual-mode tests green + focused commits.\n\n## Important Details\n- M1 source fully read; no README in repo; pre-existing commits 33e5f98 (feat) + b97185a (test); tree was clean before this work\n- New in-session protocol decision (bug-driven): sysexits verdicts (64/65/66/70/74/77) are 2-digit → ILLEGAL as HTTP status lines (http.client BadStatusLine). Final shape: all command responses ride HTTP 200; verdict lives in transport-only envelope field `\"code\"` (0 ok, else sysexits); contract fields stay `{content, error, diff}` for byte-identical re-emit; transport statuses (403 bad token / 400 bad JSON / 404 unknown path) carry NO verdict → client forgets daemon + falls back direct\n- Fence = mutation-only (write_file/edit_file/undo refuse matching paths, 77=EX_NOPERM added to exitcodes.py); reads pass through — provisional pending carry-over ①. A fenced daemon can never hold an undo entry for a fenced path (no reconfigure endpoint) → fence-at-undo is defense-in-depth only\n- Daemon holds one RLock across whole-command execution (+`busy` counter for idle watchdog); /health undo count read lock-free\n- Client: lazy start = detached spawn (POSIX `start_new_session=True`, Windows `DETACHED_PROCESS|CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP`, DEVNULL stdio), poll discovery ~10s, early-out if child dies; transport failure mid-command → exit 74 (NOT silent fallback; edit_file not idempotent); spawn must prepend package parent to child `PYTHONPATH` (child chdirs to workspace, `-m` import breaks in source checkouts)\n- Env switches: `CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER=1` (kill switch; conftest setdefault keeps 64 legacy tests direct), `CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_DISCOVERY_DIR` (tests repoint rendezvous); test spawn env MUST be built per-call (fixtures set env after module import — module-level constant caused \"daemon never became ready\"); leaked daemons from failed runs already swept from real `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\clutch-workspace`\n- `--workspace DIR` + `--no-server` global flags wired; direct path chdirs to workspace; undo is HTTP-only (no CLI subcommand); version bumped 0.1.0→0.2.0 (`__init__.py`, `pyproject.toml`, test_cli.py assert)\n- run_command tool has 30s cap → run pytest in slices (`-k` groups), full suite too long\n- Commit plan: conftest one-liner inside feat commit to keep it green; then `feat: workspace daemon + thin client (...)` + `test: ...`\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- All reads done; undo reference checked (`agent/tools/workspace.py` per-file stack, `_MAX_SNAPSHOTS_PER_FILE = 5`)\n- Written: `exitcodes.py` (+EX_NOPERM=77), `filesystem.py` (docstring + `previous_content`/`restore`), NEW `discovery.py` (sha256 key `d-<hex32>.json`, atomic write via mkstemp+os.replace, stale cleanup, Windows ctypes pid_alive), NEW `daemon.py` (argparse --workspace/--protect/--idle 600s/--port, banner, watchdog, signals, /shutdown, fence, undo cap 100), NEW `client.py` (endpoint/forward/shutdown/forget/disabled, detached spawn, `_child_env` PYTHONPATH fix, `DaemonUnreachable`)\n- `cli.py` wired: `_prepare`/`_EXECUTE`/`_execute`/`_via_daemon`/`_server_enabled`, flags, `_CONTRACT_CODES` frozenset; `conftest.py` NO_SERVER setdefault; version bumps incl. test_cli.py\n- NEW `tests/test_daemon.py`: byte-identical matrix (seed-before-each-leg), lazy start + reuse, kill switches, stale/corrupt discovery self-heal, `--workspace`, fence 77, undo restore/remove/empty-64 + refused-write-pushes-nothing, HTTP guards, idle suicide, clean shutdown, missing-workspace 66, discovery primitives\n- 64 legacy tests PASS (12.41s)\n\n### Active\n- Mid-refactor to verdict-rides-200: `_verdict`/`_verdict_err`/`_transport_err` helpers + daemon docstring just written, but `_Handler._get`/`_post` still call removed `_err_envelope` (403/404/400 + CommandError/success paths need rewiring); `cli._via_daemon` still maps by HTTP status (needs: status!=200 → forget+direct; 200 → error?CommandError(env[\"code\"]):Result)\n- Tests pending fixes: `daemon_env` fixture must `disc.mkdir` (stale-discovery write hit FileNotFoundError); `test_http_guards` 404 loop includes `/write_file {\"nope\":1}` which is now verdict 64 — split out\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Rewire `_Handler._get`/`_post` to `_transport_err`(403/404/400) + `200 + _verdict/_verdict_err` (missing field = `_verdict_err(EX_USAGE, ...)`); update `cli._via_daemon` mapping\n2. Fix `test_daemon.py` (fixture mkdir, http_guards split), rerun slices `-k forwarded/lazy/no_server/stale/workspace_flag/fence/undo/http/idle/shutdown/missing/workspace_key/pid_alive`, then full legacy suite; commit `feat: workspace daemon + thin client (lazy start, --no-server, undo, fence)` + `test: daemon dual-mode suite` in clutch-workspace\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/daemon.py` — NEW; handler responses mid-rewire to verdict envelopes\n- `clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/client.py` — NEW; forward comment/flow must match 200-rides-verdict\n- `clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/cli.py` — `_via_daemon` remap pending; flags + routing done\n- `clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/discovery.py` — NEW; rendezvous + pid liveness\n- `clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/filesystem.py` — `previous_content`/`restore` seams for daemon undo\n- `clutch-workspace/clutch_workspace/exitcodes.py` — EX_NOPERM=77 added\n- `clutch-workspace/tests/test_daemon.py` — NEW; fixture mkdir + guards split pending\n- `clutch-workspace/tests/conftest.py` — NO_SERVER setdefault (keep 64 legacy tests direct)\n- `clutch-workspace/pyproject.toml` + `clutch_workspace/__init__.py` — 0.2.0\n- `/tmp/diag_spawn.py`, `/tmp/diag_missing.py`, `/tmp/sweep.py` — throwaway diag/sweep scripts (not committed)\n- `agent/tools/workspace.py`, `agent/procmgr/` (main repo