cute/_via_daemon/_server_enabled, flags, _CONTRACT_CODES frozenset; conftest.py NO_SERVER setdefault\" — and \"64 legacy tests PASS (12.41s)\". The order of those events isn't fully clear; the legacy suite run may have happened before cli wiring. So these two failures are fallout of enabling daemon mode by default in-process: tests that call cli.main directly without the env kill switch now try the daemon.\n\nFix options:\n1. In conftest, set the env var at import/collection time for the whole pytest process: `os.environ.setdefault(\"CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER\", \"1\")` at module level (not just inside _run). That keeps all in-process legacy calls direct. The daemon tests opt back in via monkeypatch.setenv(\"CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER\", \"0\") — which works since disabled() reads env each call.\n\nThat's exactly the summary's stated intent: \"conftest setdefault keeps 64 legacy tests direct\" — but it was only implemented inside `_run`'s env dict. The in-process tests slipped through. Fix: hoist the setdefault to conftest module level (keep the one in _run too? Module-level setdefault affects the pytest process env; `_run` builds env from os.environ — which would then already include NO_SERVER=1. But daemon tests monkeypatch it to \"0\" for their subprocess runs via monkeypatch.setenv — monkeypatch.setenv modifies the test process env during the test, and `_run` copies os.environ → child gets \"0\". After the test, monkeypatch restores to \"1\".\n\nSo: module-level `os.environ.setdefault(\"CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER\", \"1\")` in conftest + keep the explicit env.setdefault in _run (harmless, or drop it — keeping is fine and explicit). Then the two in-process tests run direct → monkeypatched read_file throws → 130/70. \n\nAlso note the captured stderr \"ERROR: file not found: f.txt\" — consistent with the daemon having answered 66.\n\nAlso: those failing runs actually lazy-started real daemons for tmp dirs in %LOCALAPPDATA% discovery? The discovery dir: tests didn't override it for these legacy tests. endpoint() → discovery.read(str(tmp_path)) → no record → _spawn_and_wait → spawned daemon, wrote discovery to the REAL discovery dir, forwarded, answered 66. Daemon stays alive until idle timeout (600s) or my sweep. After the test, discovery entry remains → leaked daemon + discovery file. I should sweep again after fixing: remove discovery entries + shut down daemons for those tmp paths. My earlier sweep script was /tmp/sweep.py (throwaway, may still exist). Let me check and rerun it.\n\nPlan:\n1. Edit conftest.py: add module-level setdefault.\n2. Re-run the two tests → green.\n3. Full legacy suite → green.\n4. Sweep leaked daemons/discovery files.\n5. Commit feat + test.\n\nAlso consider: is module-level env mutation in conftest acceptable? It's the documented mechanism (\"tests set this so the default suite stays in-process\"). daemon tests override per-test. Good.\n\nLet me check whether /tmp/sweep.py still exists, and write the conftest fix."}
