{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789902125.2756085, "id": "08970bf85ee1", "content": "64 全绿。清理刚才回归期间泄漏的真实 daemon(两个失败测试曾 lazy-start 到真实 discovery 目录)：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_f6314f5e5604490fa3dc6b16", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat > clutch-workspace/_sweep.py <<'EOF'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"One-off sweep: shut down any leaked workspace daemons + clear discovery.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json, os, urllib.request\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\ndisc = Path(os.environ[\\\"LOCALAPPDATA\\\"]) / \\\"clutch-workspace\\\"\\nif not disc.is_dir():\\n    print(\\\"no discovery dir\\\"); raise SystemExit\\nfor f in sorted(disc.glob(\\\"*.json\\\")):\\n    try:\\n        rec = json.loads(f.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\n        port, token = rec[\\\"port\\\"], rec[\\\"token\\\"]\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError):\\n        print(\\\"unparsable, removing:\\\", f.name); f.unlink(missing_ok=True); continue\\n    req = urllib.request.Request(f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/shutdown\\\", data=b\\\"{}\\\",\\n                                 headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"X-Clutch-Token\\\": token},\\n                                 method=\\\"POST\\\")\\n    try:\\n        urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=3)\\n        print(\\\"shut down:\\\", f.name)\\n    except OSError as e:\\n        print(\\\"already dead:\\\", f.name, type(e).__name__)\\n    f.unlink(missing_ok=True)\\nprint(\\\"remaining:\\\", sorted(p.name for p in disc.glob(\\\"*.json\\\")))\\nEOF\\ncd clutch-workspace && ./.venv/Scripts/python.exe _sweep.py && rm _sweep.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "64 legacy green. Now sweep leaked daemons from the two failing runs (they lazy-started real daemons into the real discovery dir). The earlier sweep script was /tmp/sweep.py — check if it still exists; if yes run it, else write a quick inline sweep.\n\nSweep logic: list discovery dir (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\clutch-workspace), for each d-*.json read port/token, call /shu