{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1789902161.746595, "id": "08b5ba39d8cb", "tool_call_id": "call_de4ab466a37a45fb8592c5f8", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\ndiff --git a/tests/conftest.py b/tests/conftest.py\nindex 7d76851..9a8ba7f 100644\n--- a/tests/conftest.py\n+++ b/tests/conftest.py\n@@ -14,9 +14,18 @@ ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:  # lets tests import clutch_workspace for constants\n     sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n \n+# daemon OFF for the whole pytest PROCESS, not just spawned children: tests\n+# that drive cli.main in-process would otherwise lazy-start real daemons and\n+# dodge their monkeypatches. Daemon tests opt back in per-test with\n+# CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER=0 (monkeypatch restores this afterwards).\n+os.environ.setdefault(\"CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER\", \"1\")\n+\n \n def _run(*args: object, cwd: Path | str, stdin: str | None = None):\n+    # daemon OFF by default here so the whole suite exercises the direct\n+    # path; daemon tests opt back in with CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER=0\n     env = dict(os.environ, PYTHONPATH=str(ROOT), PYTHONUTF8=\"1\")\n+    env.setdefault(\"CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER\", \"1\")\n     return subprocess.run(\n         [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"clutch_workspace\", *(str(a) for a in args)],\n         cwd=str(cwd),\ndiff --git a/tests/test_cli.py b/tests/test_cli.py\nindex 6268388..2a45107 100644\n--- a/tests/test_cli.py\n+++ b/tests/test_cli.py\n@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ from clutch_workspace.exitcodes import EX_IOERR, EX_NOINPUT, EX_SIGINT, EX_SOFTW\n def test_version(run):\n     proc = run(\"--version\")\n     assert proc.returncode == 0\n-    assert proc.stdout == \"clutch-workspace 0.1.0\\n\"\n+    assert proc.stdout == \"clutch-workspace 0.2.0\\n\"\n \n \n def test_no_args_prints_usage_and_exits_64(run):\n\nstderr:\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in tests/conftest.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\nwarning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in tests/test_cli.py.\nThe file will have its original line endings in your working directory\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789902177.6116138, "id": "25617c2f723d", "content": "按计划提交:feat(源码 + conftest 保绿 + 版本断言)与 test(daemon 套件)分开：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_6b2a9dfe46c34b8a85968cb4", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cd clutch-workspace && git add clutch_workspace/__init__.py clutch_workspace/cli.py clutch_workspace/exitcodes.py clutch_workspace/filesystem.py clutch_workspace/client.py clutch_workspace/daemon.py clutch_workspace/discovery.py pyproject.toml tests/conftest.py tests/test_cli.py && git commit -q -m \\\"feat: workspace daemon + thin client (lazy start, --no-server, undo, fence)\\n\\nOne long-lived HTTP daemon per workspace (127.0.0.1, token-gated), found\\nvia a sha256-keyed discovery file; the CLI becomes a thin client that\\nforwards each command and re-emits the envelope byte-identically.\\n\\n- protocol: every command answer rides HTTP 200 with the verdict in a\\n  transport-only \\\\\\\"code\\\\\\\" field (0 ok, else sysexits) — 2-digit codes are\\n  illegal HTTP status lines; 403/400/404 are transport-only (no verdict)\\n  and the client forgets that daemon and falls back to direct execution\\n- lazy start: detached spawn (own session / DETACHED_PROCESS), ~10s\\n  discovery poll, early-out if the child dies; stale/corrupt discovery\\n  self-heals via pid liveness; a daemon lost MID-command is exit 74, not\\n  a silent re-run (edit_file is not idempotent)\\n- --no-server / CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER=1 force the direct path;\\n  --workspace DIR keys the daemon and chdirs the direct path too\\n- undo lives in daemon memory (per-file snapshots, cap 100, HTTP-only\\n  /undo); --protect GLOB fences mutations with exit 77 (new EX_NOPERM),\\n  matching basename, CWD-relative and directory-suffix forms\\n- one RLock around whole-command execution; idle watchdog exits at\\n  --idle seconds (default 600), signals and /shutdown unpublish cleanly\\n- conftest defaults the whole pytest process to NO_SERVER so in-process\\n  cli.main tests stay direct; version 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0\\\" && git commit -q -m \\\"test: daemon dual-mode suite (forwarding, fence, undo, lifecycle)\\n\\n15 black-box cases: byte-identical output vs the direct path, lazy start\\nand same-daemon reuse, --no-server/env kill switches, stale+corrupt\\ndiscovery self-heal, --workspace keying, fence 77 (incl. nested paths\\nand read pass-through), undo restore/remove/empty over HTTP, refused\\nwrites pushing no undo entry, 403/404/400 transport guards with no\\nverdict, verdict-in-200, idle suicide, clean shutdown, missing-workspace\\n66, discovery key stability and pid liveness.\\\" tests/test_daemon.py && git log --oneline -4 && git status --short\"}"}], "reasoning": "Diffs are exactly as expected. Now commit:\n\nCommit 1 (feat): clutch_workspace/{__init__,cli,exitcodes,filesystem}.py, new client.py/daemon.py/discovery.py, pyproject.toml, tests/conftest.py, tests/test_cli.py.\nCommit 2 (test): tests/test_daemon.py."}
