{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1789902259.9348521, "id": "69aeb6d159ff", "content": "79/79 全绿。保存本次的关键协议决策到项目记忆：", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_9607e61800f045b68b7d10b5", "name": "save_memory", "arguments": "{\"title\":\"workspace daemon shipped: verdict-rides-200 protocol\",\"content\":\"clutch-workspace M1 daemon work COMPLETE and committed (e4b9e3f feat + 5978094 test on top of 33e5f98/b97185a; version 0.2.0). 79/79 tests green (64 legacy direct + 15 daemon dual-mode).\\n\\nProtocol (bug-driven in-session decision, now law): ALL command responses ride HTTP 200; the verdict lives in a transport-only envelope field \\\"code\\\" (0 ok, else sysexits). Reason: sysexits codes (64/65/66/70/74/77) are 2-digit → illegal as HTTP status lines (http.client BadStatusLine). Contract fields stay {content, error, diff} for byte-identical re-emit. Transport statuses (403 bad token / 400 bad JSON-or-missing-field / 404 unknown path) carry NO \\\"code\\\" → cli._via_daemon calls client.forget(workspace) and falls back to direct execution. Daemon-internal bug = 200 + code 70. cli maps: status!=200 → forget+direct; 200+error → CommandError(env[\\\"code\\\"]) (non-int code → EX_SOFTWARE); 200 else → Result.\\n\\nOther fixes landed this session:\\n- _fence_candidates now yields every directory SUFFIX of the CWD-relative path in both separator flavors, so --protect \\\"secrets/*\\\" also catches deep/secrets/x.txt (nested-path fence was a real bug caught by tests).\\n- conftest.py sets CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER=1 at MODULE level (os.environ.setdefault), not just in _run's child env: tests that drive cli.main IN-PROCESS otherwise lazy-start real daemons and dodge monkeypatches (manifested as test_keyboard_interrupt_is_130 / test_internal_bug_is_70_with_traceback returning 66). Daemon tests opt back in per-test with monkeypatch.setenv(..., \\\"0\\\").\\n- Test env gotcha kept: _spawn_env() must be built per-call, never at module import.\\n\\nTools: repo has its own .venv — run tests via cd clutch-workspace && ./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest (plain `python` is 3.14 without pytest). run_command 30s cap: full suite ≈ 29s (tight), split with -k if needed.\"}"}], "reasoning": "79/79 green in one suite run. Task complete. Save memory of the ratified protocol decision (verdict-rides-200) since it's a durable cross-session fact, and the M1 completion status.\n\nPer the memory list: \"clutch-workspace M1 实现+测试全绿，4 个决策待用户拍板\" and \"clutch-workspace M1 committed: 4 decisions ratified\" exist. New durable facts:\n1. The in-session protocol decision: verdict rides 200 in \"code\" field (bug-driven: sysexits 2-digit illegal as HTTP status). This is now implemented and committed — future sessions must know.\n2. The conftest process-level NO_SERVER default gotcha (in-process cli.main tests lazy-start real daemons and dodge monkeypatches) — a real trap worth remembering.\n3. Fence candidates now include directory suffixes.\n\nShould I update the existing \"M1 committed\" memory? I can't see its content; I'll write a new memory \"workspace daemon M1 shipped: verdict-rides-200 protocol\" with the key facts. Actually better to update/overwrite related ones? I don't know their exact titles' content. A new memory is safe.\n\nLet me save one memory, then give the final summary."}
