{"title": "workspace daemon shipped: verdict-rides-200 protocol", "content": "clutch-workspace M1 daemon work COMPLETE and committed (e4b9e3f feat + 5978094 test on top of 33e5f98/b97185a; version 0.2.0). 79/79 tests green (64 legacy direct + 15 daemon dual-mode).\n\nProtocol (bug-driven in-session decision, now law): ALL command responses ride HTTP 200; the verdict lives in a transport-only envelope field \"code\" (0 ok, else sysexits). Reason: sysexits codes (64/65/66/70/74/77) are 2-digit → illegal as HTTP status lines (http.client BadStatusLine). Contract fields stay {content, error, diff} for byte-identical re-emit. Transport statuses (403 bad token / 400 bad JSON-or-missing-field / 404 unknown path) carry NO \"code\" → cli._via_daemon calls client.forget(workspace) and falls back to direct execution. Daemon-internal bug = 200 + code 70. cli maps: status!=200 → forget+direct; 200+error → CommandError(env[\"code\"]) (non-int code → EX_SOFTWARE); 200 else → Result.\n\nOther fixes landed this session:\n- _fence_candidates now yields every directory SUFFIX of the CWD-relative path in both separator flavors, so --protect \"secrets/*\" also catches deep/secrets/x.txt (nested-path fence was a real bug caught by tests).\n- conftest.py sets CLUTCH_WORKSPACE_NO_SERVER=1 at MODULE level (os.environ.setdefault), not just in _run's child env: tests that drive cli.main IN-PROCESS otherwise lazy-start real daemons and dodge monkeypatches (manifested as test_keyboard_interrupt_is_130 / test_internal_bug_is_70_with_traceback returning 66). Daemon tests opt back in per-test with monkeypatch.setenv(..., \"0\").\n- Test env gotcha kept: _spawn_env() must be built per-call, never at module import.\n\nTools: repo has its own .venv — run tests via cd clutch-workspace && ./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest (plain `python` is 3.14 without pytest). run_command 30s cap: full suite ≈ 29s (tight), split with -k if needed.", "updated": 1789902259.9438326}
